[Term]
id: HP:0000081
name: Duplicated collecting system
def: "A duplication of the collecting system of the kidney, defined as a kidney with two (instead of, normally, one) pyelocaliceal systems. The pyelocaliceal system is comprised of the renal pelvis and calices. The duplicated renal collecting system can be associated with a single ureter or with double ureters. In the latter case, the two ureters empty separately into the bladder or fuse to form a single ureteral orifice." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Double collecting system" EXACT []
synonym: "Double urinary collecting systems on intravenous pyelography" EXACT []
synonym: "Duplex collecting system" EXACT []
synonym: "Duplicated renal collecting system" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004742 ! Abnormal renal collecting system morphology
