[Term]
id: HP:0000531
name: Corneal crystals
alt_id: HP:0007760
def: "Refractile, glittering, or needle-shaped particles said to resemble crystals and located within the corneal epithelium and/or stroma, visible on slit-lamp examination, resulting from the focal accumulation of lipid, protein, or other metabolic material." [PMID:19236704]
comment: The differential diagnosis includes Schnyder corneal dystrophy, cystinosis, immunoglobulin/paraprotein crystals, infectious crystalline keratopathy, and drug-induced crystalline deposits. Crystalline deposits are typically ascertained by slit lamp examination.
synonym: "Corneal deposits" EXACT []
