[Term]
id: HP:0000657
name: Oculomotor apraxia
alt_id: HP:0000628
alt_id: HP:0007764
def: "Ocular motor apraxia is a deficiency in voluntary, horizontal, lateral, fast eye movements (saccades) with retention of slow pursuit movements. The inability to follow objects visually is often compensated by head movements. There may be decreased smooth pursuit, and cancelation of the vestibulo-ocular reflex." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20615230]
comment: Oculomotor apraxia leads defective or absent horizontal voluntary eye movements with head thrusting to look at objects to the side as well as jerky, abnormal eye movements.
synonym: "Defective or absent horizontal voluntary eye movements" RELATED []
synonym: "Ocular motor apraxia" EXACT []
