[Term]
id: HP:0000713
name: Agitation
def: "A state of excessive motor activity that is associated with mental distress or a feeling of substantial unease or inner tension. Distinguished from restlessness by the increased level of emotional distress and negative intensity of the experience. Agitation has a significant level of physical activity that is typically threatening to the self or others." []
synonym: "Psychomotor agitation" EXACT []
