[Term]
id: HP:0000728
name: Reduced ability to form peer relationships
def: "Difficulty to establish relations with others in a comparable social group (peers) that may be manifested in pehnomena such as not being able to initiative a conversation, understand social cues, or to discuss shared interests. This feature is associated with poor integration within a community or group." []
synonym: "Impaired ability to form peer relationships" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012760 ! Reduced social responsiveness

[Term]
id: HP:0000729
name: Autistic behavior
def: "Persistent deficits in social interaction and communication and interaction as well as a markedly restricted repertoire of activity and interest as well as repetitive patterns of behavior." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:28879490]
comment: This term can be used to refer to autism spectrum disorder as a phenotypic feature that can be a component of a disease. Autism spectrum disorder range from a severe form, called autistic disorder, to a milder form, Asperger syndrome. If possible, we recommend annotating using more specific terms.
synonym: "ASD" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Autism spectrum disorder" RELATED layperson []
synonym: "Autism spectrum disorders" RELATED layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autistic behaviors" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autistic behaviour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Autistic behaviours" RELATED uk_spelling []
synonym: "Pervasive developmental disorder" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025783 ! Diagnostic behavioral phenotype

[Term]
id: HP:0000732
name: Inflexible adherence to routines
def: "A need to strictly adhere to repetitive routines or patterns of behavior which are created by the environment. One becomes upset or distressed when their routines are disrupted or altered." []
is_a: HP:5200130 ! Insistence on sameness
