[Term]
id: HP:0000741
name: Apathy
def: "Apathy is a quantitative reduction of interest, motivation and the initiation and persistence of goal-directed behavior, where often the accompanying emotions, thoughts, and social interactions are also diminished. The individual is typically non-reactive to provocations, positive or negative, and appears to not care. Distinguished from lethargy which involves lack of physical or mental energy." []
comment: Apathy may co-occur with lethargy.
synonym: "Lack of feeling, emotion, interest" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
synonym: "Lack of feeling, emotion, interest, motivation, initiation" EXACT []
synonym: "State of indifference" EXACT []
