[Term]
id: HP:0000877
name: Insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus at puberty
def: "A type of insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus that develops around the time of publerty in contrast to the common form of type 2 diabetes-associated insulin resistance that typically presents in mid-to-late adulthood." [PMID:21865368, PMID:31214120]
comment: Subjects affected by congenital generalized lipodystrophy (CGL) develop insulin resistance in early childhood and almost half of them manifest diabetes mellitus at puberty. In these patients diabetes mellitus is resistant to ketosis, meaning that there is a tendency not to develop ketoacidosis despite marked hyperglycemia.
synonym: "Insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus at puberty" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0000831 ! Insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus

