[Term]
id: HP:0001047
name: Atopic dermatitis
alt_id: HP:0007533
alt_id: HP:0007564
def: "Atopic dermatitis (AD) or atopic eczema is an itchy, inflammatory skin condition with a predilection for the skin flexures. It is characterized by poorly defined erythema with edema, vesicles, and weeping in the acute stage and skin thickening (lichenification) in the chronic stage." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:27904186]
comment: In infants, atopic dermatitis is known as infantile eczema.
synonym: "Allergic eczema" EXACT []
synonym: "Atopic dermatitis, chronic" EXACT []
synonym: "Atopic eczema" EXACT []
synonym: "Baby eczema" RELATED layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Dermatitis, Atopic" EXACT []
synonym: "Infantile eczema" EXACT []
synonym: "Neurodermatitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Prurigo Besnier" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000964 ! Eczematoid dermatitis

[Term]
id: HP:0001048
name: Cavernous hemangioma
def: "The presence of a cavernous hemangioma. A hemangioma characterized by large endothelial spaces (caverns) is called a cavernous hemangioma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Cavernous angioma" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
