[Term]
id: HP:0001056
name: Milia
def: "Presence of multiple small cysts containing keratin (skin protein) and presenting as tiny pearly-white bumps just under the surface of the skin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Milia are a normal finding in newborn babies (40-50%), often occurring around the nose.
