[Term]
id: HP:0001709
name: Third degree atrioventricular block
def: "Third-degree atrioventricular (AV) block (also referred to as complete heart block) is the complete dissociation of the atria and the ventricles. Third-degree AV block exists when more P waves than QRS complexes exist and no relationship (no conduction) exists between them." [PMID:21841933]
