id: HP:0002396
name: Cogwheel rigidity
def: "A type of rigidity in which a muscle responds with cogwheellike jerks to the use of constant force in bending the limb (i.e., it gives way in little, repeated jerks when the muscle is passively stretched)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Cogwheel rigidity is a typical manifestation of Parkinson disease.
