is_a: HP:0004377 ! Hematological neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0002666
name: Pheochromocytoma
def: "Pheochromocytomas (also known as chromaffin tumors) produce, store, and secrete catecholamines. Pheochromocytomas usually originate from the adrenal medulla but may also develop from chromaffin cells in or about sympathetic ganglia. A common symptom of pheochromocytoma is hypertension owing to release of catecholamines." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Chromaffin tumors" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Chromaffin tumours" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C3326
is_a: HP:0100634 ! Neuroendocrine neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0002667
name: Nephroblastoma
alt_id: HP:0000115
def: "The presence of a nephroblastoma, which is a neoplasm of the kidney that primarily affects children." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Nephroblastoma is characterized by an abnormal proliferation of the metanephric blastema cells, which are believed to be primitive embryologic cells of the kidney. Clinically, nephroblastoma usually presents as an abdominal mass, and in some cases with abdominal pain, hypertension, hematuria, and fever.
synonym: "Wilms tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Wilms tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C40407
is_a: HP:0011794 ! Embryonal renal neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0002668
name: Paraganglioma
alt_id: HP:0002670
alt_id: HP:0003004
def: "A carotid body tumor (also called paraganglionoma or chemodectoma) is a tumor found in the upper neck at the branching of the carotid artery. They arise from the chemoreceptor organ (paraganglion) located in the adventitia of the carotid artery bifurcation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Carotid body tumors" EXACT []
synonym: "Carotid body tumours" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Paragangliomas" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
