[Term]
id: HP:0002683
name: Abnormal calvaria morphology
alt_id: HP:0002648
def: "Abnormality of the morphology (structure) of the calvaria (skullcap), that is, of that part of the skull that is made up of the superior portions of the frontal bone, occipital bone, and parietal bones and covers the cranial cavity that contains the brain." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The calvaria, or skull cap, is the upper part of the skull (cranium) and comprises the frontal, occipital and right and left parietal bones. Occasionally, calvaria is misspelled as 'calvarium' in the medical literature.
synonym: "Abnormality of calvarium" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
