[Term]
id: HP:0002728
name: Recurrent mucocutaneous candidiasis
alt_id: HP:0005392
def: "Recurrent or persistent superficial Candida infections of the skin, mucous membranes, and nails." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20859203]
comment: The most commonly involved Candida species is Candida albicans. Chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis (CMC) is usually confined to the cutaneous surface without systemic dissemination. CMC does not represent a specific disease, but rather a phenotypic feature of several immunologic, endocrinologic, and autoimmune disorders.
synonym: "Chronic candidiasis of mucosa, skin and nails" EXACT []
synonym: "Chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis" EXACT []
synonym: "Mucocutaneous candidiasis" EXACT []
synonym: "Persistent mucocutaneous candidiasis" EXACT []
