[Term]
id: HP:0002888
name: Ependymoma
def: "The presence of an ependymoma of the central nervous system." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: According to MPATH, ependymomas are neoplasms derived from the ependymal cells lining the ventricles and aqueduct of the brain and the central canal of the spinal cord and may be malignant or benign.
