[Term]
id: HP:0002963
name: Abnormal delayed hypersensitivity skin test
def: "Delay in cutaneous immune reaction to specific antigens mediated not by antibodies but by cells. The delayed hypersensitivity test is an immune function test measuring the presence of activated T cells that recognize a specific antigen and is performed by injecting a small amount of the antigen into the skin. The area of the injection is examined 48-72 hours thereafter." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This is an immune function test measuring the presence of activated T cells that recognize a certain substance.
is_a: HP:0011840 ! Abnormal T cell physiology

