comment: The product of the enzyme, succinyl-CoA, is a key molecule of the TCA (Krebs) cycle. The substrate of the enzyme, methylmalonyl-CoA, is primarily derived from propionyl-CoA, a substance formed from the catabolism of isoleucine, valine, threonine, methionine, thymine, uracil, cholesterol, or odd-chain fatty acids.
