alt_id: HP:0008842
def: "A narrowing of the sacrosciatic notch, i.e., the deep indentation in the posterior border of the hip bone at the point of union of the ilium and ischium." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The sacroiliac joint in the bony pelvis connects the sacrum and the ilium of the pelvis, which are joined by strong ligaments. The notch is located directly superior to the joint. This term refers to a reduction in the lateral dimension of the notch.
synonym: "Narrow greater sacrosciatic notches" EXACT plural_form []
