alt_id: HP:0006907
alt_id: HP:0008170
def: "A type of decreased nerve conduction velocity that affects the motor neuron." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Newborn infants have values that are approximately half that of adults, and adult values are normally reached by age 3 or 4. Motor nerve conduction is evaluated by recording the compound muscle action potential (CMAP) associated with a mechanical contraction of a given muscle in response to electrical stimulation of the motor nerve fibers supplying that muscle. The CMAP is the sum of all the action potentials occurring individually in the contracting muscle fibers.
