def: "Increased time to coagulation in the partial thromboplastin time (PTT) test, a measure of the intrinsic and common coagulation pathways. Phospholipid, and activator, and calcium are mixed into an anticoagulated plasma sample, and the time is measured until a thrombus forms." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormal partial thromboplastin time" EXACT []
