[Term]
id: HP:0003829
name: Typified by incomplete penetrance
alt_id: HP:0003830
def: "Description of conditions in which not all individuals with a given genotype exhibit the disease. Penetrance is the proportion that develop disease given a lifespan of 80 years." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: For example, Van der Woude syndrome due to IRF6 causes cleft lip and/or palate with penetrance estimated at 80%, and C9orf72 causes frontotemporal dementia and/or amyotrophic lateral sclerosis with approximately 50% penetrance.
synonym: "Incomplete penetrance" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced penetrance" EXACT []
