[Term]
id: HP:0004057
name: Mitten deformity
def: "Fusion of the hands and feet by a thin membrane of skin (scarring) seen in forms of dystrophic epidermolysis bullosa and leading to a \"mitten\" hand deformity." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20301304]
comment: Mitten deformity is also referred to as pseudosyndactyly, which should not be confused with true syndactyly (actual and complete fusion of fingers). Antenatally, pseudosyndactyly can be misinterpreted as syndactyly.
synonym: "Pseudosyndactyly" EXACT []
