[Term]
id: HP:0004222
name: Cone-shaped epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the 5th finger
def: "A cone-shaped appearance of the epiphysis of the distal phalanx of the little finger of the hand, producing a 'ball-in-a-socket' appearance. This epiphysis is located at the proximal end of the phalanx and is normally nearly flat. The related entity 'angel-shaped' epiphysis refers to a pronounced cone-shaped epiphysis in combination with a pseudoepiphysis at the distal end of the phalanx." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
