[Term]
id: HP:0004279
name: Short palm
alt_id: HP:0001165
def: "Short palm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19125433]
comment: This term refers to a developmental finding resulting in short palms. This term is reserved for individuals with shortening of all four metacarpals 2-5. Individuals with fewer than four shortened metacarpals (in a eudactylous hand, the metacarpals of F2-5) should be coded as Metacarpal, short. See the entry for Hand, small for a discussion of this finding. "Short hand" should not be used as it is a bundle of two readily separable terms, Fingers, short (which, as noted above, can itself be a bundled term) and Palm, short.
synonym: "Hypoplastic hands" RELATED []
synonym: "Short hands" RELATED layperson []
synonym: "Short palm" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Short palms" RELATED layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0005927 ! Aplasia/hypoplasia involving bones of the hand
is_a: HP:0100871 ! Abnormal palm morphology

