[Term]
id: HP:0005115
name: Supraventricular arrhythmia
def: "A type of arrhythmia that originates above the ventricles, whereby the electrical impulse propagates down the normal His Purkinje system similar to normal sinus rhythm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Supraventricular arrhythmia includes atrial arrhythmias (atrial tachycardia, atrial flutter, atrial fibrillation), atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia, junctional ectopic tachycardia, atrioventricular reentrant tachycardia (Wolf-Parkinson-White Syndrome), orthodromic or antidromic. Supraventricular arrhythmia is distinct from ventricular tachycardia, which originates in the ventricles.
synonym: "Supraventricular arrhythmias" EXACT plural_form [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0011675 ! Arrhythmia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2008-03-25T06:37:00Z" xsd:dateTime

