[Term]
id: HP:0005202
name: Helicobacter pylori infection
def: "A recurrent infection of the GI tract with helicobacter pylori, a gram-negative, microaerophilic bacterium usually found in the stomach." [PMID:23652324]
comment: The bacterial pathogen Helicobacter pylori has co-evolved with humans and colonizes approximately half of the human population, but only causes overt gastric disease in a subset of infected hosts.
is_a: HP:0004798 ! Recurrent infection of the gastrointestinal tract

[Term]
id: HP:0005203
name: Spontaneous esophageal perforation
alt_id: HP:0005251
def: "The occurrence of the full-thickness tear (perforation) of the wall of the esophagus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Esophageal perforation can lead to retained gastric contents, saliva, bile, and other substances entering the mediastinum, resulting in mediastinitis, which in turn may lead to sepsis.
synonym: "Boerhaave syndrome" RELATED []
synonym: "Spontaneous esophageal rupture" EXACT []
