id: HP:0005352
name: Severe T-cell immunodeficiency
def: "A primary immune deficiency that is characterized by defects or deficiencies of T-lymphocytes that causes specific susceptibility to intracellular micro-organisms." [PMID:18755723]
comment: Several diseases are classified as severe T cell immunodeficiencies: severe combined immunodeficiency syndrome (SCID), reticular dysgenesis, thymic dysplasia (Nezelof syndrome), combined immunodeficiency disease (CID), and Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome (WAS).
synonym: "Severe T-cell immunodeficiency" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0005374 ! Cellular immunodeficiency

[Term]
id: HP:0005353
name: Recurrent herpes
def: "Increased susceptibility to herpesvirus, as manifested by recurrent episodes of herpesvirus." []
synonym: "Susceptibility to herpesvirus" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0034318 ! Unusual virus reactivation

