[Term]
id: HP:0005357
name: Defective B cell differentiation
def: "Reduced functionality of the process in which a precursor cell type acquires the specialized features of a B cell. A B cell is a lymphocyte of B lineage with the phenotype CD19-positive and capable of B cell mediated immunity." [GO:0030183]
