[Term]
id: HP:0005372
name: Abnormal B cell physiology
alt_id: HP:0005398
def: "An abnormality of the physiological functioning of B cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This term refers to any abnormality of the B cells, which play a role in the humoral immune response. The main functions of B cells are to produce antibodies, to perform the role of antigen presenting cells, and to develop into memory cells.
synonym: "Abnormality of B cell physiology" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Reduced B cell function" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0031409 ! Abnormal lymphocyte physiology

