[Term]
id: HP:0005681
name: Juvenile idiopathic arthritis
def: "Juvenile idiopathic arthritis (JIA) is comprised of a heterogeneous group of several disease subtypes that are characterized by the onset of arthritis before the age of 16 years and has symptoms lasting at least 6 weeks." [PMID:21218014, PMID:25903287]
comment: JIA is a disease diagnosis, but since JIA can be a feature of other diseases, it is retained as an HPO term. It is recommended to annotate the specific features of joint disease is possible.
