[Term]
id: HP:0005920
name: Abnormal epiphysis morphology of the phalanges of the hand
alt_id: HP:0009151
def: "Abnormality of one or all of the epiphyses of the phalanges of the hand. Note that this includes the epiphysis of the 1st metacarpal. In contrast to the metacarpals 2-5, the first metacarpal is embryologically of phalangeal origin and as such equivalent to the proximal phalanges of the digits 2-5 (whereas the proximal phalanx of the thumb is equivalent to the middle phalanges of the other digits)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0005918 ! Abnormal finger phalanx morphology
is_a: HP:0005924 ! Abnormal hand epiphysis morphology
