[Term]
id: HP:0006544
name: Extrapulmonary lobar sequestration
alt_id: HP:0010962
def: "A type of pulmonary sequestration that is completely enclosed in its own pleural sac, occurring above, within, or below the diaphragm, and without communication with the tracheobronchial tree." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20610189]
comment: Extralobar sequestration (ELS) may be asymptomatic. Infants with symptomatic lesions may present with respiratory distress, pneumonia, feeding difficulties, hemorrhage, or even congestive heart failure. The sequestered lobe may cause substantial arteriovenous shunting, leading to high-output cardiac failure. Extrapulmonary sequestra nearly all appear on the left side.
synonym: "Diaphragmatic sequestrum" RELATED []
synonym: "Extralobar sequestration" EXACT []
synonym: "Extrapulmonary sequestrum" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100632 ! Pulmonary sequestration

[Term]
id: HP:0006548
name: Pulmonary arteriovenous malformation
alt_id: HP:0002114
alt_id: HP:0006537
def: "Pulmonary arteriovenous malformation, a condition most commonly associated with hereditary hemorrhagic telangiectasia, is an abnormal communication between the pulmonary artery and pulmonary vein without an intervening capillary communication. HRCT images usually show a coarse spidery appearance of the peripheral vascular markings in the lungs. More specific findings are obtained in the pulmonary angiogram where the normally invisible capillary phase is replaced by irregular vascular channels bridging the peripheral branches of pulmonary arteries and veins." [PMID:30386957, PMID:788535]
synonym: "Pulmonary AV malformation" EXACT []
xref: Fyler:2210
is_a: HP:0004930 ! Abnormality of the pulmonary vasculature
is_a: HP:0100026 ! Arteriovenous malformation

