[Term]
id: HP:0006640
name: Multiple rib fractures
alt_id: HP:0000923
def: "More than one fracture of the ribs. Callus formation around multiple rib fractures can produce a row of multiple rounded expansions (beadlike prominences) giving the appearance of beaded ribs. Note that rachitic rosary would have one bead per rib (a swelling at the costochondral junction), while beaded ribs in the context of multiple rib fractures have multiple beads (fractures) along the same rib." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
