[Term]
id: HP:0006679
name: Granulomatous coronary arteritis
def: "Inflammation of the coronary arteries involving a granulomatous response, i.e., a non-specific inflammatory response involving granulomas, defined as a compact organized collection of mature mononuclear phagocytes including epithelioid and giant cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:937513]
comment: A granuloma is a compact (organized) collection of mature mononuclear phagocytes (macrophages and/or epithelioid cells) which may or may not be accompanied by accessory features such as necrosis or the infiltration of other inflammatory leukocytes (Adams DO. The granulomatous inflammatory response. Am J Pathol 1976:84:163-192).
is_a: HP:0006704 ! Abnormal coronary artery morphology
is_a: HP:0012089 ! Arteritis

