[Term]
id: HP:0007011
name: Fourth cranial nerve palsy
def: "Paralysis of the fourth cranial (trochlear) nerve manifested as weakness of the superior oblique muscle which causes vertical diplopia that is maximal when the affected eye is adducted and directed inferiorly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
comment: The fourth cranial nerve crosses as it exits the midbrain dorsally and may be injured along its course through the intracranial space, cavernous sinus, superior orbital fissure, or orbit.
