[Term]
id: HP:0008321
name: Reduced factor X activity
def: "Reduced activity of coagulation factor X. The extrinsic and intrinsic pathways converge at factor X (fX). The extrinsic pathway activates fX by means of d factor VII with its cofactor, tissue factor. The intrinsic pathway activates fX by means of the tenase complex (Ca2+ and factors VIIIa, IXa and X) on the surface of activated platelets. Factor Xa in turn activates prothrombin (factor II) to thrombin (factor IIa)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Decreased factor x activity" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Factor X deficiency" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0010990 ! Abnormality of the common coagulation pathway

