[Term]
id: HP:0008823
name: Inferior pubic ramus hypoplasia
def: "Underdevelopment of the lower branch of the pubis bone (inferior pubic ramus)." []
comment: The pubis is the anterior part of the hip bone and forms the anterior and inferior borders of the obturator foramen (the obturator foramen is the opening between the ischium and pubic bones). It is divisible into a body, a superior and an inferior ramus.
synonym: "Hypoplastic inferior pubic rami" EXACT []
