[Term]
id: HP:0009657
name: Triangular shaped thumb phalanx
alt_id: HP:0004072
def: "Abnormal shape of one or more phalanges of the thumb such that affected phalanges resemble a triangle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A triangular or so called delta shaped phalanx is a typical result after a bracket epiphysis of the affected phalanx (in this case metacarpal, see explanation above).
