[Term]
id: HP:0009886
name: Trichorrhexis nodosa
def: "Trichorrhexis nodosa is the formation of nodes along the hair shaft through which breakage readily occurs. It is thus a focal defect in the hair fiber that is characterized by thickening or weak points (nodes) that cause the hair to break off easily. The result is defective, abnormally fragile hair." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0003328 ! Abnormal hairshaft morphology
