property_value: terms:date "2009-05-01T03:00:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0009909
name: Uplifted earlobe
alt_id: HP:0009764
def: "An abnormal orientation of the earlobes such that they point out- and upward. That is, the lateral surface of ear lobe faces superiorly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19152421]
comment: This finding is characteristic of Mowat-Wilson syndrome.
synonym: "Fleshy upturned lobules" EXACT []
synonym: "Lobe, uplifted" EXACT layperson []
