[Term]
id: HP:0009917
name: Persistent pupillary membrane
def: "The presence of remnants of a fetal membrane that persist as strands of tissue crossing the pupil." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The tunica vasculosa lentis anterior (pupillary membrane) normally undergoes atrophy in the third trimester of pregnancy. If the membrane does not completely atrophy, then remnants of membranous structures can be observed to emrge from the iris.
is_a: HP:0000615 ! Abnormal pupil morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
