[Term]
id: HP:0010469
name: Absent testis
def: "Testis not palpable in the scrotum or inguinal canal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23650202]
comment: Absence can be congenital or not (vanishing testis). Definitive assessment can only be made by imaging or surgical studies, in order to exclude an intra-abdominal testis, which should be coded as Cryptorchidism. True absence of a testis can be difficult to prove. Anorchia is true absence of both testes, and can only be determined by imaging or surgical studies.
synonym: "Absence of palpable testicules" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
