[Term]
id: HP:0010518
name: Thyroglossal cyst
def: "An abnormality of the thyroid gland owing to the presence of a fibrous cyst resulting from the persistence of the thyroglossal duct." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A developmental defect resulting in the presence of a thyroglossal cyst, a fibrous cyst that forms from a persistent thyroglossal duct. During the embryologic development of the thyroid gland, the precursor of the thyroid migrates from the base of the tongue inferiorly though the thyroglossal duct. This duct normally disappears following the development and migration of the thyroid gland, but if a portion of the duct remain it can form a thyroglossal cyst.
synonym: "Thyroglossal duct cyst" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011772 ! Abnormal thyroid morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2009-09-19T04:38:04Z" xsd:dateTime

