[Term]
id: HP:0010569
name: Elevated circulating 7-dehydrocholesterol concentration
def: "The concentration of 7-dehydrocholesterol in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Elevated 7-dehydrocholesterol levels occur as the result of a deficiency of the enzyme delta-7-sterol reductase, the penultimate enzyme of mammalian sterol biosynthesis that converts 7-dehydrocholesterol (7-DHC) to cholesterol. This enzyme removes the C(7-8) double bond introduced by the sterol delta8-delta7 isomerases. In addition, its role in drug-induced malformations is known: inhibitors of the last step of cholesterol biosynthesis such as AY9944 and BM15766 severely impair brain development. Homozygous mutations in the gene encoding for this enzyme are the molecular genetic cause of Smith-Lemli-Opitz Syndrome.
synonym: "Elevated 7-dehydrocholesterol concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated 7-dehydrocholesterol level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated 7-dehydrocholesterol level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated levels of cholesta-5,7-dien-3beta-ol" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased 7-dehydrocholesterol concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased 7-dehydrocholesterol level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased 7-dehydrocholesterol level in blood" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034934 ! Abnormal circulating 7-dehydrocholesterol concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2009-10-19T08:49:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010570
name: Low maternal circulating alpha-fetoprotein concentration
def: "An abnormally low concentration of serum alpha-fetoprotein as compared to normal values for gestational-age." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Reduced levels of alpha-fetoprotein can be seen in some fetal disorders such as Down syndrome.
synonym: "Low maternal serum alpha-fetoprotein" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0011436 ! Abnormal maternal serum screening
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2009-10-20T07:01:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010571
name: Elevated circulating phytanic acid concentration
def: "An abnormal elevation of phytanic acid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Phytanic acid (3,7,11,15-tetramethyl hexadecanoic acid) is a fatty acid that is derived from chlorophyll and present in the diet. The metabolism of phytanic acid involves alpha-oxidation in the peroxisome, which converts phytanic acid to pristanic acid. Peroxisomes involved in the catabolism of very long chain fatty acids and phytanic acid. Peroxisomal malfunctioning can lead to over-accumulation of very long chain fatty acids and phytanic acid, among other things.
synonym: "Elevated level of phytanic acid" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated levels of phytanic acid" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0010965 ! Abnormal circulating phytanic acid concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2009-10-20T07:19:29Z" xsd:dateTime

