[Term]
id: HP:0010587
name: Triangular epiphysis
def: "Longitudinal epiphyseal bracket or bracket epiphysis is an uncommon disorder of growth. Alternatively known as a delta phalanx, it is due to an anomalous secondary ossification center that extends longitudinally along the diaphysis. Although rare, longitudinal epiphyseal bracket most commonly manifests in the hands as clinodactyly and in the feet as hallux varus." [PMID:24432108]
synonym: "Longitudinal epiphyseal bracket" EXACT []
synonym: "Triangular end part of bone" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Triangular epiphyses" EXACT plural_form []
