[Term]
id: HP:0010762
name: Chordoma
def: "A chordoma is a tumor that arises from embryonic remnants of the notochord along the length of the neuraxis. Chordomas generally occur in the sacrum, intracranially at the clivus, or along the spinal axis." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The notochord is a mesodermal embryonic structure that defines the primitive axis of the embryo and which survives in the adult vertebral column as the intervertebral disks.
xref: NCIT:C2947
is_a: HP:0010622 ! Neoplasm of the skeletal system
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-06-25T09:00:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010763
name: Low insertion of columella
def: "Insertion of the posterior columella below the nasal base." [PMID:19152422]
comment: This feature is different from a convex Low hanging columella that has a normal insertion. It may be associated with a Short philtrum, but this should be assessed and coded separately. A low insertion is best appreciated when viewed from the side.
synonym: "Ala higher than columella" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Columella, low insertion" EXACT []
