property_value: terms:date "2010-07-05T11:13:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010815
name: Nevus sebaceous
def: "A congenital, hairless plaque consisting of overgrown epidermis, sebaceous glands, hair follicles, apocrine glands and connective tissue. They are a variant of epidermal naevi. Sebaceous naevi most often appear on the scalp, but they may also arise on the face, neck or forehead. At birth, a sevaceous nevus typically appears as a solitary, smooth, yellow-orange hairless patch. Sebaceous naevi become more pronounced around adolescence, often appearing bumpy, warty or scaly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Naevus sebaceous" EXACT []
synonym: "Organoid nevus" EXACT []
synonym: "Sebaceous mole" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Sebaceous naevus" EXACT []
synonym: "Sebaceous nevus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010816 ! Epidermal nevus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T12:07:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010816
name: Epidermal nevus
def: "Epidermal naevi are due to an overgrowth of the epidermis and may be present at birth (50%) or develop during childhood." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20542174]
comment: Epidermal nevus arises from a defect in the ectoderm and in general are due to an overgrowth of keratinocytes. Subclasses of epidermal nevus include Linear epidermal naevus, epidermolytic epidermal naevus, acantholytic epidermal naevus, linear porokeratosis, and systematized epidermal naevus. Several other conditions are also characterized by benign overgrowth of the epidermis and its appendages (organoid naevi), including inflammatory linear verrucous epidermal naevus, sebaceous naevus, sweat gland naevi, comedone naevus, and Becker naevus.
synonym: "Epidermal nevi" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0003764 ! Nevus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T12:12:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010817
name: Linear nevus sebaceous
def: "A type of nevus sebaceous with a linear form, raised borders and yellowish color." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0010815 ! Nevus sebaceous
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T12:17:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010818
name: Generalized tonic seizure
alt_id: HP:0002184
def: "A generalized tonic seizure is a type of generalized motor seizure characterized by bilateral limb stiffening or elevation, often with neck stiffening without a subsequent clonic phase. The tonic activity can be a sustained abnormal posture, either in extension or flexion, sometimes accompanied by tremor of the extremities." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:11580774, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: Characterized by a sudden increase in muscle tone whereby the body, arms, or legs make sudden stiffening movements and consciousness is usually preserved. Tonic seizures can occur during sleep. Tonic seizures usually affect both sides of the body, and cause a fall if the affected person was standing when the seizure started.
synonym: "Generalised hypertonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalised tonic seizure" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Generalised tonic seizures" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Generalized hypertonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalized tonic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Hypertonic seizures" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0032677 ! Generalized-onset motor seizure
is_a: HP:0032792 ! Tonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T03:03:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010819
name: Atonic seizure
alt_id: HP:0002124
def: "Atonic seizure is a type of motor seizure characterized by a sudden loss or diminution of muscle tone without apparent preceding myoclonic or tonic event lasting about 1 to 2 seconds, involving head, trunk, jaw, or limb musculature." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11580774]
comment: This term describes the initial semiology of the seizure without specifying whether the onset is focal or generalized. Thus it can be used for coding atonic seizures when the onset is not known.
synonym: "Astatic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Astatic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Atonic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Drop attacks" EXACT []
synonym: "Drop seizures" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Hypotonic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypotonic seizures" RELATED plural_form []
synonym: "Sudden loss of muscle tone" RELATED layperson []
is_a: HP:0020219 ! Motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T03:13:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010820
name: Focal emotional seizure with crying
def: "Focal emotional seizure with crying (dacrystic) is characterized by the presence of stereotyped crying, this may be accompanied by lacrimation, sad facial expression and sobbing. The subjective emotion of sadness may or may not be present." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:28276060, PMID:993803]
comment: Crying is a rare feature of an epileptic seizure, and is more commonly a feature of a non-epileptic seizure. The word dacrystic is derived from the Greek word dakryon (tear).
synonym: "Dacrystic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Dacrystic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
is_a: HP:0025613 ! Focal emotional seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T03:23:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010821
name: Focal emotional seizure with laughing
def: "Focal emotional seizure with laughing (gelastic) is characterized by bursts of laughter or giggling, usually without appropriate related emotion of happiness, and described as 'mirthless'." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: This seizure type is characteristic of seizures arising in the hypothalamus (see hypothalamic hamartoma), but can occur in seizures arising in the frontal or temporal lobes.
synonym: "Gelastic seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Gelastic seizures" EXACT plural_form []
is_a: HP:0025613 ! Focal emotional seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T03:27:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0010822
name: Scintillating scotoma
def: "A scintillating scotoma is a common visual aura that can precede a migraine, whereby a spot of flickering light near the center of the visual fields occurs. The spot prevents vision, and is thus termed scotoma. The scotoma can extend into one or more shimmering arcs of white or colored flashing lights." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0000575 ! Scotoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2010-07-10T03:35:29Z" xsd:dateTime

