[Term]
id: HP:0010934
name: Xanthinuria
def: "An increased concentration of xanthine in the urine." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:gcarletti]
comment: Xanthinuria is generally caused by a defect in the xanthine oxidase, an enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation of hypoxanthine to xanthine and can further catalyze the oxidation of xanthine to uric acid. The formation of xanthine stones in the urinary tract is the main evidence of this abnormality.
synonym: "Increased urinary xanthine" EXACT []
