[Term]
id: HP:0010979
name: Abnormal circulating lipoprotein cholesterol concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of lipoprotein cholesterol in the blood circulation." []
comment: Lipoproteins transport fats (lipids) in the blood circulation. Lipids are insoluble in water, meaning that they could not be transported in the blood circulation on their own. There are five major types of lipoproteins: (i) chylomicrons; VLDL (very low-density lipoprotein); (iii) IDL (intermediate-density lipoprotein); (iv) LDL (low-density lipoprotein); and (v) HDL (high-density lipoprotein). Clinical measures assess the amount of cholesterol carried by different lipoproteins. For instance, LDL-cholesterol (LDL-C) is the maount of cholesterol carried by LDL.
synonym: "Abnormal lipoprotein cholesterol level" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of the level of lipoprotein cholesterol" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003107 ! Abnormal circulating cholesterol concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2011-02-07T09:47:29Z" xsd:dateTime

