[Term]
id: HP:0011137
name: Non-pruritic urticaria
def: "Pale reddish slightly elevated papules and plaques of 0.5-3 cm in diameter and not accompanied by pruritus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Although the English-language names for uritcaria and non-pruritic urticaria are very similar these are treated as distinct lesions. Non-pruritic urticaria should not be considered to be a subclass of urticaria, because the latter is characterized by pruritus.
synonym: "Non-itchy hives" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
