[Term]
id: HP:0011138
name: Abnormal skin adnexa morphology
def: "An abnormality of the skin adnexa (skin appendages), which are specialized skin structures located within the dermis and focally within the subcutaneous fatty tissue, comprising three histologically distinct structures: (1) the pilosebaceous unit (hair follicle and sebaceous glands); (2) the eccrine sweat glands; and (3) the apocrine glands." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormal skin appendage" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Abnormality of skin adnexa morphology" EXACT []
