[Term]
id: HP:0011165
name: Focal sensory seizure with visual features
alt_id: HP:0007175
alt_id: HP:0025121
def: "A seizure characterized by elementary visual hallucinations such as flashing or flickering lights/colors, or other shapes, simple patterns, scotomata, or amaurosis as its first clinical manifestation." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jalbers]
comment: More complex visual hallucinations such as seeing formed images are considered a focal cognitive seizure. Focal sensory visual seizures arise in the occipital lobe. Note that there is a distinction between Visual aura and Simple partial occipital seizures. See HPO term HP:0025121 for comments.
synonym: "Focal visual seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial visual seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Simple partial occipital seizures" RELATED []
synonym: "Visual aura" EXACT []
synonym: "Visual auras" EXACT plural_form []
