[Term]
id: HP:0011219
name: Short face
def: "Facial height (length) is more than two standard deviations below the mean (objective); or an apparent decrease in the height (length) of the face (subjective)." [PMID:19125436]
comment: Objective measurement of face height is made with sliding calipers from the nasion, just above the depth of the nasal root to the gnathion, the inferior border of the mandible, both in the midline. Note that short face is distinct from wide face.
synonym: "Decreased height of face" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Decreased length of face" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Decreased vertical dimension of face" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Short face" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Short facies" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical deficiency of face" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical Facial Deficiency" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical facial insufficiency" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical hypoplasia of face" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical insufficiency of face" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Vertical shortening of face" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
is_a: HP:0000274 ! Small face
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-07T09:01:18Z" xsd:dateTime

