[Term]
id: HP:0011275
name: Recurrent mycobacterium avium complex infections
def: "Increased susceptibility to mycobacterial avium complex infections as manifested by recurrent episodes of mycobacterial infection." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) is a group of species including M. avium, M. avium paratuberculosis, and others. Disseminated MAC infections can be seen associated with HIV infection. Pulmonary disease and cervical adenitis are other sequellae of MAC infection.
is_a: HP:0011274 ! Recurrent mycobacterial infections
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-28T12:16:46Z" xsd:dateTime

