id: HP:0011396
name: Abnormality of the cochlear nerve
def: "Any anomaly of the cohclear nerve, which is the part of the vestibulocochlear nerve that is responsible for transmitting auditory signals from the inner ear to the cochlear nuclei within the brainstem and ultimately to the primary auditory cortex within the temporal lobe." [PMID:30726044]
