[Term]
id: HP:0011397
name: Abnormal spinal cord dorsal column morphology
def: "An abnormality of the dorsal columns, i.e., of the dorsal portion of the gray substance of the spinal cord. The dorsal column consists of the fasciculus gracilis and fasciculus cuneatus and itself is part of the dorsal funiculus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The dorsal column represents an ascending pathway mediating well-localized fine touch and conscious proprioception.
