[Term]
id: HP:0011529
name: Multiple congenital hypertrophy of retinal pigment epithelium
def: "Unilateral or bilateral small, well-demarcated pigmented lesions localized in the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE). Lesions are dark in the center, with a pale circumference and are mostly located in the periphery." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8727-6592]
comment: Bilateral multiple CHRPE is strongly associated with familial adenomatous polyposis coli.
synonym: "Multiple bilateral CHRPE" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Multiple bilateral congenital hypertrophy of retinal pigment epithelium" EXACT []
