[Term]
id: HP:0011530
name: Retinal hole
def: "A full-thickness defect in the retina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: A retinal hole can be asymptomatic or can lead to the sudden appearance of many floaters or flashes, blurry, or wavy vision, or of a a dark shadow or curtain in the peripheral visual field.
