[Term]
id: HP:0011579
name: Unbalanced atrioventricular canal defect
def: "Anatomic features of unbalanced atrioventricular septal defect (AVSD) include varying amounts of ventricular hypoplasia, as well as malalignment of the atrioventricular junction. In complete AVSD, the common AV valve can be situated either equally over the right and left ventricles (balanced) or unequally over the ventricles (unbalanced)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown, PMID:20837915]
