[Term]
id: HP:0011647
name: Postductal coarctation of the aorta
def: "Narrowing or constriction of the aorta localized distal to the ductus arteriosus, i.e., to the postductal region of aortic arch." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:DDD_dbrown]
comment: Blood flow to the aorta distal to the coarctation may be dependent on a patent ductus arteriosus, and hence closure of the ductus arteriosus can lead to serious ischemia of the affected tissues.
synonym: "Postductal aortic coarctation" EXACT []
