[Term]
id: HP:0011679
name: Tetralogy of Fallot with pulmonary stenosis
def: "The commonest form of tetralogy of Fallot characterized by pulmonary stenosis, overriding aorta, ventricular septum defect, and right ventricular hypertrophy, without pulmonary atresia, absent pulmonary valve, atrioventricular canal defect or absent subarterial conus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0001636 ! Tetralogy of Fallot
