[Term]
id: HP:0011770
name: Tertiary hyperparathyroidism
def: "A type of hyperparathyroidism that occurs following kidney transplantation, which is a treatment for secondary hyperparathyroidism. Although kidney transplantation leads to a normalization of serum calcium and parathyroid hormone in most patients. The state of persistent hypercalcemia and hyperparathyroidism is referred to as tertiary hyperparathyroidism." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0538-4547]
