[Term]
id: HP:0011961
name: Non-obstructive azoospermia
def: "Absence of any measurable level of sperm in his semen, resulting from a defect in the production of spermatozoa in the testes. This can be differentiated from obstructive azoospermia on the basis of testicular biopsy." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20514278]
