[Term]
id: HP:0011995
name: Atrial septal dilatation
def: "A bulging of the interatrial septum towards one side. In adults, atrial septal aneurysm can be defined as a protrusion of the aneurysm of >10 mm beyond the plane of the atrial septum as measured by transesophageal echocardiography." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:7758185]
comment: Atrial septal aneurysm formation may be secondary to raised interatrial pressure gradients, producing a bulging septal shift toward the low-pressure side. However, it has been also found in patients with normal atrial pressures, suggesting a primary (congenital) malformation.
synonym: "Atrial septal aneurysm" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0011994 ! Abnormal atrial septum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-19T11:35:07Z" xsd:dateTime

