[Term]
id: HP:0012034
name: Liposarcoma
def: "Malignant neoplasms which probably originate in primitive mesenchymal stem cell populations differentiating down a lipomatous pathway." [MPATH:418]
xref: MPATH:418 "Liposarcoma"
is_a: HP:0012031 ! Lipomatous tumor
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T01:40:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012035
name: Steatocystoma multiplex
def: "Multiple, localized or widespread, asymptomatic or inflammatory dermal cysts involving the pilosebaceous units. Lesions can appear anywhere on the body, but steatocystoma multiplex is more commonly involved with those areas of the skin with a high density of developed pilosebaceous units (e.g., the axilla, groin, neck, and proximal extremities)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20631281]
comment: Steatocystoma multiplex can present with localized, generalized, facial, acral, or suppurative involvement.
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T01:45:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012036
name: Sternocleidomastoid amyotrophy
def: "Wasting of the sternocleidomastoid muscle, the muscle in the anterior part of the neck that acts to flex and rotate the head." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0003202 ! Skeletal muscle atrophy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T01:51:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012037
name: Pectoralis amyotrophy
def: "Wasting of the pectoral muscles, i.e., of the pectoralis major and pectoralis minor. This finding is often manifested by prominent axillary creases or double axillary creases." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Wasting of pec muscles" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0003202 ! Skeletal muscle atrophy
is_a: HP:0011957 ! Abnormal pectoral muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T01:55:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012038
name: Corneal guttata
def: "Corneal guttata are droplet-like accumulations of non-banded collagen on the posterior surface of Descemet's membrane. The presence of focal thickenings of Descemet's membrane histologically named guttae. Cornea guttata can be easily diagnosed in vivo and ex vivo by means of specular microscopy as it gives dark areas where no endothelial cells are visible." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:10611102, PMID:11222329]
comment: Corneal guttata are often observed in elderly people and are known to be associated with Fuchs corneal endothelial dystrophy, and also with trauma, congenital glaucoma, and macular dystrophy.
synonym: "Corneal endothelial guttata" EXACT []
synonym: "Corneal guttae" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011490 ! Abnormal Descemet membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T02:06:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012039
name: Descemet Membrane Folds
def: "Presence of folds in the Descemet membrane, which is the basement membrane of the endothelial (inner) cell layer of the cornea. Descemet membrane folds are generally a manifestation of inflammation or edema of the cornea." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0011490 ! Abnormal Descemet membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T02:14:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012040
name: Corneal stromal edema
def: "Abnormal accumulation of fluid and swelling of the stroma of cornea." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Corneal stromal oedema" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0000969 ! Edema
is_a: HP:0011492 ! Abnormal corneal stroma morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-27T02:19:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012041
name: Decreased fertility in males
synonym: "Decreased fertility in males" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0000144 ! Decreased fertility
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-07-30T06:50:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012042
name: Aspirin-induced asthma
def: "A type of asthma in which aspirin and other nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) that inhibit cyclooxygen-ase 1 (COX-1) exacerbate bronchoconstriction." [PMID:12743549]
synonym: "Aspirin-induced asthma" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0002099 ! Asthma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T11:22:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012043
name: Pendular nystagmus
def: "Rhythmic, involuntary sinusoidal oscillations of one or both eyes. The waveform of pendular nystagmus may occur in any direction." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Nystagmus, continuous pendular" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Nystagmus, pendular" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0000639 ! Nystagmus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:04:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012044
name: Seesaw nystagmus
def: "Seesaw nystagmus is a type of pendular nystagmus where a half cycle consists of the elevation and intorsion of one eye, concurrently with the depression and extortion of the fellow eye. In the other half cycle, there is an inversion of the ocular movements." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Seesaw nystagmus can be a manifestation of lesions of the optic chiasma.
is_a: HP:0012043 ! Pendular nystagmus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:06:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012045
name: Retinal flecks
def: "Presence of multiple yellowish-white lesions of various size and configuration on the retina not related to vascular lesions." [PMID:7952338]
is_a: HP:0030506 ! Yellow/white retinal lesion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:17:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012046
name: Areflexia of upper limbs
def: "Inability to elicit tendon reflexes in the upper limbs." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0001284 ! Areflexia
is_a: HP:0002817 ! Abnormality of the upper limb
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:24:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012047
name: Hemeralopia
def: "A visual defect characterized by the inability to see as clearly in bright light as in dim light. The word hemeralopia literally means day blindness." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Day blindness" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
is_a: HP:0000504 ! Abnormality of vision
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:26:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012048
name: Oromandibular dystonia
alt_id: HP:0001494
def: "A kind of focal dystonia characterized by forceful contractions of the face, jaw, and/or tongue causing difficulty in opening and closing the mouth and often affecting chewing and speech." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Cranial dystonia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012179 ! Craniofacial dystonia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:29:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012049
name: Laryngeal dystonia
def: "A form of focal dystonia that affects the vocal cords, associated with involuntary contractions of the vocal cords causing interruptions of speech and affecting the voice quality and often leading to patterned, repeated breaks in speech." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Spasmodic dysphonia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001618 ! Dysphonia
is_a: HP:0004373 ! Focal dystonia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:34:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012050
name: Anasarca
def: "An extreme form of generalized edema with widespread and massive edema due to effusion of fluid into the extracellular space." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Extreme generalised oedema" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Extreme generalized edema" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0007430 ! Generalized edema
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:53:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012051
name: Reactive hypoglycemia
def: "Hypoglycermia following a meal (or more generally, after intake of glucose)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Reactive hypoglycemia may be the result of an exaggerated insulin response.
synonym: "Low blood sugar after a meal" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Postprandial hypoglycemia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001943 ! Hypoglycemia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T12:57:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012052
name: Decreased circulating calcitriol concentration
def: "The concentration of calcitriol in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Calcitriol is also known as 1,25-dihydroxycholecalciferol or 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3.
synonym: "Low serum 1,25-dihydroxycholecalciferol" EXACT []
synonym: "Low serum 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3" EXACT []
synonym: "Low serum calcitriol" EXACT []
