property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T01:04:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012054
name: Choroidal melanoma
def: "Malignant tumor of melanocytes of the choroid. The classic appearance of choroidal melanoma is a pigmented dome-shaped or collar button-shaped tumor with an associated exudative retinal detachment. Choroidal melanoma is usually pigmented, but can be variably pigmented and even amelanotic (non-pigmented)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22557869]
xref: NCIT:C3224
is_a: HP:0007716 ! Uveal melanoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T01:59:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012055
name: Ciliary body melanoma
def: "Malignant tumor of melanocytes of the ciliary body." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: NCIT:C3224
is_a: HP:0007716 ! Uveal melanoma
is_a: HP:0012776 ! Abnormal ciliary body morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:01:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012056
name: Cutaneous melanoma
def: "The presence of a melanoma of the skin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The phenotypic presentation of melanomas is often described using the ABCDE mnemomic: A) Asymmetry; B) Borders of the lesion are irregular; C) Color changes from one area of the lesion to another, with shades of tan, brown, or black, and sometimes white, red, or blue; D) Diameter of the lesionis usually larger than 6 mm; E) Evolution of the appearance of the lesion with time. These rules do not, however, apply to every melanoma.
xref: NCIT:C3224
is_a: HP:0002861 ! Melanoma
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:04:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012057
name: Superficial spreading melanoma
def: "A type of melanoma that is flat and irregular in shape and color, with different shades of black and brown." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012056 ! Cutaneous melanoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:07:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012058
name: Nodular melanoma
def: "A type of melanoma that starts as a raised area that is usually dark blackish-blue or bluish-red but may not have any color." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012056 ! Cutaneous melanoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:08:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012059
name: Lentigo maligna melanoma
def: "A subtype of melanoma in situ that typically develops on sun-damaged skin. The lesion is typically a large, irregularly pigmented macule that has developed from an ordinary lentigo (a small pigmented spot on the skin with a clearly-defined edge). Change to a malignant lentigo typically takes place over 20 years or more, and many patients accept the change as a consequence of aging." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012056 ! Cutaneous melanoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:16:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012060
name: Acral lentiginous melanoma
def: "A type of cutaneous melanoma localized to the palm, sole, or beneath the nail (subungual melanoma). Acral lentiginous melanoma starts as a slowly-enlarging flat patch of discolored skin and usually displays a size above 6 mm and often several centimeters or more in diameter upon diagnosis and variable pigmentation with a mixutre of colors including brown, and blue-grey, black and red. The surface of the lesion is initially smooth but later in the course may become thicker and irregular, and may ulcerate or bleed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012056 ! Cutaneous melanoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-01T02:17:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012061
name: Urinary excretion of sialylated oligosaccharides
def: "Excretion of oligosaccharides conjugated to sialic acid in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Increased urinary sialyloligosaccharides" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010471 ! Oligosacchariduria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-04T02:14:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012062
name: Bone cyst
alt_id: HP:0100696
def: "A fluid filled cavity that develops with a bone." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Many bone cysts are asymptomatic. However, larger cysts can make the bone more susceptible to fracture.
synonym: "Bone cyst" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Bone cysts" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0003330 ! Abnormal bone structure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-03T02:35:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012063
name: Aneurysmal bone cyst
def: "Radiographic features include a dilated, radiolucent lesion typically located eccentrically within the metaphyseal portion of the bone, with fluid levels visible on magnetic resonance imaging." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22474093, PMID:7863874]
is_a: HP:0012062 ! Bone cyst
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-03T02:35:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012064
name: Unicameral bone cyst
def: "A benign fluid filled simple cyst of bone filled with serous fluid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012062 ! Bone cyst
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-03T02:42:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012065
name: Multiple bony cystic lesions
def: "Presence of multiple cystic changes in multiple areas or multiple bones." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Multiple bony cystic lesions" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0012062 ! Bone cyst
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-03T02:45:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012066
name: Increased urinary disaccharide excretion
def: "Increased concentration of disaccharide in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Excess amount of disaccharides such as mannosyl-N-acetylglucosamine excreted in the urine.
is_a: HP:0010471 ! Oligosacchariduria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-04T02:54:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012067
name: Glycopeptiduria
def: "Increased excretion of glycopeptides in the urine. Glycopeptides are peptides with carbohydrate moieties covalently attached to the side chains of the amino acid residues." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This feature is often the result of a defect in glycosidase activate. Glycosidases catalyze the release of sugar moieties.
synonym: "High urine glycopeptide levels" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0033354 ! Abnormal urine metabolite level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-04T03:03:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012068
name: Aspartylglucosaminuria
def: "Excretion of excess amounts of aspartylglucosamine in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "High urine aspartylglucosamine levels" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0012067 ! Glycopeptiduria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2012-08-04T03:15:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012069
name: Keratan sulfate excretion in urine
def: "An increased concentration of keratan sulfate in the urine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Keratan sulfate is a a glycosaminoglycan.
synonym: "Keratan sulphate excretion in urine" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0008155 ! Mucopolysacchariduria
