[Term]
id: HP:0012130
name: Abnormal erythroid lineage cell morphology
def: "An anomaly of erythroid lineage cells, that is, of the erythropoietic cells in the lineage leading to and including erythrocytes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2945-4463]
comment: Proerythroblasts are the earliest recognizable erythroid precursors. They are followined during the process of hematopoiesis by basophilic erythroblasts, polychromatic (polychromatophilic) erythroblasts, orthochromatic erythroblasts (normoblasts), reticulocytes, and finally mature erythrocytes (red blood cells). This term encompasses structural anomalies of erythroblast precursors in the bone marrow.
synonym: "Abnormality of cells of the erythroid lineage" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0005561 ! Abnormal bone marrow cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2012-09-16T07:14:03Z" xsd:dateTime

