[Term]
id: HP:0012154
name: Anhedonia
def: "Decreased ability or inability to experience, feel, or anticipate pleasure from activities, experiences, or stimuli that are typically found pleasurable by the individual. This may involve diminished enjoyment of previously rewarding experiences (e.g., hobbies, social interactions, or sexual activity) or reduced pleasure in response to stimuli processed through the senses (e.g., music, food, or tactile contact). Anhedonia is a disruption in the capacity to derive emotional reward and is not due to primary sensory deficits or medical conditions (e.g., anosmia from viral illness). The phenomenon involves altered affective processing rather than impaired sensory perception." [PMID:3107136, PMID:32789515, PMID:33631251, PMID:37424409]
synonym: "Anhedonic" EXACT []
synonym: "Diminished capacity for joy" BROAD layperson []
synonym: "Diminished pleasure response" EXACT []
synonym: "Inability to experience pleasure" EXACT []
synonym: "Loss of ability to enjoy things" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Loss of enjoyment" BROAD []
synonym: "Loss of interest in pleasurable activities" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced pleasure response" BROAD []
is_a: HP:0031467 ! Dysregulated negative emotional state
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1111-7357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7954-5235
