[Term]
id: HP:0012196
name: Cheyne-Stokes respiration
def: "An abnormal pattern of respiration characterized by cycles of respiration that are increasingly deeper then shallower with possible periods of apnea. Affected patients may display a 10 to 20 second episode of hypoventilation or apnea, followed by respiration of increased depth and frequency over the course of about one minute. The cycle repeats every 45 seconds to 3 minutes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Cheyne-Stokes breathing" EXACT []
synonym: "Periodic respiration" EXACT []
