[Term]
id: HP:0012367
name: Supernumerary fontanelle
def: "An extra soft spot (fontanelle) on an infant's skull beyond the standard six normal fontanelles." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:31194354]
comment: Fontanelles, often referred to as "soft spots," are one of the most prominent anatomical features of the newborn's skull. Six fontanelles are present during infancy, with the most notable being the anterior and posterior fontanelles. The typical fontanelles are the anterior, posterior, mastoid, sphenoid, and third fontanelles. Extra fontanelles include glabellar, metopic, sagittal (parietal) and cerebellar fontanelles.
synonym: "Extra fontanelle" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011328 ! Abnormal fontanelle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-10-13T12:27:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012368
name: Flat face
def: "Absence of concavity or convexity of the face when viewed in profile." [PMID:19125436]
comment: A useful guide is to imagine that a line connecting the glabella to the anterior most part of the mandible touches the top of the philtrum where it meets the base of the columella. The glabella is the most prominent point on the frontal bone above the root of the nose. If the superior philtrum is anterior to this line the face is convex, if the superior philtrum is posterior to this line the face is concave.
synonym: "Flat face" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Flat facial profile" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Flat facial shape" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Flat facies" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
is_a: HP:0001999 ! Abnormal facial shape
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-10-13T01:49:13Z" xsd:dateTime

