[Term]
id: HP:0012407
name: Scissor gait
def: "A type of spastic paraparetic gait in which the muscle tone in the adductors is marked. It is characterized by hypertonia and flexion in the legs, hips and pelvis accompanied by extreme adduction leading to the knees and thighs hitting, or sometimes even crossing, in a scissors-like movement. The opposing muscles (abductors) become comparatively weak from lack of use." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Scissor gait is a form of gait abnormality primarily associated with spastic cerebral palsy.
synonym: "Scissor gait" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Scissor walk" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Scissoring gait" EXACT []
synonym: "Scissoring of the lower extremities" EXACT []
synonym: "Scissoring of the lower limbs" EXACT []
synonym: "Scissors gait" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0031958 ! Spastic paraparetic gait
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-11-09T04:15:36Z" xsd:dateTime

