property_value: terms:date "2013-11-10T05:07:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012419
name: Hyperoxemia
def: "An abnormally high level of blood oxygen." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Note that hyperoxemia is defined as a condition where arterial oxygen tension is above normal (80-100mmHg). Hyperoxia is defined as increased oxygen tension at the tissue level. Hyperoxia is not measured directly by a standard laboratory value.
is_a: HP:0500165 ! Abnormal blood oxygen level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
