def: "Reduced ability to flex the femur, that is, to pull the knee upward." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
comment: Hip flexion is mediated by multiple muscles including the iliopsoas, the rectus femoris, the sartorius, and several muscles from the medial compartment of thigh.
is_a: HP:0003749 ! Pelvic girdle muscle weakness
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-08T09:14:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012516
name: Tetralogy of Fallot with pulmonary atresia
def: "An extreme form of tetralogy of Fallot characterized by absence of flow from the right ventricle to the pulmonary arteries." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, PMID:22368654]
comment: Tetralogy of Fallot with Pulmonary Atresia (TOF/PA) is a complex lesion with many different anatomic variants. The primary source of variability in this lesion is in the anatomy of the pulmonary arteries, with the spectrum ranging from well-formed, confluent pulmonary artery branches to completely absent native pulmonary arteries and major aorto-pulmonary collaterals (MAPCA's) providing all the pulmonary blood flow. The majority of cases fall somewhere in between these two ends of the spectrum, with the total pulmonary blood flow provided by a combination of diminutive native pulmonary arteries and multiple MAPCA.
is_a: HP:0001636 ! Tetralogy of Fallot
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-08T09:44:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012517
name: Reduced circulating catalase activity
def: "Activity or concentration of catalase in the blood circulation below the lower limit of normal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Catalase catalyzes the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide to water and oxygen.
synonym: "Reduced catalase level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-09T06:49:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012518
name: Abnormal circle of Willis morphology
def: "An anomaly of the circle of Willis, also known as the cerebral arterial circle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The circle of Willis is a circulatory anastomosis in the brain comprised of the anterior cerebral arteries, the anterior communicating artery, the internal carotid arteries, the posterior cerebral arteries, and the posterior communicating arteries.
synonym: "Abnormality of the cerebral arterial circle" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
is_a: HP:0009145 ! Abnormal cerebral artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-09T07:03:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012519
name: Hypoplastic posterior communicating artery
def: "A developmental anomnaly characterized by underdevelopment of the posterior communicating artery." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
comment: The posterior communicating arteries connect the internal carotid artery just proximal to its bifurcation into the anterior cerebral artery and middle cerebral artery with the posterior cerebral artery. The posterior communicating artery is part of the circle of Willis.
synonym: "Hypoplastic posterior communicating arteries" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0031772 ! Abnormal posterior circulating artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-09T07:06:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012520
name: Dilation of Virchow-Robin spaces
def: "Increased dimensions of the Virchow-Robin spaces (also known as perivascular spaces), which surround the walls of vessels as they course from the subarachnoid space through the brain parenchyma. Perivascular spaces are commonly microscopic, and not visible on conventional neuroimaging. This term refers to an increase of size of these spaces such that they are visible on neuroimaging (usually magnetic resonance imaging). The dilatations are regular cavities that always contain a patent artery." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, PMID:17620468, PMID:23867200, PMID:25564639]
comment: Virchow-Robin spaces are commonly seen at magnetic resonance imaging. These perivascular spaces as fluid-filled spaces that follow the typical course of a vessel as it goes through gray or white matter. The spaces have signal intensity similar to that of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) on all magnetic resonance sequences.
synonym: "Dilated cerebral perivascular spaces" RELATED []
synonym: "Dilated Virchow-Robin spaces" EXACT []
synonym: "Perivascular spaces" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100659 ! Abnormal cerebral vascular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-09T07:17:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012521
name: Optic nerve aplasia
def: "Congenital absence of the optic nerve." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Absent optic nerve" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Aplastic optic nerve" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008058 ! Aplasia/Hypoplasia of the optic nerve
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-12T02:15:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012522
name: Spider hemangioma
def: "A form of telangiectasis characterized by a central elevated red dot the size of a pinhead, representing an arteriole, with numerous small blood vessels that radiate out thereby resembling the legs of a spider. Characteristically, compression of the central arteriole causes the entire lesion to blanch, and the lesion quickly refills once the compression is released." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22356347]
comment: Spider hemangiomas are up to a few centimeters in diameter.
is_a: HP:0100585 ! Telangiectasia of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2013-12-14T08:31:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012523
name: Oral aversion
def: "Reluctance or refusal of a child to be breastfed or eat, manifested as gagging, vomiting, turning head away from food, or avoidance of sensation in or around the mouth (i.e. toothbrushing or face-washing)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
