[Term]
id: HP:0012663
name: Mildly reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
def: "A small reduction in the fraction of blood pumped from the left ventricle with each cardiac cycle. The normal range in adults is at least 50 percent, and a mild reduction is defined as 40-49 percent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16376782, PMID:27206819]
synonym: "Mildly reduced ejection fraction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012664 ! Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:06:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012664
name: Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
def: "A diminution of the volumetric fraction of blood pumped out of the ventricle with each cardiac cycle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The normal range is at least 55 percent.
synonym: "Reduced ejection fraction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025169 ! Left ventricular systolic dysfunction
is_a: HP:0034314 ! Abnormal left ventricular ejection fraction
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:03:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012665
name: Moderately reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
def: "A medium reduction in the fraction of blood pumped from the left ventricle with each cardiac cycle, defined as a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30-39 percent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16376782, PMID:27206819, PMID:29083812]
comment: The normal range in adults is over 50 percent, and a moderate reduction can be defined as 30-39 percent.
synonym: "Moderately reduced ejection fraction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012664 ! Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:08:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012666
name: Severely reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
def: "A large reduction in the fraction of blood pumped from the left ventricle with each cardiac cycle. The normal range in adults is at over 50 percent, and a severe reduction is defined as less than 30 percent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16376782, PMID:27206819, PMID:29083812]
synonym: "Severely reduced ejection fraction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012664 ! Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:09:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012667
name: Regional left ventricular wall motion abnormality
def: "An abnormal motion of a segment of the left ventricle during the cardiac cycle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: This feature can be appreciated using color kinesis, which tracks the motion of the endocardium in real time throughout systole and results in color-encoded images reflecting the magnitude and timing of endocardial motion.
is_a: HP:0005162 ! Abnormal left ventricular function
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:12:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012668
name: Vasovagal syncope
def: "A vasovagal episode or vasovagal syncope is the most common form of reflex syncope. Reflex syncope is a general term used to describe types of syncope resulting from a failure in autoregulation of blood pressure, and ultimately, in cerebral perfusion pressure resulting in transient loss of consciousness. The mechanisms responsible for this are complex and involve both depression of cardiac output as well as a decrease in vascular tone." [PMID:29262088]
synonym: "Neurocardiogenic syncope" EXACT []
synonym: "Reflex syncope" EXACT []
synonym: "Situational syncope" EXACT []
synonym: "Vasovagal episode" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001279 ! Syncope
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:33:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012669
name: Carotid sinus syncope
def: "An exaggerated response to carotid sinus baroreceptor stimulation resulting in syncope from transient diminished cerebral perfusion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Carotid sinus syncope cam be elicited mechanical manipulation of the carotid sinuses (eg, taking pulses in the neck, shaving).
is_a: HP:0001279 ! Syncope
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:39:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012670
name: Orthostatic syncope
def: "Syncope following a quick change in position from lying down to standing." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0001279 ! Syncope
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-15T01:41:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012671
name: Abulia
def: "Abulia is characterized by difficulty in initiating and sustaining spontaneous movements; the person often appears frozen but will move hesitantly on request. There are frequently substantial reductions in emotional responsiveness, spontaneous speech, and social interaction. The individual appears to be content to remain still and inactive with minimal movement, but moves or reacts hesitantly in response to interactions." []
comment: Abulia is less severe than kinetic mutism and more severe than apathy.
synonym: "Aboulia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000745 ! Abnormal diminished volition
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1111-7357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7954-5235
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2897-0458
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4298-5074
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4618-6544
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-27T10:48:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012672
name: Akinetic mutism
def: "The combined absence of spontaneous movement (akinesia) and speech (mutism). There may be eye movements consistent with visual tracking and the person may remember the events occurring at the time of the experience of stupor." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Akinetic mutism is essentially characterized by a total absence of spontaneous behavior and speech occurring in the presence of preserved visual tracking.
synonym: "Stuporous mutism" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000745 ! Abnormal diminished volition
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-27T10:50:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012673
name: Aplasia of the upper vagina
def: "A failure to develop of the upper vagina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The female reproductive tract primarily develops from the Mullerian ducts (MD), which form as an invagination of the coelomic epithelium and further develop into the upper two-thirds of the vagina, the uterus and the Fallopian tubes. Complete aplasia of the uterus, cervix, and upper vagina is termed Mullerian aplasia. This term refers to the aplasia of the upper roughly two thirds of the vagina that is characteristic of Mullerian aplasia.
synonym: "Absent upper vagina" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0003250 ! Aplasia of the vagina
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-02-27T11:00:26Z" xsd:dateTime

