[Term]
id: HP:0012683
name: Pineal cyst
def: "A glial uniloculated or multiloculated fluid-filled sac that either reside within or completely replace the pineal gland." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21801982]
comment: Pineal cysts are benign and often asymptomatic lesions. They are typically visualized by computed tomography or magnetic resonance imaging.
