[Term]
id: HP:0012790
name: Abnormal intramembranous ossification
def: "An anomaly in the process of intramembranous ossification by which flat bones (cranial bones of the skull, i.e., the frontal, parietal, occipital, and temporal bones, and the clavicles) are formed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
