[Term]
id: HP:0012793
name: Kinked brainstem
def: "A kinked appearance of the brainstem, i.e., an exaggerated flexure." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16301726]
comment: Kinked brainstem is an indicator of severe neurodysgenesis arising early in gestation. This sign can be appreciated in prenatal magnetic resonance imaging.
synonym: "Kinked brain stem" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002363 ! Abnormal brainstem morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-04-25T02:51:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012794
name: Periventricular white matter hypodensities
def: "Multiple areas of darker than expected signal on magnetic resonance imaging emanating from the cerebral white matter that surrounds the cerebral ventricles." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16239634]
comment: See also definition for "Deep white matter hypodensities". These two entities are in contra-distinction to each other.
synonym: "Periventricular cerebral white matter hypodensities" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0007103 ! Hypointensity of cerebral white matter on MRI
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-04-25T03:00:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012795
name: Abnormal optic disc morphology
def: "A morphological abnormality of the optic disc, i.e., of the portion of the optic nerve clinically visible on fundoscopic examination." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The term 'optic disc' is frequently used to describe the portion of the optic nerve clinically visible on fundoscopic examination.
is_a: HP:0000587 ! Abnormal optic nerve morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-05-24T04:37:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012796
name: Increased cup-to-disc ratio
def: "An elevation in the ratio of the diameter of the cup of the optic disc to the total diameter of the disk. The optic disc has an orange-pink rim with a pale center (the cup) that does not contain neuroretinal tissue. An increase in this ratio therefore may indicate a decrease in the quantity of healthy neuroretinal cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23557744]
comment: A cup to disk ratio of 0.3 is generally considered normal. Note that the ratio is measured in the vertical orientation unless otherwise specified.
synonym: "Elevated cup to disc ratio" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Elevated cup to disk ratio" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cup disc ratio" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Increased cup disk ratio" EXACT []
synonym: "Optic cupping" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012795 ! Abnormal optic disc morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2014-05-24T04:43:52Z" xsd:dateTime

