property_value: terms:date "2014-05-25T10:35:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012800
name: Accessory cranial suture
def: "A cranial suture that is in addition to canonical membrane-covered openings in the incompletely ossified skull of the fetus or newborn infant." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20496093]
comment: The parietal and occipital bones in particular are common regions for accessory sutures because of their multiple ossification centers. Accessory sutures can be explained on the basis of incomplete union of the two separate ossification centers. Accessory sutures usually will show a zigzag pattern with interdigitations and sclerotic borders similar to major calvarial sutures.
synonym: "Extra cranial suture" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Supernumary cranial suture" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
is_a: HP:0011329 ! Abnormality of cranial sutures
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2014-05-25T10:54:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012801
name: Narrow jaw
def: "Bigonial distance (lower facial width) more than 2 standard deviations below the mean (objective); or an apparently decreased width of the lower jaw (mandible) when viewed from the front (subjective)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19125436]
comment: The width of the jaw is measured from the right gonion to the left gonion using spreading calipers. The gonion is the point at the angle of the bony mandible where the ramus changes direction to become the body of the mandible. It faces inferiorly and medially and is best found by placing a finger over the outward facing angle and rolling the finger downwards and inwards.
synonym: "Narrow jaw" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Narrow lower face" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Narrow lower jaw" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Narrow mandible" EXACT []
synonym: "Thin lower face" RELATED layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
synonym: "Thin lower jaw" RELATED layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5889-4463]
is_a: HP:0000277 ! Abnormal mandible morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2014-05-25T02:37:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0012802
name: Broad jaw
def: "Bigonial distance (lower facial width) more than 2 SD above the mean (objective); or an apparently increased width of the lower jaw (mandible) when viewed from the front (subjective)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19125436]
comment: The lower jaw is measured from the right gonion to the left gonion using spreading calipers. The gonion is the point at the angle of the bony mandible where the ramus changes direction to become the body of the mandible. It faces inferiorly and medially and is best found by placing a finger over the outward facing angle and rolling the finger downwards and inwards. When a broad jaw is accompanied by a broad upper face the term Square face is used.
synonym: "Broad jaw" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Broad lower face" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Broad mandible" EXACT []
synonym: "Wide jaw" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Wide mandible" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000277 ! Abnormal mandible morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6996-5279
property_value: terms:date "2014-05-25T02:41:43Z" xsd:dateTime

