[Term]
id: HP:0012847
name: Epilepsia partialis continua
def: "Epilepsia partialis continua (also called Kojevnikov's or Kozhevnikov's epilepsia) is a type of focal motor status epilepticus characterized by repeated stereotyped simple motor manifestations such as jerks, typically of a limb or the face, recurring every few seconds or minutes for extended periods (days or years)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: The focal motor features may exhibit a Jacksonian march and a post-ictal (Todd's) paresis may be seen in the affected body part.
synonym: "Epilepsia partialis continua of Kojevnikov" EXACT []
synonym: "Kojevnikov's epilepsia" EXACT []
synonym: "Kozhevnikov's epilepsia" EXACT []
