[Term]
id: HP:0020006
name: Ciliary body coloboma
def: "A coloboma of the ciliary body." []
is_a: HP:0000589 ! Coloboma

[Term]
id: HP:0020007
name: Abnormal affect regulation
def: "A disturbance in the processes by which emotional responses are initiated, modulated, sustained, or terminated in a contextually appropriate manner. Abnormal affect regulation involves maladaptive patterns in the generation, intensity, or control of affective experience and expression, leading to inconsistent, excessive, or insufficient modulation of emotion relative to situational demands." [PMID:23216067, PMID:37925091]
comment: This category encompasses enduring tendencies or dynamic features that influence emotional reactivity and control - such as emotional hypersensitivity, emotional lability, emotional insecurity, and low frustration tolerance. These features represent alterations in the mechanisms governing affective modulation rather than discrete affective states themselves.
is_a: HP:0025766 ! Abnormal affect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-17T15:13:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020008
name: History of disease onset in winter
def: "The initial manifestation of a disease or symptom occurring during the winter season." []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:12:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020009
name: History of disease onset in summer
def: "The initial manifestation of a disease or symptom occurring during the summer season." []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:14:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020010
name: Cutaneous lesion morphology
def: "A description of structural or physical characteristics of a skin lesion, describing how the lesion appears or is composed." []
is_a: HP:0012823 ! Clinical modifier
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:25:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020011
name: Bleeding into skin lesions
def: "Presence of bleeding within (pre-existing) cutaneous lesions such as blisters or vesicles, resulting in blood-filled lesions." []
synonym: "Hemorrhagic nature to skin lesions" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020010 ! Cutaneous lesion morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:27:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020012
name: Crusted skin lesions
def: "Lesions covered by a hardened layer of dried exudate, blood, or serum." []
is_a: HP:0020010 ! Cutaneous lesion morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:28:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020013
name: Slough
def: "Slough is a type of necrotic skin lesion that is characterized as being yellow, tan, green or brown in color and may be moist, loose and stringy in appearance." [PMID:16455730]
is_a: HP:0033126 ! Cutaneous necrosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:34:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020014
name: Local paresthesia at bite site
def: "Abnormal tingling, burning, or itching sensation localized to the site of an animal bite, typically occurring after the wound has healed." [PMID:15043965, PMID:29188797]
comment: This phenomenon may represent an early neuropathic involvement in rabies infection and is distinct from immediate wound pain or inflammatory itch.
is_a: HP:0003401 ! Paresthesia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T07:52:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020015
name: Amyloid deposition by anatomical site
def: "Amyloid deposition categorized according to the anatomical site of deposition." []
is_a: HP:0011034 ! Amyloid deposition
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:27:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020016
name: Amyloid deposition by type of amyloid
def: "Amyloid deposition categorized according to the category of pathological amyloid fiber being deposited." []
is_a: HP:0011034 ! Amyloid deposition
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:28:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020017
name: Transthyretin amyloid deposition
def: "Deposition of misfolded transthyretin (TTR) protein in tissue." [PMID:34662045]
comment: Transthyretin (previously known as prealbumin) is a normal circulating protein that functions as a carrier protein for retinol (vitamin A) and thyroxine. Usually, it circulates in a tetrameric form composed of 4 beta-sheet-rich monomers. However, structural changes in the TTR protein can cause it to misfold and lose the tetrameric form, causing it to aggregate and deposit in various tissues.
is_a: HP:0020016 ! Amyloid deposition by type of amyloid
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:29:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020018
name: Cerebral transthyretin amyloid deposition
def: "Accumulation of misfolded transthyretin protein in brain tissue." [PMID:36198883]
comment: Leptomeninges and subarachnoid vessels affected earlier, followed by perforating cortical vessels and subpial deposition, and finally subependymal deposition and involvement of basal ganglia vessels near the ependymal lining. Interestingly, brainstem and spinal cord show early severe involvement, with amyloid subpial deposition already seen in the initial stages. Despite massive CNS amyloid deposition, no parenchymal deposition is found in the cortex or white matter.
is_a: HP:0020017 ! Transthyretin amyloid deposition
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:40:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020019
name: Abnormal CSF 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid concentration
def: "The concentration of 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) is above or below the limits of normal." []
is_a: HP:0500183 ! Abnormal CSF carboxylic acid concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:48:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020020
name: Decreased CSF 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid concentration
def: "The concentration of 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) is below the lower limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0020019 ! Abnormal CSF 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T08:49:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020021
name: Hip external rotation contracture
def: "A condition where the hip joint is limited in its range of motion due to the shortening of muscles that externally rotate the hip, causing the leg and foot to point outward when standing or walking. The knee is turned past neutral in the direction moving away from the midline, where the neutral position for the hip is with knee pointing directly anteriorly." [PMID:40176701]
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:00:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020022
name: Hip abduction contracture
def: "Abduction contracture of the hip is characterized by the limitation of active and/or passive adduction of the hip joint in the coronal plane; a chronic reduction in the ability to move the proximal segment of the lower extremity actively or passively medially towards the body midline past the sagittal plane of the body." []
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:16:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020023
name: Hip adduction contracture
def: "Inability of hip to bring from medial side to neutral position, where the neutral position for the hip is with the thigh segment in line with the anatomic plane of the pelvis, both in the coronal and sagittal planes." [PMID:40176701]
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:17:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020024
name: Hip extension contracture
def: "Inability to flex the hip past the extension range from the neutral position, where the neutral position for the hip is with the hip and thigh segment in line in the same coronal plane as the pelvis." [PMID:40176701]
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:18:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020025
name: Hip flexion contracture
def: "The inability to bring a flexed hip to neutral in the sagittal plane, where the neutral position for the hip is with the thigh segment in line with the anatomic plane of the pelvis, both in the coronal and sagittal planes." [PMID:40176701]
is_a: HP:0003273 ! Hip contracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:19:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020026
name: Positive Coombs test
def: "A positive (abnormal) result of the direct antiglobulin test (DAT; sometimes referred to as the Coombs test). The test is a method of demonstrating the presence of antibody or complement bound to red blood cell (RBC) membranes by the use of anti-human globulin to form a visible agglutination reaction. The DAT tests for antibodies or complement bound directly to erythrocytes, indicating in vivo sensitization." []
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:34:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020027
name: Direct antiglobulin test positive for IgG
def: "Demonstration of the presence of IgG antibodies bound to red blood cell (RBC) membranes by the use of anti-human globulin to form a visible agglutination reaction." []
synonym: "IgG+ Coombs test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020026 ! Positive Coombs test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:36:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020028
name: Direct antiglobulin test positive for IgM
def: "Demonstration of the presence of IgM antibodies bound to red blood cell (RBC) membranes by the use of anti-human globulin to form a visible agglutination reaction." []
comment: Cold agglutinin disease is a form of autoimmune hemolytic anemia in which cold agglutinins (IgM autoantibodies against red blood cell [RBC] antigens that bind at cold temperatures) can cause clinical symptoms related to RBC agglutination in cooler parts of the body and hemolytic anemia.
synonym: "IgM+ Coombs test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020026 ! Positive Coombs test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T09:37:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020029
name: Abnormal spinal cord white matter morphology
def: "Any structural abnormality affecting the white matter of the spinal cord, including sensory tracts (dorsal columns) and motor tracts (corticospinal tracts). Abnormalities may involve myelin, axons, or tract organization and can result in sensory, motor, or autonomic deficits." []
is_a: HP:0002143 ! Abnormal spinal cord morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T10:02:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020030
name: Abnormal spinal cord lateral corticospinal tract morphology
def: "Any structural abnormality affecting the lateral corticospinal tracts of the spinal cord, which may involve axonal loss, demyelination, or tract degeneration, and can result in motor deficits such as weakness, spasticity, or impaired voluntary movement." []
is_a: HP:0020029 ! Abnormal spinal cord white matter morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T10:05:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020031
name: Direct antiglobulin test positive for C3d
def: "Demonstration of the presence of C3d complement fragments bound to red blood cell (RBC) membranes using anti-human globulin (Coombs reagent), which produces a visible agglutination reaction." []
is_a: HP:0020026 ! Positive Coombs test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T10:09:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020032
name: Hyperreflective retinal dots on OCT
def: "Abnormal hyperreflective dots (HRDs) detected in Optical coherence tomography (OCT) scans. The HRDs are scattered, punctiform, small in size, mainly located in the outer retinal layers and/or around pockets of fluid accumulation and are typically not confluent." [PMID:25926902]
synonym: "Hyperreflective retinal foci on OCT" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030612 ! Abnormal retinal morphology on macular OCT
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T10:13:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020033
name: Irregularity of the retinal pigment epithelium layer on OCT
def: "Lack of uniformity in the morphology of the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) layer observed on optical coherence tomography (OCT) imaging. The RPE lies between the neurosensory retina (photoreceptors) and Bruch membrane/choroid, and normally appears as a thin, hyperreflective (bright) band on OCT imaging. This term comprises irregularities which may manifest as thickening, thinning, undulations, or loss of normal reflectivity, potentially affecting retinal structure or function." [PMID:19797228]
is_a: HP:0030603 ! Abnormal optical coherence tomography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T10:37:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020034
name: Diffuse
def: "A spatial pattern that is spread out, i.e., not localized." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern
property_value: terms:date "2016-04-15T15:16:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020035
name: Lower limb dysmetria
def: "A lack of coordination of leg movement manifested by undershoot or overshoot of the intended position of the leg." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2353-596X, PMID:25573808]
is_a: HP:0002406 ! Limb dysmetria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-10-13T12:24:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020036
name: Upper limb dysmetria
def: "A lack of coordination of arm movement manifested by undershoot or overshoot of the intended position of the arm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2353-596X, PMID:20301629]
is_a: HP:0002406 ! Limb dysmetria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-10-13T12:28:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020037
name: Astasia
def: "A postural abnormality characterized by the inability to stand without external support despite having sufficient muscle strength." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2353-596X, PMID:27821973]
is_a: HP:0100022 ! Abnormality of movement
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-10-13T12:38:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020038
name: Vertebrobasilar dolichoectasia
def: "Elongation, dilatation, and/or tortuosity of the vertebrobasilar segment. The definition of VBD includes: (i) diameter of basilar or vertebral artery over 4.5 mm; or (ii) deviation of any portion more than 10 mm from the shortest expected course; and (iii) length of basilar artery over 29.5 mm or length of intracranial vertebral artery over 23.5 mm." [PMID:24765483]
comment: The basilar artery arises from the confluence of the two vertebral arteries.
is_a: HP:0030321 ! Abnormal vertebral artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-10-13T12:54:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020039
name: Retinal thickening on OCT
def: "Anteroposterior thickness of the retina above the upper limit of normal. This phenotype can be appreciated by retinal optical coherence tomography (OCT)." []
is_a: HP:0020040 ! Abnormal anteroposterior retina thickness on OCT
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:10:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020040
name: Abnormal anteroposterior retina thickness on OCT
def: "Anteroposterior thickness of the retina outside the limits of normal. This phenotype can be appreciated by retinal optical coherence tomography (OCT)." []
is_a: HP:0030603 ! Abnormal optical coherence tomography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:11:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020041
name: Double elevator palsy
def: "A type of incomitant strabismus in which both elevator muscles (i.e., the inferior oblique and superior rectus muscles) of the same eye are weak leading to restricted elevation and hypotropia." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123, PMID:23479532]
is_a: HP:0025068 ! Incomitant strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:09:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020042
name: Double depressor palsy
def: "An ocular movement abnormality characterized by simultaneous weakness of the inferior rectus muscle and superior oblique muscle of the same eye." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0025068 ! Incomitant strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:12:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020043
name: Vertical incomitant strabismus
def: "A type of incomitant strabismus in which the angle of deviation varies as the patient's gaze shifts upwards and/or downwards." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0025068 ! Incomitant strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:14:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020044
name: Horizontal incomitant strabismus
comment: A type of incomitant strabismus in which the angle of deviation varies as the patient's gaze shifts horizontally.
is_a: HP:0025068 ! Incomitant strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:14:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020045
name: Esodeviation
def: "A manifest or latent ocular deviation in which one or both eyes tends to deviate nasally." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Convergent squint" EXACT []
synonym: "Convergent strabismus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000486 ! Strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:20:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020046
name: Accommodative esotropia
def: "A form of esotropia (convergent deviation of the eyes) associated with activation of the accommodative reflex." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: Accommodative esotropia refers to strabismus (cross of the eyes) that occurs with focusing efforts of the eyes.
is_a: HP:0000565 ! Esotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-20T17:25:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020047
name: Abnormal myeloid cell morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of a cell of the monocyte, granulocyte, mast cell, megakaryocyte, or erythroid lineage." []
is_a: HP:0005561 ! Abnormal bone marrow cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-22T14:32:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020048
name: Reduced bone-marrow pro-B cell count
def: "A reduction in the numbers of pro-B cells (defined by coexpression of CD34 and CD19). Earlier B-cell precursors are defined by expressing surface CD34 and cytoplasmic TdT in the absence of CD19." []
is_a: HP:0005561 ! Abnormal bone marrow cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-22T14:57:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020049
name: Exodeviation
def: "A manifest or latent ocular deviation in which one or both eyes tends to deviate temporally." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Divergent strabismus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000486 ! Strabismus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-22T15:01:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020050
name: Anti-granulocyte-macrophage colony stimulating factor antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the serum that react against granulocyte-macrophage colony stimulating factor." [PMID:23509356]
comment: Anti-granulocyte macrophage-colony stimulating factor (GM-CSF) autoantibodies have been shown to cause acquired pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP)(1, 2), a chronic lung disease characterized by abnormalities of surfactant metabolism.
synonym: "Anti-GM-CSF antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-22T15:05:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020051
name: Abnormal seminiferous tubule morphology
def: "Any anomaly in the structure or density (count of tubules per volume) of the seminiferous tubules, i.e., the coiled structures within the testis that contain Sertoli cells, which support and nurture germ cells as they develop into mature spermatozoa." []
is_a: HP:0000035 ! Abnormal testis morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:19:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020052
name: Necrotizing lymph node granuloma
def: "A granuloma located within a lymph node that is associated with necrosis. Usually, the necrosis is surrounded by collections of histiocytes. A granuloma is a focal aggregate of immune cells that forms in response to a persistent inflammatory stimulus. It characteristically demonstrates the compact organization of mature macrophages, which may or may not be associated with other inflammatory cell types." []
is_a: HP:0020229 ! Abnormal lymph-node biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:24:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020053
name: Abnormal marker expression
def: "Aberrant marker expression is a phenomenon of abnormal gain or loss of lineage specific or associated antigens. It involves changes in the presence, absence, quantity, or localization of molecular or immunohistochemical markers." []
comment: In cancer pathology, abnormal marker expression is generally measured in tumor cells compared to normal cells of the same tissue type.
is_a: HP:0020228 ! Biospecimen phenotypic feature
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:35:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020054
name: Abnormal erythrocyte physiology
def: "Any functional abnormality of erythrocytes (red-blood cells)." []
is_a: HP:0001871 ! Abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-09-28T23:39:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020055
name: Diminished MLH1 expression
def: "Immunohistochemistry (IHC) demonstrating loss of expression of the mismatch repair gene product mutL homolog 1 (MLH1)." []
comment: This abnormality may be observed in a tumor of the Lynch syndrome spectrum (e.g., colorectal, endometrial, ovarian, stomach, small bowel, urinary tract, biliary tract, prostate, brain [usually glioblastoma], skin [sebaceous adenomas, sebaceous carcinomas, and keratoacanthomas], and pancreas).
is_a: HP:0020053 ! Abnormal marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:39:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020056
name: Diminished MSH2 expression
def: "Immunohistochemistry (IHC) demonstrating loss of expression of the mismatch repair gene product mutS homolog 2 (MSH2)." []
comment: This abnormality may be observed in a tumor of the Lynch syndrome spectrum (e.g., colorectal, endometrial, ovarian, stomach, small bowel, urinary tract, biliary tract, prostate, brain [usually glioblastoma], skin [sebaceous adenomas, sebaceous carcinomas, and keratoacanthomas], and pancreas).
is_a: HP:0020053 ! Abnormal marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:43:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020057
name: Diminished MSH6 expression
def: "Immunohistochemistry (IHC) demonstrating loss of expression of the mismatch repair gene product mutS homolog 6 (MSH6)." []
comment: This abnormality may be observed in a tumor of the Lynch syndrome spectrum (e.g., colorectal, endometrial, ovarian, stomach, small bowel, urinary tract, biliary tract, prostate, brain [usually glioblastoma], skin [sebaceous adenomas, sebaceous carcinomas, and keratoacanthomas], and pancreas).
is_a: HP:0020053 ! Abnormal marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T11:47:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020058
name: Abnormal red blood cell count
