[Term]
id: HP:0020094
name: Squamous metaplasia
def: "Metaplasia of an epithelium (normally a unilayer of cuboidal or columnar cells) with squamous epithelium (squamous means scale-like). Metaplastic squamous epithelium becomes stratified (i.e., has multiple layers)." [PMID:28860646]
comment: Metaplasia is the replacement of one differentiated somatic cell type with another differentiated somatic cell type in the same tissue. Typically, metaplasia is triggered by environmental stimuli, which may act in concert with the deleterious effects of microorganisms and inflammation.
is_a: HP:0020092 ! Histopathological abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-26T12:34:17Z" xsd:dateTime

