[Term]
id: HP:0020097
name: Infection due to encapsulated bacteria
def: "Increased susceptibility to infections with encapsulated bacteria, as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with encapsulated bacterial organisms such as Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae type b, or Neisseria meningitidis." []
comment: Encapsulated bacteria have been responsible for the majority of bacteremia and meningitis in children for many decades. In children aged over 3 months, Streptococcus pneumoniae (pneumococcus), Neisseria meningitidis (meningococcus), and Haemophilus influenzae have been the predominant pathogens, with H. influenzae being a less significant problem since the introduction of vaccines against type b organisms. Disease is most common in young children less than 5 years of age and older adults aged over 65 years. In neonates and young infants, Group B Streptococcus (GBS) is the major cause of bacteremia and meningitis. These organisms have the shared characteristic of being surrounded by a polysaccharide capsule, which is a key virulence factor because it helps the bacteria evade complement deposition and subsequent phagocytosis and killing. These polysaccharides have also been the basis for successful vaccines against all except GBS, because immune responses against the polysaccharide capsule are the primary mechanism of protection for the human host. Each species can be encapsulated by polysaccharides of different biochemical compositions, which has been used for categorization into capsular groups or serotypes.
is_a: HP:5210000 ! Unusual bacterial infection
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-9822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9382-150X
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2029-0733
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3577-9021
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4315-9105
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8124-8864
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-08T18:54:35Z" xsd:dateTime

