property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-07-05T19:49:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020150
name: Elevated urinary uromodulin level
def: "The concentration of uromodulin (also known as Tamm Horsfall protein) in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:28781372]
comment: Uromodulin (also known as Tamm Horsfall protein) is exclusively produced in the kidney and is the most abundant protein in normal urine. Levels of uromodulin in the urine and in the blood, where it is present in lower amounts, are valuable biomarkers for tubular mass and renal function.
synonym: "Elevated urinary Tamm-Horsfall protein concentration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034885 ! Abnormal urinary uromodulin level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-07-05T19:52:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020151
name: Anti-dsDNA antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the serum that react against double-stranded DNA." [PMID:15804704]
comment: Anti-DNA antibodies can be observed in persons with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), being a formal classification criterion.
synonym: "Anti-double-stranded DNA antibody positivity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020359 ! Anti-nucleosome antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-07-05T20:03:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020152
name: Distal joint hypermobility
def: "Lack of stability of a distal joint (e.g., finger)." []
synonym: "Distal joint laxity" EXACT []
