def: "Activity or concentration of cholinesterase in the blood circulation below the lower limit of normal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8169-9049, PMID:29853783]
comment: Serum cholinesterase (butyrylcholinesterase (BChE)) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes acetylcholine. BChE is synthetized in the liver and has conventionally been used as a liver function test.
