[Term]
id: HP:0020193
name: Prolonged reptilase time
def: "An abnormally increased duration of the reptilase time. Reptilase time is a functional plasma clotting assay, which is based on the enzymatic activity of batroxobin. By specifically cleaving fibrinogen A from fibrinogen, batroxobin leads to the formation of a stable fibrin clot. The time, starting from the addition of batroxobin to the plasma sample, until clot formation is the reptilase time and is given in seconds." [PMID:23546720]
comment: Reptilase time may be increased with a deficiency of fibronogen. Unlike the thrombin time, this assay is not affected by the presence of heparin, hirudin, or direct thrombin inhibitors in a blood sample.
is_a: HP:0001928 ! Abnormality of coagulation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-09-05T13:57:09Z" xsd:dateTime

