[Term]
id: HP:0020207
name: Reflex seizure
def: "Seizures precipitated by exogenous stimuli." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
comment: Included in 2001 ILAE Proposed Classification of Seizures. Seizures precipitated by fever, head injury, or alcohol withdrawal or anti-epileptic medication withdrawal are not provoked seizures.
is_a: HP:0001250 ! Seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:36:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020208
name: Eating-induced seizure
def: "A seizure precipitated by aspects of anticipating food, eating itself, or the post-prandial period." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:39:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020209
name: Hot water-induced seizure
def: "A seizure precipitated by pouring cupfuls of very hot water (40 to 50 degrees Celsius) in rapid succession over the head. Bathing in this manner is the most common trigger." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:40:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020210
name: Praxis-induced seizure
def: "A seizure precipitated by complex, cognition-guided tasks often involving visuomotor coordination and decision-making." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340, PMID:24512781]
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:41:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020211
name: Proprioceptive-induced seizure
def: "A seizure precipitated by movement or a change in posture." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:46:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020212
name: Reading-induced seizure
def: "A seizure precipitated by reading." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
comment: These are typically manifest by myoclonic movements of the jaw or throat, increasing in frequency and potentially culminating in a bilateral tonic-clonic seizure if reading continues.
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:47:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020213
name: Somatosensory-induced seizure
def: "A somatosensory reflex seizure is a seizure precipitated by somatic stimulation of a specific part of the body in the absence of startle or surprise." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:48:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020214
name: Startle-induced seizure
def: "Startle-induced seizures are triggered by multiple and non-specific stimuli (auditory, somatosensory, and rarely visual) and are characterized by their sudden unexpected nature. Sudden noise rather than pure sound is the most effective acoustic stimulus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
comment: Seizures are stereotyped and typically unilateral or bilateral tonic in nature.
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:51:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020215
name: Thinking-induced seizure
def: "Seizures induced by thinking and decision-making." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
comment: These have been reported occurring in response to higher nonverbal mental activity such as playing chess or card games, performing mathematical calculation, drawing complex figures, manipulating spatial information, and typing.
synonym: "Cognition induced seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:53:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020216
name: Visually-induced seizure
def: "Seizures evoked by visual stimuli. This includes clinical seizures induced by strobe lighting, television and other screens, flickering environmental lighting and self-induction by causing a strobe effect." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:11422340]
synonym: "Photosensitive seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020207 ! Reflex seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-24T13:55:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020217
name: Focal aware motor seizure
def: "A type of focal motor seizure in which awareness is retained throughout the seizure." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
synonym: "Focal motor aware seizure" EXACT []
