[Term]
id: HP:0020229
name: Abnormal lymph-node biospecimen
def: "Any abnormal phenotypic feature observed in a biospecimen derived from a lymph node, generally obtained by lymph node biopsy (removal of lymph node tissue for microscopic examination)." [PMID:17067938]
comment: The lymph nodes are organized lymphoid organs that contain lymphocytes within a fine reticular stroma. The structures within a lymph node include the capsule, subcapsular sinus, cortex (B cell zone with follicles and germinal centers), paracortex (T cell zone), medullary sinuses, medullary cords and hilus.
is_a: HP:0020228 ! Biospecimen phenotypic feature
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T16:45:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020230
name: Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality of the architecture of the tissue of a lymph node." []
comment: Each tissue is composed of many different cell types that assemble into organized patterns. Tissue architecture is defined by the cellular and extracellular compartments that cooperate with each other through division of labor.
is_a: HP:0020229 ! Abnormal lymph-node biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T16:51:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020231
name: Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality within cells located in a lymph node." []
is_a: HP:0020229 ! Abnormal lymph-node biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T16:53:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020232
name: Abnormal Q wave
def: "An anomaly of the Q wave of the electrocardiogram." [PMID:31747210]
comment: Physiologically, the Q wave is mainly observed in the lateral leads aVL, I, V5, and V6 and is not observed in leads V1 to V3. The Q wave points downward and has a width less than 0.03s (i.e., 1 small square) and a depth of less than 3 mm (3 small squares), and it does not exceed 1/4 of the R wave in the given lead. The development of pathological Q waves has long been correlated with worsened outcome in patients with ST elevation myocardial infarction
synonym: "Pathological Q wave" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0025074 ! Abnormal QRS complex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-29T07:00:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020233
name: Abnormal lymph-node cellular antigen expression
def: "Abnormal expression of an antigen (marker) by cells located in a lymph node." []
is_a: HP:0020229 ! Abnormal lymph-node biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T16:56:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020234
name: Altered lymph-node tissue architecture
def: "An alteration that affects multiple components of the architecture of a lymph node." []
synonym: "Distorted lymph node architecture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T16:56:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020235
name: Effaced lymph-node architecture
def: "Effacement of architecture typically refers to a cellular infiltrate destroying the normal follicular architecture of a lymph node. This effacement may result in sheets of cells that do not form clear architecture (seen in many lymphomas) or may lead to replacement of the normal architecture by atypical architecture, for example effacement of normal lymph node architecture (including normal follicles and patent lymph node sinuses) by many abnormal follicles in follicular lymphoma." []
is_a: HP:0020234 ! Altered lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:09:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020236
name: Vaguely nodular lymph-node architecture
def: "In contrast to normal lymph node architecture or that of follicular lymphoma, where follicles are typically distinct and readily identifiable on H&E stained biopsy sections, the cells within an atypical lymph node may show what appear to groups of cells forming vague nodules but not forming clear follicles." []
comment: This finding, if not an artifact of poor tissue processing, favors lymphoma but may be seen in reactive states.
is_a: HP:0020234 ! Altered lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:10:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020237
name: Lymph-node capsular invasion by lymphocytes
def: "Migration of substantial numbers of lymphocytes into the capsule of a lymph node." []
comment: Lymph node capsules are formed by fibrous tissue encapsulating the lymph node, and typically have few or no lymphocytes within the capsule itself.
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:22:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020238
name: Lymph-node extracapsular extension by lymph-node lymphocytes
def: "Migration of lymphocytes into the soft tissues surrounding the lymph node." []
comment: Lymph node capsules are formed by fibrous tissue encapsulating the lymph node, and typically the lymphocytes within a lymph node do not extravasate outside of the capsule into soft tissues surrounding the lymph node.
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:23:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020239
name: Increased lymph-node epithelioid histiocyte count
def: "Number of epithelioid histiocytes (histiocytes are tissue-resident macrophages) located within a lymph node above the upper limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:28:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020240
name: Scattered lymph node individual epithelioid histiocytes
def: "Many individual (not clustered) epithelioid histiocytes throughout at least part of a lymph node." []
comment: Histiocytes are tissue-resident macrophages with a moderate amount of cytoplasm that can occasionally show more abundant cytoplasm and appear similar to epithelial cells. These epithelioid histiocytes may be scattered and/or clustered together within lymph nodes under certain conditions, but are generally not prominent in benign non-reactive lymph nodes.
is_a: HP:0020239 ! Increased lymph-node epithelioid histiocyte count
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:29:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020241
name: Clustered lymph node epithelioid histiocytes
def: "Formation of clusters (group of cells positioned near each other) of epithelioid histiocytes within a lymph node." []
comment: Histiocytes are tissue-resident macrophages with a moderate amount of cytoplasm that can occasionally show more abundant cytoplasm and appear similar to epithelial cells. These epithelioid histiocytes may be scattered and/or clustered together within lymph nodes under certain conditions, but are generally not prominent in benign non-reactive lymph nodes.
is_a: HP:0020239 ! Increased lymph-node epithelioid histiocyte count
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:29:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020242
name: Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality of the architecture of follicles of a lymph node." [PMID:17067937]
comment: A lymph node follicle is a loosely arranged structure with an outer mantle of small T lymphocytes and a germinal center composed of B lymphocytes, follicular dendritic cells, and macrophages.
synonym: "Abnormal follicular lymph-node architecture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:30:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020243
name: Floral-pattern lymph node follicles
def: "Atypical lymph node follicles that have mantle zone cells invaginating/infiltrating into the follicle centers, which is said to confer a flower-like appearance." []
synonym: "Floral follicular lymph node architecture" EXACT []
synonym: "Floral growth pattern" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:33:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020244
name: Colonization of follicles by lymphoma cells
def: "In contrast to follicular lymphoma, which typically is a lymphoma that forms follicles or potentially completely replaces normal follicles, some lymphomas (most commonly marginal zone lymphoma) can infiltrate normal follicles so both normal lymphocytes and the infiltrating lymphoma cells are present. This is called colonization of follicles by the lymphoma cells." []
synonym: "Follicular colonisation" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Follicular colonization" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:36:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020245
name: Crowded lymph-node follicles
def: "Reduction in the average distance between adjacent lymph node follicles." []
comment: Follicles in lymph nodes are usually spaced apart, however in certain conditions such as florid reactive follicular hyperplasia and follicular lymphoma, the follicles can become very crowded, even back-to-back with few interfollicular cells in between.
synonym: "Crowded follicles" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:50:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020246
name: Lymph-node follicular lysis
def: "An abnormal morphology of hyperplastic lymph node follicles characterized by distortion of the follicular architecture by tongues and clusters of dark blue mantle cells impinging on and invading the reactive germinal center (Mostly T cells and mantle-zone B cells)." [PMID:14502795]
synonym: "Follicular lysis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T17:51:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020247
name: Non-polarized lymph node germinal centers
def: "A loss of the typical polarization of the architecture of a lymph node germinal center." []
comment: Germinal centers typically have one side containing mostly larger centroblasts and the other side containing mostly small centrocytes. The side with more centroblasts appears darker on an H&E stained section and is termed the dark zone and the other side appears lighter and is termed the light zone. This polarization of germinal center topology is often visualized on H&E stained sections of reactive lymph nodes but may not be as obvious if the germinal centers are small or if the specific section happens to contain mostly dark zone or mostly light zone. This polarization is typically lost in follicular lymphomas.
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T18:54:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020248
name: Irregularly shaped lymph node germinal centers
def: "A deviation from the typically fairly round or oval form of a lymph node germinal center." []
comment: Germinal centers may become more elongated and/or take on irregular shapes such as somewhat snake-like/serpentine or other shapes.
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T18:59:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020249
name: Abnormal lymph-node marginal or mantle zone morphology
def: "An abnormality of the structure of the mantle or marginal zone of a lymph node." []
comment: The normal marginal zone is the area circumferentially adjacent to the mantle zone and distal to the germinal center of a reactive (secondary) follicle.
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:13:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020250
name: Abnormal lymph node marginal zone morphology
comment: Marginal zones are not typically present in lymph nodes, and when they are, they are difficult to distinguish from mantle zones on H&E. Marginal zones are a rim/band of lymphocytes surrounding mantle zones in secondary follicles (those containing germinal centers), and are typically only visualized in specific locations such as Peyer patches of the small bowel, or spleen, and not normally seen in lymph nodes. Expansion of marginal zones should prompt evaluation for a possible marginal zone lymphoma.
is_a: HP:0020249 ! Abnormal lymph-node marginal or mantle zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:13:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020251
name: Abnormal lymph node mantle zone morphology
is_a: HP:0020249 ! Abnormal lymph-node marginal or mantle zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:13:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020252
name: Abnormal bursal fluid morphology
def: "An anomaly of the synovial-like fluid found within a bursa, which is a small, closed sac lined by synovial membrane that reduces friction between tissues such as tendons, muscles, ligaments, and bones." []
is_a: HP:0001367 ! Abnormal joint morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-29T07:08:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020253
name: Lymph node with expanded mantle zones
def: "Enlargement of the typical outer ring of small lymphocytes (mantle zone) surrounding a germinal center of a lymph node." []
comment: Secondary follicles (follicles with germinal centers) typically show mantle zones which are a rim or band of mostly B cells surrounding germinal centers that on H&E appears as densely packed small lymphocytes immediately surrounding germinal centers. The mantle zone is usually relatively thin (i.e. only a few rows of lymphocytes extending out from the germinal center), however may be significantly expanded, particularly in mantle cell lymphoma.
synonym: "Germinal centers with expanded mantle zones" EXACT []
synonym: "Germinal centres with expanded mantle zones" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0020251 ! Abnormal lymph node mantle zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:15:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020254
name: Lymph node with poorly defined germinal center borders
def: "Reduced demarcation of the border between germinal centers and mantle zones. This border is typically seen as a crisp line on hematoxylin and eosin (H&E)-stained lymph node sections." []
comment: Although not necessarily a neoplastic feature, the border between germinal centers and mantle zones may become poorly demarcated in certain lymphomas.
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:16:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020255
name: Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality of germinal centers of a lymph node." [PMID:30410492]
comment: The germinal center is a specialized microstructure that forms in secondary lymphoid tissues, producing long-lived antibody secreting plasma cells and memory B cells, which can provide protection against reinfection.
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:18:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020256
name: Elevated bursal fluid leukocyte count
def: "The count of leukocytes per unit volume in a bursa aspirate specimen is above the uppper limit of normal." []
comment: This finding is characteristic of septic arthritis. To ascertain this finding, typically, a specimen of bursal fluid is removed from the inflammed joint with a needle and syringe (aspiration) and examined microscopically.
is_a: HP:0020252 ! Abnormal bursal fluid morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-29T07:10:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020257
name: Mantle zone pattern
def: "This refers to an architectural pattern of infiltration where atypical lymphocytes surround germinal centers, often expanding the mantle zones but without effacing architecture." []
comment: This pattern may be observed in mantle cell lymphoma.
is_a: HP:0020251 ! Abnormal lymph node mantle zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:32:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020258
name: Germinal centers with absent marginal zones
is_a: HP:0020250 ! Abnormal lymph node marginal zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:32:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020259
name: Decreased biparietal diameter
def: "Fetal head width measurement, taken between the outer edge of the proximal parietal bone and the inner edge of the distal parietal bone, below the lower limit of normal, usually taken to be two standard deviations below the norm or above the 3rd percentile for the gestational age." []
synonym: "Decreased BPD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:6001417 ! Abnormal biparietal diameter
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-16T15:57:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020260
name: Increased biparietal diameter
def: "Fetal head width measurement, taken between the outer edge of the proximal parietal bone and the inner edge of the distal parietal bone, above the upper limit of normal, usually taken to be two standard deviations above the norm or above the 97th percentile for the gestational age." []
synonym: "Increased BPD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:6001417 ! Abnormal biparietal diameter
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-16T15:57:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020261
name: Poorly defined primary lymph-node follicles
def: "Lack of the typical easily recognized delineation of primary follicles within lymph nodes." []
comment: Follicles generally are relatively distinct at low magnification on H&E stained slides, however may not be obvious on the H&E stained slide, requiring immunohistochemistry to confirm the presence of follicle formation.
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:36:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020262
name: Progressive transformation of germinal centers
def: "This is a condition sometimes seen in a subset of germinal centers of reactive lymph nodes where germinal centers become enlarged and infiltrated by benign mantle zone cells and some T cells." [PMID:14502795]
comment: While PTGC is a relatively common finding, there is an association with nodular lymphocyte predominant Hodgkin lymphoma, and morphologically may mimic follicular lymphoma (as well as immunohistochemically with regard to BCL2 staining if not carefully evaluated at high magnification), particularly the floral variant.
synonym: "PTGC" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:37:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020263
name: Absent germinal center tingible body macrophages
def: "Lack of observable tingible body macrophages (TBMs) in germinal centers (GCs) of secondary lymphoid follicles. TBMs represent unique, large phagocytic cells that reside and are a subset of mononuclear phagocytes." [PMID:33967475]
comment: Germinal centers typically contain macrophages that are engulfing cells undergoing apoptosis from the antigen selection process. The macrophages have relatively abundant cytoplasm containing apoptotic debris and are termed tingible-body macrophages (tingible is a somewhat non-specific term simply meaning capable of being stained). Tingible-body macrophages may be rare or absent in abnormal germinal centers such as in follicular lymphoma. Tingible body macrophages owe their name to their ability to actively phagocytose apoptotic lymphoid cells, and the tingible bodies (TBs) observed in their cytoplasm are apoptotic bodies.
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:49:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020264
name: Lack of germinal center mitotic figures
def: "Absence of extreme paucity of mitotic figures in a lymph node germinal center." []
comment: Germinal centers typically have many cells undergoing cell division and therefore mitotic figures are frequently seen within germinal centers. If multiple germinal centers are present, it is unusual not to see at least some mitotic figures. Absent/decreased mitotic figures is an abnormal finding typically seen in low grade follicular lymphomas.
is_a: HP:0020255 ! Abnormal lymph-node germinal center morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:54:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020265
name: Non-polarized mantle zones
def: "Lack of the typical polarization of the outer ring of small lymphocytes (mantle zone) surrounding a germinal center of a lymph node." []
comment: Secondary follicles (follicles with germinal centers) typically show mantle zones which are a rim or band of mostly B cells surrounding germinal centers that on H&E appears as densely packed small lymphocytes immediately surrounding germinal centers. The mantle zones typically are thicker (are several rows of lymphocytes extending out from the germinal center) on one side and thinner (only one or very few rows of lymphocytes extending out from the germinal center) on the other side. This polarization is not always obvious but is often seen, and is often lost in some atypical conditions such as lymphomas involving or surrounding germinal centers.
is_a: HP:0020251 ! Abnormal lymph node mantle zone morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T19:55:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020266
name: Hyalinized lymph-node vessels
def: "Hyalinized means to become clear/translucent such as collagen becoming more pale staining (collagen is typically quite eosinophilic, meaning attracted to the pink/red dye eosin); however, with regard to vessels in the lymph node, hyalinization is often used to describe vessel walls that appear markedly thickened or surrounded by eosinophilic material such as collagen, not necessarily translucent appearing." []
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:10:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020267
name: Lymph-node follicular sclerosis
def: "Collagen deposition, typically with decreased cellularity, within lymph-node follicles." []
synonym: "Follicular sclerosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020242 ! Abnormal lymph-node follicle architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:12:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020268
name: Compressed lymph-node sinuses
def: "Loss of the typical patency (openness) of lymph node sinuses." []
comment: Lymph node sinuses are structures that carry fluid and some cells traveling to and from the lymph node parenchyma, and often contain some histiocytes. These are normally patent but may be compressed by proliferating or infiltrating cells such as lymphoma to the point where they are no longer visible on routine H&E stained sections.
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:14:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020269
name: Lymph-node proliferation centers
def: "Proliferation centers are a finding specific to chronic lymphocytic leukemia/small lymphocytic lymphoma where regions (typically relatively small, comparable to the size of a lymph node follicle) appear more pale on H&E stained sections (though they may become enlarged to merge together). These areas contain increased numbers of enlarged lymphoma cells with nucleoli (prolymphocytes and paraimmunoblasts) and show a higher proliferation rate (readily visualized with a Ki-67 immunohistochemical stain) than surrounding lymphoma cells. They can be mistaken as vague follicle formation and are therefore sometimes referred to as pseudofollicles." []
synonym: "Pseudofollicles" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020230 ! Abnormal lymph-node tissue architecture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:15:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020270
name: Cytologic atypia in mantle cells
def: "Lymphocytes in the mantle zones of lymph node secondary follicles show cellular atypia such as enlarged size, increased cytoplasm, atypical distribution of chromatin, or irregular nuclear contours." []
comment: This finding may raise suspicion of a neoplasm of mantle zone cells such as mantle cell lymphoma. Other lymphomas with cytologic atypia such as marginal zone lymphoma may also replace normal mantle zone cells.
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:16:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020271
name: Increased lymph-node eosinophils
def: "Eosinophils count within a lymph node above normal limits." []
comment: Lymph nodes typically contain very few if any eosinophils but the number of eosinophils may be high in certain reactive or neoplastic states.
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:39:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020272
name: Increased lymph-node plasma cells
def: "Number of plasma cells per lymph node above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Lymph nodes typically contain some plasma cells and the number of plasma cells may be increased, sometimes forming sheets of plasma cells, in certain reactive or neoplastic conditions.
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:40:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020273
name: High lymph node non-germinal center mitotic activity
def: "Increased numbers of mitotic figures outside of germinal centers." []
comment: Within lymph nodes, germinal centers typically show a high rate of cell division and correspondingly high number of cells undergoing mitosis. Cells outside of germinal centers typically show low levels of cell division visualized as low numbers of mitotic figures. Increased numbers of mitotic figures outside of germinal centers may be seen in certain reactive or neoplastic states.
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:42:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020274
name: Lymph-node lymphocyte monocytoid morphology
def: "Lymphocytes that show morphologic features resembling monocytes, such as increased cytoplasm and slightly enlarged nuclei that are more irregular than most lymph node lymphocytes." []
comment: This finding may be seen in reactive conditions such as monocytoid B-cell hyperplasia of certain infections or in neoplastic states such as certain marginal zone lymphomas.
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:43:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020275
name: Reduced lymph node lymphocyte morphological variability
def: "Decreased morphological variability of lymph node lymphocytes as compared to the typically somewhat heterogeneous morphology of populations of benign lymph node lymphocytes." []
comment: Lymph nodes often contain primarily small lymphocytes but typically have some admixed larger lymphocytes and show a little morphological variability. Neoplastic states may show increased morphological variability or decreased morphological variability, the latter showing unusually monotonous morphology among the population of lymphocytes.
synonym: "Monomorphic cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:48:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020276
name: Increased large lymphocytes in lymph node
def: "An increased number of large lymphocytes within a lymph node compared to a normal non-reactive lymph node." []
comment: Lymph nodes will often show primarily small lymphocytes with relatively few scattered large lymphocytes (often termed immunoblasts). Increased large cells may indicate a reactive condition such as mononucleosis or a neoplastic condition. It may also help differentiate two different neoplasms such as marginal zone lymphoma (which often has increased scattered large cells) and mantle cell lymphoma (which usually has decreased scattered large cells).
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:51:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020277
name: Hodgkin morphology cells
def: "Hodgkin cells are typically large and often show very large nucleoli and sometimes binucleation or multinucleation. Reed-Sternberg cells are a type of Hodgkin cell that is binucleated with very large nucleoli that stains slightly red on H&E stained sections (often said to mimic owl eyes). Other Hodgkin cell morphologies include cells that are dying with dark basophilic (blue) nuclei that appear somewhat smudged (mummified cells) and cells with a large space around or adjacent to the nuclei and retracted cytoplasm after tissue fixation (lacunar cells). Hodgkin cells are characteristic of Hodgkin lymphoma, however several non-Hodgkin lymphomas and noN-neoplastic conditions are known to sometimes show a few similar morphology cells." [PMID:31194473]
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:56:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020278
name: Abnormal lymph-node lymphoctye nuclear morphology
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T20:58:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020279
name: Irregular lymph-node lymphocyte nuclei
def: "Lymph node lymphocyte nuclei that are more irregular than the typical round to slightly oval shapes of the majority of lymph node lymphocytes." []
comment: More irregularly shaped nuclei can be seen in normal germinal centers (i.e. centrocytes) and in many types of lymphomas.
is_a: HP:0020278 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphoctye nuclear morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:00:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020280
name: Lymph-node Dutcher bodies
def: "Dutcher bodies are collections of immunoglobulin protein that overlie or invaginate into the nucleus of plasma cells. These nuclear pseudoinclusions can occasionally be seen in reactive states and may be increased in specific neoplastic conditions." [PMID:31309083]
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:07:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020281
name: Finely dispersed lymph node lymphocyte chromatin
def: "Nuclei of lymphocytes with less dense, evenly distributed chromatin than the normal densely packed, often clumped chromatin of mature lymphocytes." []
comment: This finding is seen in very immature lymphocyte precursors (i.e. lymphoblasts in lymphoblastic leukemia/lymphoma) or blastoid cells such as in blastoid mantle cell lymphoma.
is_a: HP:0020282 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte chromatin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:10:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020282
name: Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte chromatin
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality of the chromatin (complex of DNA and protein which comprises chromosomes) of lymphocytes that are located within a lymph node." []
is_a: HP:0020278 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphoctye nuclear morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:12:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020283
name: Clumping of lymph node lymphocyte chromatin
def: "Nuclei of lymphocytes show multiple small densely packed areas of chromatin that appear as relatively evenly spaced clumps of basophilic (blue) staining within the nuclei on Hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) stained sections." []
comment: This is a somewhat non-specific finding but one that is often more prominent in lymphocytes of chronic lymphocytic leukemia/small lymphocytic lymphoma.
is_a: HP:0020282 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte chromatin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:12:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020284
name: Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte cytoplasm morphology
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality of the cytoplasm (material located within the cell membrane but excluding the nucleus) of lymphocytes that are located within a lymph node." []
is_a: HP:0020231 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:14:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020285
name: Decreased lymph node lymphocyte cytoplasm
def: "The amount of cytoplasm in lymphocytes is even less than the relatively little cytoplasm found in the majority of lymphocytes within lymph nodes." []
comment: This finding is typically seen in centrocytes, either within normal germinal centers or neoplastic centrocytes in follicles of follicular lymphoma.
synonym: "Scant lymph node lymphocyte cytoplasm" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020284 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte cytoplasm morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:15:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020286
name: Increased lymph node lymphocyte cytoplasm
def: "Increased amount of cytoplasm compared to the majority of lymphocytes in a benign lymph node." []
comment: This finding may be observed in reactive or neoplastic lymphocytes located in a lymph node.
is_a: HP:0020284 ! Abnormal lymph-node lymphocyte cytoplasm morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:16:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020287
name: Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD19 expression
def: "Detection of an abnormal level of CD19 on the cell(s) of interest in a lymph node with the use of anti-CD19 antibodies conjugated to a chromogen (for immunohistochemistry) or fluorophore (for flow cytometry)." []
comment: Most B-lineage lymphomas and leukemias show CD19 expression. Neoplastic plasma cells (plasma cells are derived from B cells), however, often lose CD19 expression.
is_a: HP:0020288 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular B-cell marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:24:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020288
name: Abnormal lymph-node cellular B-cell marker expression
def: "Abnormal expression of an antigen (marker) that is normally expressed by B lymphocytes." []
comment: This term is intended to be applied to findings of lymph-node biopsies in diseases such as lymphoma.
is_a: HP:0020233 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular antigen expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:25:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020289
name: Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD20 expression
def: "Detection of abnormal levels of CD20 on the cell(s) of interest with the use of anti-CD20 antibodies conjugated to a chromogen (for immunohistochemistry) or fluorophore (for flow cytometry)." []
comment: CD20 is normally expressed fairly highly on B-lineage cells, except plasma cells (down-regulate CD20 expression to the point where only a small subset of cells show expression).
is_a: HP:0020288 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular B-cell marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:25:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020290
name: CD79a expression
def: "Detection of the presence of CD79a on the cell(s) of interest with the use of anti-CD79a antibodies conjugated to a chromogen (for immunohistochemistry) or fluorophore (for flow cytometry)." []
comment: Most B-lineage lymphomas and leukemias as well as plasma cell neoplasms (plasma cells are derived from B cells) show CD79a expression.
is_a: HP:0430091 ! Marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:26:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020291
name: Increased lymph-node cellular CD20 expression
def: "Increased levels of CD20 expression compared to normal B cells." []
comment: CD20 is normally expressed fairly highly on B-lineage cells, but occasionally may show increased levels of expression relative to normal resting B cells. Increased expression is best visualized using flow cytometry when a population of normal B cells is present for comparison.
is_a: HP:0020289 ! Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD20 expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:27:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020292
name: Decreased lymph-node cellular CD20 expression
def: "Decreased levels of CD20 expression compared to normal B cells." []
comment: CD20 is normally expressed fairly highly on B-lineage cells, but occasionally may show decreased levels of expression relative to normal resting B cells. Decreased expression is best visualized using flow cytometry when a population of normal B cells is present for comparison.
is_a: HP:0020289 ! Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD20 expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:27:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020293
name: Decreased lymph-node cellular CD19 expression
def: "Decreased levels of CD19 expression compared to normal B cells." []
comment: CD19 is normally expressed fairly highly on B-lineage cells, but occasionally may show decreased levels of expression relative to normal resting B cells. Decreased expression is best visualized using flow cytometry when a population of normal B cells is present for comparison.
is_a: HP:0020287 ! Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD19 expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:28:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020294
name: Increased lymph-node cellular CD19 expression
def: "Increased levels of CD19 expression compared to normal B cells." []
comment: CD19 is normally expressed fairly highly on B-lineage cells, but occasionally may show increased levels of expression relative to normal resting B cells. Increased expression is best visualized using flow cytometry when a population of normal B cells is present for comparison.
is_a: HP:0020287 ! Abnormal level of lymph-node cellular CD19 expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:28:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020295
name: PAX5 expression
def: "Detection of the presence of PAX5 on the cell(s) of interest with the use of anti-PAX5 antibodies conjugated to a chromogen (for immunohistochemistry)." []
comment: PAX5 is a transcription factor that helps control B-cell lineage differentiation and is expressed in the nucleus of immature and mature B cells (including most neoplastic forms), but not in plasma cells.
is_a: HP:0430091 ! Marker expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:28:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020296
name: Germinal center B-lymphocyte BCL2 expression
def: "Positive staining for BCL2 apoptosis regulator protein in lymph-node germinal center B cells." []
comment: The BCL2 family of proteins regulate apoptosis, and BCL2 itself displays anti-apoptotic functions. In normal germinal centers, where antigenic selection leads to apoptosis of B cells that recognize self proteins, BCL2 is not expressed. Most low grade follicular lymphomas show aberrant expression of the anti-apoptotic protein BCL2, presumably helping to prevent the germinal center derived neoplastic B cells from undergoing apoptosis. Expression of BCL2 by germinal center B cells is abnormal and typically seen in low grade follicular lymphomas and in at least a subset of B cells in many high grade follicular lymphomas as well. Careful inspection is required when interpreting the stain, however, as normal T cells and occasionally infiltrating mantle zone B cells may also be seen in germinal centers, and these should not be interpreted as BCL2 expression in germinal center B cells.
is_a: HP:0020233 ! Abnormal lymph-node cellular antigen expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-11-10T21:31:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020297
name: Abnormal occipitofrontal diameter
def: "Abnormal occipitofrontal diameter (OFD) refers to a fetal head width measurement, taken between the root of the nose to the most prominent part of the occiput on an ultrasound image that lies outside the expected range for a given gestational age. The expected range typically falls between the 3rd percentile (or more than 2 standard deviations below the mean) and the 97th percentile (or more than 2 standard deviations above the mean)." []
is_a: HP:0034245 ! Fetal head anomaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-16T17:17:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020298
name: Decreased occipitofrontal diameter
def: "Occipitofrontal diameter, measured with fetal sonography, below the lower limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0020297 ! Abnormal occipitofrontal diameter
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-16T17:22:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020299
name: Increased occipitofrontal diameter
def: "Occipitofrontal diameter, measured with fetal sonography, above the upper limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0020297 ! Abnormal occipitofrontal diameter
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-16T17:22:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020300
name: Abnormal elbow morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the joint that connects the upper and the lower arm." []
is_a: HP:0009811 ! Abnormality of the elbow
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T07:45:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020301
name: Abnormal elbow physiology
def: "A functional anomaly of the joint that connects the upper and the lower arm." []
is_a: HP:0009811 ! Abnormality of the elbow
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T07:45:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020302
name: Restrictive eating
def: "A behavioral pattern characterized by a deliberate and sustained limitation of food intake, often involving avoidance of certain foods, restriction of portion size, or prolonged fasting, resulting in reduced energy or nutrient consumption relative to physiological needs." [PMID:26310991]
comment: Restrictive eating refers to the intentional restriction of eating, not merely a loss of appetite. This behavior is a characteristic feature of anorexia nervosa and some other eating disorders.
synonym: "Anorexia nervosa" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0100738 ! Abnormal eating behavior
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:08:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020303
name: Abnormal fetal abdominal circumference
def: "Any deviation from the normal range of the fetal abdominal circumference, which is typically measured sonographically in a transverse view using the outer borders of the skin line at the plane where the fetal stomach, umbilical vein and portal sinus is visible. Abnormal fetal abdominal circumference is defined as less than the 10th or greater than the 90th percentile for gestational age." []
is_a: HP:0034207 ! Abnormal fetal gastrointestinal system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5177-8109
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:14:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020304
name: Increased fetal abdominal circumference
def: "The distance around the abdomen of a fetus, generally as measured by prenatal sonography, is above the upper limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0020303 ! Abnormal fetal abdominal circumference
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:16:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020305
name: Abnormal fetal head circumference
def: "Any deviation from the normal range of the fetal head circumference, which is typically measured sonographically in the axial plane at the level of the thalami and cavum septic pellucidi, using the outer border of the bony calvarium. Abnormal fetal head circumference is defined as less than the thrid percentile or 2 standard deviations below the mean or greater than the 97the percentile or 2 standard deviations above the mean." [PMID:35928073]
is_a: HP:0034245 ! Fetal head anomaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5177-8109
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:18:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020306
name: Decreased fetal head circumference
def: "Fetal head circumference less than the third percentile or 2 standard deviations below the mean." [PMID:35928073]
is_a: HP:0020305 ! Abnormal fetal head circumference
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:20:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020307
name: Increased fetal head circumference
def: "Fetal head circumference above the 97th percentile or 2 standard deviations above the mean." []
is_a: HP:0020305 ! Abnormal fetal head circumference
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T08:21:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020308
name: Increased anteroposterior lens thickness
def: "Increase in the anteroposterior (axial) dimension of the crystalline lens relative to the overall length of the globe." [PMID:21397065]
is_a: HP:0011526 ! Abnormality of lens shape
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:17:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020309
name: Ankle instability
def: "Failure of ligamentous and muscular structures of the ankle to maintain normal joint alignment during movement, resulting in excessive motion that causes manifestations such as subjective or objective feeling of clunking/clicking in the ankle with movement, ankle 'giving way' or sensation of ankle dislocating." [PMID:40188228]
is_a: HP:0034674 ! Abnormal ankle physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T14:24:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020310
name: Retinal phlebitis
def: "Inflammation of retinal venules as manifested by perivascular sheathing or cuffing, vascular leakage and/or occlusion." [PMID:40445440]
comment: Retinal phelbitis is typically seen in sarcoidosis.
is_a: HP:0025188 ! Retinal vasculitis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-07T10:25:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020311
name: Ophthalmic artery hypoperfusion
def: "Chronic hypoperfusion due to large vessel disease e.g. carotid artery stenosis, Takayasu disease. Typically presents dilated veins, low retinal arterial pressure, peripheral microaneurysms, ocular hypotension and may lead to iris neovascularisation. Patients may have postural hypotension." [PMID:12121370]
is_a: HP:0000630 ! Abnormal retinal arterial/arteriolar morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-07T10:29:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020312
name: Focal hyperpigmented area associated with subretinal scar tissue
def: "Localized hyperpigmented areas, in the context of subretinal scar tissue, as seen after subretinal neovascularisation." []
comment: This includes Fuchs spot seen in myopic retinopathy.
is_a: HP:0011512 ! Fundus hyperpigmentation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-07T16:30:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020313
name: Discrete fundus hypopigmentation
def: "Well-demarcated areas of the fundus, with relative reduction in pigment, with respect to the rest of the fundus." []
comment: Discrete fundus hypopigmentation is seen in vitiligo, lacunae of CHRPE and achromatic retinal patches.
is_a: HP:0007894 ! Fundus hypopigmentation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-07T16:34:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020314
name: Macular pseudohole
def: "A macular pseudohole is a partial-thickness gap in a normal-thickness fovea, located in the center of the macula." [PMID:20703497]
comment: The diagnosis of macular pseudohole requires an examination by optical coherence tomography (OCT).
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-14T08:47:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020315
name: Lamellar macular hole
def: "A lamellar macular hole is a structural abnormality of the macula, characterized by a partial-thickness gap in a thinner fovea, located in the center of the macula." [PMID:30625477]
comment: Lamellar macular hole (LMH) is a vitreoretinal disorder characterized by an irregular foveal contour, a break in the inner fovea, dehiscence of the inner foveal retina from the outer retina, and the absence of a full-thickness foveal defect with intact foveal photoreceptors. The diagnosis of LMH requires an examination by optical coherence tomography (OCT).
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-01-14T08:48:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020316
name: Middle cerebral artery berry aneurysm
def: "A small, sac-like aneurysm (outpouching) of the middle cerebral artery (MCA). MCA berry aneurysms may occur at the MCA bifurcation, on the anterior communicant artery, the anterior cerebral artery, the internal carotid artery, or on the posterior communicant artery." [PMID:29304371]
is_a: HP:0007029 ! Cerebral berry aneurysm
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3873-102X
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-08T15:44:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020317
name: Abnormal abdominal aorta branch artery morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of an artery that originates from the abdominal aorta." [PMID:39350866]
comment: The abdominal aorta extends from the T12 vertebra and terminates at the L4 vertebra. It gives off anterior, lateral, and posterior branches that supply the abdominal viscera and vertebrae at this level, eventually dividing into the common iliac arteries. Upaired branches (and their typical location) comprise the celiac artery (T12), the superior mesenteric artery (L1), the inferior mesenteric artery (L3), and the median sacral artery. Paired branches comprise the middle adrenal arteries, the renal arteries (L1-2), the gonadal arteries (between L2 and L3), the inferior phrenic arteries, and the lumbar arteries. The abdominal aorta bifurcates into right and left common iliac arteries at L4.
is_a: HP:0011004 ! Abnormal systemic arterial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-24T07:16:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020318
name: Posterior humeral circumflex artery occlusion
def: "Blockage of the posterior circumflex humeral artery (PCHA), which arises from the third part of the axillary artery and supplies the shoulder joint and a number of its associated muscles. The lesion can be ascertained angiographically, whereby dye is injected both with patient's humerus at the side of the body and again with shoulder held in abduction and external rotation. Test is positive if there is evidence of PCHA occlusion with arm in abduction and external rotation but artery is patent when arm is held at the side." []
comment: The axillary artery can be compressed by the humeral head owing to abduction and external rotation of the shoulder joint caused by overhead motion, as typified by pitching.
is_a: HP:0011004 ! Abnormal systemic arterial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-24T07:41:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020319
name: Scapulothoracic incongruity
def: "A lack of smooth, physiological alignment or movement between the scapula (shoulder blade) and the posterior thoracic wall (the rib cage). The scapulothoracic joint is unique, as it lacks true synovial articulation and is dynamically controlled through surrounding muscular contractions. The scapula glides on the posterior thorax covered with muscle layers rather than a cartilaginous surface. This feature can be ascertained by radiography or CT scan of the scapula showing incongruity of the scapulothoracic space." [PMID:34241560]
comment: Snapping scapula syndrome, washboard syndrome, or scapulothoracic crepitobursitis are clinical manifestations of scapulothoracic incongruity usually associated with painful crepitus and shoulder joint dysfunction when attempting overhead motion.
is_a: HP:0000782 ! Abnormal scapula morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-24T07:47:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020320
name: Latissimus dorsi rupture
def: "A tear of the latissimus dorsi (LD). Injury to the LD can occur at various locations, from the tendon to the muscle belly. The LD is a broad, flat muscle occupying most of the lower posterior thorax. The muscle's primary function is to move the upper extremity, but it is also considered an accessory muscle of respiration." [PMID:28846224, PMID:41179423]
is_a: HP:0009127 ! Abnormal appendicular muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-24T07:56:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020321
name: Distal clavicular osteolysis
def: "Degeneration and resorption of the distal part of the clavicle near the acromioclavicular (AC) joint. Distal clavicular osteolysis (DCO) is an atypical injury occurring most often in athletes and weight lifters, specifically those who perform repetitive overhead movements. DCO results from repetitive excess load to the AC joint, typically through horizontal adduction, adduction, internal rotation, and forward/lateral flexion of the shoulder, such as bench pressing or overhead lifting. Imaging (AP clavicle and/or Zanca view of the AC joint) of DCO often demonstrates microcysts, loss of subchondral bone detail, and osteolysis of the distal clavicle." [PMID:35881753]
is_a: HP:0000889 ! Abnormal clavicle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T07:36:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020322
name: Abnormal breast-tissue biospecimen
def: "Any abnormal phenotypic feature observed in a biospecimen derived from breast tissue." []
is_a: HP:0020228 ! Biospecimen phenotypic feature
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:16:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020323
name: Abnormal breast-tissue cellular antigen expression
def: "Abnormal expression of an antigen (marker) by cells located in breast tissue." []
is_a: HP:0020322 ! Abnormal breast-tissue biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:18:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020324
name: Increased breast-tissue HER2 expression
def: "Increased level of human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2) expression in breast tissue." [PMID:29846122]
comment: HER2 gene amplification assessed by in situ hybridization (ISH) or protein overexpression assessed by IHC remains the primary predictor of responsiveness to HER2-targeted therapies in breast cancer.
synonym: "HER2 positive breast tissue" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020323 ! Abnormal breast-tissue cellular antigen expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020325
name: Increased breast-tissue estrogen receptor expression
def: "Increased level of estrogen receptor expression in breast tissue." [PMID:35668111]
comment: More than 70% of all breast cancers are classified as ER+ based on the detection of ER expression by immunohistochemistry in at least 1% of the tumor cells.
synonym: "Estrogen receptor positive in breast" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020323 ! Abnormal breast-tissue cellular antigen expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:24:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020326
name: Increased breast-tissue progesterone receptor expression
comment: Almost 70% of breast cancers are hormone receptor-positive. Their cells have positive expression of estrogen receptor (ER) and/or progesterone receptor (PR), which are related to cancer cell growth and spread. Estrogen and its receptor, ER, play a critical role in the development and progression of breast cancer. PR is an upregulated target gene of ER, its expression is dependent on estrogen, and PR can modulate ER action. PR is also a valuable prognostic biomarker of overall survival or disease-free survival in breast cancer. {xref="PMID:35115765"}
is_a: HP:0020323 ! Abnormal breast-tissue cellular antigen expression
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:39:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020327
name: Abnormal breast-tissue cellular finding
def: "Any phenotypic abnormality within cells located in breast tissue." []
is_a: HP:0020322 ! Abnormal breast-tissue biospecimen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:46:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020328
name: Mammary ductal epithelial cell hyperplasia
def: "Abnormal (increased) proliferation of epithelial cells in a mammary duct. Intraductal papilloma is a benign tumor found within breast ducts. The abnormal proliferation of ductal epithelial cells causes growth. A solitary intraductal papilloma is usually found centrally posterior to the nipple, affecting the central duct." [PMID:30137824]
is_a: HP:0020327 ! Abnormal breast-tissue cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:47:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020329
name: Mammary ductal apocrine metaplasia
def: "A biopsy finding in breast tissue of enlarged epithelial cells with abundant granular eosinophilic cytoplasm that can show apical snouting. Metaplastic apocrine cells within the breast are similar to normal axillary, areolar and perineal apocrine cells, having apocrine secretions and identical staining reactions. One of the reasons, however, that these are often not regarded as normal components is that examples of gradual metaplastic change from the normal cuboidal epithelium can be seen and cells with intermediate features can also be discerned on careful examination, suggesting that these are true metaplasia." [PMID:18042688]
comment: See Figure 1 of PMID:18042688.
is_a: HP:0020327 ! Abnormal breast-tissue cellular finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T08:53:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020330
name: Abnormal circulating inorganic anion concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of inorganic anion in the blood circulation." []
comment: Inorganic anions are negatively charged mineral ions that do not contain carbon-hydrogen bonds. The major clinically important anions are chloride, bicarbonate, and phosphate. Additionally, sulfate, nitrate, nitrite, fluoride, and bromide are measured for certain indications.
is_a: HP:0003111 ! Abnormal circulating electrolyte concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-03-09T07:31:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020331
name: Blue-field entoptic phenomenon
def: "Unremitting, positive visual phenomena, present in the entire visual field and characterized by uncountable tiny flickering dots interposed between the person's vision and the background. The dots are said to resemble static and are typically black and white but can also be colored, flashing, or transparent. In addition to the static, or snow, patients can experience additional visual symptoms of either direct neurological origin, such as palinopsia, photophobia, and nyctalopia (i.e., impaired night vision), or that arise from the optic apparatus." [PMID:29140814, PMID:34671311]
comment: Blue field phenomenon is thought to result from the autovisualization of the own leukocytes in the retinal capillaries.
synonym: "Visual snow" RELATED []
is_a: HP:6001103 ! Entoptic phenomenon
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T09:31:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020332
name: Phosphene
def: "A phosphene is the perception of light without light actually entering the eye, for instance caused by pressure applied to the closed eyes." [PMID:30306317]
comment: During a hydropic vertigo attack, patients may report nausea, vomiting, sweating, urge to defecate, urge to urinate, phosphenes, headache, photophobia, phonophobia and even transient loss of consciousness.
is_a: HP:6001103 ! Entoptic phenomenon
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T09:36:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020333
name: Palinopsia
def: "Palinopsia refers to visual images that persist despite removal of the eliciting object; plainopsia presents as persistent afterimages of stationary objects or trailing of images behind moving objects." [PMID:39412817]
comment: Palinopsia has been reported in visual snow syndrome.
is_a: HP:0000504 ! Abnormality of vision
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T09:39:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020334
name: Positive scapular compression test
def: "A type of function test in which the examiner uses one hand to apply a posterior to anterior force is directly over the scapula and the anterior chest wall is stabilized with the other hand. Test is positive if this scapular stabilization allows for increased shoulder flexion compared to when no stabilization is applied." [PMID:39319823]
synonym: "Positive scapular assistance test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025823 ! Positive provocative functional shoulder test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-26T11:29:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020335
