[Term]
id: HP:0020338
name: Malignant melanotic nerve sheath tumor
def: "Malignant melanotic nerve sheath tumors (MMNSTs) are uncommon pigmented tumors of Schwann cell origin, most often found along the spinal nerves. MMNSTs were formerly known as melanotic schwannoma. Although MMNSTs can occur along cranial nerves, they tend to grow along the dorsal spinal nerve roots, and patients often present with indolent pain, weakness, or paresthesia along a corresponding dermatome. On imaging, spinal MMNSTs generally appear similar to the appearance presented in the current case: intradural, extramedullary tumors. In the spine, the tumors typically grow along spinal nerve roots, sometimes assuming a dumbbell configuration if they extend through a foramen. Tumors demonstrate enhancement on CT and are FDG-avid on PET." [PMID:36302602]
comment: MMNST often carry an inactivating mutation in the protein kinase A inhibitory subunit gene protein kinase cAMP-dependent type I regulatory subunit alpha (PRKAR1A) on chromosome 17p22-24, which acts as a tumor suppressor. MMNST occur in some patients with Carney Complex.
is_a: HP:0030448 ! Soft tissue sarcoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-03-09T07:51:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020339
name: Increased mucosal-associated invariant T cell proportion
def: "An increased proportion of mucosal-associated invariant T (MAIT) cells among peripheral blood T lymphocytes, above the upper reference limit for age. MAIT cells are innate-like T cells that recognise riboflavin metabolite antigens presented by MR1." [PMID:26940855]
synonym: "Elevated MAIT cell proportion" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased MAIT cell frequency" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020340 ! Abnormal mucosal-associated invariant T cell proportion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1526-4557
property_value: terms:date "2026-03-26T12:19:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020340
name: Abnormal mucosal-associated invariant T cell proportion
def: "An increased or decreased proportion of mucosal-associated invariant T (MAIT) cells among peripheral blood T lymphocytes, above the upper reference limit for age. MAIT cells are innate-like T cells that recognise riboflavin metabolite antigens presented by MR1." [PMID:26940855]
