[Term]
id: HP:0020347
name: Abnormal circulating monosaccharide concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of a monosaccharide in the blood circulation." []
comment: The simplest carbohydrates are called monosaccharides, or simple sugars. They are the building blocks (monomers) for the synthesis of polymers or complex carbohydrates. Monosaccharides are classified based on the number of carbons in the molecule. General categories are identified using a prefix that indicates the number of carbons and the suffix -ose, which indicates a saccharide; for example, triose (three carbons), tetrose (four carbons), pentose (five carbons), and hexose (six carbons). The hexose D-glucose is the most abundant monosaccharide in nature.
is_a: HP:0011013 ! Abnormal circulating carbohydrate concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-05-24T08:11:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020348
name: Abnormal circulating disaccharide concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of a disaccharide in the blood circulation." []
comment: A disaccharide is formed by a glycosidic bonds form between hydroxyl groups of the two monosaccharide molecules.
is_a: HP:0011013 ! Abnormal circulating carbohydrate concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-05-24T08:21:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020349
name: Abnormal circulating sugar alcohol concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of a sugar alcohol in the blood circulation." []
comment: Sugar alcohols are organic compounds, typically derived from sugars, containing one hydroxyl group (-OH) attached to each carbon atom.
is_a: HP:0011013 ! Abnormal circulating carbohydrate concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
