property_value: terms:date "2026-05-24T08:55:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020352
name: Lisfranc injury
def: "Lisfranc injuries refer to bony or ligamentous compromise of the tarsometatarsal and intercuneiform joint complex and include a spectrum of injuries ranging from a stable, partial sprain to a grossly displaced and unstable fracture or fracture-dislocation of the midfoot. Foot x-ray shows either widening of the space between the 1st and 2nd metatarsal to over 2mm at the base, dorsal displacement of the base of the 1st or 2nd metatarsal, discontinuity of a line drawn from the medial base of the 2nd metatarsal to the medial side of the medial cuneiform, irregularity between the medial side of the 5th metatarsal base and the medial side of the cuboid, or disruption of the line connecting the medial aspect of the navicular bone to the medial cuneiform." [PMID:28188544]
comment: Ironically, the injury is named after Jaques Lisfranc de Saint-Martin, a French army field surgeon, who actually described a traumatic amputation through the midfoot.
synonym: "Lisfranc fracture-dislocation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001832 ! Abnormal metatarsal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-06-03T15:50:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020354
name: Abnormal dental physiology
def: "A functional anomaly of one or more teeth." []
is_a: HP:0031815 ! Abnormal oral physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-02T09:50:49Z" xsd:string

[Term]
id: HP:0020355
name: Dental hypermobility
def: "Dental hypermobility is the loosening or excessive movement of a tooth within its socket beyond its normal physiological limits." [PMID:1058939]
comment: The Miller classification of dental hypermobility defines grade 1 as the first distinguishable sign of movement greater than normal; grade 2 as a movement of a tooth that allows its crown to move one millimeter from its normal position in any direction; and grade 3 as movement of more than one millimeter. Teeth that may be rotated or depressed in their alveoli are classified as grade 3.
is_a: HP:0020354 ! Abnormal dental physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-02T09:51:37Z" xsd:string

[Term]
id: HP:0020356
name: Antichromatin antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that react against the chromatin. Human autoantibodies that bind to chromatin targets can be divided into those that recognize dsDNA, protein components of chromatin (i.e., histones, HMG proteins), mononucleosomes, or macromolecular components of nucleosomes as represented by low salt extracted nucleosomes (core particle)." [PMID:24804269]
comment: Eukaryotic chromatin is comprised of approximately 40% DNA, 40% histones, 20% nonhistone proteins (i.e., HMG proteins), RNA, and other macromolecules.
is_a: HP:0003493 ! Antinuclear antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-02T11:47:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020357
name: Head and neck squamous cell carcinoma
def: "A squamous cell carcinoma that arises arising from the squamous mucosal epithelium of the upper aerodigestive tract (the oral cavity, pharynx (naso-, oro-, and hypopharynx), and larynx." [PMID:33243986]
comment: Head and neck squamous cell carcinomas develop from the mucosal epithelium in the oral cavity, pharynx and larynx and are the most common malignancies that arise in the head and neck
is_a: HP:0012288 ! Neoplasm of head and neck
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-07T11:04:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020358
name: Positive stool Cyclospora cayetanensis oocyst test
def: "Detection of Cyclospora cayetanensis oocysts in a stool specimen by microscopy." [PMID:15872269]
comment: Cyclospora cayetanensis is a coccidian protozoan parasite of the human small intestine. The transmission stage of Cyclospora, known as an oocyst, is spherical and 8 to 10 micrometers in diameter. Unsporulated oocysts are shed into the environment with the feces of infected individuals. Oocysts undergo sporulation, becoming infective within a few days or weeks, depending upon environmental conditions. Infection may result when sporulated oocysts are ingested, primarily through contaminated water or food. Diagnosis usually involves microscopic examination of stool specimens for the presence of oocysts.
is_a: HP:0034866 ! Positive stool infectious agent test
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-10T05:20:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020359
name: Anti-nucleosome antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that are directed exclusively (or predominantly) against nucleosomes or subnucleosomal structures, consisting of DNA plus core histones." [PMID:11892702, PMID:24804269]
comment: The term nucleosome defines a basic unit of chromatin. Each nucleosome consists of 146 base pairs of double stranded DNA, wrapped twice around a histone octamer, a protein core. A histone octamer consists of two molecules each of histones H2A, H2B, H3, and H4. In a chromatin, nucleosomes are connected by 15-80 base pairs of linker DNA, to which histone H1 is attached. Anti-dsDNA and anti-histone antibodies (AHA) belong to the nucleosome family as do anti-nuc specific antibodies, since nucleosomes share several common epitopes with dsDNA and histones. Nucleosome specific antibodies do not react with the individual components of the nucleosome, that is, DNA and histones, but recognize conformational epitopes resulting from interactions between the DNA and histone.
is_a: HP:0020356 ! Antichromatin antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-08-10T08:57:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0020360
name: Decreased circulating insulin-like growth factor binding protein 1 concentration
def: "The concentration of insulin-like growth factor binding protein 1 in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:42353827]
comment: Insulin-like growth factor-binding protein 1 (IGFBP-1) is a member of the highly conserved IGFBP family, which comprises six homologous proteins (IGFBP-1 through IGFBP-6). IGFBP-1 contributes to the regulation of IGFs for metabolism and growth and has IGF-independent actions.
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2026-09-01T06:19:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025002
name: Abnormal cecum morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the cecum, which is the proximal blind pouch of the ascending colon, is located at the ileocecal junction in the right iliac fossa." [PMID:29261962]
synonym: "Abnormal caecum morphology" EXACT uk_spelling []
