[Term]
id: HP:0025088
name: Onychomadesis
def: "Complete shedding (separation) of the nail from the proximal matrix. Onychomadesis is the proximal separation of the nail plate from the nail matrix due to a temporary cessation of nail growth." [PMID:24882996, PMID:25473242, PMID:28207011]
comment: Onychomadesis is defined as proximal nail plate separation from the nail matrix and nail bed caused by a temporary arrest in nail matrix activity, and may present as a Beau's line.
is_a: HP:0001806 ! Onycholysis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-24T00:35:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025089
name: Feculent vomiting
def: "Vomiting of material that is of fecal origin." []
comment: Feculent vomiting is usually due to mechanical intestinal obstruction but it can be due to paralytic obstruction (adynamic ileus).
synonym: "Faecal vomiting" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Fecal vomiting" EXACT []
synonym: "Stercoraceous vomiting" EXACT []
synonym: "Vomiting faecal matter" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Vomiting fecal matter" EXACT []
