[Term]
id: HP:0025103
name: Umbilicated nodule
def: "A type of skin nodule that has a small depression that resembles a navel (i.e., is umbilicated)." [PMID:24050295]
is_a: HP:0200036 ! Skin nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-28T07:30:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025104
name: Capillary malformation
def: "A capillary malformation is a flat, sharply defined vascular stain of the skin. It may cover a large surface area or it may be scattered and appear as little islands of color. In a capillary maformation, the predominant vessels are small, slow-flow vessels (i.e., arterioles and postcapillary venules)." [PMID:22483320, PMID:25864701]
comment: There are many different classifications, and some authors treat the term capillary malformation as being synonymous with port wine stain (nevus flammeus). We refer to the detailed classification of Happle (PMID:25864701), which we do not completely follow.
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-28T23:39:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025105
name: Nevus anemicus
def: "A congenital skin lesion characterized by irregular hypopigmented macules that coalesce to form plaques and occur particularly on the chest. It is generally present at birth or develops in the first days of life. It is more common in females. Diagnosis is confirmed by applying gentle friction to the lesion and the surrounding skin and checking that the erythema produced in the healthy skin does not appear in the hypopigmented lesion. This pale macule becomes more conspicuous when the lesion and its surroundings are rubbed. The margin of the naevus is ill-defined and consists of an archipelago of small anemic spots." [PMID:22483320, PMID:25864701]
synonym: "Naevus anaemicus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025104 ! Capillary malformation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-28T23:49:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025106
name: Nevus roseus
def: "A variant of port-wine stain characterized by a pale red or even pink tone, in contrast to the darker hue of the port-wine stain. By analogy with the term port-wine stain, this variant rose-wine stain, or nevus roseus. Nevus roseus, however, cannot be definitely diagnosed until adulthood as port-wine stains are sometimes pink in children. While the natural history of port-wine stains includes hypertrophy, darkening, and nodularity, nevus roseus remains unchanged for life." [PMID:22483320, PMID:25864701]
is_a: HP:0025104 ! Capillary malformation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-28T23:53:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025107
name: Cutis marmorata telangiectatica congenita
def: "A congenital vascular malformation that presents as localized or generalized erythematous-telangiectatic lesions with a reticular pattern; the lesions are almost always present at birth or develop in the first days of life. Cutis marmorata telangiectatica congenita (CMTC) appears as marble-like pattern (mottling) on the surface of the skin. In contrast to cutis marmorata, the marbling is more severe and always visible." [PMID:22483320, PMID:25864701]
is_a: HP:0025104 ! Capillary malformation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-29T00:22:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025108
name: Angioma serpentinum
def: "Angioma serpiginosum consists of punctate, tightly packed telangiectatic lesions. Characteristic histopathological features are dilated and tortuous capillaries involving the uppermost part of the dermis." [PMID:25864701]
comment: Two different forms can be distinguished. Diffuse, non-segmental angioma serpiginosum occurs as a hereditary trait, and autosomal dominant transmission is presently assumed.
is_a: HP:0025104 ! Capillary malformation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-29T00:31:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025109
name: Reduced red cell pyruvate kinase level
def: "Decrease in the level of pyruvate kinase (PK) within erythrocytes. PK catalyzes the reaction: ATP + pyruvate = ADP + phosphoenolpyruvate." [PMID:7949104]
synonym: "Reduced erythrocyte pyruvate kinase activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030272 ! Abnormal erythrocyte enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-10-29T00:37:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025110
name: Placoid macular lesion
def: "Large yellow/white, sharply delineated lesion, typically of inflammatory nature, involving the macula, more specifically at the outer retinal level (RPE/photoreceptor)." []
is_a: HP:0030500 ! Yellow/white macular lesion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-11-01T01:20:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025111
name: Acquired aphakia
def: "Absence of the crystalline lens in the eye known to be the result of a non-congenital condition, e.g., following surgical removal of the lens for cataracts or trauma." []
is_a: HP:6001302 ! Aphakia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-08-31T15:32:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025112
name: Auditory sensitivity
def: "Decreased tolerance to sound." []
comment: Sound sensitivity impliees a difficulty tolerating sounds which do not seem loud or unpleasant to others.
synonym: "Noise sensitivity" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8430-6039, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4422-1708, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3777-1389]
is_a: HP:5200058 ! Sensory hypersensitivity
