property_value: terms:date "2025-10-20T12:36:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025188
name: Retinal vasculitis
def: "Inflammation of retinal blood vessels as manifested by perivascular sheathing or cuffing, vascular leakage and/or occlusion. It can affect veins, arteries or both." [PMID:38925285]
comment: This term refers to the appearance of the retinal vessels on fundoscopy or other investigations. Retinal vasculitis may be associated with other manifestations such as visual impairment.
is_a: HP:0008046 ! Abnormal retinal vascular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-12-04T22:37:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025189
name: Hypnic jerks
def: "Hypnic jerks are characterized by sudden and brief (less than 1 second), non-periodic simultaneous contractions of the whole body or one or more extremities at the onset of sleep." [PMID:26329450]
comment: Although hypnic jerks are generally benign, there have been increasing reports of excessive hypnic jerks in neurological disorders such as Parkinsonism, migraine, and brainstem lesions and children with neurologic disorders.
synonym: "Sleep starts" EXACT []
is_a: HP:5200300 ! Abnormal movement during sleep
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-20T12:48:37Z" xsd:dateTime

