[Term]
id: HP:0025269
name: Panic attack
def: "A sudden episode of intense fear in a situation where there is no danger or apparent cause." []
comment: The panic attack is accompanied by symptoms such as palpitations, sweating, and chills or hot flushes. There may be a sensation of dyspnea (feeling out of breath), chest pain, or abdominal distress. Some individuals with panic attacks may experience depersonalization, a fear of going crazy, or a fear of dying.
synonym: "Panic attack" EXACT layperson []
