[Term]
id: HP:0025320
name: Leakage of dye on fundus fluorescein angiography
def: "Leakage of fluorescein dye observed upon retinal fluorescein angiography. Areas of leakage can be appreciated as showing gradual enlargement with blurring of margins." []
comment: Leakage can be caused by incompetent blood vessels such as with choroidal or diabetic neovascularization. Alternatively, leakage can be associated with a diseased retinal pigment epithelium resulting in leakage of fluorescein from the choroid.
synonym: "Fluorescein leakage" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030604 ! Abnormal fundus fluorescein angiography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-25T14:52:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025321
name: Copper accumulation in liver
def: "An anomalous build up of copper (Cu) in the liver." []
synonym: "Liver copper accumulation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034644 ! Abnormal liver metabolite concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-02-03T11:46:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025322
name: Venous occlusion
def: "Blockage of venous return (flow of blood from the periphery back towards the right atrium) in a vein." []
is_a: HP:0030846 ! Abnormality of venous physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-02-03T12:05:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025323
name: Abnormal arterial physiology
