[Term]
id: HP:0025430
name: High-pitched cry
def: "A type of crying in an abnormally high-pitched voice." []
comment: This type of cry may be observed with cerebral irritability due to factors such as meningitis, hydrocephalus, or kernicterus. High-pitched cry may also be observed with other conditions including Cornelia-de-Lange syndrome.
is_a: HP:0025429 ! Abnormal cry
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-04-23T12:59:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025431
name: Staccato cry
def: "A type of cry that is abnormal because it is consists of unusually shortened and detached vocalizations." []
is_a: HP:0025429 ! Abnormal cry
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-04-23T13:07:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025432
name: Acanthoma
def: "A benign epithelial skin tumor manifesting as a slightly elevated circular plaque or nodule with a red, pink or brown color and a diameter up to 22 mm." []
