[Term]
id: HP:0025485
name: Vaginal adenosis
def: "Vaginal adenosis is defined by the presence of metaplastic cervical or endometrial epithelium within the vaginal wall, thought to be derived from persistent Müllerian (synonymous with paramesonephric) epithelium islets in postembryonic life." [PMID:9764164]
comment: Spontaneous vaginal adenosis appears to be a fairly common (present in about 10% of adult women) but mostly insignificant coincidental finding. In women prenatally exposed to diethylstilboestrol (DES), vaginal adenosis may arise in up to 90% and is associated with a high risk of vaginal carcinoma.
is_a: HP:0000142 ! Abnormal vagina morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T16:40:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025486
name: Fused labia majora
def: "The outer labia are sealed together." []
is_a: HP:0012881 ! Abnormal labia majora morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T17:00:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025487
name: Abnormal bladder morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of the bladder." []
synonym: "Abnormality of bladder morphology" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000014 ! Abnormality of the bladder
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T17:07:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025488
name: Detrusor sphincter dyssynergia
def: "A urodynamic anomaly characterized by bladder outlet obstruction from detrusor muscle contraction with concomitant involuntary urethral sphincter activation." [PMID:26904418]
comment: Detrusor sphincter dyssynergia (DSD) is associated with neurologic conditions such as spinal cord injury, multiple sclerosis, and spina bifida and some of these neurogenic bladder patients with DSD may be at risk for autonomic dysreflexia, recurrent urinary tract infections, or upper tract compromise if the condition is not followed and treated appropriately. It is diagnosed most commonly during the voiding phase of urodynamic studies using EMG recordings and voiding cystourethrograms, although urethral pressure monitoring could also potentially be used.
is_a: HP:0000009 ! Functional abnormality of the bladder
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T17:09:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025489
name: Bladder duplication
def: "A congenital anomaly characterized by the presence of two bladders." [PMID:25657554]
is_a: HP:0025487 ! Abnormal bladder morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T17:16:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025490
name: Myocardial bridging
def: "A congenital variant of a coronary artery in which a portion of an epicardial coronary artery (most frequently the middle segment of the left anterior descending artery) takes an intramuscular course." [PMID:25999138]
comment: Myocardial bridging, in which a tunneled segment of the artery under the bridge of overlying myocardium frequently results in vessel compression during systole. While frequently asymptomatic, this condition in many cases may be responsible for adverse complications including angina, myocardial ischemia, acute coronary syndromes, left ventricular dysfunction, arrhythmias, and even sudden cardiac death.
synonym: "Intramyocardial coronary artery course" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011686 ! Abnormal coronary artery course
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:08:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025491
name: Venous stenosis
def: "Narrowing of a vein due to intimal hyperplasia and fibrosis." []
comment: Venous stenosis can be secondary to placement of central venous catheters, pacemaker leads, hemodialysis catheters, prior radiation, trauma, or extrinsic compression by musculoskeletal structures.
is_a: HP:0002624 ! Abnormal venous morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:22:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025492
name: Microcoria
def: "A small pupil (typically diameter less than 2 mm) that dilates poorly or not at all in response to topically administered mydriatic drugs." [PMID:25772937]
is_a: HP:0000615 ! Abnormal pupil morphology
is_a: HP:0007700 ! Ocular anterior segment dysgenesis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:32:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025493
name: Palmoplantar erythema
def: "Redness of the skin of the palm of the hand and the sole of the foot caused by hyperemia of the capillaries in the lower layers of the skin." []
is_a: HP:0010783 ! Erythema
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:34:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025494
name: Coated aorta
def: "Regular circumferential periaortic fibrosis involving the whole aorta and leading to a coated aorta appearance on computed tomography scans" [PMID:25017251]
comment: This feature is characteristic of Erdheim Chester disease.
is_a: HP:0001679 ! Abnormal aortic morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:37:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025495
name: Descending aorta hypoplasia
def: "Significant luminal narrowing of a long segment of the descending aorta." [PMID:12368748, PMID:24516866]
comment: Coarctation of the aorta is defined as significant luminal narrowing of the aorta that produces hemodynamically significant obstruction to the flow of blood. This process may affect a short isolated segment of the aorta or a longer and more diffuse segment. When longer segments of the aorta are narrowed, the term hypoplasia is often used. Much less common than segmental coarctation, aortic hypoplasia has been described in all portions of the thoracic and abdominal aorta.
is_a: HP:0031934 ! Abnormal descending aorta morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-14T19:49:11Z" xsd:dateTime

