[Term]
id: HP:0025523
name: Abnormal morphology of the chordae tendinae of the mitral valve
def: "A structural anomaly of the chordae tendinae of the mitral valve, whose main function is to transmit the contraction and relaxation of the papillary muscles during the cardiac cycle, thus ensuring the closing of the leaflets of the mitral valve." [PMID:23304176]
is_a: HP:0001633 ! Abnormal mitral valve morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-17T23:44:02Z" xsd:dateTime

