[Term]
id: HP:0025530
name: Xanthomas of the palmar creases
def: "The presence of multiple xanthomas (xanthomata) in the skin distributed in the creases of the palm of the hand. Xanthomas are yellowish, firm, lipid-laden nodules in the skin." []
synonym: "Xanthoma palmare striatum" EXACT []
synonym: "Xanthoma striatum palmare" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000991 ! Xanthomatosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-18T00:34:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025531
name: Harlequin phenomenon
def: "The Harlequin phenomenon consists of a sudden change in skin color, resulting in two different body colors, one on each half of the body." [PMID:21575077]
comment: The Harlequin phenomenon (HF) is most common in the newborn and can be a generalized phenomenon or only involve a specific body area. The HF of the newborn is thought to be secondary to a relative hypothalamic control immaturity of the sympathetic peripheral vascular tonus, although it has also been described in other age groups, primarily located to the face and neck and mostly caused by a sympathetic disautonomy. While certainly peculiar, the HF is a benign event in the newborn.
is_a: HP:0011122 ! Abnormal skin physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-18T00:38:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025532
name: Positive pathergy test
def: "With the pathergy test, a small, sterile needle is inserted into the skin of the forearm. The site of injectionis circuled and observed after one and two days. If a small red bump or pustule at the site of needle insertion occurs, the pathergy test is considered to have a positive (abnormal) result." []
comment: A positive pathergy test indicates the immune system is overreacting to a minor injury. A positive test result can be seen in Behcet disease and other conditions.
is_a: HP:0011122 ! Abnormal skin physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-18T00:41:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025533
name: Peau d'orange
comment: A swelling of the skin in which the skin is tethered by the sweat ducts it contains producing tiny dimples. THe overall appearance is said to resemble the skin (peal) of an orange.
is_a: HP:0000969 ! Edema
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-18T01:05:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025534
name: Ocular melanocytosis
def: "A congenital lesion of the sclera characterized by unilateral patchy but extensive slate-gray or bluish discoloration of the sclera . The conjunctiva are spared." []
comment: In ocular melanocytosis, Intraocular pigmentation is also increased, which contributes to a higher incidence of glaucoma and increases the risk of malignant melanoma.
synonym: "Melanosis oculi" EXACT []
synonym: "Ocular melanosis" EXACT []
