property_value: terms:date "2017-12-14T13:58:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025572
name: Punctal stenosis
def: "Punctal stenosis is a condition in which the external opening of the lacrimal canaliculus is narrowed or occluded." [PMID:22848141]
comment: Epiphora is a common complaint encountered by ophthalmologists, with a broad differential diagnosis. One of the least discussed etiologies of epiphora is stenosis of the external lacrimal punctum. When it occurs, the most common presenting symptom is tearing, but patients may have vague complaints of ocular discomfort.
synonym: "Lacrimal punctum stenosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Stenosis of the lacrimal punctum" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011479 ! Abnormal lacrimal punctum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-14T14:21:45Z" xsd:dateTime

