[Term]
id: HP:0025606
name: Abnormal medial rectus muscle physiology
def: "A functional anomaly of the medial rectus muscle, an extraocular muscle that is innervated by the inferior division of the oculomotor nerve and whose sole action is the adduction of the eyeball." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
