[Term]
id: HP:0025682
name: Crouch gait
def: "A gait disturbance that is characterized by excessive ankle dorsiflexion, knee and hip flexion during the stance phase." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157, PMID:26709688, PMID:28279852]
comment: Crouch gait may be observed in individuals affected by cerebral palsy.
