[Term]
id: HP:0025683
name: Abnormal amyloid beta 42 peptide CSF concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of amyloid beta 42 peptide in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF). Amyloid beta is a peptide of 36-43 amino acids that is processed from the Amyloid precursor protein. ABeta42, which is 42 amino acids in length, is the longer form." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2307-1226, PMID:27025652]
comment: The amyloid cascade hypothesis has been the prevailing paradigm for understanding Alzheimer's disease (AD) pathogenesis. According to this hypothesis, the fibrillogenic 42-amino acid beta amyloid peptide (Abeta42) aggregates into toxic beta-sheet rich assemblies, triggering a cascade of neurotoxic events, including intracellular tau accumulation as neurofibrillary tangles and neuroinflammation, which ultimately result in neurodegeneration and subsequent cognitive impairment.
is_a: HP:0025688 ! Abnormal amyloid beta peptide CSF concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-01-31T04:50:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025684
name: Decreased amyloid beta 42 peptide CSF concentration
def: "A reduction from the normal concentration of amyloid beta 42 peptide in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2307-1226, PMID:15992827, PMID:31391004]
is_a: HP:0025683 ! Abnormal amyloid beta 42 peptide CSF concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-01-31T04:50:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025685
name: Increased amyloid beta 42 peptide CSF concentration
def: "An elevation above the normal concentration of amyloid beta 42 peptide in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2307-1226]
is_a: HP:0025683 ! Abnormal amyloid beta 42 peptide CSF concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-01-31T04:50:28Z" xsd:dateTime

