[Term]
id: HP:0025754
name: Reduced beta-hexosaminidase A activity
def: "The concentration or activity of beta hexosaminidase A in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." []
comment: The HEXA gene encodes the alpha subunit of hexosaminidase A (EC 3.2.1.52), a lysosomal enzyme involved in the breakdown of gangliosides. There are 2 isoenzymes of hexosaminidase: Hex-A and Hex-B. Hex-A has the structure alpha-beta, while Hex-B has the structure beta-beta.
synonym: "Hexosaminidase A deficiency" EXACT []
