is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: HP:0010975

[Term]
id: HP:0025807
name: Decreased natural killer cell degranulation
def: "Abnormal decrease of NK cell degranulation in response to stimulation, commonly measured through surface CD107a expression in response to cocultivation with a murine cell line. Other methods may be used by different laboratories." [PMID:32569607]
is_a: HP:0012177 ! Abnormal natural killer cell physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-17T10:49:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025808
name: Decreased natural killer cell-induced killing of target cells
def: "Abnormal decrease of natural killer (NK) cell cytotoxicity. Assaying NK cytotoxicity involves coculturing NK calls with target cells and measuring the extent of cell death by methods such as luminescence-based (luciferase) assays, biophotonic assays, and flow cytometry-based Cr-release assays." [PMID:22258454]
is_a: HP:0012177 ! Abnormal natural killer cell physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-17T11:44:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025809
name: Generalized scaling
def: "Desquamation (scaling) involving nearly all of the surface of the skin." [PMID:24506793]
comment: Figure 1A of PMID:24506793 shows an infant with generalized (fine) scaling of skin.
synonym: "Diffuse desquamation" EXACT []
synonym: "Diffuse scaling" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040189 ! Scaling skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-17T16:10:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025810
name: Ichthyosis linearis circumflexa
def: "A type of ichthyosis characterized by migratory, annular and polycyclic erythematous patches with double-edged scales at the periphery of the lesions." [PMID:25710899]
comment: The erythematous patch (flat area of redness 1 cm or more in width) that is ring-shaped (annular) or serpiginous (with multiple ring-shaped lesions (polycyclic). The lesions are bordered by two distinct rings of scale at their outer edges (double-edged). The distribution of the lesions changes with time (migratory). Ichthyosis linearis circumflexa (ILC) may rarely be observed as an isolated lesion, but is a characteristic manifestation of Netherton syndrome. Lesions are often described as serpiginous scaling or double-edged scaling.
synonym: "Double-edged scaling" EXACT []
synonym: "Serpiginous scaling" BROAD []
is_a: HP:0008064 ! Ichthyosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-17T16:14:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025811
name: Trichorrhexis invaginata
def: "A type of hair shaft dysmorphology in which the proximal part of the hair shaft overlaps the distal part, showing a bamboo-like appearance. This feature is pathognomic for Netherton syndrome, and can be ascertained by light microscopy." [PMID:32029302, PMID:34659759]
comment: Mostly, these hairs are fragile, short, and brittle. A longitudinal twist in the hair shaft may be seen, known as a helical hair.
synonym: "Bamboo hair" EXACT []
synonym: "Helical hair" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003328 ! Abnormal hairshaft morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-17T16:19:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025812
name: Seborrheic scales on scalp
def: "Fine white-greasy scales on scalp." []
comment: Seborrhoeic scales on scalp are mainly related to overgrowth of Malassezia Furfur species in association with seborrheic dermatitis, but are also seen in many other diseases. Seborrheic scales can also be seen on different parts of the body and face.
synonym: "Seborrhoeic scales on scalp" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0001051 ! Seborrheic dermatitis
is_a: HP:0040189 ! Scaling skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:23:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025813
name: Eyebrow scaling skin
def: "Loss of the outer layer of the epidermis in the area of the eyebrow in large, scale-like flakes." []
comment: Size of scaling can be variable from fine-white to thick scaling. Sscales on eyebrows are often related to seborrheic dermatitis, psoriasis, ichthyosis, etc.
synonym: "Scales on eyebrows" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040189 ! Scaling skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:44:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025814
name: Patchy stratum granulosum of epidermis
def: "The stratum granulosum of the epidermis (granular layer) displays areas of discontinuity." [PMID:11123448]
synonym: "Patchy granular layer of the skin" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0033806 ! Abnormal epidermis stratum granulosum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:47:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025815
name: Absent stratum granulosum of epidermis
def: "The stratum granulosum of the epidermis (granular layer) cannot be observed." []
comment: This finding can be ascertained by microscopy of a skin biopsy specimen and may be acquired or congenital.
synonym: "Absent granular layer of skin" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033806 ! Abnormal epidermis stratum granulosum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:49:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025816
name: Hypogranulosis
def: "The height (thickness) of the stratum granulosum of the epidermis (granular layer) is below the lower limit of normal but the stratum granulosum is visible." [PMID:34611907]
synonym: "Diminished granular layer" EXACT []
synonym: "Reduced granular layer" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033806 ! Abnormal epidermis stratum granulosum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:54:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025817
name: Psoriasiform acanthosis
def: "A type of epidermal acanthosis characterized by regular elongated rete ridges." []
comment: Because of elongated rete ridges, this is different from common epidermal acanthosis. The etiology in cases with psoriasiform acanthosis is wide, such as: psoriasis, pustular psoriasis, Reiter syndrome, pityriasis rubra pilaris, parapsoriasis, lichen simplex chronicus, erythroderma, mycosis fungoides, chronic candidosis, Norwegian scabies, Bowen disease, clear cell acanthoma, lamellar ichthyosis, pityriasis rosea, acrodermatitis enteropathica, and secondary syphilis. In psoriasis, usually characterized by psoriasiform acanthosis, no significant hyperplasia can be seen in early lesions. Diagnosis is often made with other histological features and with clinicopathological correlation.
synonym: "Psoriasiform epidermal hyperplasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Psoriasiform epidermis" EXACT []
synonym: "Psoriasiform hyperplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025092 ! Epidermal acanthosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T15:58:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025818
name: Intraepidermal microabscess formation
def: "Infiltrating neutrophils in the epidermis, mostly into the stratum corneum. Characteristic for psoriasis." [PMID:31942132]
comment: In the stratum corneum, they are called Munro microabscesses, often present in psoriasis and geographic tongue. In pustular psoriasis, the neutrophils extend to the suprabasal layer, forming spongiosis, so-called Kogoj spongiform pustule.
is_a: HP:0011124 ! Abnormal epidermal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T16:10:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025819
name: Palmoplantar peeling
def: "Splitting within the the upper lyer (stratum corneum) of the epidermis clinically characterized by shedding of dead cells from the outermost layer of skin." []
synonym: "Dyshidrosis lamellosa sicca" RELATED []
synonym: "Exfoliative keratolysis" RELATED []
synonym: "Focal palmoplantar peeling" RELATED []
synonym: "Palmoplantar desquamation" EXACT []
synonym: "Palmoplantar keratolysis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100872 ! Abnormality of the plantar skin of foot
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T16:20:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025820
name: Offspring of consanguineous relationship
def: "The parents of the index patient are related as second cousins or closer." []
comment: Consanguinity has a major role in congenital and genetic diseases.
synonym: "Consanguineous" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032316 ! Family history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-24T16:26:47Z" xsd:dateTime

