property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T12:20:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025823
name: Positive provocative functional shoulder test
def: "Abnormal result of a physical test of the shoulder that attempts to provoke pain in order to diagnosis a specific injury." [PMID:36277881]
is_a: HP:0033129 ! Abnormal shoulder physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T12:29:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025824
name: Decreased neutrophil phagocytosis
def: "Abnormal decrease of neutrophil phagocytic activity, commonly measured after stimulation with E. coli using flow cytometry." [PMID:33679791]
is_a: HP:0011990 ! Abnormal neutrophil physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-27T05:20:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025825
name: Decreased neutrophil adhesion
alt_id: HP:0033798
def: "Abnormal decrease of neutrophil adhesion capacity, commonly measured as surface expression of CD18, CD11a or CD11b using flow cytometry." [PMID:19037827, PMID:23351991, PMID:25045887]
comment: Neutrophil firm adhesion to endothelial cells (EC) is a highly regulated process and plays an essential role in inflammatory responses3,4. The firm adhesion of neutrophil follows initial neutrophil rolling and capture on the EC and ultimately can result in transmigration in vivo.
synonym: "Impaired leukocyte adhesion" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0011990 ! Abnormal neutrophil physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-27T05:27:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025826
name: Severely decreased neutrophil count
def: "Severe decrease in circulating neutrophils, usually characterized as fewer than 500 neutrophils per microlitre." []
is_a: HP:0001875 ! Decreased total neutrophil count
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-27T05:31:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025827
name: Abnormal Th1 T cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of Th1 cells, commonly characterized through the intracellular synthesis of IFNg or surface expression of CXCR3, measured as proportion of total CD3+CD4+ T cells, usually after stimulation. The stimulation is usually unspecific and may include the use of anti-CD3 beads or antibodies or the use of phorbol-12-myristate-13-acetate (PMA) with ionomycin. Length of incubation and strength of stimulation may vary between laboratories." [PMID:10579123]
comment: Type 1 T helper (Th1) cells produce interferon-gamma, interleukin (IL)-2, and tumour necrosis factor (TNF)-beta, which activate macrophages and are responsible for cell-mediated immunity and phagocyte-dependent protective responses. This term is placed under physiology because the cells are typically measured following stimulation.
is_a: HP:0011840 ! Abnormal T cell physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-27T06:18:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025828
name: Increased Th1 T cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase of Th1 cells, commonly characterized through the intracellular synthesis of IFNg or surface expression of CXCR3, measured as proportion of total CD3+CD4+ T cells, usually after stimulation. The stimulation is usually unspecific and may include the use of anti-CD3 beads or antibodies or the use of phorbol-12-myristate-13-acetate (PMA) with ionomycin. Length of incubation and strength of stimulation may vary between laboratories." [PMID:10579123]
is_a: HP:0025827 ! Abnormal Th1 T cell proportion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-27T06:20:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0025829
name: Decreased Th1 T cell proportion
def: "Abnormal decrease of Th1 cells, commonly characterized through the intracellular synthesis of IFNg or surface expression of CXCR3, measured as proportion of total CD3+CD4+ T cells, usually after stimulation. The stimulation is usually unspecific and may include the use of anti-CD3 beads or antibodies or the use of phorbol-12-myristate-13-acetate (PMA) with ionomycin. Length of incubation and strength of stimulation may vary between laboratories." [PMID:10579123]
