[Term]
id: HP:0030014
name: Female sexual dysfunction
def: "A problem occurring during any phase of the female sexual response cycle that prevents the individual from experiencing satisfaction from the sexual activity" [PMID:26953829]
is_a: HP:0030012 ! Abnormal female reproductive system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030015
name: Female anorgasmia
def: "The persistent of recurrent difficulty, delay in, or absence of attaining orgasm following sufficient sexual stimulation and arousal." [PMID:16391543]
synonym: "Female orgasmic disorder" BROAD layperson []
is_a: HP:0030014 ! Female sexual dysfunction
is_a: HP:0046502 ! Anorgasmia

[Term]
id: HP:0030016
name: Dyspareunia
def: "Recurrent or persistent genital pain associated with sexual intercourse." [PMID:1225983, PMID:16391543]
comment: In females, dyspareunia can develop secondary to medical problems such as vestibulitis, vaginal atrophy, or vaginal infection. It can be either physiologically or psychologically based, or a combination of the two. In males, dyspareunia may be related to conditions of the prepuce, glans penis, penile shaft, testicles, and urethra and prostate gland.
is_a: HP:0000080 ! Abnormality of reproductive system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030017
name: Vaginismus
def: "Recurrent or persistent involuntary spasms of the musculature of the outer third of the vagina that interferes with vaginal penetration, and which causes personal distress." [PMID:16391543]
comment: Vaginismus usually develops as a conditioned response to painful penetration, or secondary to psychological/emotional factors.
synonym: "Myalgia of pelvic floor" EXACT []
synonym: "Pelvic floor myalgia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030014 ! Female sexual dysfunction

