def: "Western blot reveals reduced calpain-3 protein in the muscle biopsy tissue." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang]
synonym: "Reduced muscle fibre calpain-3" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0030119 ! Abnormal muscle fiber calpain-3

[Term]
id: HP:0030122
name: Reduced muscle fiber perlecan
def: "Immunohistochemistry reveals reduced perlecan protein in the muscle biopsy. Perlecan is a basement membrane-specific heparan sulfate proteoglycan core protein (HSPG) also known as heparan sulfate proteoglycan 2 (HSPG2)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Reduced muscle fibre perlecan" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0030089 ! Abnormal muscle fiber protein expression

[Term]
id: HP:0030123
name: Abnormal muscle fiber lamin A/C
def: "A deviation from the normal amount of lamin A/C in muscle tissue. The LMNA gene gives rise to at least three splicing isoforms including the two main isoforms, lamin A and lamin C. These are constitutive components of the fibrous nuclear lamina and have different roles, ranging from mechanical nuclear membrane maintenance to gene regulation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24843229]
synonym: "Abnormal muscle fibre lamin A/C" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0030089 ! Abnormal muscle fiber protein expression

[Term]
id: HP:0030124
name: Reduced muscle fiber lamin A/C
def: "A decreased amount of lamin A/C in muscle tissue. This feature can be shown by immunohistochemistry or Western blotting of muscle tissue." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_htrang, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Reduced muscle fibre lamin A/C" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0030123 ! Abnormal muscle fiber lamin A/C

[Term]
id: HP:0030125
name: Sacralization of the fifth lumbar vertebra
def: "A congenital anomaly, in which the transverse process of the last lumbar vertebra (L5) fuses to the sacrum on one side or both, or to ilium, or both." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:UToronto_bgallinger]
comment: This anomaly is observed at about 3.5 percent of people and is usually bilateral.
synonym: "L5 sacralization" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002948 ! Vertebral fusion

[Term]
id: HP:0030126
name: Abnormal endometrium morphology
def: "An anomaly of the inner mucous membrane of the uterus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormality of the endometrium" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031105 ! Abnormal uterus morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030127
name: Endometriosis
alt_id: HP:0030013
def: "The growth of endometrial tissue outside the uterus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25221341]
comment: The main manifestations of endometriosis are chronic upper abdominal pain and infertility. Endometriosis occurs primarily on the pelvic peritoneum, ovaries, and rectovaginal septum, and in rare cases on the diaphragm, pleura, and pericardium. Endometriosis affects 6 to 10% of women of reproductive age, 50 to 60% of women and teenage girls with pelvic pain, and up to 50% of women with infertility. Peritoneal disease, which is dependent on estrogen for growth, derives from retrograde menstruation of steroid hormone sensitive endometrial cells and tissues, which implant on peritoneal surfaces and elicit an inflammatory response. This response is accompanied by angiogenesis, adhesions, fibrosis, scarring, neuronal infiltration, and anatomical distortion resulting in pain and infertility.
is_a: HP:0030012 ! Abnormal female reproductive system physiology
is_a: HP:0030126 ! Abnormal endometrium morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030129
name: Impaired ristocetin cofactor assay activity
def: "Abnormal response to ristocetin as manifested by reduced or lacking aggregation of platelets upon addition of ristocetin to platelet-poor plasma." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
comment: Ristocetin induced platelet agglutination (RIPA) is similar to the Ristocetin Cofactor Assay but RIPA measures platelet agglutination induced by Ristocetin-mediated VWF binding to the platelet Gp1b receptor. WITH RIPA, the ristocetin is added directly to the patient's platelet rich plasma and there are no serial dilutions of the plasma sample.
is_a: HP:0012146 ! Abnormality of von Willebrand factor

[Term]
id: HP:0030130
name: Impaired von Willebrand factor collagen binding activity
def: "Reduced ability of von Willebrand factor (vWF) to bind collagen. Abnormal response to collagen as manifested by reduced or lacking ability of plasma von WIllebrand Factor to bind collagen. An ELISA-based assay is typically used; the test is sensitive to loss of von Willebrand Factor high molecular weight multimers." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller, PMID:18809794]
comment: This abnormality may be seen in von Willebrand disease type 1, type 2A, type 2B, and type 3.
is_a: HP:0012146 ! Abnormality of von Willebrand factor

[Term]
id: HP:0030131
name: Abnormal von Willebrand factor multimer distribution
def: "Deviation from the normal von Willebrand factor multimer pattern." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
is_a: HP:0012146 ! Abnormality of von Willebrand factor

[Term]
id: HP:0030132
name: Absence of large von Willebrand factor multimers
def: "Absence of large von Willebrand Factor multimers on gel electrophoresis." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
comment: Type 2B von Willebrand disease is characterized by lack of large von Willebrand factor multimers with an otherwise normal von Willebrand factor multimer pattern.
is_a: HP:0030131 ! Abnormal von Willebrand factor multimer distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030133
name: Abnormal presence of ultra-large von Willebrand factor multimers
def: "Detection of abnormal ultra-large von Willebrand factor multimers." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller, PMID:11756169, PMID:25983111]
comment: The type Vicenza variant of von Willebrand disease (VWD) is characterized by a low plasma von Willebrand factor (VWF) level and supranormal VWF multimers.
is_a: HP:0030131 ! Abnormal von Willebrand factor multimer distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030134
name: Total absence von Willebrand factor multimers
def: "Complete absence of all von Willebrand factor multimers." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
is_a: HP:0030131 ! Abnormal von Willebrand factor multimer distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030135
name: Absence of intermediate von Willebrand factor multimers
def: "Lack of intermediate von Willebrand Factor multimers on gel electrophoresis." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
comment: Type 2A von Willebrand disease is characterized by the absence of large and intermediate von Willebrand Factor multimers on gel electrophoresis, with preservation of an otherwise normal multimer pattern.
is_a: HP:0030131 ! Abnormal von Willebrand factor multimer distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030136
name: Enhanced ristocetin cofactor assay activity
def: "Abnormal response to ristocetin as manifested by increased aggregation of platelets upon addition of low-dose ristocetin to platelet-rich plasma." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:cmiller]
comment: This abnormality is characteristic of type 2B von Willebrand disease.
is_a: HP:0012146 ! Abnormality of von Willebrand factor

