[Term]
id: HP:0030357
name: Small cell lung carcinoma
def: "Small cell lung cancer (SCLC) is a type of highly malignant lung cancer that is composed of small ovoid cells. In the past, SCLC was called oat cell carcinoma because the microscopic appearance of the cells was felt to resemble oats. SLCLC usually originates near the bronchi and in many cases may grow and metastasize quickly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Oat cell carcinoma of lung" EXACT []
synonym: "Oat cell lung cancer" EXACT []
synonym: "Small cell lung cancer" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100526 ! Neoplasm of the lung

[Term]
id: HP:0030358
name: Non-small cell lung carcinoma
synonym: "Non-small cell lung cancer" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100526 ! Neoplasm of the lung

[Term]
id: HP:0030359
name: Squamous cell lung carcinoma
def: "A type of non-small cell lung carcinoma that is derived from stratified squamous epithelial cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Four subtypes of squamous cell lung carcinoma exist: (i) papillary; (ii) clear cell; (iii) small cell (distinct from small cell lung cancer); and (iv) basaloid.
is_a: HP:0030358 ! Non-small cell lung carcinoma

[Term]
id: HP:0030360
name: Large cell lung carcinoma
def: "A type of non-small cell lung carcinoma that is derived from undifferentiated malignant neoplasms originating from transformed epithelial cells in the lung, and which is differentiate from small-cell lung carcinoma by the larger size of the anaplastic cells, a higher cytoplasmic-to-nuclear size ratio, and a lack of salt-and-pepper appearance of the chromatin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030358 ! Non-small cell lung carcinoma

[Term]
id: HP:0030361
name: Abnormal circulating icosanoid concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of icosanoid in the blood circulation." []
comment: Icosanoids (also known as eicosanoids) are signaling molecules derived from oxidation of 20-carbon fatty acids. Most are produced from arachidonic acid, a 20-carbon polyunsaturated fatty acid (5,8,11,14-eicosatetraenoic acid). The icosanoids include the prostaglandins, prostacyclins, thromboxanes, leukotrienes, and epoxyeicosatrienoic acids. Icosanoids have various roles in processes that regulate inflammation, fever, blood pressure, blood clotting, immune system function, reproductive processes and tissue growth, and the sleep/wake cycle.
synonym: "Abnormal icosanoid level" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormality of icosanoid metabolism" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011022 ! Abnormal circulating unsaturated fatty acid concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0030362
name: Reduced muscle carnitine level
def: "A reduction in the level of carnitine in muscle tissue." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:8174281, PMID:8472351]
comment: Carnitine deficiency may be observed in a systemic form or be limited to skeletal muscle tissue. Carnitine levels can be measured by assays of muscle tissue (biopsy). Alternatively, 1H-NMR spectroscopy can be used for qualitative measurement of muscle carnitine levels.
is_a: HP:0034370 ! Abnormal muscle tissue metabolite concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0030363
name: Primary Caesarian section
def: "Delivery by Caesarian section representing the first time the mother has delivered by Caesarian section." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0011410 ! Caesarean section

[Term]
id: HP:0030364
name: Secondary Caesarian section
def: "Delivery by Caesarian section representing where the mother has already had a previous Cesarean delivery, and this is a repeat Cesarean birth." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0011410 ! Caesarean section

[Term]
id: HP:0030365
name: Vaginal birth after Caesarean
def: "Vaginal birth after Caesarean (VBAC) refers to the situation where the mother has had a previous Cesarean delivery but has now delivered vaginally." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24104780]
is_a: HP:0001787 ! Abnormal delivery

[Term]
id: HP:0030366
name: Delivery by Odon device
def: "The Odon device is an instrument for assisted vaginal deliveries that is applied on the head of the baby and used to apply traction to assist the birth process." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23962177]
is_a: HP:0001787 ! Abnormal delivery

[Term]
id: HP:0030367
name: Finger hyperphalangy
def: "Hyperphalangy is a digit morphology in which increased numbers of phalanges are arranged linearly within a digit. That is, there is an accessory phalanx that is arranged linearly with the other phalanges." []
is_a: HP:0005918 ! Abnormal finger phalanx morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030368
name: Hyperphalangy of the 2nd finger
def: "An accessory phalanx of the index (second) finger that is arranged linearly with the other phalanges. Hyperphalangy of the index finger results from an accessory ossification center at the metacarpophalangeal joint, resulting in radial deviation of the index finger. Note that this term refers only to this type of hyperphalangy." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25480037, PMID:6540680]
synonym: "Hyperphalangy of index finger" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030367 ! Finger hyperphalangy

[Term]
id: HP:0030369
name: Induced vaginal delivery
def: "Vaginal delivery following induction of labor, a procedure used to stimulate uterine contractions during pregnancy before labor begins on its own." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0001787 ! Abnormal delivery

[Term]
id: HP:0030370
name: Abnormal naive B cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of the naive B cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD27-IgM+, measured as percentage of total B cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:32569607]
comment: Naive B cells represent one of the subtypes of B cells in the peripheral blood, and are B cells that have not been exposed to antigen
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of naive B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025539 ! Abnormal B cell subset distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030371
name: Increased naive B cell proportion
def: "The proportion of naive B cellsin the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal with respect to the reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:32569607]
synonym: "Increased proportion of naive B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030370 ! Abnormal naive B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030372
name: Decreased naive B cell proportion
def: "The proportion of naive B cellsin the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal with respect to the reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:32569607]
synonym: "Decreased proportion of naive B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030370 ! Abnormal naive B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030373
name: Abnormal memory B cell proportion
def: "A deviation of the normal proportion of memory B cells in circulation relative to total number of B cells. Memory B cells develop from naive B cells. Upon antigen rechallenge, memory B cells rapidly expand and differentiate into plasma cells under the cognate control of memory Th cells (Phase IV)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:15771579]
comment: Memory B cells can be defined as CD19+/CD27+ or CD20+/CD27+ cells in flow cytometry.
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of memory B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025539 ! Abnormal B cell subset distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030374
name: Decreased memory B cell proportion
def: "A reduction in the normal proportion of memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells. Memory B cells develop from naive B cells. Upon antigen rechallenge, memory B cells rapidly expand and differentiate into plasma cells under the cognate control of memory Th cells (Phase IV)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030373 ! Abnormal memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030375
name: Increased memory B cell proportion
def: "An elevation in the proportion of memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells. Memory B cells develop from naive B cells. Upon antigen rechallenge, memory B cells rapidly expand and differentiate into plasma cells under the cognate control of memory Th cells (Phase IV)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030373 ! Abnormal memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030376
name: Abnormal immature B cell proportion
def: "A deviation from normal proportion of immature B cells (CD19+/ CD21low) in circulation relative to total number of B cells. Immature B cells (IgM+) are still in final stages of development within the bone marrow. Naive B cells are those which have left the bone marrow, before they bind to the antigen for which they're specific (IgM+/IgD+)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD19+/CD21low B cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of immature B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025539 ! Abnormal B cell subset distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030377
name: Increased immature B cell proportion
def: "An elevation in the proportion above normal of immature B cells (CD19+/ CD21low) in circulation relative to total number of B cells. Immature B cells (IgM+) are still in final stages of development within the bone marrow. Naive B cells are those which have left the bone marrow, before they bind to the antigen for which they're specific (IgM+/IgD+)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Increased proportion of CD19+/CD21low B cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased proportion of immature B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030376 ! Abnormal immature B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030378
name: Decreased immature B cell proportion
def: "A reduction in normal proportion of immature B cells (CD19+/ CD21low)in circulation relative to total number of B cells. Immature B cells (IgM+) are still in final stages of development within the bone marrow. Naive B cells are those which have left the bone marrow, before they bind to the antigen for which they're specific (IgM+/IgD+)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Decreased proportion of CD19+/CD21low B cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Decreased proportion of immature B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030376 ! Abnormal immature B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030379
name: Abnormal transitional B cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of the transitional B cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD27-CD24hiCD38hi or CD27-IgMhiCD38hi, measured as percentage of total B cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23731328]
comment: B cells originate from precursors in the bone marrow, and the first cells which migrate to the peripheral blood have been classified as transitional B cells.
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD19+CD38+IgM+ cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of transitional B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025539 ! Abnormal B cell subset distribution

[Term]
id: HP:0030380
name: Decreased transitional B cell proportion
def: "Abnormal decrease of the transitional B cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD27-CD24hiCD38hi or CD27-IgMhiCD38hi, measured as percentage of total B cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Decreased proportion of CD19+CD38+IgM+ cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Decreased proportion of transitional B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030379 ! Abnormal transitional B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030381
name: Increased transitional B cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase of the transitional B cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD27-CD24hiCD38hi or CD27-IgMhiCD38hi, measured as percentage of total B cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Increased proportion of CD19+CD38+IgM+ cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased proportion of transitional B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030379 ! Abnormal transitional B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030383
name: Abnormal marginal zone B cell proportion
def: "A deviation of the normal proportion of marginal zone B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:9802980]
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of marginal zone B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030373 ! Abnormal memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030384
name: Decreased marginal zone B cell proportion
def: "A reduction in the normal proportion of marginal zone B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells." [PMID:9802980]
is_a: HP:0030383 ! Abnormal marginal zone B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030385
name: Increased marginal zone B cell proportion
def: "An elevation in the normal proportion of marginal zone B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:9802980]
is_a: HP:0030383 ! Abnormal marginal zone B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030386
name: Abnormal class-switched memory B cell proportion
def: "A deviation of the normal proportion of class-switched memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM-/IgD-) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells. Marginal zone B cells undergo limited somatic hypermutation and produce high-affinity IgM and some IgG, whereas class-switched memory B cells synthetize IgG, IgM, and IgA." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19342988]
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD19+CD27+IgD- cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of class-switched memory B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030373 ! Abnormal memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030387
name: Increased class-switched memory B cell proportion
def: "An increase in the normal proportion of class-switched memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) relative to the total number of B cells. Marginal zone B cells undergo limited somatic hypermutation and produce high-affinity IgM and some IgG, whereas class-switched memory B cells synthetize IgG, IgM, and IgA." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Increased proportion of CD19+CD27+IgD- cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030375 ! Increased memory B cell proportion
is_a: HP:0030386 ! Abnormal class-switched memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030388
name: Decreased class-switched memory B cell proportion
def: "A reduction in the normal proportion of class-switched memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) relative to the total number of B cells. Marginal zone B cells undergo limited somatic hypermutation and produce high-affinity IgM and some IgG, whereas class-switched memory B cells synthetize IgG, IgM, and IgA." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Decreased proportion of CD19+CD27+IgD- cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Decreased proportion of class-switched memory B cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030374 ! Decreased memory B cell proportion
is_a: HP:0030386 ! Abnormal class-switched memory B cell proportion

[Term]
id: HP:0030389
name: Abnormal circulating thromboxane concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of thromboxane in the blood circulation." []
comment: Thromboxanes are derived from prostaglandin precursors in platelets, and stimulate aggregation of platelets and constriction of blood vessels.
synonym: "Abnormal thromboxane level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030361 ! Abnormal circulating icosanoid concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0030390
name: Reduced circulating leukotriene C4 concentration
def: "An abnormally decreased concentration of leukotriene C4 in the blood circulation." [PMID:9820300]
comment: Cysteinyl leukotrienes including LTC4 are potent lipid mediators derived from arachidonic acid in the 5 lipoxygenase pathway.
is_a: HP:0030361 ! Abnormal circulating icosanoid concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0030391
name: Spoken word recognition deficit
def: "Reduced ability of lexical discrimination, which refers to the process of distinguishing a stimulus word from other phonologically similar words. Lexical discrimination can be defined as the process of correctly identifying words in the mental lexicon to match the phonological input of a stimulus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0002463 ! Language impairment

[Term]
id: HP:0030392
name: Choroid plexus carcinoma
def: "Intraventricular papillary neoplasm derived from choroid plexus epithelium. Plexus tumors are most common in the lateral and fourth ventricles; while 80% of lateral ventricle tumors present in children, fourth ventricle tumors are evenly distributed in all age groups. Clinically, choroid plexus tumors tend to cause hydrocephalus and increased intracranial pressure. Histologically, choroid plexus papillomas correspond to WHO grade I, choroid plexus carcinomas to WHO grade III." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:11135453]
is_a: HP:0007376 ! Abnormal choroid plexus morphology
is_a: HP:0100836 ! Malignant neoplasm of the central nervous system

[Term]
id: HP:0030393
name: Endolymphatic sac tumor
def: "A low-grade papillary epithelial neoplasm (adenocarcinoma) with a slow growth pattern. The endolymphatic duct emerges from the posterior wall of the saccule (of the inner ear) and ends in a blind pouch, the endolymphatic sac. Endolymphatic sac tumors (ELSTs) are known under different names in the literature (Heffner tumor, aggressive papillary middle ear tumor, and low-grade adenocarcinoma of endolymphatic sac origin)." [PMID:24966979]
comment: Endolymphatic sac tumors (ELSTs) may arise sporadically or in von Hippel-Lindau (VHL) disease. The symptoms (hearing loss with or without tinnitus, vertigo, impairment of cranial nerve function) and the physical and neuro-otologic examination and imaging findings (computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging) are not specific for tumors of the cerebellopontine angle (CPA). The final diagnosis can often only be reached through histopathological and immunohistochemical evaluation of the tumor specimen. The differential diagnosis in tumors of the CPA includes paraganglioma, chondroid tumor, atypical schwannoma, meningioma, and also rare entities such as aneurysm, hemangioblastoma, craniopharyngioma, and choroid plexus papilloma.
synonym: "Aggressive papillary middle ear tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Aggressive papillary middle ear tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Endolymphatic sac tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Heffner tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Heffner tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Low-grade adenocarcinoma of endolymphatic sac origin" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040096 ! Neoplasm of the inner ear

[Term]
id: HP:0030394
name: Fallopian tube carcinoma
def: "Carcinoma that originates in the Fallopian tube. It may be located in the wall or within the lumen as a growth attached to the wall by a stalk." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, NCIT:C3867]
is_a: HP:0033020 ! Female reproductive system neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030396
name: Abnormal platelet granule secretion
def: "Platelets are replete with secretory granules, which are critical to normal platelet function. Among the three types of platelet secretory granules - alpha-granules, dense granules, and lysosomes - the alpha-granule is the most abundant. Granule contents must be released from their intracellular repository in order to achieve their physiologic function, and this term refers to a functional defect in granule secretion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19450911]
is_a: HP:0011869 ! Abnormal platelet function

[Term]
id: HP:0030397
name: Abnormal platelet dense granule secretion
def: "Abnormal release of dense granules from platelets." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Dense granules contain adenosine diphosphate, adenosine triphosphate, ionized calcium, histamine and serotonin.
is_a: HP:0030396 ! Abnormal platelet granule secretion

[Term]
id: HP:0030398
name: Abnormal platelet ATP dense granule secretion
def: "Abnormal secretion of the platelet dense-granule content adenosine triphosphate (ATP)." []
is_a: HP:0030397 ! Abnormal platelet dense granule secretion

[Term]
id: HP:0030399
name: Abnormal platelet alpha granule secretion
def: "Abnormal release of alpha granule contents from platelets." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030396 ! Abnormal platelet granule secretion

[Term]
id: HP:0030400
name: Abnormal platelet lysosome secretion
def: "Abnormal release of lysosome contents from platelets." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030396 ! Abnormal platelet granule secretion

[Term]
id: HP:0030401
name: Abnormal platelet dense granule ATP/ADP ratio
def: "Deviation from normal of the ratio of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to adenosine diphosphate (ADP) within platelets." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0012484 ! Abnormal dense granules

[Term]
id: HP:0030402
name: Abnormal platelet aggregation
def: "An abnormality in the rate and degree to which platelets aggregate after the addition of an agonist that stimulates platelet clumping. Platelet aggregation is measured using aggregometer to measure the optical density of platelet-rich plasma, whereby platelet aggregation causes the plasma to become more transparent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0011869 ! Abnormal platelet function

[Term]
id: HP:0030403
name: Spontaneous platelet aggregation
def: "Clumping together of platelets in the blood in a platelet aggregation test without addition of agents normally used to induce aggregation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030402 ! Abnormal platelet aggregation

[Term]
id: HP:0030404
name: Glucagonoma
def: "An endocrine tumor of the pancreas that secretes excessive amounts of glucagon." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The excessive glucagon secreted by a glucagonoma may lead to dermatitis (migratory necrolytic erythema), glucose intolerance, weight loss, anemia, diarrhea, and thromboembolism.
is_a: HP:0030405 ! Pancreatic endocrine tumor

[Term]
id: HP:0030405
name: Pancreatic endocrine tumor
def: "A neuroendocrine tumor originating in a hormone-producing cell (islet cell) of the pancreas." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Pancreatic endocrine tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0100634 ! Neuroendocrine neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030406
name: Primary peritoneal carcinoma
def: "A type of cancer that originates in the peritoneum. It is to be distinguished from metastatic cancer of the peritoneum. Peritoneal cancer can occur anywhere in the abdominal space, and affects the surface of organs contained inside the peritoneum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0007378 ! Neoplasm of the gastrointestinal tract

[Term]
id: HP:0030407
name: Pineocytoma
def: "A type of pineal parenchymal cell neoplasm that is a mature well-differentiated tumor (WHO grade I)." []
xref: NCIT:C6966
is_a: HP:0030694 ! Pineal parenchymal cell neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030408
name: Pineoblastoma
alt_id: HP:0040193
def: "Pineoblastoma is a rare primitive neuroectodermal tumor (PNET) arising in the pineal gland. Pineoblastomas are classified as a WHO grade IV tumor and comprise one-fourth to one-half of pineal parenchymal tumors. Pineoblastoma is a highly cellular tumor originating in the pineal gland and containing small, poorly differentiated cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21717450]
comment: Pineoblastomas are rare, malignant, pineal region lesions that account for <0.1% of all intracranial tumors. Pineoblastomas harbor a poor prognosis and can metastasize along the neuroaxis. Although they typically appear radiographically as a focal enhancing mass, pineoblastomas can be locally invasive and spread outside the pineal region through the subarachnoid space. Pineoblastomas are more common in children than in adults, and adults account for <10% of patients.
synonym: "Pinealoblastoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030694 ! Pineal parenchymal cell neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030409
name: Renal transitional cell carcinoma
def: "A malignant tumor that arises from the transitional (urothelial) epithelial cells lining the urinary tract from the renal calyces to the ureteral orifice." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "renal TCC" EXACT []
synonym: "Renal urothelial carcinoma" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Transitional renal cell carcinoma" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0009726 ! Renal neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030410
name: Sebaceous gland carcinoma
def: "A carcinoma that arises in a sebaseous gland (an exocrine gland of the skin that secretes sebum, a waxy substance)" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Sebaceous carcinoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012842 ! Skin appendage neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030411
name: Jejunal adenocarcinoma
def: "A malignant epithelial tumor with a glandular organization that originates in the jejunum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: NCIT:C2852
is_a: HP:0040274 ! Adenocarcinoma of the small intestine

[Term]
id: HP:0030412
name: Ileal adenocarcinoma
def: "A malignant epithelial tumor with a glandular organization that originates in the ileum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: NCIT:C2852
is_a: HP:0040274 ! Adenocarcinoma of the small intestine

[Term]
id: HP:0030413
name: Squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue
def: "A carcinoma derived from a squamous epithelial cell of the tongue." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue is often painless and may present as a non-healing ulcer that demonstrates growth over time.
is_a: HP:0020357 ! Head and neck squamous cell carcinoma
is_a: HP:0100648 ! Neoplasm of the tongue

[Term]
id: HP:0030414
name: Verrucous cell carcinoma of the tongue
def: "A low-grade variant of squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue with a warty (verrucous) appearance." []
is_a: HP:0030413 ! Squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue

[Term]
id: HP:0030415
name: Sarcomatoid carcinoma of the tongue
def: "Sarcomatoid (spindle cell) carcinomas of the tongue is a variant of squamous carcinoma of tongue that is monoclonal, having evolved from a conventional squamous carcinoma with dedifferentiation associated with sarcomatoid transformation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20730609]
synonym: "Spindle cell carcinoma of the tongue" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030413 ! Squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue

[Term]
id: HP:0030416
name: Vulvar neoplasm
def: "A tumor (abnormal growth of tissue) of the female external genital tract (vulva)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Neoplasm of the vulva" EXACT []
synonym: "Tumor of the vulva" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6908-9849]
synonym: "Tumour of the vulva" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C3262
is_a: HP:0033020 ! Female reproductive system neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030417
name: Squamous cell carcinoma of the vulva
def: "A cancer that originates in the squamous cells that line the surface of the vulva." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25848321]
synonym: "Vulval squamous cell carcinoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030416 ! Vulvar neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030418
name: Vulvar melanoma
def: "A type of vulvar cancer that originates from melanocytes of the vulva." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:8723827]
comment: The first symptoms typically noticed by the patients are bleeding, pruritus, or a mass in the groin. Vulvar melanomas are mostly located at the labia minora.
is_a: HP:0030416 ! Vulvar neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030419
name: Bartholin gland carcinoma
def: "A cancer arising in a cell of the Bartholin gland, a racemose gland located slightly posterior to the opening of the vagina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25013508]
comment: Carcinomas of Bartholin's gland are rare tumors that account for less than 1% of all gynecological malignancies. Two major histological types, squamous cell carcinoma and adenocarcinoma, account for 80% to 90% of primary cases. The remainder are adenoid-cystic, transitional, or undifferentiated carcinomas.
is_a: HP:0030416 ! Vulvar neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030420
name: Vulvar adenocarcinoma
def: "An adenocarcinoma arising in the vulva." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23761517]
is_a: HP:0030416 ! Vulvar neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030421
name: Epididymal neoplasm
def: "A tumor (abnormal growth of tissue) of the epididymis, an duct that transports spermatozoa from the testis to the vas deferens." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
xref: NCIT:C3262
is_a: HP:0010785 ! Gonadal neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030422
name: obsolete Papillary cystadenoma of the epididymis
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: HP:0009715

[Term]
id: HP:0030423
name: Splenic cyst
def: "A closed sac located in the spleen." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24794024]
synonym: "Cyst on spleen" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0025408 ! Abnormal spleen morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030424
name: Epididymal cyst
def: "A smooth, extratesticular, spherical cyst in the head of the epididymis." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:14767330]
comment: Diagnosis of epididymal cyst can be confirmed by scrotal ultrasound. Patients can present with scrotal mass or pain. Epididymal cysts are usually between 3-30 mm in diameter. In some cases they can resolve spontaneously.
synonym: "Epididymal cysts" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0009714 ! Abnormal epididymis morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030425
name: Calcified ovarian cyst
def: "A cyst of the ovary that exhibits deposition of calcium salts." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0000138 ! Ovarian cyst

[Term]
id: HP:0030426
name: Ossifying fibroma
def: "A benign central bone tumor composed of fibrous connective tissue within which bone is formed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0010614 ! Fibroma

[Term]
id: HP:0030427
name: Ossifying fibroma of the jaw
def: "A benign central bone tumor of the jaw composed of fibrous connective tissue within which bone is formed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The mandible is most commonly affected.
is_a: HP:0030426 ! Ossifying fibroma
is_a: HP:0100649 ! Neoplasm of the oral cavity

[Term]
id: HP:0030428
name: Cutaneous myxoma
def: "A myxoma originating in the skin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25118746]
comment: Cutaneous myxomas are sharply demarcated nodules of the dermis or subcutis that may occur as solitary lesions or in association with Carney complex. Microscopically, cutaneous myxomas in the Carney complex have sharp circumscription, hypocellularity, abundant myxoid stroma, prominent capillaries and an occasional epithelial component.
xref: NCIT:C6577
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin

[Term]
id: HP:0030429
name: Juvenile nasopharyngeal angiofibroma
def: "A benign but highly vascular nasopharyngeal neoplasm. The tumor originates from the sphenopalatine foramen and involves both the pterygopalatine fossa and the posterior nasal cavity." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:15661706]
is_a: HP:0012288 ! Neoplasm of head and neck

[Term]
id: HP:0030430
name: Neuroma
def: "A tumor made up of nerve cells and nerve fibers." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Nerve tumor" EXACT layperson [http://www.apma.org/learn/foothealth.cfm?itemnumber=987, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Nerve tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Pinched nerve" EXACT layperson [http://www.apma.org/learn/foothealth.cfm?itemnumber=987, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
is_a: HP:0100007 ! Neoplasm of the peripheral nervous system

[Term]
id: HP:0030431
name: Osteochondroma
def: "A cartilage capped bony outgrowth of a long bone. Osteochondroma arises on the external surface of bone containing a marrow cavity that is continuous with that of the underlying bone." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:18271966]
synonym: "Osteocartilaginous exostoses" EXACT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/osteochondroma, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Osteochondromas" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0010622 ! Neoplasm of the skeletal system

[Term]
id: HP:0030432
name: Chondroblastoma
def: "A usually benign tumor composed of cells which arise from chondroblasts or their precursors and which tend to differentiate into cartilage cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19387641]
comment: Chondroblastomas of bone are rare benign bone tumors, arising at the cartilaginous growth plate, representing approximately 1-2% of all bone tumors. The most common sites are the proximal humerus and the proximal tibia, but the third most common site is the proximal femur. Histologically, the tumor consists predominantly of well-defined polygonal chondroblast-type cells similar to epiphyseal chondrocytes, with large nucleoli and benign-looking nuclei that have a tendency to be multilobulate and have a continuous dense band of substance along the inner nuclear membrane, intra-cytoplasmic inclusions of glycogen and lipids, numerous mitochondria and superficial secretion vesicles arising from a well developed rough endoplasmic reticulum. There are multi-nucleated giant cells, foci of chondroid matrix, with focal calcification that may acquire a "chicken wire" appearance. Aneurysmal bone cysts are associated with chondroblastoma in 14% of cases.
is_a: HP:0010622 ! Neoplasm of the skeletal system

[Term]
id: HP:0030433
name: Osteoid osteoma
def: "A bening tumor of bone composed of a central zone named nidus which is an atypical bone completely enclosed within a well vascularized stroma and a peripheral sclerotic reaction zone." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23329939]
is_a: HP:0100246 ! Osteoma

[Term]
id: HP:0030434
name: Pilomatrixoma
def: "Pilomatricoma is an asymptomatic slowly growing benign cutaneous tumor, differentiating towards the hair matrix of the hair follicle. It is covered by normal or hyperemic skin, and usually varies in size from 0.5 to 3 cm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21430899]
comment: Pilomatricomas usually are asymptomatic (pain appears only with associated inflammation and ulceration); deeply seated, firm, nontender subcutaneous masses adherent to the skin but not fixed to the underlying tissue. Stretching of the skin over the tumor shows the "tent sign" with multiple facets and angles, a pathognomonic sign for pilomatricoma. In addition, pressing on one edge of the lesion causes the opposite edge to protrude from the skin like a "teeter-totter". Both these "tent sign" and "teeter-totter sign" are the most helpful clinical clues to the diagnosis of pilomatricoma.
is_a: HP:0012842 ! Skin appendage neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030436
name: Fibrofolliculoma
def: "Fibrofolliculoma is a clinically asymptomatic, 2-4 mm, skin-colored, dome-shaped smooth papule. It usually arises in the form of multiple lesions in adults in different areas such as the scalp, forehead, face, and neck. According to histology, the lesion is a fibrotic hamartoma characterized by infundibular epithelial proliferation and perifollicular fibrous proliferation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:17804924]
synonym: "Fibrofolliculomas" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin

[Term]
id: HP:0030437
name: Anal canal neoplasm
synonym: "Anal canal tumor" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432]
synonym: "Anal canal tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C3262
is_a: HP:0032186 ! Anal neoplasm
is_a: HP:0100834 ! Neoplasm of the large intestine

[Term]
id: HP:0030438
name: Anal canal squamous cell carcinoma
def: "A squamous cell carcinoma that originates in the anal canal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Patients typically present with bright red bleeding, pain, and/or a palpable mass. When a clinically suspicious lesion is identified, diagnosis relies on cytologic or histologic confirmation.
is_a: HP:0030437 ! Anal canal neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030439
name: Anal canal adenocarcinoma
def: "An adenoma carcinoma that originates in the anal canal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Differentiating true anal canal adenocarcinoma from low rectal adenocarcinoma can be challenging. Most anal canal adenocarcinomas originate from anal glands, but cases developing in chronic tracts from fistula in ano are described. Multiple factors, including infection with HPV and HIV, history of receptive anal intercourse, smoking, and immunosuppression have been identified as risk factors. Clinical features include anal pain, induration of the anal canal, or abscess formation and a palpable lump.
xref: NCIT:C2852
is_a: HP:0030437 ! Anal canal neoplasm
is_a: HP:0040275 ! Adenocarcinoma of the large intestine

[Term]
id: HP:0030440
name: Anal margin neoplasm
def: "A tumor of the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: The anal canal is defined as the caudal part of the large intestine extending from the anorectal ring to the anal verge and is about 3 to 5 cm in length. Outside of the anal verge lies the anal margin, also referred to as the perianal skin, which commonly encompasses a radius of 5 cm. The anal verge can be identified visually as the part of the anal canal remaining closed when the buttocks are gently retracted. The upper anal canal is lined by columnar tissue that transitions into squamous epithelium at the dentate line. The dentate line, identified by the termination of the anal columns, lies 1 to 2 cm above the anal verge.
is_a: HP:0007378 ! Neoplasm of the gastrointestinal tract

[Term]
id: HP:0030441
name: Anal margin Paget's disease
def: "An intraepithelial adenocarcinoma originating in the anal margin and characterized by presence of typical Paget's cells, appearing as large rounded vacuolated cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Macroscopically, anal margin Paget's disease presents as an erythematous and eczematous rash similar to benign skin conditions or other perianal diseases such as Bowen's disease, hydradenitis suppurativa, pruritus ani, or Crohn's disease.
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030442
name: Anal margin squamous cell carcinoma
def: "A squamous cell carcinoma that originates in the skin of the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22379406]
comment: Clinical presentations include pain, bleeding, palpable lump, and discharge. Typically, SCC of the anal margin appears as an ulcerated lesion with rolled everted edges. A significant number of patients are misdiagnosed with an anal fissure, fistula, eczema, or hemorrhoids; therefore a biopsy is recommended for any persistent anal margin lesion not responding to conservative therapy.
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030443
name: Anal margin basal cell carcinoma
def: "A basal cell carcinoma that originates in the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030444
name: Anal margin melanoma
def: "A melanoma that originates in the anal margin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030440 ! Anal margin neoplasm

[Term]
id: HP:0030445
name: Pulmonary carcinoid tumor
def: "A malignant neuroendocrine tumor of the lung. According to histopathologic criteria (WHO 2004), carcinoids are divided into four groups i.e. typical and atypical carcinoids, large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma and small cell lung carcinoma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:21043816, PMID:24179657]
synonym: "Lung carcinoid tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Lung carcinoid tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Pulmonary carcinoid tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0100570 ! Carcinoid tumor

[Term]
id: HP:0030446
name: Atypical pulmonary carcinoid tumor
synonym: "Atypical pulmonary carcinoid tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0030445 ! Pulmonary carcinoid tumor

[Term]
id: HP:0030447
name: Merkel cell skin cancer
def: "A malignant cutaneous tumor of the elderly that is characterized by an aggressive course with regional nodal involvement, distant metastases and a high rate of recurrence. Most patients present with rapidly growing, painless, firm, non-tender, dome-shaped red, occasionally ulcerated skin nodules, which have a red or bluish color, measuring up to several centimeters, on predominantly sun-exposed areas of the body. The overlying skin is smooth and shiny, sometimes exhibiting ulcerative, acneiform or telangiectatic features." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:16565213]
synonym: "Anaplastic carcinoma of the skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Cutaneous APUDoma" EXACT []
synonym: "Merkel cell cancer of the skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Neuroendocrine carcinoma of the skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Neuroendocrine tumor of the skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Neuroendocrine tumour of the skin" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Primary small cell carcinoma of the skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Primary undifferentiated carcinoma of the skin" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin
is_a: HP:0040192 ! APUdoma

[Term]
id: HP:0030448
name: Soft tissue sarcoma
def: "A type of sarcoma (A connective tissue neoplasm formed by proliferation of mesodermal cells) that develops from soft tissues like fat, muscle, nerves, fibrous tissues, blood vessels, or deep skin tissues." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Soft tissue sarcomas can be found in any part of the body but most often originate in the arms or legs. They can also be found in the trunk, head and neck area, internal organs, and in the retroperitoneum.
synonym: "Soft tissue sarcomas" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
is_a: HP:0100242 ! Sarcoma

[Term]
id: HP:0030449
name: Therapeutic abortion
def: "Delivery by means of therapeutic termination of pregnancy. Therapeutic abortion may be done to end a pregnancy if the mother's life is in danger or if the baby has abnormalities involving the major organ systems and is not expected to survive after birth or by choice." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0001787 ! Abnormal delivery

[Term]
id: HP:0030450
name: Neoplasm of the autonomic nervous system
def: "A tumor that arises from an element of the autonomic nervous system." []
xref: NCIT:C5112
is_a: HP:0100007 ! Neoplasm of the peripheral nervous system

[Term]
id: HP:0030451
name: Mesenteric cyst
def: "A closed fluid filled sac originating from the mesentary." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24936122]
comment: A mesenteric cyst is defined as any cyst located in the mesentery; it may or may not extend into the retroperitoneum, which has a recognizable lining of endothelium or mesothelial cell. Mesenteric cyst can occur anywhere in the mesentery of gastrointestinal tract from duodenum to rectum. Mesenteric cysts can be simple or multiple, unilocular or multilocular, and they may contain hemorrhagic, serous, chylous, or infected fluid. They can range in size from a few millimeters to few cm in diameter, however, at times may be so large that it may mimic tubercular ascites.
is_a: HP:0100016 ! Abnormal mesentery morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030452
name: Chylolymphatic mesenteric cyst
def: "A type of mesenteric cyst that is lined with a thin endothelium or mesothelium and filled with chylous and lymphatic fluid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19946589]
is_a: HP:0030451 ! Mesenteric cyst

