[Term]
id: HP:0030465
name: Undetectable light-adapted electroretinogram
def: "No detectable response to the light-adapted 3.0 ERG (single-flash cone response). This type of ERG measures responses of the cone system; a-waves arise from cone photoreceptors and cone off-bipolar cells; the b-wave comes from On- and Off-cone bipolar cells." [PMID:25502644]
synonym: "Absent photopic (cone) responses on ERG" EXACT []
synonym: "non-detectable photopic ERG" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008275 ! Abnormal light-adapted electroretinogram

[Term]
id: HP:0030466
name: Abnormal full-field electroretinogram
def: "An anomaly observed by full-field electroretinogram (ffERG). The ffERG measures the light-induced electrical activity of the retina at the corneal surface. Specifically, the ffERG records the global or total retinal electrical response to a full-field (Ganzfield) light stimulus. Isolation of the rod and cone components has important diagnostic value in differentiating between various retinal diseases. Modifying the properties of the light-stimulus (wavelength, strength, and flicker rate) as well as the adaptive state of the retina can separate the rod and cone functions of the ffERG." [PMID:32491415]
comment: The full-field electroretinogram (ffERG) is an ophthalmologic test that provides non-invasive objective quantitative measures of the electrical activity in the retina. The ffERG represents an electrical response from the retina to a flash of light and measures global retinal function.
is_a: HP:0000512 ! Abnormal electroretinogram

[Term]
id: HP:0030467
name: Abnormal pattern electroretinogram
def: "An anomalous response to a pattern electroretinogram (PERG), a particular kind of ERG obtained in response to contrast modulation of patterned visual stimuli at constant mean luminance-typically contrast-reversing gratings or checkerboards-whose characteristics are fundamentally different from those of the traditional ERG in response to diffuse flashes of light." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:17522779, PMID:3076152]
is_a: HP:0000512 ! Abnormal electroretinogram

[Term]
id: HP:0030468
name: Abnormal multifocal electroretinogram
is_a: HP:0000512 ! Abnormal electroretinogram

[Term]
id: HP:0030469
name: Abnormal dark-adapted electroretinogram
def: "An electroretinographic anomaly detected by dark-adapted full-field ERG. The dark adapted ERG targets rod-pathway function." [PMID:10532405]
comment: After a period of dark adaptation (usually 20 to 30 minutes), the retinal rods reach peak sensitivity.
is_a: HP:0030466 ! Abnormal full-field electroretinogram

