[Term]
id: HP:0030496
name: Macular exudate
def: "Yellow-white intraretinal deposits in the macula typically associated with damaged inner blood-retina barrier and exudation of serous fluid and lipids from the retinal microvasculature." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Macular exudates" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Macular exudation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030495 ! Abnormal macular vasculature morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030497
name: Macular cotton wool spot
def: "Fluffy white patch in the macula, representing localized areas of dense white swelling of the retinal nerve fiber layer." [PMID:6169833]
comment: Cotton-wool spots (CWSs) are common retinal manifestations of ischemia in the inner retina, due to many diseases including diabetes mellitus, systemic hypertension, and acquired immunodeficiency syndrome.
is_a: HP:0030500 ! Yellow/white macular lesion
is_a: HP:0031606 ! Retinal cotton wool spot

[Term]
id: HP:0030498
name: Macular thickening
def: "Abnormal increase in retinal thickness in the macular area observed on fundoscopy or fundus imaging." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030499
name: Macular drusen
def: "Drusen localted in the macula." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Drusen (singular, 'druse') are yellow or white accumulations of extracellular material that build up external to the pigment epithelium in Bruch membrane of the eye.
synonym: "Lipid accumulation in macula" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0011510 ! Drusen
is_a: HP:0030500 ! Yellow/white macular lesion

[Term]
id: HP:0030500
name: Yellow/white macular lesion
def: "A type of white and/or yellow lesion located anywhere within the macula. These lesions can be flat or raised and can vary in size from very small to bigger." []
synonym: "Yellow/white lesion of the macula" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology
is_a: HP:0030506 ! Yellow/white retinal lesion

[Term]
id: HP:0030501
name: Macular crystals
def: "Crystalline deposits in the macula, located intra-retinally." []
comment: This feature can be ascertained by fundoscopy and fundus photography. Some crystals can be better visualized with monochromatic light imaging.
synonym: "Refractile lesions in the macula" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030500 ! Yellow/white macular lesion

[Term]
id: HP:0030502
name: Retinoschisis
def: "Splitting of the neuroretinal layers of the retina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0000479 ! Abnormal retinal morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030503
name: Macular telangiectasia
def: "Localized irregular dilatation of small tortuous intraretinal blood vessels in the macular area." []
comment: Macular telangiectasia can be unilateral or bilateral and may be associated to peripheral telangiectasis.
synonym: "Juxtafoveal telangiectasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Parafoveal telangiectasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0007763 ! Retinal telangiectasia
is_a: HP:0030495 ! Abnormal macular vasculature morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030504
name: Clustered congenital hypertrophy of retinal pigment epithelium
def: "Grouped, flat, well-demarcated pigmented lesions at the level of the pigment epithelium (that are said to resemble bear tracks). Less frequently, the lesions may be white ('polar bear tracks')." []
comment: This is a benign finding, which should be distinguished from the multiple pigmented lesions associated with familial polyposis.
synonym: "Bear track congenital hypertrophy of retinal pigment epithelium" EXACT []
synonym: "Grouped congenital hypertrophy of retinal pigment epithelium" EXACT []
