[Term]
id: HP:0030505
name: Nummular pigmentation of the retina
def: "Clumped pigmentary changes of nummular appearance (i.e., thought to resemble the shape of a coin or multiple coins stuck together) at the level of the retinal pigment epithelium." [PMID:21763485]
comment: This type of pigmentation is encountered in CRB1-, NRL- and NR2E3-retinopathies
synonym: "Nummular pigmentation of the fundus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0007703 ! Abnormal retinal pigmentation

[Term]
id: HP:0030506
name: Yellow/white retinal lesion
def: "An area anywhere within the retina showing pale yellow or white discoloration. Such lesions can be flat or raised and there size can range from very small to big." []
synonym: "Yellow/white lesions of the retina" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000479 ! Abnormal retinal morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0030507
name: Retinal crystals
def: "Crystalline deposits in the retina." [PMID:12498506]
comment: Crystalline deposits in the retina may be associated with a wide variety of systemic disorders such as oxalosis, cystinosis, hyperornithinaemia and Sjogren-Larsson syndrome. Refractile crystalline deposits may also be a manifestation of drug toxicity like the antineoplastic agent tamoxifen, the anesthetic methoxyflurane and the oral tanning agent canthaxanthine. Crystals may also occur in drug abusers who inject multiple crushed tablets of methadone or meperidine intravenously (talc retinopathy).
is_a: HP:0030506 ! Yellow/white retinal lesion

