is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern

[Term]
id: HP:0030651
name: Multifocal
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern

[Term]
id: HP:0030652
name: Vitreous haze
def: "Vitreous haze is the obscuration of fundus details by vitreous cells and protein exudation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:20719302]
is_a: HP:0011531 ! Vitritis

[Term]
id: HP:0030654
name: Umbilical cord cyst
def: "Any cystic lesion associated with the umbilical cord." [PMID:10206815, PMID:12666213]
comment: Umbilical cord cysts can be single or multiple. Most usually, a solitary umbilical cyst is observed. They can be classified as (i) true cysts if they have an epithelial lining (allentoic cyst or omphalomesenteric duct cyst) or false cysts if they do not have an epithelial lining (umbilical cord pseudocyst).
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030655
name: Umbilical cord knot
def: "An entwining of a segment of umbilical cord, usually without obstructing fetal circulation and commonly result from fetal slippage through a loop of the cord." [PMID:25184085]
comment: When the true knot remains tight, it may impede the circulation of the fetus and may result to fetal death in utero especially in labor.
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030656
name: Umbilical vein varix
def: "Focal dilation of the umbilical vein." []
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030657
name: Umbilical cord hematoma
def: "Bleeding from the vessels of the cord with extravasation of blood into the Wharton jelly surrounding the umbilical cord vessels." []
synonym: "Umbilical cord haematoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030658
name: Marginal umbilical cord insertion
def: "Insertion of the umbilical cord within 2 cm from the placental edge." [PMID:26366000, PMID:29201670]
comment: Marginal cord insertion has an incidence of about 7 percent of births. It is associated with intrauterine growth retardation, preterm labor and development of velamentous cord insertion. The synonym battledore placenta is so named because of its resemblance to the bat used in the medieval game of battledore and shuttlecock.
synonym: "Battledore placenta" EXACT []
synonym: "Marginal cord insertion" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011418 ! Abnormal insertion of umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030659
name: Velamentous cord insertion
def: "Insertion of the umbilical cord into the chorio-amniotic membranes of the placenta." [PMID:26366000]
comment: Velamentous cord insertion and an incidence of 1.1 percent of singleton births, and 8.7 to 16 percent of twin births.
is_a: HP:0011418 ! Abnormal insertion of umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030660
name: Furcate cord insertion
def: "Branching of the umbilical cord before its insertion into the placenta." []
is_a: HP:0011418 ! Abnormal insertion of umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T12:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030661
name: Vitreous snowballs
def: "Yellow-white inflammatory aggregates in the vitreous that are found in the midvitreous and inferior periphery." [PMID:20029143]
comment: Vitreous snowballs can be observed in intermediate uveitis.
is_a: HP:0011531 ! Vitritis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T22:32:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030662
name: Vitreous inflammatory cells
def: "The presence of inflammatory cells such as lymphocytes and macrophages in the vitreous." []
comment: Normally, there are no leukocytes in the vitreous as this is an immune-privileged site. If the blood-retinal barrier is disrupted, then leukocytes gain access to the vitreous. Vitreous inflammatory cells can be measured by flow cytometry of vitreous fluid.
is_a: HP:0011531 ! Vitritis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T22:32:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030663
name: Optically empty vitreous
def: "Vestigial vitreous gel occupying the immediate retrolental space and minimal to no discernible gel in the central vitreous cavity, giving the appearance of an empty vitreous cavity." [PMID:15557460, PMID:7867814]
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T22:41:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030664
name: Beevor's sign
def: "Weakness of the inferior portion of the rectus abdominal muscle, which is ascertained clinically as follows. When a patient sits up or raises the head from a recumbent position, the umbilicus is displaced toward the head. This is the result of paralysis of the inferior portion of the rectus abdominal muscle, so that the upper fibers predominate pulling upwards the umbilicus." [PMID:2146943]
comment: Beevor's sign is said to be characteristic of a spinal cord lesion at the T10 level, but is also described inter alia in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis and in facioscapulohumeral muscular dystrophy.
is_a: HP:0009023 ! Abdominal wall muscle weakness
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T23:16:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030665
name: Rubral tremor
def: "Rubral tremor is characterized by a slow coarse tremor at rest that is exacerbated by postural adjustments and by guided voluntary movements." [PMID:6568936]
comment: Rubral tremor can be observed with midbrain injury and probably results from combined lesions of the superior cerebellar peduncle, substantia nigra, and red nucleus with interruption of the outflow pathway from the cerebellum to the motor thalamus. This tremor is present at rest but tends to be slower (3 to 5 Hz) than typical Parkinson tremor (5 to 7 Hz). It also persists unchanged or even increases with postural changes or goal-directed activity.
synonym: "Holmes' tremor" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001337 ! Tremor
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T23:16:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030666
name: Retinal neovascularization
alt_id: HP:0007850
def: "In ischemic retinal disease, neovascularization (NV) involves the sprouting of new vessels from pre-existent vessels. Ischemia invariably leads to the upregulation of Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor (VEGF) production. Most frequently the new vessels grow internal to the plane of the retina. However, intraretinal proliferation of new vessels can also occur." [PMID:23329331]
synonym: "Retinal vascular proliferation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008046 ! Abnormal retinal vascular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T23:35:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030667
name: Peripheral retinal neovascularization
def: "A type of retinal neovascularization that affects the periphery of the retina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:22076700]
is_a: HP:0030666 ! Retinal neovascularization
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-21T23:35:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030668
name: Periorbital dermoid cyst
def: "A cyst that is localized in the region of the orbit and exhibits an epithelial lining with a keratin-filled lumen. Hair follicles are one of the adnexal structures that are commonly found in walls of dermoid cysts." []
comment: A periorbital dermoid cyst may present as a subcutaneous mass at the lateral aspect of an eyelid.
is_a: HP:0001144 ! Orbital cyst
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-22T11:36:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030669
name: Abnormal ocular adnexa morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the adjacent structures (i.e., adnexa) of the eye, defined as the lacrimal apparatus, the extraocular muscles and the eyelids, eyelashes, eyebrows and the conjunctiva." []
is_a: HP:0032039 ! Abnormality of the ocular adnexa
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-22T11:58:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030670
name: Hamartoma of the orbital region
def: "A hamartoma (disordered proliferation of mature tissues) which can originate from any tissue of the orbital region." []
is_a: HP:0000315 ! Abnormality of the orbital region
is_a: HP:0010566 ! Hamartoma
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T14:15:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030671
name: Abnormal common tendinous ring morphology
def: "Any anomaly of the ring of fibrous tissue that surrounds the optic nerve at its entrance at the apex of the orbit. The common tendinous ring, also known as the annulus of Zinn or annular tendon, is the origin for five of the seven extraocular muscles." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Abnormality of the common tendinous ring" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030669 ! Abnormal ocular adnexa morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T14:27:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030672
name: Asteroid hyalosis
def: "The presence of small, white vitreous opacities consisting of calcium phosphate and complex, layered lipid deposits." []
comment: Asteroid hyalosis is a degenerative process.
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T14:43:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030673
name: Erosive vitreoretinopathy
def: "A form of vitreoretinopathy characterized by thinning (erosion) of the retinal pigment epithelium that permits increased visualization of the choroidal vessels." [PMID:8152765]
is_a: HP:0007773 ! Vitreoretinopathy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T15:03:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030674
name: Antenatal onset
def: "Onset prior to birth." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Intrauterine onset" EXACT []
synonym: "Onset in utero" EXACT []
synonym: "Prenatal onset" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003674 ! Onset
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T15:25:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030675
name: Contracture of proximal interphalangeal joints of 2nd-5th fingers
def: "Chronic loss of joint motion of the proximal interphalangeal joint of the 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th fingers due to structural changes in non-bony tissue." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:jdavis]
is_a: HP:0001215 ! Camptodactyly of 2nd-5th fingers
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T15:30:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030676
name: Satyr ear
def: "Sharp pointed superior portion of the ear, with variable overfolding of the helix." [PMID:19152421]
comment: The satyr ear appears to have an abnormally small upper-lateral portion. More extensive underdevelopment continuing down to and including the lobe produces a more extreme anomaly that, unfortunately, has been called Devil ear.
synonym: "Devil ear" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000377 ! Abnormal pinna morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T15:34:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030677
name: Mozart ear
def: "A congenital auricular deformity, which is mainly characterized by a bulging appearance of the anterosuperior portion of the auricle, a convexly protruded cavum conchae, and a slit-like narrowing of the orifice of the external auditory meatus." [PMID:21587051]
is_a: HP:0000377 ! Abnormal pinna morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-23T15:38:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030679
name: Ash-leaf spot
def: "A hypopigmented spot in the shape of a leaf from the mountain ash tree." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23761491, PMID:9637809]
comment: Wood's light is a blue light with an emission peak of 360 nm. The blue end of visible light is absorbed by epidermal pigmentation. If there is no epidermal pigmentation in a site, the area will appear nonpigmented as compared with the surrounding skin. Minimally visible hypopigmented spots are more easily visualized with the Wood's lamp. Ash-leaf spots are only one variety of hypopigmented macules present on the skin of patients who have tuberous sclerosis.
is_a: HP:0009719 ! Hypomelanotic macule
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T17:28:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030680
name: Abnormal cardiovascular system morphology
alt_id: HP:0001632
alt_id: HP:0002564
alt_id: HP:0002565
def: "Any structural anomaly of the heart and blood vessels." []
synonym: "Abnormality of cardiovascular system morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "Cardiovascular malformations" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001626 ! Abnormality of the cardiovascular system
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:00:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030681
name: Abnormal morphology of myocardial trabeculae
def: "Any structural anomaly of the muscular columns which project from the inner surface of the right and left ventricles of the heart (cardiac trabeculae, trabeculae carneae)." []
is_a: HP:0001637 ! Abnormal myocardium morphology
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:13:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030682
name: Left ventricular noncompaction
def: "Left ventricular noncompaction (LVNC) is defined by 3 markers: prominent left ventricular (LV) trabeculae, deep intertrabecular recesses, and the thin compacted layer." [PMID:16670098, PMID:25443708]
is_a: HP:0031192 ! Abnormal morphology of left ventricular trabeculae
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:13:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030683
name: Recurrent bacterial vaginosis
def: "Repeated symptomatic episodes of inflammation of the vagina that can result from a spectrum of conditions that cause vaginal and sometimes vulvar symptoms, such as itching, burning, irritation, odor, and vaginal discharge." []
comment: The most common infectious causes of vaginitis are bacterial vaginosis, vulvovaginal candidiasis, and trichomoniasis. Physicians traditionally diagnose vaginitis using the combination of symptoms, physical examination, pH of vaginal fluid, microscopy, and the whiff test.
synonym: "Vaginitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Vulvovaginitis" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0000142 ! Abnormal vagina morphology
is_a: HP:0012649 ! Increased inflammatory response
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:16:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030684
name: Abnormal adiponectin level
def: "A deviation from the normal circulating concentration of adiponectin, a 30-kDa complement C1-related protein that is the most abundant secreted protein expressed in adipose tissue, and that plays a crucial role in the regulation of insulin sensitivity and glucose metabolism." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:26221520]
comment: Lower circulating adiponectin levels is associated with obesity and negatively correlated with insulin resistance. Adiponectin may exert antidiabetic, anti-atherogenic and anti-inflammatory activities in metabolic diseases.
is_a: HP:0003117 ! Abnormal circulating hormone concentration
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:34:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030685
name: Decreased adiponectin level
def: "A reduced circulating concentration of adiponectin, a 30-kDa complement C1-related protein that is the most abundant secreted protein expressed in adipose tissue." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
is_a: HP:0030684 ! Abnormal adiponectin level
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:34:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030686
name: Increased adiponectin level
def: "An elevated circulating concentration of adiponectin, a 30-kDa complement C1-related protein that is the most abundant secreted protein expressed in adipose tissue." []
is_a: HP:0030684 ! Abnormal adiponectin level
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:34:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030687
name: Abnormal circulating glucagon concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of glucagon in the blood circulation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: Glucagon is a 29-amino acid polypeptide that is manufactured by the alpha cells of the pancreatic islets. It plays a key role in glucose counterregulation in response to hypoglycemia. Hypoglycemia is normally a powerful stimulator of glucagon secretion.
synonym: "Abnormal glucagon level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003117 ! Abnormal circulating hormone concentration
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:45:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030688
name: Increased glucagon level
def: "An elevated concentration of glucagon in the blood circulation." []
is_a: HP:0030687 ! Abnormal circulating glucagon concentration
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:45:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030689
name: Decreased glucagon level
def: "A reduced concentration of glucagon in the blood circulation." []
is_a: HP:0030687 ! Abnormal circulating glucagon concentration
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-28T18:45:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030690
name: Gingival cleft
def: "A fissure in the gingiva (gums), i.e., the mucosal tissue that lies over the mandible and maxilla." []
is_a: HP:0000168 ! Abnormal gingiva morphology
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-29T14:03:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030691
name: Divergence nystagmus
def: "A condition in which both eyes beat outward simultaneously." []
comment: This is a rare condition that may be related to posterior foass abnormalities and can occur with spinocerebellar degeneration.
is_a: HP:0000639 ! Nystagmus
property_value: terms:date "2015-12-29T14:03:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030692
name: Brain neoplasm
def: "A benign or malignant neoplasm that arises from or metastasizes to the brain." []
synonym: "Brain tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Brain tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C2907
is_a: HP:0012443 ! Abnormal brain morphology
is_a: HP:0100006 ! Neoplasm of the central nervous system
property_value: terms:date "2016-01-07T22:49:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030693
name: Supratentorial neoplasm
def: "A benign or malignant neoplasm that occurs within the intracranial cavity above the tentorium cerebelli." []
comment: This represents a group of related tumors ranging from the relatively benign to the highly malignant.
synonym: "Pineal parenchymal tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Pineal parenchymal tumour" EXACT uk_spelling []
xref: NCIT:C3328
is_a: HP:0030692 ! Brain neoplasm
property_value: terms:date "2016-01-07T22:49:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030694
name: Pineal parenchymal cell neoplasm
is_a: HP:0010799 ! Pinealoma
property_value: terms:date "2016-01-07T22:49:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030706
name: Ranula
def: "A ranula is a mucocele that occurs in the floor of the mouth and usually involve the major salivary glands. Specifically, the ranula originates in the body of the sublingual gland, in the ducts of the sublingual gland, in the Wharton's duct of the submandibular gland or infrequently from the minor salivary glands at this location." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:23291329]
synonym: "Sublingual cyst" EXACT []
synonym: "Sublingual ptyalocele" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010286 ! Abnormal salivary gland morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:10:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030707
name: Unilateral lung agenesis
def: "Lack of development of one lung." []
synonym: "Unilateral pulmonary agenesis" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
is_a: HP:0006703 ! Aplasia/Hypoplasia of the lungs
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:12:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030708
name: Myeloschisis
def: "The severe form of a neural tube defect where the open neural tube appears as a flattened, plate-like mass of nervous tissue with no overlying membrane." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:20885122]
comment: Myeloschisis is a cleft spinal cord arising from a failure of neural tube closure. The placode is defined as a plate of embryonic epithelial cells constituting a primordial cell group from which the spinal cord arises and is often seen in a myelomeningocele. In a myelomeningocele, an exposed placode is often a myeloschisis. In other words, a myeloschisis is a collapsed myelomeningocele. When the placode in the myelomeningocele sac is a cleft spinal cord, this anomaly is classified as myeloschisis rather than myelomeningocele.
is_a: HP:0010301 ! Spinal dysraphism
is_a: HP:0034237 ! Open neural tube defect
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:26:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030709
name: Myelocystocele
def: "Myelocystocele is characterized by a large, ependyma-lined, cystic dilation of the caudal end of the central canal of the spinal cord; it projects dorsally through a lamina defect, with overlying varying amounts of lipomatous subcutaneous tissue. Myelocystoceles are associated with a tethered cord and meningocele, which communicates with the spinal subarachnoid space, but not with the central canal cyst." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:9514174]
comment: Localized dilatation of the central canal of the spinal cord which produces a fluid-filled sac or diverticulum which then protrudes through the cord and the defective dorsal dura between the posterior parts of the vertebra.
is_a: HP:0002196 ! Myelopathy
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:32:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030710
name: Lipomeningocele
def: "A form of closed neural tube defect in which the spinal tissue lies within the spinal cord having a junction between the spinal cord and the lipoma. Intact skin covers the defect. Neurologic findings first appear during the second year of life." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
is_a: HP:0002435 ! Meningocele
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:40:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030711
name: Hydrocolpos
def: "Distention of the vagina caused by accumulation of fluid due to congenital vaginal obstruction." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
comment: This term is distinct from Hydrometrocolpos (HP:0030010), which indicates additional uterine dilation.
is_a: HP:0000142 ! Abnormal vagina morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:44:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030712
name: Uterine synechiae
def: "Adhesions or scar tissue that form inside the cavity of the uterus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
comment: Asherman syndrome is a condition characterized by formation of intrauterine adhesions and results from injury to the endometrium. Asherman syndrome is often associated with infertility.
synonym: "Asherman syndrome" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0031105 ! Abnormal uterus morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T21:50:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030713
name: Vein of Galen aneurysmal malformation
def: "Vein of Galen aneurysmal malformation is a choroidal type of arteriovenous malformation that develops between 6 and 11 weeks of gestation. It results from 1 or more arteriovenous fistulas shunting blood toward the prosencephalic vein of Markowski, the embryonic precursor of the vein of Galen. This abnormal shunt leads to progressive dilation of the vein and prevents its involution and subsequent development into the vein of Galen." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:32706613, PMID:33168212]
comment: The most common vascular CNS anomaly in the fetal brain is the vein of Galen malformation. At prenatal US, an anechoic cystic mass is seen in the midline, superior and posterior to the third ventricle and thalamus. Color and spectral Doppler imaging demonstrate the presence of low-resistance flow and a turbulent waveform. Blood flow may be seen draining posteriorly into the venous sinuses. See Figure 13 of PMID:32706613.
synonym: "Median prosencephalic arteriovenous fistula" EXACT []
synonym: "Vein of Galen aneurysm" EXACT []
synonym: "Vein of Galen malformation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012480 ! Abnormal cerebral vein morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T22:07:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030714
name: Subchorionic thrombohematoma
def: "A large maternal clot that separates the chorionic plate from the villous chorion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:11125254]
synonym: "Breus' mole" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100767 ! Abnormal placenta morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T22:12:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030715
name: Bronchial atresia
def: "A developmental anomaly characterized by focal obliteration of the proximal segment of a bronchus. The bronchial pattern is entirely normal distal to the site of stenosis." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
synonym: "Congenital bronchial atresia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025426 ! Abnormal bronchus morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T22:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030716
name: Acrania
def: "Partial or complete absence of the flat bones of the cranial vault. The condition is frequently, though not always, associated with anencephaly." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
is_a: HP:0002683 ! Abnormal calvaria morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T22:21:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030717
name: Meconium peritonitis
def: "Peritonitis caused by intrauterine intestinal rupture and spillage of fetal meconium into the fetal peritoneal cavity. Intra-peritoneal meconium usually calcifies, sometimes within 24 hours. Ultrasound findings may include intraabdominal calcifications." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:3317498]
is_a: HP:0002586 ! Peritonitis
property_value: terms:date "2016-02-25T22:28:31Z" xsd:dateTime

