[Term]
id: HP:0030752
name: Dacryocystocele
def: "A nasolacrimal duct obstruction presenting as a grey-blue cystic swelling just below the medial canthus. Believed to be a result of concomitant upper obstruction of the Rosenmuller valve and lower obstruction of the Hasner valve." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754, PMID:19205594]
synonym: "Timo cyst" EXACT []
