[Term]
id: HP:0030762
name: Mesangiolysis
def: "Partial or complete dissolution of the mesangial matrix, identified by reduced staining on a periodic acid-Schiff (PAS) or silver stain." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:32866505, PMID:6353041]
comment: Dissolution or attenuation of mesangial matrix and degeneration of mesangial cells. In essence, mesangiolysis is an injurious process which affects the glomerular mesangium without causing obvious damage to the capillary basement membranes. The matrix swells, loosens, and eventually dissolves; the mesangial cells may show only edema and vacuolization, or may undergo severe degeneration and necrosis.
is_a: HP:0033232 ! Abnormal glomerular mesangial matrix morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-03-16T20:39:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030763
name: Amniotic Sheet
def: "A sheet like projection that can result from uterine synechiae that has been encompassed by the expanding chorion and amnion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0003-6754]
synonym: "Amniotic shelf" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011409 ! Abnormal placental membrane morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-03-16T20:41:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030764
name: Ochronosis
def: "Brown or blue-gray discoloration of the skin that can present on the axillary and inguinal areas, face, palms or soles. In addition, blue-black discoloration can be apparent on skin overlying cartilage in which the pigment is deposited, such as the ears. This is a characteristic manifestation of alkaptonuria, which is an autosomal recessively inherited deficiency of homogentisic acid oxidase that results in accumulation of homogentisic acid in collagenous structures. The sclerae are also typically involved." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24447956, PMID:26929770]
synonym: "Ochronotic arthritis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011121 ! Abnormal skin morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-03-17T06:27:31Z" xsd:dateTime

