[Term]
id: HP:0030824
name: Mizuo phenomenon
def: "Change in the color of the fundus from red in the dark-adapted state to golden immediately or shortly after the onset of the light. The color of the fundus reflex in the light adapted state has also been described as golden-yellow, gray-white, and yellow-white. This reflex can appear either homogeneous or in streaks in the fundus. The retinal vessels appear to be protruding in contrast to the radiant background. Dark adaptation leads to disappearance of the unusual fundus coloration [Digital Journal of Ophthalmology 2008; Volume 14, Number 14]." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Mizuo-Nakamura phenomenon" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001098 ! Abnormal fundus morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-04-15T21:19:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030825
name: Absent foveal reflex
def: "Absent reflectivity of the fovea, which normally is a bright pinpoint of light that is observed to move sideways or up and down in response to movement of the opthalmoscope." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:27491360]
comment: Absence of the foveal reflex can occur with macular edema, central serous retinopathy, or other macular abnormalities such as macular dystrophy. The macular reflex is often less pronounced in adults than in children, and may be absent in otherwise normal eyes of older individuals.
synonym: "Foveal reflex absent" EXACT []
synonym: "Loss of foveal reflex" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000493 ! Abnormal foveal morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-04-15T21:29:14Z" xsd:dateTime

