[Term]
id: HP:0030883
name: Femoroacetabular impingement
def: "Femoroacetabular impingement (FAI) results from one or more bony abnormalities that lead to abnormal contact between the acetabulum and the femoral head or neck. The femoral abnormality is proposed to cause compression and shear stresses in the region between the labrum and cartilage, anterosuperiorly. These stresses cause a separation between the labrum and cartilage as the labrum is pushed outwards and the cartilage is pushed centrally. This eventually leads to articular degeneration and eventually global hip osteoarthritis." [PMID:22108232]
synonym: "Femoral acetabular impingement" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001384 ! Abnormal hip joint morphology
property_value: terms:date "2016-07-02T08:33:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030884
name: Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy
def: "Feeding problem necessitating gastrojejunal tube feeding." [PMID:11827911]
comment: The rationale for gastrojejunal tube feeding is that placing the tip of the tube beyond the ligament of Treitz prevented duodenogastric reflux or gastro-esophageal reflux. Gastrojejunal feeding tubes have since been used in children who are deemed too unfit for antireflux surgery or where fundoplication has failed.
synonym: "Gastro-jejunal tube feeding in infancy" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008872 ! Feeding difficulties in infancy
is_a: HP:0033454 ! Tube feeding
property_value: terms:date "2016-07-02T08:46:47Z" xsd:dateTime

