[Term]
id: HP:0030934
name: Oral erythroplakia
def: "A velvety red but not ulcerated lesion of the oral mucosa. The texture may be roughened or normal, and the lesion is neither raised nor depressed." []
comment: Oral erythroplakia may be related to local irritants and infection, candida infection. Oral erythroplakia may be dysplastic or (pre-)neoplastic.
synonym: "Oral erythroplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011830 ! Abnormal oral mucosa morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-11-07T18:48:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030935
name: Abnormal intestinal smooth muscle morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the nonstriated, involuntary muscle tissue of the intestine." []
synonym: "Abnormality of intestinal smooth muscle morphology" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002242 ! Abnormal intestine morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-12-02T15:17:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030936
name: Abnormal layering of muscularis propria
def: "Abnormal layering of the intestinal muscularis propria into three layers; (1) inner circular; (2) additional oblique; and (3) outer longitudinal layer." [PMID:18788889, PMID:26078585]
comment: The intestinal muscularis propria is organized into discrete inner circular and outer longitudinal layers of muscle fibers that are oriented perpendicular to one another, except in the appendix, where the arrangement is more haphazard. The myenteric plexus of ganglia and nerves is sandwiched between the 2 muscle layers and is required for peristaltic activity. Maldevelopment or disruption of the neural or muscular elements can impair intestinal motility and cause intestinal pseudo-obstruction. This term refers to a malformation of the muscularis propria, with supernumerary and/or haphazard orientation of muscle fibers.
synonym: "Muscularis propria malformation" EXACT []
synonym: "Segmental additional circular muscle coat" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030935 ! Abnormal intestinal smooth muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-12-02T15:21:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030937
name: Fibrotic muscularis propria
def: "The presence of excessive fibrous connective tissue in the muscularis propria of the intestine. Fibrosis is a reparative or reactive process." []
is_a: HP:0030935 ! Abnormal intestinal smooth muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2016-12-02T21:21:03Z" xsd:dateTime

