[Term]
id: HP:0030946
name: Conjunctival papillae
def: "Raised tissue masses located on the palpebral conjunctiva with a central vessel. Papillae are created by a focal infiltration of inflammatory cells." []
comment: Papillae may be observed with papillary conjunctivitis. The inflammatory cells in the papillae may differ according to the cause. For instance, eosinophils predominate in allergic conditions and neutrophils in bacterial disease.
synonym: "Bumps under the upper eyelid" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Tarsal papillae" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T20:21:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030947
name: Conjunctival follicles
def: "Small, dome-shaped nodules without a prominent central vessel located on the conjunctiva. The lymphoid follicles are located in the subendothelial region of the conjunctiva. They consist of a germinal center that contains immature, proliferating lymphocytes, as well as a corona that contains mature lymphocytes and plasma cells." []
comment: The follicles in follicular conjunctivitis are usually most prominent in the inferior palpebral and forniceal conjunctiva. As compared to conjunctival papillae, conjunctival follicles appear more pale on the surface and redder at the base.
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T20:23:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030948
name: Elevated gamma-glutamyltransferase level
def: "Increased level of the enzyme gamma-glutamyltransferase (GGT). GGT is mainly present in kidney, liver, and pancreatic cells, but small amounts are present in other tissues." [PMID:26543300]
comment: Gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT) is elevated with most liver diseases and with bile duct damage. Its main clinical use is in the evaluation of patients with isolated elevation in alkaline phosphatase (which can be of hepatic or bone origin). However, there are extrahepatic causes of GGT elevation including pancreatitis, prostate carcinoma, breast carcinoma, lung carcinoma, systemic lupus erythematosus, and congestive heart failure.
synonym: "Elevated serum GGT" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0034444 ! Abnormal gamma-glutamyltransferase level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T21:20:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030949
name: Glomerular deposits
def: "An abnormal accumulation of protein in the glomerulus." []
is_a: HP:0000095 ! Abnormal renal glomerulus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T21:44:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030950
name: Pulmonary venous hypertension
def: "An abnormal increase in pressure in the pulmonary veins, usually as a result of left atrial hypertension." []
comment: Common causes of pulmonary venous hypertension are obstruction to left ventricular (LV) inflow, LV systolic dysfunction, severe mitral regurgitation, and acute pulmonary and systemic volume overload. As the pulmonary venous pressure nears 22 mm Hg, interstitial pulmonmary edema may develop. As it reaches 25 mm Hg, alveolar edema may ensue.
is_a: HP:0030875 ! Abnormality of pulmonary circulation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T21:56:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030951
name: Skeletal muscle fibrosis
def: "Excessive formation of fibrous bands of scar tissue in between muscle fibers." [PMID:21798099]
comment: Pathophysiologic fibrosis, which is essentially an excessive accumulation of extracellular matrix components, particularly collagen, is the end result of a cascade of events proceeding from tissue injury via inflammation, and resulting in permanent scar formation. Fibrosis can impair tissue function. In skeletal muscle, fibrosis is most often associated with the muscular dystrophies.
synonym: "Muscle biopsy: fibrosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011805 ! Abnormal skeletal muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T22:27:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0030952
name: Birdshot choroidal lesions
def: "Multiple cream-yellow colored hypopigmented lesions typically located at the level of the outer choroid. They are between 50 and 1,500 micrometers in size with a characteristic nasal, radial distribution in the postequatorial fundus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9114-8737, PMID:25667738, PMID:33845003]
comment: Birdshot choroidal lesions are associated with Birdshot retinochoroidopathy.
synonym: "Birdshot laesions" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Birdshot lesions" EXACT []
synonym: "Birdshot retinochoroidopathy" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000610 ! Abnormal choroid morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-01-13T22:33:03Z" xsd:dateTime

