[Term]
id: HP:0031015
name: Intrahepatic portal vein sclerosis
def: "Sclerosis of the intrahepatic portal veins of the liver and generally accompanied by non-cirrhotic portal hypertension, features of which may include splenomegaly and varices." [PMID:25796481]
comment: The diagnosis is based on histological examination of the liver. Clinical manifestations include encephalopathy, ascites and variceal bleeding.
synonym: "Idiopathic non-cirrhotic portal hypertension" RELATED []
synonym: "Incomplete septal cirrhosis" RELATED []
synonym: "Non cirrhotic portal fibrosis" RELATED []
synonym: "Obliterative portal venopathy" RELATED []
