property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-20T11:15:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031016
name: Alternating radiolucent and radiodense metaphyseal lines
def: "Areas of radio-opaque sclerotic bands alternating with those of normal lucency give rise to stripes akin to a zebra." [PMID:28384951]
comment: In cases where this sign arises in children treated with bisphosphonates, the sign is known as the zebra stripe sign, which is radiological manifestation of cyclical bisphosphonate therapy prior to closure of epiphyseal growth plates.
synonym: "Zebra stripe sign" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0000944 ! Abnormal metaphysis morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-20T11:32:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031017
name: Swiss cheese atrial septal defect
def: "Multiple defects in the atrial septum." [PMID:18559707]
comment: The label derives from the resemblance of the multiple atrial defects to Emmental cheese, a medium-hard cheese of Swiss origin that features characteristic holes.
is_a: HP:0001631 ! Atrial septal defect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-20T11:43:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031018
name: Eccrine syringofibroadenoma
def: "Eccrine syringofibroadenoma (ESFA) is a benign adnexal tumor arising most often on the extremities of elderly individuals characterized by anastomosing cords of cuboidal epithelial cells surrounded by a fibrovascular stroma containing plasma cells and ductal structures. ESFA stains positively with epithelial membrane antigen (EMA) and carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA)." [NCIT:CL017969, PMID:26937300]
synonym: "Acrosyringeal adenomatosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Eccrine syringofibroadenomatous hyperplasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Syringofibroadenoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-31T00:32:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031019
name: Pyknotic bone marrow neutrophils
def: "Nuclear lobes of neutrophils in the bone marrow are thickened and condensed, and individual lobes are connected by unusually long chromatin filaments." []
is_a: HP:0011992 ! Abnormal neutrophil morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-14T16:30:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031020
name: Bone marrow hypercellularity
def: "A larger than normal amount or percentage of hematopoietic cells relative to marrow fat." []
synonym: "Myeloid hyperplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012145 ! Abnormality of multiple cell lineages in the bone marrow
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-14T16:35:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031021
name: Squamous Papilloma
def: "A benign epithelial neoplasm characterized by a papillary growth pattern and a proliferation of neoplastic squamous cells without morphologic evidence of malignancy [NCI thesaurus]." []
xref: NCIT:C3712
is_a: HP:0012740 ! Papilloma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T13:13:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031022
name: Oropharyngeal squamous papilloma
def: "A benign exophytic neoplasm that arises from the oropharynx. It is characterized by the presence of a connective tissue core covered by stratified squamous epithelium [NCI thesaurus]." []
synonym: "Squamous papilloma of the uvula" NARROW []
xref: NCIT:C6038
