property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T13:15:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031023
name: Multiple mucosal neuromas
def: "Multiple painful, dome-shaped, translucent pink to skin-colored papules on oral mucosa. Histologically, the lesions may demonstrate dermal proliferation of well-demarcated nerve bundles associated with abundant mucin and surrounded by a distinct perineural sheath." [PMID:16702501]
xref: NCIT:C6559
is_a: HP:0030430 ! Neuroma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T13:18:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031024
name: Cylindroma
def: "A benign skin adnexal tumor of eccrine differentiation." [NCIT:C27094, PMID:27294061]
comment: Cylindromas can be single or multiple and commonly involve the scalp (turban tumor) and face. Multiple cylindromas can have a syndromic association as seen in Brooke-Spiegler syndrome and familial cylindromatosis.
is_a: HP:0012842 ! Skin appendage neoplasm
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T13:32:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031025
name: Gastric leiomyosarcoma
def: "A malignant neoplasm of the stomach that grows submucosally in the gastric wall. Necrosis and hemorrhage may be visible radiologically. Histologically, spindle cells with abnormal mitotic activity may be visible." [NCIT:C27200, PMID:25069607]
comment: Gastric leiomyosarcomas are often clinically silent until they reach a large size, bleed or rupture. Thus, the diagnosis is rarely made preoperatively. Since in many cases the mucosa is normal, a definitive diagnosis for resectable tumor is often made after surgery. Seeding of tumor deposits into the serosa or omentum is almost invariably a sign of malignancy.
is_a: HP:0006753 ! Neoplasm of the stomach
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T13:42:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031026
name: Snail-like ilia
def: "The ilia is round and hypoplastic with a very flat acetabular roof and a very unusual medial projection of bone that is said to resemble the head of a snail. Figure 4 of PMID:3799723 illustrates this feature." [PMID:3799723]
comment: This feature was first observed in a condition that was termed Schneckenbecken dysplasia, Schneckenbecken is a German word that means snail-like pelvis.
synonym: "Schneckenbecken dysplasia" RELATED []
synonym: "Snail-like pelvis" EXACT []
synonym: "Snail-shaped ilia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002867 ! Abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T15:50:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031027
name: Internal notch of the femoral head
def: "A small V-shaped indentation on the internal aspect of the femoral head. This feature is well illustrated in Figure 5 of PMID:11694546." [PMID:11694546, PMID:24339047]
is_a: HP:0003368 ! Abnormal femoral head morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-21T16:09:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031028
name: Lactescent serum
def: "Serum sample with a grossly white (milk-like, i.e., lactescent) appearance. This feature is indicative of an extremely elevated serum triglyceride level." [PMID:15368719]
comment: The normal range for serum triglycerides can be taken to be 40 to 150 mg per dL (0.45 to 1.69 mmol per L). Lactescent serum can be seen with triglyceride levels of several thousand mg per dL.
synonym: "Milk-like serum" EXACT []
synonym: "Plasma lactescence" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002155 ! Hypertriglyceridemia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T10:37:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031029
name: Elevated circulating CEA concentration
def: "The concentration of CEA (carcinoembryonic antigen) in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a member of the immunoglobulin supergene family. The human CEA gene family is clustered on chromosome 19q and comprises 29 genes. CEA is highly expressed in embryonic tissue and in some cancers, and is a widely used tumor marker.
synonym: "Elevated carcinoembryonic antigen level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased plasma CEA" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T10:48:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031030
name: Elevated circulating mucin 16 concentration
def: "The concentration of mucin-16 (also known as CA-125) in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Cancer-antigen 125 (CA-125) is used as a biomarker for ovarian and other cancers. Mucin 16 (cancer antigen 125) is a cell surface glycoprotein that plays a role in promoting cancer cell growth in ovarian cancer.
synonym: "Elevated carcinoma antigen 125 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated circulating CA-125 concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated mucin-16 concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated mucin-16 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated mucin-16 level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased mucin-16 concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased mucin-16 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased mucin-16 level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased plasma CA125" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T10:54:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031031
name: Abnormal circulating retinol-binding protein concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of retinol-binding protein in the blood circulation." []
comment: The most commonly used indicator of vitamin A status is the serum retinol concentration (retinol is one of the several compounds known as vitamin A). The serum retinol-binding protein (RBP) concentration is used as a surrogate measure for serum retinol.
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T10:59:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031032
name: Decreased circulating retinol-binding protein concentration
def: "The concentration of retinol-binding protein in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0031031 ! Abnormal circulating retinol-binding protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:03:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031033
name: Impaired urinary acidification
def: "The kidney contributes towards acid-base homeostasis by excreting H+ ions and retaining bicarbonate. This process is known as acidification of the urine. The pH of urine ranges normally from 4.5 to 8. The inability to reduce the pH of the urine in a situation where it would be otherwise expected is known as an acidification defect." [PMID:6876936]
synonym: "Renal acidification defect" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012211 ! Abnormal renal physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:07:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031034
name: Abnormal circulating insulin-like growth factor-binding protein acid labile subunit concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of insulin-like growth factor-binding protein acid labile subunit in the blood circulation." [PMID:8816745]
comment: Insulin like growth factor binding protein acid labile subunit (IGFALS; Entrez Gene ID 3483) acts in the insulin-like growth (IGF) system by binding circulating IGF1 in a ternary complex with binding protein (IGFBP)-3 to prevent IGF1 from crossing the endothelial barrier. This term refers specifically to the circulating concentration of the acid-labile subunit.
synonym: "Abnormal insulin-like growth factor-binding protein complex acid labile subunit level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:20:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031035
name: Chronic infection
def: "Presence of a protracted or persistent infection by a pathogen potentially related to an underlying abnormality of the immune system that is not able to clear the infection." []
is_a: HP:0032101 ! Unusual infection
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-14T16:40:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031036
name: Decreased circulating GH-binding protein concentration
def: "The concentration of GH-binding protein (= growth hormone-binding protein) in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." []
synonym: "Decreased plasma GH-binding protein" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:34:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031037
name: Reduced insulin-like factor 3 level
def: "Blood concentration of insulin-like factor 3 (ILF3) is below normal limits." [PMID:24640568]
comment: Insulin-like factor 3 (INSL3) is a peptide hormone produced in leydig cells of the testes. Its role in the adult male is unknown but INSL3 and its receptor RXFP2 have been linked to bone cell differentiation. It is speculated that low levels of INSL3 could be responsible for low bone mineral density in patients with primary osteoporosis and Klinefelter Syndrome.
synonym: "Reduced plasma INSL3 level" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:44:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031038
name: Spermatogenesis maturation arrest
def: "Maturation arrest (MA) is defined as germ cells that fail to complete maturation. Uniform MA is characterized by spermatogenic arrest at the same stage of spermatogenesis throughout the seminiferous tubules. MA is subcategorized into early MA, in which only spermatogonia or spermatocytes are found, and late MA, in which spermatids are detected without spermatozoa." [PMID:21684558]
comment: Maturation arrest (MA) of spermatogenesis is diagnosed on histology as interruption of spermatogenesis before the final stage without impairment of Sertoli or Leydig cells. It is considered a condition of irreversible or absolute infertility.
synonym: "Meiotic maturation arrest of spermatogenesis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008669 ! Abnormal spermatogenesis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:49:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031039
name: Spermatocyte maturation arrest
def: "A type of spermatogenesis maturation arrest in which the block of developmental occurs in the spermatocyte stage. Testicular histology shows seminiferous tubules with Sertoli cells, spermatogonial cells and spermatocytes but no further differentiated cells like round spermatids." [PMID:21684558]
synonym: "Spermatocyte arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Spermatocyte meiotic arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Spermatocytic arrest" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031038 ! Spermatogenesis maturation arrest
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:50:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031040
name: Round spermatid arrest
def: "A failure of spermatogenesis to progress beyond the round spermatid stage. The round spermatid is the first haploid cells produced during spermatogenesis and normally further develop into mature spermatozoa. This abnormality can be visualized with testicular biopsy and is characterized seminiferous tubules with increased numbers of round spermatids with few or no mature spermatozoa." [PMID:21684558, PMID:9510006]
comment: See Figure 2c and 2d of PMID:9510006.
synonym: "Late spermatogenesis maturation arrest" RELATED []
synonym: "Maturation arrest of spermatogenesis at spermatid stage" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031038 ! Spermatogenesis maturation arrest
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T11:51:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031041
name: Obstruction of the superior vena cava
def: "Blockage of blood flow through the superior vena cava (SVC). Because the venous drainage from the upper extremities, upper thorax and head is obstructed, SVC obstruction presents with symptoms related to engorgement of these areas. Both the degree of SVC compromise and the extent of collateral veins determine the varied clinical presentation, which can be as mild as slight facial and upper extremity edema or as dire as intracranial swelling, seizures, hemodynamic instability and tracheal obstruction." []
comment: Diagnosis of superior vena cava obstruction may be made by computed tomography with contrast and other means.
synonym: "Superior vena cava obstruction" EXACT []
synonym: "Superior vena cava syndrome" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0025575 ! Abnormal superior vena cava morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T12:23:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031042
name: Strawberry tongue
def: "Inflamed tongue with hyperplastic (enlarged) fungiform papillae that is said to resemble a strawberry or raspberry." [PMID:26222562]
synonym: "Raspberry tongue" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030809 ! Abnormal tongue morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T13:34:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031043
name: Type A4 brachydactyly
def: "A type of brachydactyly characterized by brachymesophalangy affecting mainly the 2nd and 5th digits." [PMID:8387724]
is_a: HP:0009370 ! Type A brachydactyly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T13:45:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031044
name: Type A5 brachydactyly
def: "A type of brachydactyly characterized by absent middle phalanges of digits 2 to 5." [PMID:18554391]
comment: Individuals with BDA5 may have nail dysplasia; this should be coded separately.
is_a: HP:0009370 ! Type A brachydactyly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-05-27T13:48:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031045
name: Acral blistering
