[Term]
id: HP:0031136
name: Decreased acrosin in sperm head
def: "A reduced amount of the enzyme acrosin in the sperm head acrosome. The acrosome is an organelle in the anterior half of the head of spermatozoa, and acrosin is a protease that contributes to the digestation of the zona pellucida in the fertilization process." []
is_a: HP:0012865 ! Abnormal sperm head morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-10T15:21:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031137
name: Storage in hepatocytes
def: "Hepatocytes (liver parenchymal cells) exhibit a bloated appearance because of expansion of the cytoplasm by accumulated material." []
is_a: HP:0034644 ! Abnormal liver metabolite concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-10T15:30:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031138
name: Abnormal circulating B-type natriuretic peptide concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal circulating concentration of B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP)." [PMID:22145138]
comment: Increased plasma levels of circulating natriuretic peptides (NP) have been described in patients with congestive heart failure and are directly proportional to the severity of congestive heart failure as classified by the New York Heart Association criteria.
synonym: "Abnormal B-type natriuretic peptide level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:6000692 ! Abnormal circulating proANP concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-10T18:39:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031139
name: Frog-leg posture
def: "A type of rest posture in an infant that indicated a generalized reduction in muscle tone. The hips are flexed and the legs are abducted to an extent that causes the lateral thigh to rest upon the supporting surface. This posture is said to resemble the legs of a frog." []
is_a: HP:0001252 ! Hypotonia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-10T22:38:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031140
name: Abnormal liver sonography
def: "An abnormal appearance of the liver or any of its components on sonography (ultrasound)." []
is_a: HP:0410042 ! Abnormal liver morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:18:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031141
name: Increased hepatic echogenicity
def: "Increased echogenicity of liver tissue on sonography, manifested as an increased amount of white on the screen of the sonography device." [PMID:21472065]
synonym: "Hyperechogenic liver" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031142 ! Abnormal hepatic echogenicity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:19:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031142
name: Abnormal hepatic echogenicity
def: "Any deviation from the normal degree of echogenicity of the liver on sonography. Echogenicity refers to the ability of a tissue to reflect or transmit ultrasound waves in the context of surrounding tissues. Whenever there is an interface of structures with different echogenicities, a visible difference in contrast will be apparent on the screen. Based on echogenicity, a structure can be characterized as hyperechoic (white on the screen), hypoechoic (gray on the screen) and anechoic (black on the screen)." [PMID:21472065]
is_a: HP:0031140 ! Abnormal liver sonography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:20:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031143
name: Decreased hepatic echogenicity
def: "Reduced echogenicity of liver tissue on sonography, manifested as an increased amount of black on the screen of the sonography device." [PMID:21472065]
synonym: "Hypoechogenic liver" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031142 ! Abnormal hepatic echogenicity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:23:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031144
name: Coarsened hepatic echotexture
def: "The appearance of the liver in sonographic images is normally uniform. This term applies when there is an irregular or non-uniform appearance of the liver parenchyma in liver sonography." []
is_a: HP:0031140 ! Abnormal liver sonography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:31:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031145
name: Starry sky appearance on hepatic sonography
def: "An abnormal echotexture visible in liver ultrasound manifesting as a diffuse hyperechoic liver echotexture with multiple, small hypoechoic lesions. The appearance is said to resemble a starry sky (multiple white spots on a dark background)." [PMID:26157918]
is_a: HP:0031140 ! Abnormal liver sonography
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T19:50:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031146
name: Impaired oral bolus formation
def: "An abnormality of swallowing characterized by reduced tongue coordination to form bolus after chewing. Food material spreads over the oral cavity instead of being concentrated into a bolus that is easily swallowed." [PMID:16776766]
is_a: HP:0002015 ! Dysphagia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-11T20:31:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031150
name: Vitreomacular adhesion
def: "Perifoveal vitreous separation with remaining vitreomacular attachment and unperturbed foveal morphologic features. It is an OCT finding that is almost always the result of normal vitreous aging, which may lead to pathologic conditions." [PMID:24053995]
synonym: "VMA" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:09:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031151
name: Vitreomacular traction
def: "Vitreomacular traction is characterized by anomalous posterior vitreous detachment accompanied by anatomic distortion of the fovea, which may include pseudocysts, macular schisis, cystoid macular edema, and subretinal fluid. Vitreomacular traction can be subclassified by the diameter of vitreous attachment to the macular surface as measured by OCT, with attachment of 1500 micrometers or less defined as focal and attachment of more than 1500 micrometers as broad." [PMID:24053995]
synonym: "VMT" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0001103 ! Abnormal macular morphology
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:11:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031152
name: Full-thickness macular hole
def: "Full-thickness macular hole (FTMH) is defined as a foveal lesion with interruption of all retinal layers from the internal limiting membrane to the retinal pigment epithelium. Full-thickness macular hole is primary if caused by vitreous traction or secondary if directly the result of pathologic characteristics other than vitreomacular traction. Full-thickness macular hole is subclassified by size of the hole as determined by OCT and the presence or absence of vitreomacular traction." [PMID:24053995]
synonym: "FTMH" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0011508 ! Macular hole
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:12:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031153
name: Membranous vitreous appearance
def: "Vitreous humor of the eye displaying consisting of a vestigial gel in the retrolental space bounded by a convoluted membrane." [PMID:20513134, PMID:21921955]
synonym: "Membranous anomaly" EXACT []
synonym: "Membranous vitreous" EXACT []
synonym: "Membranous vitreous phenotype" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:16:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031154
name: Beaded vitreous appearance
def: "Vitreous humor of the eye displaying beaded bundles of irregular diameters." [PMID:20513134, PMID:21921955]
is_a: HP:0004327 ! Abnormal vitreous humor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:18:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031155
name: Increased Arden ratio of electrooculogram
def: "An abnormal increase in the Arden ratio, which is the ratio between the light peak and the dark trough of the smoothed (physiologic) EOG record." []
synonym: "Increased Arden ratio of EOG" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0030454 ! Abnormal electrooculogram
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T13:19:50Z" xsd:dateTime

