property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T19:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031167
name: Triggered by ingestion of potassium-rich food
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by eating or drinking foods rich in potassium." [PMID:19472919]
comment: In contrast to paramyotonia congenita or hyperkalaemic periodic paralysis, potassium-aggravated myotonias (PAM) patients show no muscle weakness and hardly any cold sensitivity. However, they show an aggravation of their myotonia after ingestion of potassium, which distinguishes them from patients with chloride channelopathies.
synonym: "Potassium-rich food triggered symptoms" EXACT []
synonym: "Triggered by ingestion of K-rich food" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0033793 ! Triggered by food ingestion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T19:18:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031169
name: Postterm pregnancy
def: "A pregnancy that extends to 42 weeks of gestation or beyond." [PMID:24753906]
comment: This term can apply to a child born of a postterm pregnancy.
is_a: HP:0001197 ! Abnormality of prenatal development or birth
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T19:54:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031170
name: Female fetal virilization
def: "Fetal masculinization of female external genitalia." []
comment: This anomaly can be observed with etiologies including 21-hydroxylase deficiency, pregnancy luteomas, and maternal intake of progesterones.
synonym: "Female foetal virilization" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034242 ! Abnormal fetal genitourinary system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T19:57:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031171
name: Femoral spur
def: "A bony projection (spur, osteophyte) originating from the femur, often in the medial femoral neck." []
synonym: "Spurring of femur" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002823 ! Abnormal femur morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T20:02:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031172
name: Sectoral retinitis pigmentosa
def: "A variant of retinitis pigmentosa in which there is a regional distribution of the retinal degeneration." []
is_a: HP:0000510 ! Rod-cone dystrophy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-18T20:05:46Z" xsd:dateTime

