[Term]
id: HP:0031192
name: Abnormal morphology of left ventricular trabeculae
def: "Any structural anomaly of the muscular columns which project from the inner surface of the left ventricle of the heart (cardiac trabeculae, trabeculae carneae)." []
is_a: HP:0030681 ! Abnormal morphology of myocardial trabeculae
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-24T14:10:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031193
name: Abnormal morphology of right ventricular trabeculae
def: "Any structural anomaly of the muscular columns which project from the inner surface of the right ventricle of the heart (cardiac trabeculae, trabeculae carneae)." []
is_a: HP:0030681 ! Abnormal morphology of myocardial trabeculae
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-24T14:10:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031194
name: Increased density of left ventricular trabeculae
def: "An increased density (number and tightness) of the muscular columns which project from the inner surface of the left ventricles of the heart (cardiac trabeculae, trabeculae carneae)." []
is_a: HP:0031192 ! Abnormal morphology of left ventricular trabeculae
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-24T14:13:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031195
name: Apical hypertrabeculation of the left ventricle
def: "An increased number and density of the trabeculae in the apex (tip) of the left ventricle." []
is_a: HP:0031192 ! Abnormal morphology of left ventricular trabeculae
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-24T14:15:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031196
name: Thin myocardium compact layer
def: "Reduced thickness of the outer, dense layer of the myocardium." []
comment: The myocardium compact layer is only in the left ventricle.
is_a: HP:0031316 ! Abnormal ventricular myocardium morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-24T14:16:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031197
name: Cellular urinary casts
def: "A type of urinary cast composed of cells incorporated in a protein matrix. The cells can be those found in the urinary sediment (erythrocytes, leuklocytes, renal tubular epithelial cells)." []
synonym: "Cellular casts" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012615 ! Cylindruria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T10:50:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031198
name: Renal tubular epithelial cell casts
def: "A type of cellular urinary cast composed of renal tubular epithelial cells." []
comment: Renal tubular epithelial cell casts can be observed in disorders including renal tubular necrosis, cytomegalovirus and other viral infections, kidney transplant rejection.
is_a: HP:0031197 ! Cellular urinary casts
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T10:53:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031199
name: Acellular urinary casts
def: "A type of urinary cast composed of a proteinaceous matrix without a substantial number of cells." []
synonym: "Acellular casts" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012615 ! Cylindruria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T10:55:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031200
name: Hyaline casts
def: "A type of acellular urinary cast that are composed only of Tamm-Horsfall glycoprotein, a fact which explains their low refractive index. Hyaline casts may display a spectrum of morphologies, which includes fluffy, compact, convoluted or wrinkled casts. Hyaline casts have a smooth texture and usually have parallel sides with clear margins and blunted ends." [PMID:26079824]
is_a: HP:0031199 ! Acellular urinary casts
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T11:00:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031201
name: Granular casts
def: "A type of acelluar casts that have a surface composed of granules, which can vary in size. The granules can be rather heterogeneous, ranging from fine (finely granular cast) up to coarse (coarsely granular cast), dark, clear, and pigmented." [PMID:26079824]
comment: It has been demonstrated that in patients with proteinuria, fine granules contain ultrafiltered proteins which have been reabsorbed by tubular cells, whilst in non-proteinuric patients coarse granules probably derive from the degeneration of cellular elements, such as leukocytes and renal epithelial cells present in the tubular lumen during cast formation.
is_a: HP:0031199 ! Acellular urinary casts
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T11:06:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031202
name: Waxy casts
def: "A type of acellular urinary casts that display a melted wax (waxy) appearance, which gives them a high refractive index. They are frequently dark, with blunt extremities, indented and cracked edges and a large size, which is often several times that of other types of casts." [PMID:26079824]
is_a: HP:0031199 ! Acellular urinary casts
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T11:08:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031203
name: Fatty casts
def: "A type of acellular urinary casts that contain lipid droplets, oval fat bodies or cholesterol crystals, and are often associated with the free forms of these elements. Their identification may require the use of polarized light microscopy, under which fatty particles embedded into the cast matrix appear as Maltese crosses." [PMID:26079824]
comment: The presence of fatty casts in urine may be associated with heavy proteinuria in patients with nephrotic syndrome.
is_a: HP:0031199 ! Acellular urinary casts
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T11:10:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031204
name: Bacterial cell casts
def: "A type of urinary cast that contain bacteria. Bacterial casts can be difficult to identify and can be distinguished from other types of casts using phase contrast microscopy. Bacterial casts are diagnostic of acute pyelonephritis or intrinsic renal infection." [PMID:26079824]
is_a: HP:0012615 ! Cylindruria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-27T11:12:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031205
name: Reduced lysosomal acid lipase activity
def: "Reduction in the activity of lysosomal acid lipase (LAL) in the blood. Lysosomal lipase activity is measured. LAL hydrolyzes cholesteryl esters derived from cell internalization of plasma lipoproteins." [PMID:22227072]
comment: Samples from patients with Wolman Disease display extremely low or unmeasurable levels of lysosomal acid lipase (LAL) activity. Samples from patients with cholesteryl ester storage disease can display residual activities in the 5 to ten percent range.
synonym: "Reduced leukocyte acid lipase activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-29T11:32:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031206
name: Striatal T2 hyperintensity
def: "Abnormally bright T2 signal from the striatum on brain magnetic resonance imaging." [PMID:27058447]
is_a: HP:0007183 ! Focal T2 hyperintense basal ganglia lesion
is_a: HP:0010994 ! Abnormal corpus striatum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-06-29T12:15:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031207
name: Hepatic hemangioma
def: "A congenital vascular malformation in the liver composed of masses of blood vessels that are atypical or irregular in arrangement and size." [NCIT:C3869, PMID:21191518]
comment: Hepatic hemangiomas are considered the most common benign mesenchymal hepatic tumors. They can be divided into two major groups: capillary hemangiomas and cavernous hemangiomas.
synonym: "Hemangioma of the liver" EXACT []
synonym: "Liver hemangioma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002896 ! Neoplasm of the liver
is_a: HP:0410266 ! Visceral hemangioma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T10:39:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031208
name: Increased pituitary glycoprotein hormone alpha subunit level
def: "An increased concentration of circulating alpha polypeptide of glycoprotein hormones (NCBI Gene 1081). This alpha subunit is common to luteinizing hormone (LH) , follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) , thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) and human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), which are glycoprotein hormones composed of an identical alpha subunit together with a beta subunit that confers biological specificity. The alpha subunit is used as a marker for tumors that produce these hormones." []
synonym: "Increased pituitary glycoprotein alpha subunit level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased pituitary glycoprotein polypeptide alpha subunit level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032481 ! Abnormal pituitary glycoprotein hormone alpha subunit level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T10:50:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031209
name: Decreased circulating lipoprotein lipase concentration
def: "Reduction in the level of lipoprotein lipase in the blood." [PMID:18194851, PMID:30725725]
comment: Decreased plasma lipoprotein lipase activity is associated with delayed clearance of triglyceride-rich lipoproteins and low fasting HDL cholesterol.
synonym: "Decreased lipoprotein lipase level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033477 ! Abnormal circulating lipoprotein lipase concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T10:57:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031210
name: Abnormal circulating hyaluronic acid concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of hyaluronic acid in the blood." [PMID:11861239]
comment: Serum hyaluronic acid (HA) is considered to be a marker of liver function. HA is a glycosaminoglycan that is rapidly cleared from the circulation by the liver via receptor mediated endocytosis into sinusoidal endothelial cells.
is_a: HP:0011012 ! Abnormal circulating polysaccharide concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:00:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031211
name: Elevated circulating cholesteryl ester concentration
alt_id: HP:0500010
def: "The concentration of cholesteryl ester in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Cholesterol esters are fatty acid esters of cholesterol and make up about two-thirds of total plasma cholesterol. The accumulation of cholesterol esters in the arterial intima is a characteristic feature of atherosclerosis.
synonym: "Elevated cholesteryl ester concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated cholesteryl ester level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated cholesteryl ester level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cholesterol esters" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cholesteryl ester concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cholesteryl ester level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cholesteryl ester level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased cholesteryl esters" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003107 ! Abnormal circulating cholesterol concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:04:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031212
name: Abnormal circulating progesterone level
is_a: HP:0033799 ! Abnormal circulating sex hormone concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:20:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031213
name: Elevated circulating 17-hydroxyprogesterone concentration
def: "An increased level of 17-hydroxyprogesterone in the blood. 17-hydroxyprogesterone is an intermediate steroid in the adrenal biosynthetic pathway from cholesterol to cortisol and is the substrate for steroid 21-hydroxylase." []
comment: An inherited deficiency of 21-hydroxylase leads to greatly increased serum concentrations of 17-hydroxyprogesterone (17-OHP), while the absence of cortisol synthesis causes an increase in adrenocorticotrophic hormone. Moderately increased levels of 17-OHP may indicate an 11-beta-hydroxylase deficiency.
synonym: "Elevated circulating 17-hydroxyprogesterone" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated circulating 17-OHP" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0031216 ! Increased circulating progesterone
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:21:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031214
name: Decreased circulating dehydroepiandrosterone concentration
comment: A reduced concentration of dehydroepiandrosterone in the blood. dehydroepiandrosterone is a weak androgen produced by the adrenal glands in both males and females.
synonym: "Decreased circulating dehydroepiandrosterone level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0500022 ! Abnormal circulating dehydroepiandrosterone concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:29:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031215
name: Decreased circulating dehydroepiandrosterone-sulfate concentration
def: "A reduced concentration of dehydroepiandrosterone-sulfate in the blood." []
comment: DHEA is transformed into DHEA-S by sulfation at the C3beta position by sulfotransferase SULT2A1.
synonym: "Decreased circulating dehydroepiandrosterone-sulfate level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030347 ! Abnormal circulating androgen level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:31:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031216
name: Increased circulating progesterone
def: "An elevated concentration of progesterone in the blood." []
is_a: HP:0031212 ! Abnormal circulating progesterone level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:33:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031217
name: Hot flashes
def: "Sudden feelings of warmth that are generally most pronounced over the face, neck and chest." []
comment: Hot flashes are most commonly due to menopause but may be observed with other conditions.
is_a: HP:0025142 ! Constitutional symptom
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:38:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031218
name: Inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion
def: "A state of increased circulating antidiuretic hormone despite hyponatremia and hypo-osmolality with normal or increased plasma volume." []
comment: Common etiologies of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone (ADH) secretion include nervous system disease, cancer, pulmonary disease, and as a side effect of a medication. This term is meant to refer to the inappropriately high level of ADH and not to the full syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), which is considered a disease entity rather than a phenotypic feature.
synonym: "Inappropriate ADH secretion" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "SIADH" RELATED abbreviation []
synonym: "Syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0031072 ! Abnormal endocrine physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:46:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031219
name: Reduced radioactive iodine uptake
def: "A decreased amount of uptake on the radioactive iodine uptake (RAIU) test, which utilizes a radioisotope of iodine to measure how much iodine the thyroid gland absorbs from the blood. The radioactive marker is measured 4-6 hours and in some cases also 24 hours after administration of the radioactive marker." []
is_a: HP:0031221 ! Abnormal radioactive iodine uptake test result
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:55:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031220
name: Increased radioactive iodine uptake
def: "An elevated amount of uptake on the radioactive iodine uptake (RAIU) test, which utilizes a radioisotope of iodine to measure how much iodine the thyroid gland absorbs from the blood. The radioactive marker is measured 4-6 hours and in some cases also 24 hours after administration of the radioactive marker." []
is_a: HP:0031221 ! Abnormal radioactive iodine uptake test result
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T11:59:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031221
name: Abnormal radioactive iodine uptake test result
def: "Any deviation from normal in the amount of uptake on the radioactive iodine uptake (RAIU) test, which utilizes a radioisotope of iodine to measure how much iodine the thyroid gland absorbs from the blood. The radioactive marker is measured 4-6 hours and in some cases also 24 hours after administration of the radioactive marker." []
is_a: HP:0002926 ! Abnormality of thyroid physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:00:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031222
name: Elevated circulating thyroxine-binding globulin concentration
def: "The concentration of thyroxine-binding globulin in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Thyroxine-binding globulin is one of the proteins that binds thyroid hormones in the circulation.
synonym: "Elevated thyroxine-binding globulin concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated thyroxine-binding globulin level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated thyroxine-binding globulin level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased thyroxine-binding globulin concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased thyroxine-binding globulin level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased thyroxine-binding globulin level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Thyroxine-binding globulin high in blood" EXACT []
