property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031223
name: Focal pancreatic islet hyperplasia
def: "Hyperplasia of the islets of Langerhans that affects only certain regions of the pancreas and not others." []
is_a: HP:0004510 ! Pancreatic islet-cell hyperplasia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:06:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031224
name: Diffuse pancreatic islet hyperplasia
def: "Hyperplasia of the islets of Langerhans with a generalized distribution." []
is_a: HP:0004510 ! Pancreatic islet-cell hyperplasia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:06:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031225
name: Intrapulmonary shunt
def: "Blood flow through a region of the lung in which little or no ventilation takes place, resulting in reduced oxygenation of the blood leaving the lungs." []
comment: Intrapulmonary shunt may be a result of blood flow through collapsed alveoli, tumors, arteriovenous pathways,and other conditions.
synonym: "Intrapulmonary shunting" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030875 ! Abnormality of pulmonary circulation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:12:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031226
name: Perinephric fluid collection
def: "An accumulation of fluid in one or more of the perinephric spaces, which consist of the subcapsular, perirenal, anterior and posterior pararenal spaces. This abnormality can be demonstrated by cross-sectional imaging, particularly computed tomography." [PMID:12014928]
is_a: HP:0012210 ! Abnormal renal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:16:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031227
name: Nasopharyngeal teratoma
def: "A teratoma arising in the nasopharyngeal region." [PMID:23056797]
comment: Nasopharyngeal teratoma is histologically benign, but can cause considerable morbidity and mortality because of the location. Nasopharyngeal teratoma represents one of the most unusual causes of respiratory distress during the neonatal period.
is_a: HP:0009792 ! Teratoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:40:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031228
name: Abnormal incisura morphology
def: "An abnormal shape of the incisura, defined as the narrowed downward continuation of the conchal space bounded anteriorly by the borders of the tragus, posteriorly by the antitragus, and along its lower lateral margins and inferior boundary by the connection between the first two. The upper boundary is a somewhat arbitrary line crossing from the apices of the antitragus and the tragus." [PMID:20082456]
is_a: HP:0011039 ! Abnormal helix morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:57:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031229
name: Increased incisura length
def: "The length of the incisura from the upper to lower border is greater than that observed in the average population." [PMID:20082456]
is_a: HP:0031228 ! Abnormal incisura morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T12:58:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031230
name: Decreased incisura length
def: "The length of the incisura from the upper to lower border is less than that observed in the average population." [PMID:20082456]
is_a: HP:0031228 ! Abnormal incisura morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T13:00:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031231
name: Narrow incisura width
def: "Width of the incisura from the anterior to posterior border less than that observed in the average population." [PMID:20082456]
is_a: HP:0031228 ! Abnormal incisura morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T13:00:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031232
name: Increased incisura width
def: "Breadth of the incisura from the anterior to posterior border greater than that observed in the average population." [PMID:20082456]
comment: This aspect may be difficult to assess in instances where the anterior and posterior walls of the incisura are not parallel.
is_a: HP:0031228 ! Abnormal incisura morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T13:02:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031233
name: Horizontal inferior border of scapula
def: "A morphological abnormality of the scapula in which there is a flat (horizontal) inferior edge of the scapula. The entire scapula is said to resemble a square, leading to the designation sqaring of the scapula (in Figure 1 of PMID:24706940 the scapulae have a roughly rectangular shape)." [PMID:24706940]
synonym: "Squaring of the inferior scapulae" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Squaring of the scapula" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000782 ! Abnormal scapula morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T13:23:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031234
name: Neutrophilic infiltration of the skin
def: "A predominantly neutrophilic infiltrate of the dermis and or epidermis (i.e., a large number of neutrophils inferred to have migrated into the skin)." []
is_a: HP:0011123 ! Inflammatory abnormality of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T19:34:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031235
name: Predominantly epidermal neutrophilic infiltrate
def: "Collection of neutrophils in the epidermis." [PMID:17675728]
comment: This feature can be seen in a variety of conditions ranging from inflammatory dermatosis like psoriasis, neonatal disorders e.g. transient neonatal pustular melanosis to neoplasms viz. keratoacanthoma.
is_a: HP:0031234 ! Neutrophilic infiltration of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T19:36:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031236
name: Predominantly dermal neutrophilic infiltrate
def: "Collection of neutrophils in the dermis." [PMID:17675728]
is_a: HP:0031234 ! Neutrophilic infiltration of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T19:38:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031237
name: Internally nucleated skeletal muscle fibers
def: "An abnormally increased proportion of nuclei of sarcomeres with an internal localization. Individual muscle fibers are syncytia, formed by embryonic fusion of many myoblasts or later, myosatellite cells. Each muscle fiber contains many nuclei, peripherally positioned immediately adjacent to the sarcolemmal membrane. In healthy muscle only 3-5% of fibers contain nuclei that are located internally, within the cell, but many disease processes lead to internal nuclei." [PMID:22938878]
comment: A normal muscle fiber contains many nuclei, peripherally positioned immediately adjacent to the sarcolemmal membrane. In healthy muscle only 3-5 percent of fibers contain nuclei that are located internally, within the cell, but many disease processes lead to internal nuclei.
synonym: "Internally nucleated skeletal muscle fibres" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0020201 ! Abnormal sarcomere morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T20:11:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031238
name: Necklace skeletal muscle fibers
def: "A histological alteration of muscle fibers that resembles a necklace (necklace fibers). A substantial proportion of fibers (4-20% in PMID:19084976) show internalized nuclei aligned in a basophilic ring (necklace) at 3 micrometers beneath the sarcolemma. Ultrastructurally, such necklaces consist of myofibrils of smaller diameter, in oblique orientation, surrounded by mitochondria, sarcoplasmic reticulum and glycogen granules." [PMID:19084976]
synonym: "Necklace skeletal muscle fibres" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0004303 ! Abnormal muscle fiber morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-07-02T20:13:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031239
name: Extrafoveal choroidal neovascularization
def: "A type of choroidal neovascularization in which the nearest edge of the area of neovascularization is located 200 to 1500 micrometers from the center of the fovea." []
is_a: HP:0011506 ! Choroidal neovascularization
