[Term]
id: HP:0031255
name: Hypothalamic arteriovenous malformation
def: "An arteriovenous malformation is a disruption of the normal vascular pattern in which arteries or arterioles connect directly to the venous collection system, bypassing any capillary bed. This term refers to an arteriovenous malformation located in the hypothalamus." [PMID:23125071]
