property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:02:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031271
name: Absent ankle pulse
def: "The pulsation of the posterior tibial artery behind the internal malleolus, or of the dorsalis pedis artery, cannot be detected on physical examination." []
comment: While examining the pulse, the observer should note its intensity, rate, rhythm, and if any blood vessel tenderness, tortuosity, or nodularity exists.
is_a: HP:0032554 ! Absent pulse
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:39:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031272
name: Pulmonary arterial atherosclerosis
def: "Accumulation of lipids and inflammatory cells along the inner walls of the pulmonary artery." []
comment: Pulmonary artery atherosclerosis is less common than systemic arterial atherosclerosis.
is_a: HP:0030966 ! Abnormal pulmonary artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:44:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031273
name: Shock
def: "The state in which profound and widespread reduction of effective tissue perfusion leads first to reversible, and then if prolonged, to irreversible cellular injury." []
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:50:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031274
name: Hypovolemic shock
def: "A state of shock characterized by decreased circulating blood volume in relation to total vascular capacity. This type of shock is characterized by a reduction of diastolic filling pressures." []
is_a: HP:0031273 ! Shock
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:57:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031275
name: Distributive shock
def: "A hyperdynamic process resulting from excessive vasodilatation. Impaired blood flow causes inadequate tissue perfusion, which can lead to end-organ damage" [PMID:28238385]
comment: Distribute shock is caused by inadequate cardiac preload due to vasodilatation and vascular leakage. Etiologies include postoperative SIRS, sepsis, anaphylactic reaction.
is_a: HP:0031273 ! Shock
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T20:59:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031276
name: Obstructive shock
def: "A type of shock characterized by inadequate cardiac preload due to obstructed venous return (e.g. pericardial tamponade, tension pneumothorax, abdominal compartment) or obstruction of arterial blood flow (e.g. pulmonary embolism)." [PMID:28785436]
is_a: HP:0031273 ! Shock
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-12T21:01:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031278
name: Abnormal thoracic duct morphology
