[Term]
id: HP:0031287
name: Seborrheic keratosis
def: "A raised growth on the skin of older individuals. The lesion usually is initially light tan and may darken to dark brown or nearly black. The consistent feature of seborrheic keratoses is their waxy, pasted-on or stuck-on look." []
comment: Seborrheic keratosis is a benign lesion of the skin that occurs more frequently in sunlight exposed areas. The lesions can appear anywhere on the body, but most often occur on the face, chest, and back. There may be just one or clusters of dozens.
synonym: "Basal cell papilloma" EXACT []
synonym: "Seborrheic verruca" EXACT []
synonym: "Senile wart" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0008069 ! Neoplasm of the skin
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-13T20:33:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031288
