[Term]
id: HP:0031300
name: Abnormal circulating properdin concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of properdin in the blood circulation." []
comment: There are three pathways of complement activation, the classical pathway, lectin pathway, and alternative pathway. Each generates a C3 convertase, a serine protease that cleaves the central complement protein, C3. Nearly all the biological consequences of complement are dependent on the resulting cleavage products. Properdin is a positive regulator of complement activation that stabilizes the alternative pathway convertases (C3bBb). Properdin is composed of multiple identical protein subunits, with each subunit carrying a separate ligand-binding site.
synonym: "Abnormal properdin level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025465 ! Abnormal circulating beta globulin concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-13T22:01:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031301
name: Peripheral arterial calcification
def: "An accumulation of calcium and phosphate in arteries with mineral deposits in the intimal or medial layer of the vessel wall." [PMID:24402839, PMID:26811161]
comment: Peripheral arterial calcification can be observed on radiographs and may be classified as either medial (linear calcifications in a train-track pattern) or atherosclerotic (distinct, nodular calcifications). A number of other techniques may also be used to detect peripheral arterial calcification including computed tomographic (CT) and magnetic resonance (MR) imaging, duplex ultrasonography, measurement of pulse wave velocity, echocardiography, planar radiographs, and indirectly, the ankle-brachial index. A discussion on the ontological description of peripheral arterial calcification can be found here: https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/6877.
synonym: "Peripheral artery calcification" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003207 ! Arterial calcification
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-08-26T20:56:01Z" xsd:dateTime

