synonym: "Increased proportion of naive T cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased proportion of naive thymus-derived, alpha-beta T cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031396 ! Abnormal naive T cell proportion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-09-03T12:53:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031399
name: Abnormal double-negative T cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of double-negative (DN) CD3+CD4-CD8- T cells, measured either as percentage of total CD3+ T cells in the blood, or as absolute number per microliter of blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group. These are usually measured within the TCR alpha/beta positive population." [PMID:16285891, PMID:22294241]
comment: T lymphocytes bearing the T cell receptor (TCR) but lacking CD4, CD8, and markers of natural killer (NK) cell differentiation, i.e., TCR(+)CD3(+)CD4(-)CD8(-), are known as double-negative (DN) T cells and are defined by their capability of inhibiting immune responses via directly killing effector T cells in an antigen specific fashion. Furthermore, DN Treg cells have been shown to develop regulatory activity after encountering specific antigens, partially mediated by the acquisition of MHC-peptide complexes from antigen presenting cells (APCs).
synonym: "Abnormal CD4-negative, CD8-negative regulatory T cell distribution" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal DN Treg distribution" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal Double negative Treg distribution" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal double-negative regulatory T cell distribution" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of double-negative regulatory T cell" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025540 ! Abnormal T cell subset number
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-09-03T12:57:22Z" xsd:dateTime

