def: "Situs inversus of thoracic and abdominal viscera with the heart remaining normally situated on the left; usually associated with congenital cardiac abnormalities such as transposition of the great vessels and/or spleen defects including asplenia or polysplenia." [Fyler:0102, Fyler:102, MP:0011253]
is_a: HP:0011534 ! Abnormal spatial orientation of the cardiac segments
