[Term]
id: HP:0031607
name: Pelvic organ prolapse
alt_id: HP:0100672
def: "Pelvic organ prolapse (POP) refers to the protrusion of one or more female pelvic organs outside the pelvis through the vagina including uterus, bladder and intestines, and causes the pelvic organs to drop downward to the vaginal wall. That is, POP is defined as the anatomical prolapse with descent of at least one of the vaginal walls to or beyond the vaginal hymen with maximal Valsalva effort with the presence either of bothersome characteristic symptoms, most commonly the sensation of vaginal bulge, or of functional or medical compromise due to prolapse without symptom bother." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6387-4317, PMID:21505577, PMID:22414610, PMID:34191102]
synonym: "Female genital prolapse" EXACT []
synonym: "Vaginal hernia" EXACT []
synonym: "Vaginal prolapse" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000142 ! Abnormal vagina morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-09T14:09:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031609
name: Macular geographic atrophy
def: "Chronic progressive degeneration of the macula that can be seen as part of late-stage age-related macular degeneration (AMD)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123, PMID:24158023]
comment: Sharply demarcated area of partial or complete depigmentation of the fundus reflecting atrophy of the retinal pigment epithelium with associated retinal photoreceptor loss. The margins of the de-pigmented area are usually scalloped and the large choroidal vessels are visible through the atrophic retinal pigment epithelium.
synonym: "Geographic atrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Geographic atrophy of the macula" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001105 ! Retinal atrophy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-10T14:57:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031610
name: Recurrent shoulder dislocation
def: "Shoulder dislocation occurring repeated times." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6387-4317, PMID:29197942]
synonym: "Multiple shoulder dislocation" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0003834 ! Shoulder dislocation
is_a: HP:0031869 ! Recurrent joint dislocation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-11T10:45:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031611
name: Sub-inner limiting membrane hemorrhage
def: "A type of intraretinal hemorrhage that is located in the superficial retina between the inner limiting membrane and the retinal nerve fiber layer." [PMID:17229799]
comment: Preretinal hemorrhages usually occur at the interface between the posterior hyaloid and inner limiting membrane (ILM). Less frequently, they are located in the superficial retina between the ILM and the retinal nerve fiber layer. These sharply demarcated, dome-shaped hemorrhages show a predilection for the macular region and consequently lead to severe visual impairment.
synonym: "Sub-ILM haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Sub-ILM hemorrhage" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Sub-inner limiting membrane haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0000573 ! Retinal hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-16T12:30:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031613
name: Inferior chorioretinal coloboma
def: "Absence of a region of the retina, retinal pigment epithelium, and choroid at the lower part of the fundus." []
is_a: HP:0000567 ! Chorioretinal coloboma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-16T12:49:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031614
name: Inferior retinal coloboma
