[Term]
id: HP:0031701
name: Anterior chamber inflammatory cells
def: "The presence of inflammatory cells in the aqueous humor of the anterior chamber of the eye." []
comment: The terms for anterior chamber cells can be used to select the grade (total number of cells) and then Anterior chamber red blood cells or inflammatory cells can be chosen to specify whether one or both cells are present. In some scenarios, both cell types may be observed, e.g., followiong trauma.
is_a: HP:0000593 ! Abnormal anterior chamber morphology
