[Term]
id: HP:0031705
name: Compensatory head posture
def: "A compensatory head posture occurs when the head is deviated out of the normal primary straight head position in order to compensate for an ocular problem." []
comment: An abnormal position of the head can be due to an ocular or a non-ocular problem. We reserve this term for abnormal head positions that are compensatory for an ocular problem.
is_a: HP:0000496 ! Abnormality of eye movement
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:24:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031706
name: Compensatory chin depression
def: "A tendency to hold the chin depressed (lowered) to compensate for a limitation of eye movement." []
is_a: HP:0031705 ! Compensatory head posture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:26:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031707
name: Compensatory face turn to the right
def: "A tendency to turn the face to the right to compensate for a limitation of eye movement." []
comment: With a sixth cranial nerve palsy there is a weakened lateral rectus muscule and the affected patient will often turn the head towards the affected eye.
is_a: HP:0031705 ! Compensatory head posture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:27:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031708
name: Compensatory face turn to the left
def: "A tendency to turn the face to the left to compensate for a limitation of eye movement." []
comment: With a sixth cranial nerve palsy there is a weakened lateral rectus muscule and the affected patient will often turn the head towards the affected eye.
is_a: HP:0031705 ! Compensatory head posture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:30:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031709
name: Compensatory head tilt to the right shoulder
def: "A tendency to tilt the head towards the right shoulder to compensate for a limitation of eye movement." []
comment: With fourth cranial nerve palsy leading to weakness of the superior oblique muscle, affected persons tilt the head away from the affected eye as both eyes are most straight in this position.
is_a: HP:0031705 ! Compensatory head posture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:31:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031710
name: Compensatory head tilt to the left shoulder
def: "A tendency to tilt the head towards the left shoulder to compensate for a limitation of eye movement." []
comment: With fourth cranial nerve palsy leading to weakness of the superior oblique muscle, affected persons tilt the head away from the affected eye as both eyes are most straight in this position.
is_a: HP:0031705 ! Compensatory head posture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-18T00:33:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031711
name: Asymmetric abdominal aortic aneurysm
def: "An abdominal aortic aneurysm that is not symmetric around its axis (not axisymmetric)." [PMID:12751282]
comment: Abdominal aortic aneurysms (AAAs) in an advanced stage of development are truly asymmetric, due to the presence of tissue surrounding the abdominal aorta and to the vertebral column located posterior to this artery segment. This makes a large AAA less fusiform and to grow apart from the centerline of the lumen, accounting for a major anterior dilation and a more flat posterior surface.
is_a: HP:0005112 ! Abdominal aortic aneurysm
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2017-12-22T11:19:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031713
name: Constant exotropia
def: "A form of divergent strabismus (exotropia) in which the eye turns outward at all distances and at all times." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:23:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031714
name: Distance exotropia
def: "A type of divergent strabismus (exotropia) in which an eye tends to turn outwards (i.e., the eye squints) mainly when looking at distant objects. The eyes tend to remain straight when they look at near objects. Distance exotropia may be constant or intermittent." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:25:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031715
name: Near exotropia
def: "An intermittent exotropia where there is binocular single vision on distance fixation and exotropia at near (intermittent or constant)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:30:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031716
name: Cyclic exotropia
def: "A type of exotropia (divergent strabismus) in which binocular single vision alternates with large angle exotropia in rhythmic cycle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:31:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031717
name: Alternating exotropia
def: "A type of exotropia in which either eye may be used for fixation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Alternating strabismus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:33:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031718
name: Consecutive exotropia
def: "Exotropia in an individual who has previously had esotropia or esophoria." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:36:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031719
name: True distance exotropia
def: "Exotropia (intermittent or constant) on distance fixation with binocular single vision on near fixation under all testing conditions. The accommodative convergence/accommodation (AC:A) ratio is within normal limits." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0031714 ! Distance exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:40:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031720
name: Simulated distance exotropia
def: "Exotropia (intermittent or constant) worse for distance fixation in which the near angle of deviation increases (or near exophoria becomes exotropia) with: (1) prolonged disruption of fusion and/or (2) elimination of accommodation." []
is_a: HP:0031714 ! Distance exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T13:40:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031721
name: Sensory exotropia
def: "A type of divergent strabismus (exotropia) that develops in a poorly seeing eye." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Secondary exotropia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000577 ! Exotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T14:03:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031722
name: Near esotropia
def: "An intermittent esotropia where there is binocular single vision on distance fixation and esotropia at near even when the accommodation is relieved." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Non-accomodative convergence excess esotropia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031760 ! Non-accomodative esotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T14:06:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031723
name: Secondary esotropia
def: "Convergent squint which follows loss or impairment of vision." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Sensory esotropia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000565 ! Esotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T14:08:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031724
name: Microtropia
def: "A small angle heterotropia (usually of 10 diopters or less) in which a form of binocular single vision occurs." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0032012 ! Heterotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T14:16:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031725
name: Hypophoria
def: "A form of latent strabismus (heterophoria) in which, on dissociation, the occluded eye deviates downwards." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0025588 ! Hypodeviation
is_a: HP:0032011 ! Heterophoria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-13T14:23:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031726
name: Incyclotropia
def: "A type of cyclotropia (torsion of one or both eye around the visual axis of the eyes) in which the upper poles of the globes are rotated inward (medially) to each other." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0031776 ! Cyclotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-14T15:35:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031727
name: Excyclotropia
def: "A type of cyclotropia (torsion of one or both eye around the visual axis of the eyes) in which the upper poles of the globes are rotated outward (laterally) to each other." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0031776 ! Cyclotropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-14T15:39:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031728
name: Mild hypermetropia
def: "A form of hypermetropia with not more than +2.00 diopters." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Mild hyperopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000540 ! Hypermetropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:18:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031729
name: Moderate hypermetropia
def: "A form of hypermetropia with more than +2.00 diopters but not more than +5.00 diopters." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Moderate hyperopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000540 ! Hypermetropia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:20:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031730
name: Axial myopia
def: "A form of myopia related to an axial length above the norm and too long for the refractive power of the whole optical system of the eye." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123, PMID:24113300]
is_a: HP:0000545 ! Myopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:22:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031731
name: Increased tear production
def: "Increased lacrimation owing to overproduction of tears." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0009926 ! Epiphora
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:27:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031732
name: Increased basal tear production
def: "A form of watery eye associated with overproduction of tears due to an increased parasympathetic drive to the secretory component of the lacrimal system (lacrimal gland); this could be due to pro-secretory drug use (e.g. pilocarpine) or autonomic disturbance." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0031731 ! Increased tear production
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:29:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031733
name: Reflex tearing
def: "A form of watery eye associated with overproduction of tears due to reflex tearing in response to a local irritant (e.g. trichiasis or foreign body), chronic ocular surface disease (e.g. blepharitis) or systemic disease (e.g. thyroid eye disease)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0031731 ! Increased tear production
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:32:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031734
name: Lacrimal pump failure
def: "A form of watery eye associated with abnormal lid tone and/or lid position. The former is due to lid laxity (common involutional change in the elderly) or a weak orbicularis muscle (e.g. due to VII cranial nerve palsy). The latter is typically associated with ectropion causing punctal eversion." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0009926 ! Epiphora
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:36:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031736
name: Involutional entropion
def: "An abnormal inversion of the eyelid towards the globe resulting from inferior retractor muscle dysfunction with tissue laxity and, possibly, overriding of the preseptal orbicularis muscle over the pretarsal orbicularis muscle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000621 ! Entropion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:40:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031737
name: Cicatricial entropion
def: "Abnormal inversion (turning inward) of the eyelid towards the globe associated with scarring that vertically shortens the posterior lamella of the eyelid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000621 ! Entropion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:41:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031738
name: Mechanical entropion
def: "A type of entropion (abnormal inversion of the eyelid towards the globe) that is related to a mass effect of a lesion (e.g., a tumor) that pulls the eyelid margin away from the globe." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0000621 ! Entropion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:42:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031739
name: Abnormal oblique muscle physiology
def: "A functional anomaly of the inferior or superior oblique muscle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
comment: The superior oblique muscle is responsible for incyclotorsion (inward turning) or the eye. The inferior oblique muscle is responsible for excyclotorsion (outward turning) or the eye.
is_a: HP:0025590 ! Abnormal extraocular muscle physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:53:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031740
name: Abnormal horizontal rectus muscle physiology
def: "A functional anomaly of the medial rectus muscle or lateral rectus muscle." []
is_a: HP:0031755 ! Abnormal rectus muscle physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-01-21T13:56:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031741
name: Inferior oblique muscle underaction
def: "Reduced ocular movement by the inferior oblique muscle which improves on testing ductions, typically associated with neurogenic palsy." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
is_a: HP:0025598 ! Inferior oblique muscle weakness
