[Term]
id: HP:0031825
name: Freezing of gait
def: "Freezing of gait is defined as a brief, episodic absence or marked reduction of forward progression of the feet despite the intention to walk." [PMID:23625316, PMID:27770207]
comment: Freezing of gait is one of the most debilitating motor symptoms in patients with Parkinson's disease as it may lead to falls and a loss of independence. Patients may report that their feet are stuck to the floor as if held by magnets when trying to walk, resulting in a temporary blockage of the motor function involved in ambulation.
synonym: "Freezing gait" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001288 ! Gait disturbance
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-02T00:28:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031826
name: Abnormal reflex
def: "Any anomaly of a reflex, i.e., of an automatic response mediated by the nervous system (a reflex does not need the intervention of conscious thought to occur)." []
is_a: HP:0100022 ! Abnormality of movement
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-02T01:05:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031827
name: Absent abdominal reflex
def: "Lack of contraction of abdominal muscles in the quadrant of the abdomen that is stimulated by scraping the skin tangential to or toward the umbilicus." [PMID:12531937, PMID:24785227]
comment: A normal abdominal reflex can be observed as a brisk contraction of the umbilicus toward the quadrant that is stimulated. An absent abdominal reflex can point to neurological disease but may also be absent due to other causes such as obesity.
synonym: "Abdominal reflex absent" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031828 ! Abnormal superficial reflex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-02T01:07:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031828
name: Abnormal superficial reflex
def: "An anomaly of a reflex that is elicited as a motor response to scraping of the skin. They are generally graded as present or absent. They differ from tendon reflexes in that the sensory signal must ascend the spinal cord to reach the brain and then descend the spinal cord to reach the motor neurons." []
is_a: HP:0031826 ! Abnormal reflex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-02T01:09:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031829
name: Absent cremaster reflex
def: "Lack of response to scratching of the skin of the medial thigh, which in males normally elicits a brisk, short elevation of the ipsilateral testis, a phenomenon that is referred to as the cremaster reflex." [PMID:12891505]
synonym: "Absent cremasteric reflex" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031828 ! Abnormal superficial reflex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-02T01:11:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031830
name: Pinguecula
def: "A pinguecula is a yellowish to brown protruding lesion in the conjunctiva that is easily seen on the nasal and temporal sides of the cornea." [PMID:24311926]
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-04T01:54:08Z" xsd:dateTime

