property_value: terms:date "2018-05-05T14:18:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031842
name: Lymphangiectasis
def: "Dilation of the lymphatic vessels, the basic process that may result in the formation of a lymphangioma." [MP:0004038]
synonym: "Lymphangiectasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100766 ! Abnormal lymphatic vessel morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-05T14:44:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031843
name: Abnormally slow thought process
def: "An inner sense from the self that thoughts are abnormally slow and the individual feels that they are unable to increase their rate of thinking. The primary pathology is the decreased rate and other qualities of thinking (e.g. naming of objects) are intact, just slowed. This may be associated with slowed speech, but may be internal and masked by speech that is limited to brief (yes or no) answers." [PMID:25850732]
synonym: "Abnormally slow thought processes" EXACT plural_form []
synonym: "Bradyphrenia" EXACT []
synonym: "Mental slowness" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Slow thought processes" EXACT []
synonym: "Slowed thinking" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Slowed thoughts" EXACT []
synonym: "Slowness of thought" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0025769 ! Disordered formal thought process
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-05T15:04:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0031844
name: Euphoria
alt_id: HP:0025767
alt_id: HP:0025768
def: "Elevation of emotional tone or mood that significantly deviates from normative affective functioning. This state is characterized by an overwhelming and all-encompassing sense of joyous well-being; it is associated with unfounded grandiosity, or grossly inflated self-esteem, rapid speech, impulsivity, and an impaired capacity for self-regulation, irrespective of context." [PMID:37636238]
comment: Euphoria may be experienced in the course of normal human activity, including sporting victory, sexual, substance use, or communal spiritual experiences; all manifestations of euphoria refer to profound elation and positive mood experiences. Euphoria in the normal context, is typically very brief and short-lived. Severe pathological euphoria may last hours to days and frequently results in marked impairments in judgment, behavior, and social or occupational functioning.
synonym: "Abnormally elevated mood" RELATED []
synonym: "Euphoric mood" EXACT []
synonym: "Excessive joyfulness" RELATED []
synonym: "Extreme elation" EXACT []
synonym: "Hyperthymia" BROAD []
synonym: "Hyperthymic state" BROAD []
synonym: "Inappropriate elation" EXACT []
synonym: "Inappropriately happy" RELATED []
synonym: "Jubilation" BROAD []
synonym: "Pathological cheerfulness" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0100851 ! Abnormal emotional state
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1111-7357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7954-5235
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2897-0458
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4298-5074
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4618-6544
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-05-05T15:29:11Z" xsd:dateTime

