def: "Clasp-knife phenomenon refers to increased muscle tone while bending or stretching a limb, whereby there is a sudden relaxation (decrease in resistance) as the muscle continues to be stretched. This phenomenon has been likened to opening a clasp knife." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
