property_value: terms:date "2018-08-25T12:36:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032017
name: Sputum eosinophilia
def: "An increased proportion of eosinophils in sputum in the differentiated cell count." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:23741092, PMID:29146301]
comment: Sputum eosinophilia can be measured in various ways including measuring the mean percentage of eosinophils in the cell count of sputum induced by application of saline. The threshold chosen differs between studies, typically ranging from 1.25 to 3 percent. Increased sputum eosinophil counts may indicate a risk for severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or severe asthma.
is_a: HP:0032016 ! Abnormal sputum
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-08-25T12:39:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032018
name: Multiple mononeuropathy
def: "A type of peripheral neuropathy that happens when there is damage to two or more different nerve areas characterized by peripheral neuropathy of both the motor and sensory nerves of at least two different nerve trunks. Different nerves are affected either simultaneously or sequentially." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:25494723]
comment: Mononeuritis multiplex can be a manifestation of several disorders including infectious, inflammatory, neoplastic, toxic, metabolic and hereditary conditions.
synonym: "Mononeuritis multiplex" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0009830 ! Peripheral neuropathy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-08-25T15:36:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032019
name: Muscle eosinophilia
def: "Eosinophil infiltration of skeletal muscle." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:24424174, PMID:24803842]
comment: This phenotype can be measured by determining the number and location of eosinophils in skeletal muscle biopsies by Giemsa and modified hematoxylin/eosin staining. However, infiltrating eosinophils are not always identified in conventional muscle histologic examination, but the eosinophil major basic protein, whose extracellular diffusion is considered a hallmark of eosinophilic cytotoxicity, is usually detected by immunostaining in muscle biopsy.
synonym: "Eosinophilic infiltration of skeletal muscle" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011805 ! Abnormal skeletal muscle morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-08-25T15:42:46Z" xsd:dateTime

