[Term]
id: HP:0032060
name: Epithelioid hemangioma
def: "A benign neoplasm that includes blood vessel proliferation and a dense eosinophilic inflammatory infiltrate, manifesting as flesh/plum-colored pruritic nodules and papules, most commonly affecting the ear and the periauricular area." [NCIT:C4298, PMID:25484503, PMID:25927152]
comment: Epithelioid hemangioma is most common in middle-aged adults.
synonym: "Angiolymphoid hyperplasia with eosinophilia" EXACT []
