[Term]
id: HP:0032064
name: Gastrointestinal eosinophilia
def: "Eosinophilic infiltration of one or more gastrointestinal organs. Gastrointestinal eosinophilia is a broad term for abnormal eosinophil accumulation in the GI tract, involving many different disease identities. These diseases include primary eosinophil associated gastrointestinal diseases, gastrointestinal eosinophilia in HES and all gastrointestinal eosinophilic states associated with known causes. Each of these diseases has its unique features but there is no absolute boundary between them." [PMID:17868858, PMID:23964139]
synonym: "Eosinophilic enteritis" EXACT []
synonym: "Eosinophilic gastroenteritis" EXACT []
synonym: "Eosinophilic gastrointestinal disease" RELATED []
synonym: "Eosinophilic gastrointestinal disorders" RELATED []
synonym: "GI eosinophilia" EXACT abbreviation []
