[Term]
id: HP:0032100
name: Abnormal doll's eye reflex
def: "The doll's eye reflex (also known as oculocephalic reflex) is a test of brain function that is performed in comatose patients by elevating the head roughly 30 degrees and rapidly rotating the head from side to side with the eyes kept open. A normal response is for the eyes to move in the opposite direction. If the eyes do not move in the opposite direction this may indicate severe brain damage." [PMID:7299406]
is_a: HP:0007670 ! Abnormal vestibulo-ocular reflex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-11-04T11:33:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032101
name: Unusual infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to infection, as manifested by recurrent infection, severe or invasive infection, infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location, or infection with opportunistic organisms, that is unusual for a healthy individual of the same age." []
comment: There are five general subtypes. (i) Opportunistic infection, meaning infection by a pathogen that is not normally able to cause infection in a healthy host (e.g., pneumonia by Pneumocystis jirovecii or CMV); (ii) Unusual location (focus) of an infection (e.g., an aspergillus brain abscess); (iii) a protracted course or lack of adequate response to treatment (e.g., chronic rhinosinusitis); (iv) Unusual severity or intensity of an infection; and (v) unusual recurrence of infections.
is_a: HP:0010978 ! Abnormality of immune system physiology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-9822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9382-150X
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2029-0733
