comment: Differentiation of B cells into plasmablasts (PB) is most commonly monitored with surface markers CD19, CD20, CD27, CD38, and CD138 and intracellular marker Ki-67. Plasmablasts are antibody-secreting cells that originate after infection or vaccination.
