[Term]
id: HP:0032159
name: Fungal meningitis
def: "A meningitis caused by fungal infection, with the principal causative organism being Cryptococcus neoformans (cryptococcal meningitis); other causes include Candida and Coccidioides species. A fungal meningitis is most often a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, particularly in severe T-cell deficiencies." []
is_a: HP:0001287 ! Meningitis
