[Term]
id: HP:0032165
name: Placental mesenchymal dysplasia
def: "Placental mesenchymal dysplasia is a rare anomaly characterized by placentomegaly, dilatation of chorionic vessels and hydropic stem villi with cistern-like formation. It is often clinically mistaken for a partial hydatidiform mole but there is no trophoblastic proliferation. P57 immunohistochemical expression is discordant, showing a normal positive expression in the cytotrophoblastic cells, and loss of expression in the stromal cells." [PMID:17227114, PMID:25171710, PMID:28515588]
comment: Placental mesenchymal dysplasia is an unusual abnormality of the stem villi of the placenta that may be mistaken for a hydatidiform mole, and in particular, partial mole, owing to the mixture of cysts and normal-appearing parenchyma.
is_a: HP:0100767 ! Abnormal placenta morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-12-09T14:14:16Z" xsd:dateTime

