[Term]
id: HP:0032167
name: Clostridium difficile enteritis
def: "An infection of the small intestine (enteritis) by clostridium difficile." []
comment: Clostridium difficile (C. difficile) is a common nosocomial infection caused by a gram-negative spore forming organism that most commonly leads to pseudomembranous colitis. Certain individuals are able to mount an effective immunoglobulin G response against C. difficile toxin A. This humoral immune response against the C. difficile toxin is believed to allow an individual to become an asymptomatic carrier. In contrast, people who fail to mount an immune response to C. difficile toxin are susceptible to infection. In general, patients on immunosuppressive therapy have a blunted ability to mount immune responses and, therefore, may be at greater risk for infection.
synonym: "C. difficile enteritis" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0032166 ! Unusual gastrointestinal infection
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2018-12-09T14:22:48Z" xsd:dateTime

