[Term]
id: HP:0032182
name: Abnormal memory T cell proportion
def: "An abnormal proportion of memory T cells compared to the total number of T cells in the blood. Memory T cells have previously encountered and responded to their cognate antigen and upon a repeated encounter with the antigen can mount a faster and stronger response." [PMID:8450264]
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD4+CD29+ cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of memory T cells" EXACT []
