property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-19T13:32:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032197
name: Deep S wave in lead V5
def: "Abnormal depth of the S wave in lead V5 of the electrocardiogram." [PMID:29279530]
comment: The S wave refers to the negative deflection after an R wave within the QRS complex. This term refers to an abnormally deep (negative) deflection of the S wave in lead V5.
is_a: HP:0032195 ! Abnormal S wave
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-19T13:39:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032198
name: Decreased prothrombin time
def: "Abnormally short time to coagulation in the prothrombin time test, which is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. The results of the prothrombin time test are often expressed in terms of the International normalized ratio (INR), which is calculated as a ratio of the patient's prothrombin time (PT) to a control PT standardized for the potency of the thromboplastin reagent developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) using the formula: INR is equal to Patient PT divided by Control PT." [PMID:21470390]
synonym: "Decreased INR" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Decreased international normalised ratio" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Decreased international normalized ratio" EXACT []
synonym: "Decreased PT" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0032199 ! Abnormal prothrombin time
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-19T15:32:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032199
name: Abnormal prothrombin time
def: "Any deviation from the normal amount of time to coagulation in the prothrombin time test, which is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. The results of the prothrombin time test are often expressed in terms of the International normalized ratio (INR), which is calculated as a ratio of the patient's prothrombin time (PT) to a control PT standardized for the potency of the thromboplastin reagent developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) using the formula: INR is equal to Patient PT divided by Control PT." [PMID:29939529]
synonym: "Abnormal PT" EXACT abbreviation []
