property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8124-8864
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-20T15:00:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032205
name: Elevated circulating galectin-3 concentration
def: "The concentration of galectin-3 in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: Galectin-3 is a member of the family of beta-galactoside-binding endogenous lectins. It is a multifunctional factor that binds to distinct ligands and triggers production of matrix metalloproteinases, and thereby plays a role in cardiac fibrosis and remodeling.
synonym: "Elevated galectin-3 concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated galectin-3 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated galectin-3 level in blood" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased galectin-3 concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased galectin-3 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased galectin-3 level in blood" EXACT []
