[Term]
id: HP:0032208
name: Increased urinary type 1 collagen N-terminal telopeptide level
def: "An increased concentration of type 1 collagen N-terminal telopeptide (NTx) level in the urine. Generally the test is performed over a period of time, for instance, 10 cc of morning urine can be collected following 12 hours overnight fasting or for 24 hours." [PMID:30572827]
comment: Telopeptides are tiny protein particles found particularly in type I collagen that include 15-20 amino acids. Telopeptides bound to the ends of these amino acids are removed from the body through the urine as a result of collagen metabolism. During resorption, amino and carboxyl terminal fragments, called telopeptides, are bound to collagens with cross links and can be released into the circulation and excreted in the urine. Some recent studies have demonstrated that the type 1 collagen N-terminal telopeptide (NTx) level is more specific to bone tissue than any other resorption markers.
synonym: "Increased collagen crosslinked N-telopeptide [Moles/volume] in 24 hour urine" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased urine NTx level" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0033384 ! Elevated urinary collagen degradation products
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-20T16:17:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032209
name: Abnormal circulating free T3 concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of free triiodothyronine (T3) in the blood circulation. A proportion of T3 is bound to plasma proteins in the blood, including mainly thyroxine binding globulin, transthyretin, and albumin. T3 that is not bound to a protein is referred to as free T3." []
synonym: "Abnormal circulating free T3 level" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal circulating free triiodotyronine concentration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031508 ! Abnormal circulating thyroid hormone concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-01-20T20:34:42Z" xsd:dateTime

