property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T13:28:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032373
name: Duffy blood group
def: "The Duffy blood group system is based on the presence of a glycoprotein termed Fy that is on the surface of erythrocytes and some other cells. There are two Duffy antigens named Fya and Fyb, and thus there are four Duffy phenotypes: a+b+, a+b-, a-b+,a-b-." [PMID:19480920]
comment: FY has two major codominant alleles, FYA and FYB, which result from a SNP (125G>A), and the corresponding Fya and Fyb antigens differ by a single amino acid (G42D). Individuals who are homozygous for a -33T>C SNP in the erythroid promoter region of the FYB allele have the phenotype Fy(a-b-) and do not express Duffy antigens on their RBCs.
is_a: HP:0032223 ! Blood group
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T13:37:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032374
name: Duffy Fya positivity
def: "Presence of the Duffy Fya antigen." [PMID:19480920]
