property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T13:42:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032376
name: Anti-beta 2 glycoprotein I antibody positivity
def: "Presence of antibodies against beta 2 glycoprotein I in the circulation. Beta-2 glycoprotein I (beta2GPI) is the principal target of autoantibodies in the antiphospholipid syndrome (APS)." [PMID:28105326]
comment: Beta2GPI was identified as a primary target of autoantibodies in patients with APS. Beta2GPI is a single-chain protein containing five repeating sequences or domains. Domain V is essential for binding to anionic phospholipid membranes, whereas domain I sticks out into the extracellular space where interactions with other proteins/antibodies can take place 1.
synonym: "Anti-B2GPI positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T13:47:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032377
name: Increased urinary orosomucoid
def: "An increased concentration in the urine of alpha-1-acid glycoprotein (AGP), also known as orosomucoid (ORM). AGP is a 41-43-kDa glycoprotein with a pI of 2.8-3.8. AGP is an acute-phase protein that has many activities including, but not limited to, acting as an acute-phase reactant and disease marker, modulating immunity, binding and carrying drugs, maintaining the barrier function of capillary, and mediating the sphingolipid metabolism." [PMID:25711902]
synonym: "Increased urinary alpha-1-acid glycoprotein" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020129 ! Abnormal urine protein level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T14:04:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032378
name: Immediate-type hypersensitivity drug reaction
def: "Hypersensitivity that is observed within 1 hr of exposures. A variety of adverse reactions can occur within minutes to hours of exposure to a drug. Some can be related to the pharmacological action of the drug (WHO Adverse Reaction Terminology type A for augmented) and usually have a low mortality. Others are not readily predictable based on the structure and pharmacological action of the drug and have a relatively high mortality risk (Type B for bizarre). The most serious form of immediate onset drug hypersensitivity reaction, anaphylaxis. Other reactions including itching, dizziness/light-headedness, nausea, chest discomfort but without any objective skin features, physical signs or physiological compromise. Skin only reactions include generalized erythema, urticaria or angioedema without any sentinel features (see below) of other organ involvement." [PMID:24286446]
comment: Hypersensitivity is broadly defined as objectively reproducible symptoms or signs, initiated by exposure to a defined stimulus at a dose tolerated by normal subjects and may be caused by immunologic (allergic) and non-immunologic mechanisms.
is_a: HP:0100326 ! Immunologic hypersensitivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T14:43:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032379
name: Polymorphous light eruption
def: "The cardinal symptom is severely pruritic skin lesions. Macular, papular, papulovesicular, urticarial, multiforme- and plaque-like variants are differentiated morphologically, hence the name polymorphous. Usually one morphology dominates in a single individual (monomorphous). The skin lesions develop a few hours to several days after sun exposure. Initially, patchy erythema develops, accompanied by pruritus. Distinct lesions then develop. The upper chest, upper arms, backs of the hands, thighs, and the sides of the face are the primary localizations. The skin lesions resolve spontaneously within several days of ceasing sun exposure and do not leave behind any traces." [PMID:21442060]
synonym: "Sun allergy" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0000992 ! Cutaneous photosensitivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T14:52:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032381
name: Hydroa vacciniforme
def: "In response to the spring sun distinct inflamed reddened skin develops on the ears, nose, cheeks, fingers, backs of the hands, and the lower arms, on which blisters with serous or hemorrhagic content develop. These dry out with the formation of a blackish scab. After shedding of the scab, depressed, varioliform, often hypopigmented scars remain. In addition, hyper- and hypopigmentation are present together, resulting in a polymorphous skin presentation." [PMID:21442060]
synonym: "Acute vesiculation and crusting and scarring following sun exposure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000992 ! Cutaneous photosensitivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T14:55:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032382
name: Uniparental disomy
def: "Inheritance of both homologues of a chromosome pair from the same parent." []
comment: UPD may comprise the whole chromosome, or just part of it (segmental UPD). Isodisomy is presented as 2 copies from the same chromosome of a parent, and heterodisomy is presented as 1 copy of each of the 2 homologues from the same parent. UPD is related to abnormalities formed during meiosis, fertilization, and mitosis. There are 5 different mechanisms that explain the etiology of UPD, including Trisomic rescue; Nullisomic gamete complementation; Monosomic rescue; Mitotic aberrations; and Structural chromosome aberrations. If prenatal genetic analysis reveals a homologous robertsonian translocation, the risk of fetal UPD is very high, and a marker chromosome or chromosome aneuploidy can be associated with UPD. {xref="PMID:29137034"}
synonym: "UPD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0034335 ! Inheritance qualifier
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T14:58:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032383
name: Uniparental heterodisomy
def: "A type of uniparental disomy in which the two different chromosomes (or chromosome segments) of the same parent are transmitted." [PMID:25547535]
is_a: HP:0032382 ! Uniparental disomy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-02-24T15:04:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032384
