[Term]
id: HP:0032459
name: Abnormal phosphoribosylpyrophosphate synthetase level
def: "Any deviation from the normal level of the enzyme phosphoribosyl pyrophosphatesynthetase, which catalyzes the synthesis of PP-ribose-P from ATP and ribose-5-phosphate." [PMID:4200723]
comment: Intracellular availability of the sugar phosphate, 5-phosphoribosyl 1-pyrophosphate (PP-ribose-P), is an important factor in regulation of the rate of purine synthesis de novo. PP-ribose- P synthetase (EC2.7.6.1) is an enzyme that catalyzes the synthesis of PP-ribose-P from ATP and ribose-5-phosphate. An increased activity of PP-ribose- P synthetase can be associated with increased PP-ribose-P concentrations and increased purine biosynthetic rates. Increased purine production in turn can be associated with gout.
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-03-09T17:34:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032460
name: Decreased phosphoribosylpyrophosphate synthetase level
def: "Abnormally reduced level of the enzyme phosphoribosyl pyrophosphatesynthetase, which catalyzes the synthesis of PP-ribose-P from ATP and ribose-5-phosphate." [PMID:17701900, PMID:20301731]
comment: It is difficult to assay PRS1 enzyme activity separately from that of the other two isoforms (PRS2 and PRS3), a decrease in PRS enzyme activity may be assumed to reflect decreased activity of PRS1, not PRS2 or PRS3.
is_a: HP:0032459 ! Abnormal phosphoribosylpyrophosphate synthetase level
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-03-09T17:35:02Z" xsd:dateTime

