id: HP:0032475
name: 6-layered lissencephaly
comment: A malformation of the pachygyria-agyria spectrum. A 6-layered cortex is characterized by bands of ectopic neurons of varying shape and size organized in columns or clusters, lying in a reduced rim of white matter. Layers I and II of the cortex are well defined, and pyramidal and polymorphic neurons of layers III, IV, V, and VI are found more or less in their appropriate location. {xref="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90573458"}
