property_value: terms:date "2019-04-12T10:39:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032495
name: Abnormal terminal:vellus ratio
def: "A deviation from the normal proportion of terminal to vellus hairs." [PMID:12894995]
comment: Scalp hairs comprise large terminal hairs and small vellus hairs. Terminal hairs are conspicuous and exceed 0.03 mm in diameter and 1 cm in length, and may be pigmented and medullated. Vellus hairs are inconspicuous and are 0.03 mm or less in diameter and less than 1 cm in length and lack melanin and medulla.
is_a: HP:0010720 ! Abnormal hair pattern
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-12T11:32:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032496
name: Elevated terminal:vellus ratio
def: "An increased proportion of terminal hairs compared to vellus hairs." [PMID:23044568]
comment: A terminal:vellus ratio over 7:1 is characteristic of chronic telogen effluvium.
is_a: HP:0032495 ! Abnormal terminal:vellus ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-12T11:35:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032497
name: Reduced terminal:vellus ratio
def: "A terminal:vellus ratio under 4:1 is characteristic of androgenetic alopecia." [PMID:23044568]
comment: An decreased proportion of terminal hairs compared to vellus hairs.
is_a: HP:0032495 ! Abnormal terminal:vellus ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-12T11:38:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032499
name: Giant neutrophil granules
def: "The presence of abnormally large granules in neutrophils. This finding can be appreciated on a peripheral blood smear. The finding is characteristic of Chediak Higashi syndrome. The giant granules are derived from azurophil granules, whereas peroxidase-negative granules are not involved in their formation." [PMID:9665278]
comment: In Chediak Higashi syndrome, stimulus-induced giant granule mobilization is severely reduced, which may contribute to the propensity for severe bacterial infections.
is_a: HP:0011992 ! Abnormal neutrophil morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-05-23T22:49:33Z" xsd:dateTime

