[Term]
id: HP:0032504
name: Lhermitte's sign
def: "An electric shock-like sensation that occurs on flexion of the neck. This sensation radiates down the spine, often into the legs, arms, and sometimes to the trunk." [PMID:26019410]
comment: Lhermitte's sign is caused by miscommunication between the nerves that have become demyelinated. The pathophysiology of Lhermitte's sign was described as the stretching of the hyper excitable demyelinated dorsal column of the spinal cord, particularly at the cervical level, thus triggering an electric shock-like sensation.
synonym: "Barber chair phenomenon" EXACT []
synonym: "Lhermitte's phenomenon" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012638 ! Abnormal nervous system physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2019-05-23T22:58:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032505
name: Hydrophobia
def: "The word hydrophobia has been used to describe the avoidance of drinking in the presence of hydrophobic spasms that can be observed in human rabies (described as a blockage in the throat with worsening of dyspnea). However, rarely, the same word has been used to describe panic reactions observed in a patient when offered a glass of water. This term does not refer to the latter meaning." [PMID:12121215, PMID:30564365]
comment: Hydrophobia has been described as a characteristic finding in rabies, which can prevent patients from drinking despite experiencing intense thirst.
is_a: HP:0002015 ! Dysphagia
