id: HP:0032637
name: Renal interstitial edema
def: "Edema is characterized but the acute swelling of the stroma, with expansion of the interstitial space without the a concurrent increase in interstitial cells or extracellular matrix. Histologically this change is appreciated as interstitial areas of lower optical density." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:24454932]
