[Term]
id: HP:0032663
name: Focal motor status epilepticus
def: "Status epilepticus with focal motor signs originating within networks limited to one hemisphere. Involves musculature in any form. The motor event could consist of an increase (positive) or decrease (negative) in muscle contraction to produce a movement." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: Including aware and unaware focal motor status epilepticus, but note that hyperkinetic status epilepticus (of focal onset) is classified separately.
is_a: HP:0032658 ! Status epilepticus with prominent motor symptoms
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:23:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032664
name: Adversive status epilepticus
def: "A type of focal motor status epilepticus characterized by continuous neck or body rotation and conjugate gaze deviation in a direction contralateral to the responsible epileptic focus. This includes some forms of tonic status epilepticus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
is_a: HP:0032663 ! Focal motor status epilepticus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:25:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032665
name: Repeated focal motor seizures
def: "A type of focal motor status epilepticus characterized by repeated motor, typically clonic events repeatedly affecting the same segments of the body with spread of clonic movements through contiguous body parts unilaterally, and repeating over a sufficiently prolonged period to reach a diagnosis of status epilepticus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:21070217, PMID:26336950]
synonym: "Jacksonian status epilepticus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032663 ! Focal motor status epilepticus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:35:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032666
name: Hyperkinetic status epilepticus
def: "Status epilepticus characterized by continuous hyperkinetic proximal limb or axial muscles producing irregular sequential ballistic movements such as pedaling pelvic thrusting, thrashing, or rocking movements." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: In 2015 the ILAE classified hyperkinetic status epilepticus separately from focal motor status epilepticus characterized by elemental motor features. Awareness may be intact or impaired.
is_a: HP:0032658 ! Status epilepticus with prominent motor symptoms
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:39:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032667
name: Myoclonic status epilepticus
def: "A type of motor status epilepticus with repeating bilateral sudden brief (less than 100 ms) involuntary single or multiple contraction of muscles or muscle groups of variable topography." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: The myoclonic seizures are usually generalized. The duration or frequency of myoclonic jerks required to qualify as myoclonic status is not defined, but they should occur frequently and long enough to significantly impair functioning. A reasonable general definition might be that myoclonus must occur either (1) at least once every 10 seconds for longer than 10 minutes or (2) at least once a minute for longer than 30 minutes.
is_a: HP:0032658 ! Status epilepticus with prominent motor symptoms
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:45:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032668
name: Myoclonic status epilepticus without coma
def: "A type of myoclonic status epilepticus in the absence of coma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
is_a: HP:0032667 ! Myoclonic status epilepticus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:45:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032669
name: Myoclonic status epilepticus with coma
def: "A type of myoclonic status epilepticus in the presence of coma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
is_a: HP:0032667 ! Myoclonic status epilepticus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:45:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032670
name: Tonic status epilepticus
def: "Tonic status epilepticus is a type of status epilepticus characterized by focal or bilateral limb stiffening or elevation, which may be electrographically generalized or focal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: This has most commonly been reported in children with neurocognitive impairment and severe epilepsy, such as Ohtahara syndrome or West syndrome and Lennox-Gastaut syndrome. The tonic activity can be a sustained abnormal posture, either in extension or flexion, sometimes accompanied by tremor of the extremities.
is_a: HP:0032658 ! Status epilepticus with prominent motor symptoms
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T11:47:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032671
name: Non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma
def: "A type of status epilepticus without prominent motor symptoms in the absence of coma." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
is_a: HP:0031475 ! Status epilepticus without prominent motor symptoms
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T12:09:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032672
name: Autonomic status epilepticus
def: "Autonomic status epilepticus is a type of non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma with prominent autonomic features regardless of whether it is electrographically generalized or focal." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: Autonomic disturbances may include tachycardia, cardiac arrhythmia, hypertension, high fever, salivation, vomiting and incontinence.
is_a: HP:0032671 ! Non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T12:19:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032673
name: Focal non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma
def: "Focal non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma is a type of status epilepticus without prominent motor signs, which is electrographically focal. It is a prolonged focal non-motor seizure." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, PMID:26336950]
comment: Semiology may include autonomic, sensory, visual, olfactory, gustatory, emotional/psychic/experiential, or cognitive symptoms. Consciousness or awareness may be intact or impaired.
is_a: HP:0032671 ! Non-convulsive status epilepticus without coma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-22T12:19:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032674
name: Cutaneous wound
def: "A cutaneous wound is a defined as a disruption of normal anatomic structure and function of the skin that occurs owing to an injury of the skin. Wound healing is a dynamic, interactive process involving soluble mediators, blood cells, extracellularmatrix, and parenchymal cells. Wound healing has three phases: inflammation, tissue formation, and tissue remodeling, that overlap in time." [PMID:10471461]
synonym: "Skin wound" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0011121 ! Abnormal skin morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-23T09:13:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032675
name: Acute cutaneous wound
def: "A cutaneous wound that is proceeding through an orderly and timely reparative process that results in sustained restoration of the anatomic and functional integrity of the skin." [PMID:30475656]
comment: Wound healing accors in multiple overlapping stages, with re=-eipthelialization normally beginning on day one or two. In most clinical settings, closure of acute and chronic wounds is considered the wound healing end point, but wounds can continue to undergo remodeling or tissue maturation for several months or even years.
is_a: HP:0032674 ! Cutaneous wound
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-23T09:13:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032676
name: Chronic cutaneous wound
def: "A cutaneous wound that has failed to proceed through the orderly and timely process to produce an atomic and functional integrity, or proceeded through the repair process without establishing a sustained anatomic and functional result." [PMID:8166487]
synonym: "Chronic nonhealing cutaneous wound" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032674 ! Cutaneous wound
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-02-23T09:13:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032677
name: Generalized-onset motor seizure
def: "A generalized motor seizure is a type of generalized-onset seizure with predominantly motor (involving musculature) signs. The motor event could consist of an increase (positive) or decrease (negative) in muscle contraction to produce a movement." [PMID:11580774, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
synonym: "Generalised onset motor seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalised-onset motor seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Generalized onset motor seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002197 ! Generalized-onset seizure
is_a: HP:0020219 ! Motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T07:11:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032678
name: Eyelid myoclonia seizure
def: "An eyelid myoclonia seizure is a type of generalized myoclonic seizure which may or may not be associated with loss of awareness." [PMID:19469840]
is_a: HP:0002123 ! Generalized myoclonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T07:17:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032679
name: Focal non-motor seizure
def: "A type of focal-onset seizure characterized by non-motor signs or symptoms (or behavior arrest) as its initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: Non-motor terms correspond to the earliest prominent sign or symptom.
synonym: "Focal seizure without motor onset" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial seizure without motor onset" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0007359 ! Focal-onset seizure
is_a: HP:0033259 ! Non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T07:50:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032680
name: Focal cognitive seizure
alt_id: HP:0011162
def: "A focal cognitive seizure involves an alteration in a cognitive function (which can be a deficit or a positive phenomenon such as forced thought), which occurs at seizure onset. To be classified as a focal cognitive seizure, the change in cognitive function should be specific and out of proportion to other relatively unimpaired aspects of cognition, because all cognition is impaired in a focal impaired awareness seizure." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: In order to characterize focal cognitive seizures, specific testing may be required early during the seizure.
synonym: "Cognitive aura" EXACT []
synonym: "Cognitive seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial cognitive seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032679 ! Focal non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T08:19:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032681
name: Focal aware cognitive seizure
alt_id: HP:0032683
alt_id: HP:0032881
def: "A focal aware cognitive seizure during which awareness is retained throughout the seizure." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
is_a: HP:0032682 ! Focal aware non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T08:24:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032682
name: Focal aware non-motor seizure
def: "A focal non-motor seizure in which awareness is retained throughout the seizure." [PMID:20196795, PMID:23739099, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
synonym: "Focal non-motor aware seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002349 ! Focal aware seizure
is_a: HP:0032679 ! Focal non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
