[Term]
id: HP:0032685
name: Focal cognitive seizure with auditory agnosia
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by auditory agnosia as the initial semiological manifestation. For example a person may hear a ringing sound, but may not connect this with the concept that the sound is from a telephone ringing." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Auditory agnosia is the inability to recognize or differentiate between sounds / words or to relate them to their meaning despite being able to hear them.
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T08:34:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032686
name: Focal aware cognitive seizure with memory impairment
def: "A focal cognitive seizure with memory impairment characterized by retained awareness throughout the seizure." [PMID:28276060]
is_a: HP:0032681 ! Focal aware cognitive seizure
is_a: HP:0032687 ! Focal cognitive seizure with memory impairment
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T08:34:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032687
name: Focal cognitive seizure with memory impairment
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by transient memory impairment as the initial semiological manifestation whilst other cognitive functions and awareness are preserved at seizure onset. The memory impairment may be an inability to recall events occurring prior to the seizure (retrograde amnesia), or failure to encode new memories for events occurring during the seizure (anterograde amnesia)." [PMID:17444534]
comment: www.epilepsydiagnosis.org focuses on anterograde amnesia during the seizure. Both ictal retrograde and anterograde amnesia have been included here given that they are well studied as ictal manifestations of 'transient epileptic amnesia'. The clinical onset of these seizures is defined by questions indicating ictal retrograde amnesia, often because of disorientation. Ictal anterograde amnesia is incomplete in many individuals with transient epileptic amnesia: half at least partly recall 'not being able to remember' during seizures.
synonym: "Amnestic aura" EXACT []
synonym: "Amnestic seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T08:36:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032688
name: Focal aware cognitive seizure with dissociation
def: "A focal cognitive seizure with dissociation characterized by retained awareness throughout the seizure." [PMID:28276060]
is_a: HP:0032681 ! Focal aware cognitive seizure
is_a: HP:0032689 ! Focal cognitive seizure with dissociation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:09:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032689
name: Focal cognitive seizure with dissociation
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by an experience of being disconnected from, though aware of, self or environment as the initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:09:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032690
name: Focal aware cognitive seizure with dyscalculia/acalculia
def: "A focal cognitive seizure with dyscalculia and or acalculia characterized by retained awareness throughout the seizure." [PMID:28276060]
is_a: HP:0032681 ! Focal aware cognitive seizure
is_a: HP:0032691 ! Focal cognitive seizure with dyscalculia/acalculia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:12:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032691
name: Focal cognitive seizure with dyscalculia/acalculia
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by dyscalculia / acalculia as the initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Dyscalculia / acalculia is difficulty completing or understanding mathematical calculation. This seizure type is seen in seizures involving the dominant hemisphere parieto-temporal lobe region.
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:14:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032692
name: Focal cognitive seizure with forced thinking
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by forced thinking as the initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Forced thinking is the presence of intrusive thoughts, ideas or crowding of thoughts. This is a rare seizure type, seen in mesial parietal, posterior parahippocampal and frontal lobe seizures.
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
is_a: HP:0033347 ! Cognitive epileptic aura
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:16:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032693
name: Focal cognitive seizure with neglect
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by neglect as the initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Neglect is unilateral failure to report or respond to stimuli presented contralaterally.
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:17:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032694
name: Focal cognitive seizure with dyslexia/alexia
def: "A focal cognitive seizure characterized by dyslexia / alexia as the initial semiological manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Dyslexia / alexia is the inability to read due to an impairment in understanding written words rather than visual impairment. This seizure type is seen in seizures involving the dominant hemisphere parieto-temporal lobe region.
is_a: HP:0032680 ! Focal cognitive seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-14T09:22:03Z" xsd:dateTime

