comment: A single or short cluster of brief muscle contractions (jerks), each jerk is typically milliseconds in duration.
is_a: HP:0011166 ! Focal myoclonic seizure
is_a: HP:0020217 ! Focal aware motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-15T10:39:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032759
name: Focal sensory seizure with vestibular features
def: "A seizure characterized by symptoms of dizziness, spinning, vertigo or sense of rotation as its first clinical manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: These seizures involve the parietal cortex, temporo-parieto-occipital junction or parieto-temporal cortex.
synonym: "Focal vestibular seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial vestibular seizure" EXACT []
synonym: "Vestibular aura" EXACT []
