id: HP:0032807
name: Neonatal seizure
def: "A seizure occurring within the neonatal period (28 days beyond the full term date)." [PMID:28276060, PMID:33522601]
comment: This term encompasses clinical only (motor or non-motor without electrographic confirmation), electro-clinical and electrographic only seizures. Where the seizure also meets the definition of status epilepticus it should be coded twice.
is_a: HP:0001250 ! Seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:23:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032808
name: Neonatal seizure with electrographic correlate
def: "Neonatal seizure is a seizure type that occurs in neonatal period and is characterized by an electrographic event with sudden, repetitive, evolving stereotyped waveforms with a beginning and an end. This event can be associated or not with a clinical manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Neonatal seizures need to be considered as a special category because of biological peculiarities, such as the immaturity of the neonatal central nervous system. Therefore, seizures are defined first as an electrographic event, that can be associated or not with clinical manifestations. Seizure types are further classified following ILAE 2017 seizure classification, however awareness is not assessable in neonates. The distinction motor vs. non motor seizure is kept, but here it reflects the predominant clinical manifestation, rather than the onset of the seizure as in adult classification.
is_a: HP:0032807 ! Neonatal seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:25:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032809
name: Neonatal electro-clinical seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical seizure is an electrographic event occurring in neonatal period and coupled with a clinical manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: The predominant clinical feature defines the neonatal electro-clinical seizure sub-types; unlike in adults, where the semiology at onset defines the seizure type.
is_a: HP:0032808 ! Neonatal seizure with electrographic correlate
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:26:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032810
name: Focal sensory seizure with cephalic sensation
def: "A seizure characterized by a sensation in the head such as light-headedness or headache as its first clinical manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
synonym: "Cephalic aura" EXACT []
synonym: "Focal seizure with cephalic sensation" EXACT []
synonym: "Partial seizure with cephalic sensation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011157 ! Focal sensory seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-16T15:35:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032811
name: Neonatal electrographic only seizure
def: "Neonatal electrographic only seizure is an electrographic event with sudden, repetitive, evolving stereotyped waveforms with a beginning and an end, which is not associated with a clinical manifestation." [PMID:28276060]
comment: The duration of the seizures has to be sufficient to demonstrate evolution in frequency and morphology of the discharges on electroencephalography, which will depend on the frequency of the discharge. The duration is arbitrary but needs to be sufficient to allow recognition of onset, evolution and resolution of an abnormal discharge. This type of seizure is particular to the neonatal period; beyond this electrographic appearance of a seizure must be associated with a clinical correlate to be classed as a seizure.
is_a: HP:0032808 ! Neonatal seizure with electrographic correlate
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:28:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032812
name: Neonatal electro-clinical non-motor seizure
is_a: HP:0032809 ! Neonatal electro-clinical seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:31:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032813
name: Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure with predominant motor features." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Neonatal motor seizures may be further sub-classified as seizures occurring with presentations such as: automatisms, clonic, epileptic spams, myoclonic, sequential, tonic.
is_a: HP:0032809 ! Neonatal electro-clinical seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:31:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032814
name: Neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure where the predominant motor feature is a regularly repeating jerking involving the same muscle groups; it can be symmetric or asymmetric." [PMID:28276064]
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical clonic seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032813 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:32:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032815
name: Neonatal electro-clinical myoclonic seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical myoclonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure where the predominant motor feature is sudden, brief (<100 msec) involuntary single or multiple contraction of muscles or muscle groups of variable topography (axial, proximal limb, distal)." [PMID:28276064]
comment: Clinically difficult to differentiate from non-epileptic myoclonus.
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical myoclonic seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032813 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:34:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032816
name: Neonatal multifocal myoclonic seizure
def: "Neonatal multifocal myoclonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure where the predominant motor feature is sudden, brief (<100 msec) involuntary single or multiple contraction of muscles or muscle groups of variable topography (axial, proximal limb, distal) that occurs at multiple sites." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032815 ! Neonatal electro-clinical myoclonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:35:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032817
name: Neonatal focal myoclonic seizure
def: "Neonatal focal myoclonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure where the predominant motor feature is sudden, brief (<100 msec) involuntary single or multiple contraction of muscles or muscle groups of variable topography (axial, proximal limb, distal) which occurs focally." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032815 ! Neonatal electro-clinical myoclonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:38:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032818
name: Neonatal focal clonic seizure
def: "Neonatal focal clonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure where the predominant motor feature is unilateral regularly repeating jerking involving the same muscle groups." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032814 ! Neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:38:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032819
name: Neonatal bilateral clonic seizure
def: "Neonatal bilateral clonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure where the clonic jerking is bilateral." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032814 ! Neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:39:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032820
name: Neonatal multifocal clonic seizure
def: "Neonatal focal clonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure where the predominant motor feature is a regularly repeating jerking involving the same muscle groups, which occurs at multiple sites." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032814 ! Neonatal electro-clinical clonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:41:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032821
name: Neonatal electro-clinical tonic seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical tonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure where the predominant motor feature is a sustained increase in muscle tone, usually focal, that can be unilateral or bilateral, and lasting a few seconds to minutes." [PMID:28276064]
comment: Usually focal, unilateral or bilateral asymmetric. Generalized tonic posturing is often not of epileptic origin.
is_a: HP:0032813 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:43:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032822
name: Neonatal electro-clinical autonomic seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical non-motor autonomic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure with predominant features of autonomic alterations, involving cardiovascular, pupillary, gastrointestinal, sudomotor, vasomotor, and thermoregulatory functions. May present as apnea." [PMID:28276064]
comment: May involve respiration (apnea). Typically seen with other seizure manifestations. EEG confirmation is mandatory.
is_a: HP:0032812 ! Neonatal electro-clinical non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:44:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032823
name: Neonatal electro-clinical seizure with behavior arrest
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical non-motor seizure with behavior arrest is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure characterized by an arrest of activities, freezing, immobilization, with or without apnea and/or other autonomic manifestations." [PMID:28276064]
comment: May be focal and/or followed by apnea, other autonomic manifestations and motor seizures.
synonym: "Neonatal electro-clinical seizure with behaviour arrest" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical seizure with behavioral arrest" EXACT []
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical seizure with behavioural arrest" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0032812 ! Neonatal electro-clinical non-motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:46:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032824
name: Neonatal focal tonic seizure
def: "Neonatal focal tonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical tonic seizure with a focal sustained increase in muscle tone, lasting a few seconds to minutes." [PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032821 ! Neonatal electro-clinical tonic seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:56:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032825
name: Neonatal electro-clinical sequential seizure
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical sequential motor seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the predominant feature cannot be detected because of seizures presenting with a variety of clinical and electrographic signs, often changing lateralization within or between seizures." [PMID:28276064]
comment: No predominant feature can be determined, instead the seizure presents with a variety of clinical signs. Several features typically occur in a sequence, often with changing lateralization within or between seizures. Most commonly seen in epilepsies of genetic etiology.
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical sequential seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032809 ! Neonatal electro-clinical seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T06:58:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032826
name: Focal neonatal sequential seizure
def: "Focal neonatal electro-clinical sequential motor seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the predominant feature cannot be detected because of seizures presenting with a variety of clinical and electrographic focal signs, often changing lateralization within or between seizures." [PMID:28276064]
comment: No predominant feature can be determined, instead the seizure presents with a variety of clinical signs. Several features typically occur in a sequence, often with changing lateralization within or between seizures. Most commonly seen in epilepsies of genetic etiology.
is_a: HP:0032825 ! Neonatal electro-clinical sequential seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
