[Term]
id: HP:0032829
name: Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure with automatism
def: "Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure with automatism is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the electrographic event is correlated with a coordinated motor activity, typically oral, usually with impaired awareness, and in association with other features." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: Normal and abnormal behavior in term and preterm infants may mimic ictal automatisms.
synonym: "Neonatal electroclinical motor seizure with automatism" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032813 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T07:05:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032830
name: Neonatal seizure with bilateral asymmetric automatism
def: "Neonatal seizure with bilateral asymmetric automatism is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the electrographic event is correlated with coordinated motor activity, typically oral, usually with impaired awareness, occurring at both sides of the body asymmetrically." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032829 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure with automatism
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
