name: Neonatal bilateral asymmetric tonic seizure
def: "Neonatal bilateral asymmetric tonic seizure is a type of neonatal electro-clinical tonic seizure where the sustained increase in muscle tone, lasting a few seconds to minutes, occurs at both sides of the body but asymmetrically." [PMID:28276064]
