[Term]
id: HP:0032833
name: Neonatal epileptic spasm
def: "A sudden flexion, extension, or mixed extension-flexion of predominantly proximal and truncal muscles that is usually more sustained than a myoclonic movement but not as sustained as a tonic seizure. Limited forms may occur: grimacing, head nodding, or subtle eye movements. May occur in clusters." [PMID:28276060]
comment: May be difficult to differentiate from myoclonic seizures without electromyography.
is_a: HP:0032813 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T07:10:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032834
name: Neonatal seizure with unilateral automatism
def: "Neonatal seizure with bilateral asymmetric automatisms is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the electrographic event is correlated with a coordinated motor activity, typically oral, usually with impaired awareness, occurring at one side of the body." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032829 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure with automatism
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-17T07:11:49Z" xsd:dateTime

