def: "Neonatal seizure with bilateral asymmetric automatism is a type of neonatal electro-clinical seizure where the electrographic event is correlated with a coordinated motor activity, typically oral, usually with impaired awareness, occurring at both sides of the body symmetrically." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
is_a: HP:0032829 ! Neonatal electro-clinical motor seizure with automatism
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
