[Term]
id: HP:0032887
name: Generalized atonic seizure
def: "Generalized atonic seizure is a type of generalized motor seizure characterized by a sudden loss or diminution of muscle tone without apparent preceding myoclonic or tonic event lasting about 1-2 s, involving head, trunk, jaw, or limb musculature." [PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: Atonic means without tone. When leg tone is lost during a generalized atonic seizure, the patient falls on the buttocks or sometimes forward onto the knees and face. Recovery is usually within seconds.
synonym: "Generalised atonic seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010819 ! Atonic seizure
is_a: HP:0032677 ! Generalized-onset motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T10:30:46Z" xsd:dateTime

