[Term]
id: HP:0032892
name: Infection-related seizure
def: "Seizure associated with a presumed or proven infection (excluding infection of the central nervous system) or inflammatory state without an alternative precipitant such as metabolic derangement, and regardless of the presence or absence of a fever." [PMID:28276060]
comment: This includes seizures in the context of febrile or afebrile infection.
is_a: HP:0001250 ! Seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T14:01:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032893
name: Gastroenteritis-related afebrile seizure
def: "Afebrile (less than 38.0 degrees Celcius), brief, and generalized seizures accompanying gastroenteritis without an alternative cause." [PMID:12453597, PMID:29935410]
comment: Most typically these seizures have been studied in children between the ages of six months and three years. They often occur in clusters.
is_a: HP:0032892 ! Infection-related seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T14:01:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032894
name: Seizure precipitated by febrile infection
def: "Any form of seizure occurring at the time of a fever (temperature at or above 38.0 degrees Celcius) without infection of the central nervous system, and without an alternative cause such as severe metabolic derangement, occurring at any age." [PMID:28276060]
comment: Typically febrile seizures are limited to the age range of 3 months to 6 years and not accompanied or preceded by afebrile seizures; in this case febrile seizures are not considered indicative of epilepsy. When febrile seizures occur prior to the age of 3 months, or continue beyond the 6th birthday, or when a person has both febrile seizures and afebrile generalized tonic-clonic seizures then a diagnosis of Febrile Seizures Plus (an epilepsy syndrome) may be made.
synonym: "Fever induced seizure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032892 ! Infection-related seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T14:01:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032895
name: Febrile seizure outside the age of 3 months to 6 years
def: "Any type of seizure (most often a generalized tonic-clonic seizure) occurring with fever (at least 38.0 degrees Celsius) but in the absence of central nervous system infection, severe metabolic disturbance or other alternative precipitant in people beyond the typical arrange of 3 months-6 years with no prior history of afebrile seizure." [PMID:30078767, PMID:9126059]
comment: Some but not all people with the epilepsy syndrome of Febrile Seizures Plus have these types of seizures.
is_a: HP:0032894 ! Seizure precipitated by febrile infection
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T14:04:47Z" xsd:dateTime

