[Term]
id: HP:0032898
name: Focal automatism seizure
def: "A focal seizure characterized at onset by coordinated motor activity. This often resembles a voluntary movement and may consist of an inappropriate continuation of preictal motor activity." [PMID:11580774, PMID:28276060, PMID:28276064]
comment: An automatism is a coordinated, repetitive motor activity, often resembling a voluntary movement, but undertaken without volition.
is_a: HP:0011153 ! Focal motor seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
