[Term]
id: HP:0032899
name: Focal orofacial automatism seizure
def: "A type of focal automatism seizure characterized by orofacial automatisms at onset." [PMID:28276060]
comment: These may include involuntary lip smacking, lip pursing, chewing, swallowing, clicking sounds, or eye-blinking.
is_a: HP:0032898 ! Focal automatism seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T15:13:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032900
name: Focal manual automatism seizure
def: "A type of focal automatism seizure characterized by manual automatisms at onset." [PMID:28276060]
comment: These may include involuntary unilateral or bilateral, fumbling, tapping, manipulating, or exploratory movements of the hands.
is_a: HP:0032898 ! Focal automatism seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T15:13:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032901
name: Focal pedal automatism seizure
def: "A type of focal automatism seizure characterized by coordinated bilateral or unilateral movements of the feet or legs at onset. The movement is more reminiscent of normal movements in amplitude, and is less frenetic or rapid in comparison to the movements seen in focal hyperkinetic seizures involving the legs." [PMID:28276060]
comment: These may include pacing, walking, or running.
is_a: HP:0032898 ! Focal automatism seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T15:13:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032902
name: Focal perseverative automatism seizure
def: "A type of focal automatism seizure characterized by inappropriate continuation of pre-seizure movement or behavior at onset." [PMID:28276060]
is_a: HP:0032898 ! Focal automatism seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-18T15:13:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032903
