[Term]
id: HP:0032932
name: Increased circulating pancreatic triacylglycerol lipase level
def: "An increased level of triacylglycerol lipase in the blood circulation (can be measured in serum or plasma)." [PMID:28431198]
comment: Acute pancreatitis is the main reason for an increase in lipase, although a number of other conditions such as chronic pancreatitis, acute cholecystitis, and bowel obstruction can increase lipase activity. In acute pancreatitis, serum lipase levels usually rise within 4 to 8 hours, peak at 24 hours, and decrease to normal or near normal levels over the next 8 to 14 days. Serum lipase remains elevated for a longer period of time compared to the period of elevation of serum amylase after acute pancreatitis. A common threshold used is three times the normal limit.
synonym: "Elevated circulating pancreatic triacylglycerol lipase activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-19T08:01:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032933
name: Airway hyperresponsiveness
def: "An increased sensitivity of the airways to an inhaled constrictor agonist, a steeper slope of the dose-response curve, and a greater maximal response to the agonist." [PMID:12629006]
is_a: HP:0002795 ! Abnormal respiratory system physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-19T08:28:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032934
name: Spontaneous cerebrospinal fluid leak
def: "A spontaneous cerebrospinal fluid leak (SCSFL) is a spontaneous and unexplained leak of the cerebrospinal fluid from the dura surrounding either the brain (cranial leak) or spine (spinal leak)." [PMID:19225307, PMID:22929030]
is_a: HP:0010651 ! Abnormal meningeal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-19T12:28:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032935
name: Posterior crocodile shagreen of the cornea
def: "Grayish, polygonal pattern of opacities with intervening clear zones across the central cornea that resembles crocodile skin." [PMID:19682623]
is_a: HP:0007881 ! Central corneal dystrophy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-03-19T12:48:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0032936
name: Intrusion symptom
def: "Unintentional re-experiencing of a traumatic event involves symptoms that typically include sensory impressions and emotional responses stemming from the trauma. These symptoms seem to lack a sense of time perspective and context." []
comment: Vivid intrusive memories, flashbacks, or nightmares are typically accompanied by strong and overwhelming emotions, such as fear or horror, as well as intense physical sensations.
synonym: "Re-experiencing symptom" EXACT []
is_a: HP:5200230 ! Maladaptive fear-related cognitions
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8430-6039
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0692-412X
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7405-0954
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0072-5522
