name: Anti-U1 ribonucleoprotein antibody positivity
def: "The presence autoantibodies in the serum that react to proteins (70 Kd, A, C) that are associated with U1 RNA and form U1snRNP." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158, PMID:15804705, PMID:29796907]
comment: High titers of anti-RNP antibodies are diagnostic of mixed connective tissue disorder (MCTD). Anti-RNP antibodies can also be found in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus. The U1 small nuclear ribonucleoprotein (U1-snRNP) particle is a complex made up of U1 RNA plus several associated proteins, the three most clinically relevant being U1-70K (RNP70), U1-A, and U1-C.
synonym: "Anti-RNP-antibodies" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Anti-Scl-34 antibody positivity" NARROW []
synonym: "Anti-U1-RNP antibody positivity" EXACT []
synonym: "Anti-U3 ribonucleoprotein antibody positivity" NARROW []
