[Term]
id: HP:0033030
name: Anti-glomerular basement membrane-antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the serum that react to the glomerular basement membrane." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0104-692X, PMID:20660402]
comment: Anti-GBM-antibodies are found in Goodpasture syndrome. Circulating antibodies are directed against the collagen of the part of the kidney known as the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), resulting in acute or rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis. Antibodies also attack the collagen of the air sacs of the lung (alveoli) resulting in bleeding of the lung (pulmonary hemorrhage).
synonym: "Anti-GBM-antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
