id: HP:0033068
name: Medication crystalluria
def: "A variety of drugs may occasionally cause transient crystalluria, in isolation or in conjunction with other urinary abnormalities. Overdose, dehydration, or hypoalbuminaemia, which increases the unbound drug which is ultrafiltrated by the glomerulus, are the factors usually favoring the precipitation of crystals within the tubular lumina. In some cases, medication-induced crystalluria has a distinct phenotypic appearance. For instance, Sulphadiazine crystals appear as strongly birefringent 'shocks of wheat' or 'shells' with an amber color. Acyclovir crystals are birefringent and needle-shaped, and when present in abundance give to urine a silky and opalescent macroscopic appearance." [PMID:8671802]
is_a: HP:0020074 ! Crystalluria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-07-25T10:55:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033069
name: Renal interstitial IgG4+ plasma cell infiltration
def: "An increased number of IgG4+ plasma cells in the interstitial space of the kidney." [PMID:21719792, PMID:29359118]
comment: IgG4-related tubulointerstitial nephritis is characterized by an increased number of IgG4+ plasma cells per high-power field on renal biopsy in addition to either elevated serum IgG4 or evidence of extra renal IgG4-related disease.
is_a: HP:0032581 ! Abnormal renal interstitial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-07-25T11:24:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033070
name: Impaired self monitoring
def: "Impaired ability to track awareness of the effect that one's behavior has on others and how it compares with standards or expectations for behavior." [NCIT:C121466, PMID:26039846]
is_a: HP:0033051 ! Impaired executive functioning
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-07-25T12:13:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033071
name: Impaired task monitoring
def: "Impaired ability to keep track of one's problem-solving success or failure, and to identify and correct mistakes during performance of a goal." [NCIT:C121470, PMID:26039846]
is_a: HP:0033051 ! Impaired executive functioning
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-07-25T12:13:49Z" xsd:dateTime

