[Term]
id: HP:0033126
name: Cutaneous necrosis
def: "Skin and subcutaneous tissue necrosis (tissue death). Clinically, cutaneous necrosis may present as a painful and extremely tender black eschar (dead tissue found in a full-thickness wound) surrounded by dusky grey-red colored skin or as slough (dead tissue, usually cream or yellow in colour)." [PMID:16455730, PMID:28470091]
