[Term]
id: HP:0033154
name: Elevated circulating deoxypyridinoline concentration
def: "An increased concentration of lysyl-pyridinoline (deoxypyridinoline) cross-links in the blood circulation." [PMID:12661898]
comment: Pyridinoline cross-links contribute to the structural rigidity and integrity of collagen fibrils in bone. When bone resorption occurs, osteoclastic degradation of bone matrix releases pyridinoline and deoxypyridinoline into the circulation; these compounds are then excreted in urine. Measurements of urinary elimination of these compounds may provide useful information on the change of bone resorption.
is_a: HP:0033386 ! Abnormal circulating collagen degradation product concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-09-20T11:19:47Z" xsd:dateTime

