[Term]
id: HP:0033180
name: Torsion of appendix of testis
def: "The appendix testis or hydatid of Morgagni, is a vestigial remnant of the Müllerian duct located on the superior pole of the testicle between the testis and epididymis. Although this appendage has no vital function, it is present in 50% of males. Torsion of twisting of this vestigial remnant can be incredibly painful, but usually requires no medical intervention." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8169-9049, PMID:31550101]
synonym: "Twisted vestigial remnant of the Muellerian duct" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000035 ! Abnormal testis morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-09-28T22:15:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033181
name: Spinal epidural abscess
def: "Spinal epidural abscess (SEA) is caused by a suppurative infection in the epidural space. The mass effect of the abscess can compress and reduce blood flow to the spinal cord, conus medullaris, or cauda equina." [PMID:24007734, PMID:26540492]
comment: Left untreated, the infection can lead to sensory loss, muscle weakness, visceral dysfunction, sepsis, and even death. Early diagnosis is essential to limit morbidity and neurologic injury. The classic triad of fever, axial pain, and neurological deficit occurs in as few as 13 percent of patients, highlighting the diagnostic challenge associated with SEA.
synonym: "A severe pyogenic infection of the epidural space" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025615 ! Abscess
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-09-28T22:20:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033182
name: Increased circulating cathepsin D level
def: "An increase in concentration of cathepsin D in the blood circulation." [PMID:26995190]
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-09-28T22:29:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033183
name: Bilobed right lung
def: "A developmental defect of pulmonary lobation characterized by the presence of only two lobes of the right lung." [PMID:19500772]
comment: The normal anatomy of the right lung comprises three lobes: the upper, middle, and lower lobes, and that of the left lung consists of two lobes: the upper and lower lobes.
is_a: HP:0002101 ! Abnormal lung lobation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-10-04T11:44:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033184
name: Triggered by infection
comment: Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by an infection, that is by invasion and multiplication of microorganisms such as bacteria, viruses, and parasites that are not normally present within the body.
is_a: HP:0025204 ! Triggered by
