[Term]
id: HP:0033193
name: Ballooning hepatocyte degeneration
def: "Swelling of the hepatocyte, rounding of its contour, and alteration of the cytoplasm, which takes on a reticulated, rarefied, or flocculant quality. The cytoplasm of the ballooned hepatocytes often contains clumps of eosinophilic ropey material known as Mallory-Denk bodies (MDBs) or Mallory hyaline, which is composed of hyperphosphorylated misfolded intermediate filaments, ubiquitin, and ubiquitin-binding protein P62." [PMID:31603713, PMID:31885839]
comment: Mallory-Denk bodies are inclusions found within the cytoplasm of ballooned hepatocytes that are composed of cytokeratin filaments, they have a twisted-rope appearance.
synonym: "Ballooning degeneration of hepatocytes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034713 ! Abnormal hepatocyte morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-10-10T15:47:08Z" xsd:dateTime

