property_value: terms:date "2020-10-11T12:16:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033199
name: Increased circulating interleukin 10 concentration
def: "An elevation of the concentration of interleukin 10 in the blood circulation." [PMID:18424693]
comment: IL-10 is an anti-inflammatory cytokine. During infection it inhibits the activity of Th1 cells, NK cells, and macrophages, all of which are required for optimal pathogen clearance but also contribute to tissue damage. In consequence, IL-10 can both impede pathogen clearance and ameliorate immunopathology.
synonym: "Increased serum interleukin 10" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034162 ! Abnormal circulating interleukin 10 concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-10-11T12:18:51Z" xsd:dateTime

