[Term]
id: HP:0033202
name: Brachioradialis hyporeflexia
def: "Reduced intensity of the brachioradialis tendon reflex." [PMID:32119424]
comment: The brachioradialis reflex is a deep tendon reflex involving the C5 and C6 nerve roots through its innervation by the radial nerve. To test brachioradialis reflex, the forearm is supported in a slightly pronated position. Then, the physician delivers a series of quick hits with the reflex hammer to the area of the styloid process of the radius at the point of brachioradialis insertion.
is_a: HP:0012391 ! Hyporeflexia of upper limbs
