[Term]
id: HP:0033222
name: Inverted CD4:CD8 ratio
def: "CD4:CD8 ratio less than 1, measured either as proportion of total CD3+ T cells, or in absolute numbers per microliter. These are usually measured within the TCR alpha/beta positive population. Normally there are relatively more CD4+ than CD8+ T cells." [PMID:29095912]
comment: A low or inverted CD4/CD8 ratio is an immune risk phenotype and is associated with altered immune function, immune senescence, and chronic inflammation in both HIV-infected and uninfected populations.
synonym: "Decreased CD4:CD8 ratio" EXACT []
synonym: "Inverted CD4/CD8 ratio" EXACT []
