[Term]
id: HP:0033240
name: Elevated RV/TLC ratio
def: "An increase in the ratio of residual volume (RV) to total lung capacity (TLC) on pulmonary function testing. RV is the amount of air remaining aftermaximal expiration and TLC is the total amount of air in theungs at full inspiration. These volumes cannot be determined by spirometry, but can be measured by inert gas dilution, nitrogen washout, and (3) body plethysmography. An elevated RV/TLC can be interpreted as a sign of air trapping and hyperinflation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0104-692X, PMID:12934788]
synonym: "Hyperinflation on pulmonary function test" RELATED []
synonym: "Overinflation on pulmonary function test" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0033772 ! Abnormal RV/TLC ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-24T10:58:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033241
name: Polyalveolar lobe
def: "An elevation of the total count of alveoli as determined by microscopic point-counting of randomly taken lung sections, not secondary to abnormalities in number, size and structure of the airways. In polyaveolar lobe, the number of alveoli is generally increased three to fivefold." [PMID:7463297]
comment: Indiviudals with polyalveolar lobe have some pulmonary function abnormalities, specifically a decrease in airway conductance, and forced expiratory volume.
