is_a: HP:0002583 ! Colitis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-27T19:37:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033257
name: Delayed ability to walk with support
def: "A failure to achieve the ability to walk with support (cruise) at an appropriate developmental stage." []
synonym: "Delayed ability to cruise" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002194 ! Delayed gross motor development
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-27T19:39:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033258
name: Sudden unexpected death in epilepsy
def: "Sudden unexpected death in epilepsy (SUDEP) is a sudden, unexpected, witnessed or unwitnessed, non-traumatic and non-drowning death, occurring in benign circumstances, in an individual with epilepsy, with or without evidence for a seizure and excluding documented status epilepticus, in which postmortem examination has not revealed a cause of death." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1735-8178, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9588-2944, PMID:22191982]
synonym: "SUDEP" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0001699 ! Sudden death
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T14:34:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033259
name: Non-motor seizure
def: "A seizure with clinical manifestation but without motor signs (other than possible behavior arrest) as its initial clinical manifestation. The electrographic onset may be generalized, focal, or unknown." [PMID:2827606, PMID:28276060]
comment: This term may be used to code the non-motor seizures of a person who cannot confirm or exclude subjective seizure experiences that would aid more detailed classification as a generalized non-motor (absence) seizure or type of focal non-motor seizure.
is_a: HP:0001250 ! Seizure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T14:43:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033260
name: Livedo racemosa
def: "Livedo racemosa describes a reddish-blue mottling of the skin in an irregular, reticular pattern. It differs from the more common livedo reticularis by its shape. Livedo racemosa consists of broken circular segments resulting in a seemingly larger pattern, as opposed to the fine, regular, complete network of livedo reticularis. Livedo racemosa results from permanent impairment of peripheral blood flow and, unlike livedo reticularis, it persists on warming." [PMID:26500860, PMID:31753828]
is_a: HP:0033832 ! Livedo
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T14:55:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033261
name: Renal artery aneurysm
def: "Increase in diameter of a segment of the renal artery that can be defined as a focal, isolated dilatation of all three layers of the arterial wall over 1.5 times the diameter of the disease-free proximal adjacent arterial segment." [PMID:25537277]
is_a: HP:0008776 ! Abnormal renal artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T14:56:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033262
name: Transphyseal fracture of the distal humerus
def: "A fracture through the distal humeral physis that separates the entire distal humeral epiphysis from the metaphysis." [PMID:26808044]
comment: Transphyseal fractures of the distal humerus typically occur in children younger than 3 years secondary to birth trauma, nonaccidental trauma, or a fall from a small height.
synonym: "Transphyseal distal humerus fracture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0041055 ! Fractured humerus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T15:04:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033263
