property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T15:12:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033265
name: Podocyte myelin figures
def: "Lamellated intracytoplasmic lipid inclusions within podocytes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Podocyte myelin inclusions" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T15:14:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033266
name: Glomerular pseudocrescent
def: "Visceral epithelial cell hyperplasia with resulting cellular crowding of the the urinary space. In contrast with true crescents, these proliferations lack inflammatory cells and fibrin. The cells are typically plump (not spindle-shaped) and often vacuolated, and Bowman's capsule is usually intact." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T15:19:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033267
name: Abnormal glomerular capillary lumen morphology
def: "Abnormal structural characteristics of the interior space of the capillary of the renal glomerulus." [PMID:24875196]
is_a: HP:0025006 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T15:58:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033268
name: Deflation of the glomerular tuft
def: "Wrinkling and folding of the capillaries without epithelial cell (podocyte) hyperplasia (formerly called ischemic type of collapse) involving o 80% of the glomerular tuft. The wrinkling is generally made by small regular folds of the glomerular basement membrane." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:27102348]
is_a: HP:0033267 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary lumen morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:01:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033269
name: Glomerular capillary collapse
def: "Collapse is generally accompanied by other descriptors such as hypertrophy and hyperplasia of overlying glomerular epithelial cells, halo, protein droplets in podocytes and glomerular parietal epithelial cells (PECs)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
comment: Wrinkling and folding of the glomerular basemement membrane (GBM) with partial or complete occlusion of the capillary lumen: wrinkling and folding of the GBM with partial or complete occlusion of the capillary lumen. The wrinkling is generally made by small and/or big irregular folds of the GBM.
synonym: "Collapse of glomerular capillary walls" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033267 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary lumen morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:04:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033270
name: Glomerular capillary congestion
def: "Global distention of glomerular capillaries with intraluminal intact red blood cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Glomerular congestion" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033267 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary lumen morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:07:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033271
name: Glomerular capillary microaneurysm
def: "Glomerular capillary dilatation due to loosening/detachment of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) from its anchoring points, usually in the context of mesangiolysis or nodular glomerulosclerosis." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033267 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary lumen morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:09:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033272
name: Abnormal glomerular endothelial cell morphology
def: "An abnormal structure of the glomerular endothelial cells, which are highly specialized cells with fenestrae and a charged luminal glycocalyx layer that contribute to the filtration barrier." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:29629372]
is_a: HP:0025006 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:20:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033273
name: Loss of glomerular endothelial cell fenestration
def: "Loss of round to oval discontinuities normally present in the glomerular capillary endothelial cell cytoplasm." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:19129259]
is_a: HP:0033272 ! Abnormal glomerular endothelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:22:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033274
name: Glomerular endotheliosis
def: "Enlargement of glomerular endothelial cells by cytoplasmic swelling with resulting partial or complete occlusion of the lumen." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:14511965]
is_a: HP:0033272 ! Abnormal glomerular endothelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:25:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033275
name: Glomerular endothelial tubuloreticular inclusion
def: "Inter-anastomosing tubular structures located within cisternae of endoplasmic reticulum, most often within endothelial cells and associated with exposure to interferon." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:23957425]
is_a: HP:0033272 ! Abnormal glomerular endothelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T16:27:12Z" xsd:dateTime

