[Term]
id: HP:0033278
name: Reduced CD95-induced lymphocyte apoptosis
def: "Reduced amount of programmed cell death in peripheral blood lymphocytes following exposure to CD95 (APO-1/Fas), which is a member of the death receptor family, a subfamily of the TNF-R superfamily. Crosslinking of CD95 with its natural ligand CD95L (CD178) or with agonistic antibodies such as anti-APO-1 induces apoptosis in sensitive cells." [PMID:21625644]
is_a: HP:0002731 ! Decreased T cell apoptosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T17:19:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033279
name: Enterocutaneous fistula
def: "An abnormal connection (fistula) between the intra-abdominal intestinal tract and the skin." [PMID:27247538]
is_a: HP:0100819 ! Intestinal fistula
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T17:55:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033280
name: Paratracheal lymphadenopathy
def: "Enlargement of lymph nodes surrounding the trachea." [PMID:4023240]
is_a: HP:0002716 ! Lymphadenopathy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T18:19:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033281
name: Circulating nucleated red blood cells
def: "The presence of nucleated red blood cells in the peripheral blood circulation." [PMID:28633658]
comment: Nucleated red blood cells (NRBCs) are early erythrocyte precursors not present in the peripheral blood of normal adults. Fenestrations in the bone marrow provide a physical filter to the release of the large NRBCs into the circulation, and the rare NRBC that escapes is rapidly cleared from peripheral blood by the spleen. The presence of circulating NRBCs in adults thus reflects extreme increases in erythropoietic activity or failure of the blood filtration mechanisms.
is_a: HP:0001877 ! Abnormal erythrocyte morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T19:50:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033282
name: Abnormal glomerular basement membrane morphology
def: "Any abnormal sttructure of the glomerular basement membrane." [PMID:29435440]
comment: The (GBM) is an integral component of the glomerular filtration barrier; an important and highly complex capillary wall that is exposed to mechanical forces driven by capillary hydrostatic pressure. This barrier is permeable to water and small molecules, and selectively withholds cells and macromolecules such as albumin in the circulation.
is_a: HP:0000095 ! Abnormal renal glomerulus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T20:24:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033283
name: Segmentally thickened glomerular basement membrane
def: "Prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting a segmental and increase in thickness (subjective estimate) with no evidence of electron dense deposits by EM. Thickening is measured from endothelial to visceral epithelial plasma membrane and mainly attributable to an increase in thickness of the lamina densa, generally to an overall thickness more than 2 standard deviations greater than that of the normal mean GBM thickness for health age- and sex matched individuals." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033285 ! Thickened glomerular basement membranes with no electron dense deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T20:34:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033284
name: Diffusely thickened glomerular basement membrane
def: "Prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate) with no evidence of electron dense deposits by EM. Thickening is measured from endothelial to visceral epithelial plasma membrane and mainly attributable to an increase in thickness of the lamina densa, generally to an overall thickness more than 2 standard deviations greater than that of the normal mean GBM thickness for health age- and sex matched individuals." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033285 ! Thickened glomerular basement membranes with no electron dense deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T20:36:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033285
name: Thickened glomerular basement membranes with no electron dense deposits
def: "Prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting an increase in thickness (subjective estimate) with no evidence of electron dense deposits by electron microscopy." []
is_a: HP:0004722 ! Thickened glomerular basement membrane
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T20:39:15Z" xsd:dateTime

