[Term]
id: HP:0033305
name: Abnormal circulating fetuin-A concentration
def: "Any deviation from the normal concentration of fetuin-A in the blood circulation." []
comment: Fetuin-A (FetA) is a 64-kDa glycoprotein that is found in relatively high concentrations in human serum. In human adults, FetA is mainly expressed and secreted from the liver and adipose tissue. Epidemiologic research consistently observes elevated circulating FetA in obesity and related complications, such as type 2 diabetes mellitus, the metabolic syndrome, and nonalcoholic fatty liver disease.
synonym: "Abnormal alpha-2-HS-glycoprotein level" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010876 ! Abnormal circulating protein concentration
