property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T22:16:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033310
name: Osmotic diarrhea
def: "Osmotic diarrhea results from the presence of osmotically active, poorly absorbed solutes in the bowel lumen that inhibit normal water and electrolyte absorption." [PMID:22677080]
comment: Osmotic diarrhea involves an unabsorbed substance that draws water from the plasma into the intestinal lumen along osmotic gradients. Secretory diarrhea results from disordered electrolyte transport and, despite the term, is more commonly caused by decreased absorption rather than net secretion. Inflammatory diseases cause diarrhea with exudative, secretory, or osmotic components.
is_a: HP:0002014 ! Diarrhea
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T22:20:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033311
name: Abdominal aortic dissection
def: "A tear in the intimal layer of the abdominal aorta causing a separation between the intima and the medial layers." [PMID:15902826]
is_a: HP:0002647 ! Aortic dissection
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-28T22:39:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033312
name: Abnormal Bowman space morphology
def: "Structural anomaly located in Bowman's space, which represents the beginning of the urinary space and is contiguous with the proximal convoluted tubule of the nephron." [PMID:32119361]
comment: Bowman's capsule is a part of the nephron that forms a cup-like sack surrounding the glomerulus. The capsule encloses a space called Bowman's space, which represents the beginning of the urinary space and is contiguous with the proximal convoluted tubule of the nephron. Bowman's capsule, Bowman's space, and the glomerular capillary network and its supporting architecture can collectively be thought of as composing the glomerulus.
is_a: HP:0031264 ! Abnormal Bowman capsule morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:07:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033313
name: Urinary space collagenization
def: "Acellular collagenous matrix within Bowman's space, not associated with extracapillary hypercellularity or necrosis, associated with sclerosis or deflation of the tuft." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Collagenization of the urinary space" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033312 ! Abnormal Bowman space morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:10:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033314
name: Visceral epithelial cell hyperplasia
def: "Increased number of visceral epithelial cells (2 or more layers), often with crowding and multilayering, but without continuity with the parietal epithelium." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Hyperplasia of visceral epithelial cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Podocyte hyperplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:17:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033315
name: Visceral epithelial hyaline droplets
def: "Round to ovoid, Periodic acid-Schiff (PAS)-positive, fuchsinophilic cytoplasmic inclusions within visceral epithelial cells." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:22:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033316
name: Glomerular crescent formation
def: "Glomerular crescent refers hyperplastic lesions involving 10% or more of the circumference of Bowman's capsule. Crescents can be composed of a variable mixture of epithelial/leukocyte hypercellularity, fibrous matrix, and fibrin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32132388]
comment: The crescent is an unspecific histopathological lesion that can be triggered by a variety of different underlying disorders. Whenever, microvascular injury leads to rupture of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), the leakage of plasma proteins drives parietal epithelial cell hyperplasia as the key cellular component of the crescent. Single nephron GFR decreases because of tuft collapse, rupture of the Bowman capsule, and influx of immune cells and fibroblasts are all secondary events that may or may not occur in individual glomeruli. Periglomerular immune cell infiltrates or fibrotic encasting of the activated parietal cells (fibrocellular crescents) are subsequent events that may affect the dynamics and prognosis of the disease.
is_a: HP:0033312 ! Abnormal Bowman space morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:27:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033317
name: Cellular crescent
def: "A type of glomerular crescent characterized by extracapillary hypercellularity of greater than two cell layers and involving more than 10% of the capsular circumference, composed of greater than 75% cells with or without fibrin, and less than 25% fibrous matrix." [PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033316 ! Glomerular crescent formation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:31:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033318
name: Fibrocellular crescent
def: "A type of glomerular crescent characterized by extracapillary hypercellularity of more than 2 cell layers and involving over 10% of the capsular circumference, composed of 25% to 75% cells with or without fibrin, and the remainder fibrous matrix." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033316 ! Glomerular crescent formation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:33:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033319
name: Fibrous crescent
def: "A type of glomerular crescent characterized by extracapillary fibrosis composed of greater than 75% matrix and of less than 25% cells with or without fibrin, usually associated with disruption of Bowman's capsule and involving over 10% of the capsular circumference." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033316 ! Glomerular crescent formation
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:37:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033320
name: Mesangial cell loss
def: "Loss of mesangial cells segmentally or globally." []
comment: Mesangial cell loss can be observed in the setting of mesangiolysis.
is_a: HP:0033231 ! Abnormal glomerular mesangial cellularity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:43:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033321
name: Glomerular obsolescence
def: "Globally sclerotic glomeruli are that are small and without hyalinosis and may appear with collapse of the tuft with collagenization of the urinary space. Bowman's capsule is completely or partially absent and there is no periglomerular fibrosis and glomerular size is decreased by more than 50% compared to all other glomeruli in the same biopsy. Obsolescent glomeruli may appear to be receding into the interstitium." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0004737 ! Global glomerulosclerosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:57:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033322
name: Glomerular capillary wall duplication without cellular interposition
def: "Double contouring of the original glomerular basement membrane (GBM)/additional layer(s) of overlying basement membrane matrix, with or without endocapillary hypercellularity and no evidence of interposed migrated cells (mesangial, endothelial, monocytes) between the layers of original GBM and de novo GBM." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0025006 ! Abnormal glomerular capillary morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2020-11-29T13:59:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
