property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-09T23:03:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033481
name: Limited lateral neck flexion
def: "Reduced range of motion resulting in decreased ability to move the ear toward the top of the shoulder." []
is_a: HP:0005986 ! Limitation of neck motion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-09T23:05:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033482
name: Limited shoulder flexion
def: "A reduced ability to flex the shoulder. Shoulder flexion is the motion that moves the arms from a resting position by the side of the body to a position above the head." []
is_a: HP:0006467 ! Limited shoulder movement
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-09T23:28:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033483
name: Podocyte infolding
def: "Folding of cytoplasmic processes of podocytes into the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) with thickening of the lamina densa and microspheres and/or microtubular structures within the GBM." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32393263, PMID:33276871]
comment: See Figure 3d of PMID:32393263 and Figures 1 and 2 of PMID:33276871 for examples.
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:12:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033484
name: Elevated circulating linoleylcarnitine concentration
def: "Increased concentration of linoleylcarnitine in the blood circulation." []
synonym: "Elevated circulating C18:2 acylcarnitine concentration" EXACT []
synonym: "Elevated plasma linoleylcarnitine, C18:2" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0035020 ! Elevated circulating C18 acylcarnitine concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:30:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033485
name: Glomerular basement membrane disruption
def: "A point of rupture in the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) where the discontinuous portions of GBM are still identifiable with a basement membrane stain such as Periodic acid Schiff (PAS) or silver." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
comment: Disruption of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) may occur in settings of inflammation (ANCA/antiGBM antibodies) or could be seen due to structural weakness of the GBM (Collagen IV disorders). This feature can be associated with extracapillary fibrin. The definition of this term intends to exclude glomeruli at the edge of the core where rupture could be iatrogenic or mechanical.
synonym: "Disruption of the glomerular basement membrane" EXACT []
synonym: "Glomerular basement membrane rupture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033282 ! Abnormal glomerular basement membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:39:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033486
name: Abnormal glomerular basement membrane texture
def: "Anomalous appearance or structure of the surface of the glomerular basement membrane." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033282 ! Abnormal glomerular basement membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:45:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033487
name: Glomerular basement membranes powdery deposit
def: "Punctate electron-dense material typically in a band-like distribution along the lamina rara interna and within tubular basement membranes within the subendothelial aspect of the glomerular basement membrane." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Glomerular basement membranes with powdery deposit" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033486 ! Abnormal glomerular basement membrane texture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:47:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033488
name: Glomerular endocapillary leukocyte hypercellularity
def: "Increased number of leukocytes internal to the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), but not limited to within glomerular capillaries." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
comment: The optimal demonstration of leukocytes may require immunohistochemistry.
synonym: "Glomerular endocapillary hypercellularity consisting of leukocytes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025363 ! Glomerular endocapillary hypercellularity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:54:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033489
name: Glomerular endocapillary neutrophil hypercellularity
def: "Increased number of neutrophils internal to the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), but not limited to within glomerular capillaries." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033488 ! Glomerular endocapillary leukocyte hypercellularity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:57:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033490
name: Glomerular endocapillary foam-cell hypercellularity
def: "Presence of lipid-filled cells, often a macrophage, with a vacuolated appearance in the glomerulus often occupying the endocapillary space." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033488 ! Glomerular endocapillary leukocyte hypercellularity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T12:59:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033491
name: Global mesangial sclerosis
def: "A generalized global (over 80%) increase of mesangial matrix that is present throughout the mesangial stalk (with or without associated mesangial hypercellularity)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
comment: Glomerular changes can be focal (only in some glomeruli) or diffuse (in all or almost all the glomeruli), and segmental (only a part of the glomerulus) or global (the entire glomerulus).
is_a: HP:0033232 ! Abnormal glomerular mesangial matrix morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:02:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033492
name: Podocyte cytoskeletal condensation
def: "Reorganization of podocyte cytoskeletal proteins at the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) aspect of the cell, with associated cytoplasmic electron density at the GBM aspect of the podocyte." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:27102348]
is_a: HP:0031265 ! Abnormal glomerular visceral epithelial cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:12:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033493
name: Mesangial matrix expansion
def: "Increased mesangial extracellular material with interspace width of over 2 mesangial cell nuclei, in one or more peripheral mesangial areas." [PMID:32866505]
synonym: "Increased glomerular mesangial matrix" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033232 ! Abnormal glomerular mesangial matrix morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:15:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033494
name: Glomerular basement membrane amyloid spicule
def: "Amyloid spicules are projections of typically silver-positive material from the outer aspect of the glomerular capillary wall, perpendicular to the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), most often caused by amyloidosis with the latter confirmed by additional stains." [PMID:25852856, PMID:32866505]
comment: See Figure 3 of PMID:25852856.
is_a: HP:0033282 ! Abnormal glomerular basement membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:18:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033495
name: Segmental glomerulosclerosis
def: "Segmental solidification of the glomerular tuft by increased extracellular matrix, causing glomerular capillary obliteration and can include hyalinosis, foam cells, hypertrophy of overlying glomerular epithelial cells, podocyte depletion, halo and adhesion of the tuft to the Bowman capsule." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
comment: Glomerular changes can be focal (only in some glomeruli) or diffuse (in all or almost all the glomeruli), and segmental (only a part of the glomerulus) or global (the entire glomerulus).
is_a: HP:0000096 ! Glomerular sclerosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:21:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033496
name: Perihilar segmental glomerulosclerosis
def: "Segmental solidification of the glomerular tuft by increased extracellular matrix, causing glomerular capillary obliteration is present at the vascular pole, involving less than 50% of the tuft. It can be accompanied by other descriptors such as hyalinosis, foam cells, hypertrophy of overlying glomerular epithelial cells, podocyte depletion, halo and adhesion of the tuft to the Bowman's capsule." [PMID:27437509]
synonym: "Segmental glomerulosclerosis, perihilar pattern" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033495 ! Segmental glomerulosclerosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:24:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033497
name: Tip variant segmental glomerulosclerosis
def: "Segmental solidification of the glomerular tuft characterized by an adhesion at the tip of the glomerular tuft abutting the proximal tubular taek-off can be accompanied by increased extracellular matrix, causing glomerular capillary obliteration at the glomerular tip. Features including hyalinosis, foam cells, hypertrophy of overlying glomerular epithelial cells can also be observed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:27437509]
synonym: "Segmental glomerulosclerosis, tip variant" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033495 ! Segmental glomerulosclerosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:27:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033498
name: Segmental glomerulosclerosis away from the vascular and tubular poles
def: "Segmental solidification of the glomerular tuft characterized by increased extracellular matrix, causing glomerular capillary obliteration at neither the tubular or vascular poles. Features including hyalinosis, foam cells, hypertrophy of overlying glomerular epithelial cells can also be observed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033495 ! Segmental glomerulosclerosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:29:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033499
name: Glomerular basement membrane electron dense deposits
def: "Electron-dense deposits in the lamina densa with a ribbon or a sausage structure." [PMID:33329990]
comment: See Figure 1 of PMID:33329990 for an example.
is_a: HP:0033282 ! Abnormal glomerular basement membrane morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:35:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033500
name: Subendothelial glomerular basement membrane electron dense deposits
def: "Electron dense deposits in the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) subendothelial space associated with a prominent GBM reflecting an increase in thickness. This feature can be associated with GBM remodeling along the endothelial aspect." []
comment: The glomerular filtration barrier consists of two cells (podocytes and endothelial cells) and the glomerular basement membrane (GBM), a specialized extracellular matrix that lies between them.
is_a: HP:0033499 ! Glomerular basement membrane electron dense deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T13:41:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033501
name: Subepithelial glomerular basement membrane electron dense deposits
def: "Prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting a diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate) with exogenous material deposited between the outer (epithelial) aspect of the GBM and the visceral epithelial cell, with varying degrees of incorporation into the GBM." []
is_a: HP:0033499 ! Glomerular basement membrane electron dense deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T14:16:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033502
name: Abnormal esterified to free carnitine ratio
def: "Any deviation from the normal ratio of acylcarnitine (i.e., esterified carnitine) to free carnitine." []
comment: Carnitine is a nutrient that is made from the amino acids methionine and lysine. Its primary role is to allow the transport of long-chain fatty acids into the mitochondrial matrix for beta-oxidation and energy production. Carnitine is stored in the skeletal muscle, heart, liver, brain, and kidney and within plasma. Carnitine is also found in the body in several different forms.
is_a: HP:0012071 ! Abnormal circulating fatty acylcarnitine concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T15:09:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033503
name: Elevated CSF fumarate concentration
def: "An increased concentration of fumarate, an intermediate in the citric acid cycle, in the cebrebrospinal fluid." [PMID:31290619]
is_a: HP:0025454 ! Abnormal CSF metabolite concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T14:28:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033504
name: Elevated circulating fumarate concentration
def: "An increased concentration of fumarate, an intermediate in the citric acid cycle, in the blood circulation." [PMID:31290619]
is_a: HP:0010995 ! Abnormal circulating dicarboxylic acid concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T14:29:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033505
name: Livedo reticularis
def: "Livedo reticularis is characterized by the presence of a bluish purple, mottled or netlike pattern in unbroken circles on the skin. Exposure to cold environments usually intensifies the vascular pattern. Presumably, the condition results from slow or stagnant blood flow, vessel-wall pathology, and decreased oxygen tension." []
comment: The distinction to cutis marmorata is that the mottling does not resolve when the skin is warmed, and the discoloration is bluish purple rather than red. The Livedo reticularis lesion is more intense and is persistent.
is_a: HP:0033832 ! Livedo
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T14:43:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033506
name: Increased esterified to free carnitine ratio
def: "An elevated ratio of acylcarnitine (i.e., esterified carnitine) to free carnitine." []
is_a: HP:0033502 ! Abnormal esterified to free carnitine ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T15:13:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033507
name: Decreased esterified to free carnitine ratio
def: "A reduced ratio of acylcarnitine (i.e., esterified carnitine) to free carnitine." []
is_a: HP:0033502 ! Abnormal esterified to free carnitine ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-10T15:13:37Z" xsd:dateTime

