[Term]
id: HP:0033558
name: Anti-histone antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the blood circulation that react against histone antigens." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:15096389]
comment: Anti-histone antibodies are found in the serum of up to 75-95% of people with drug-induced lupus and 75% of idiopathic SLE and less frequently in scleroderma, rheumatoid arthritis and undifferentiated connective tissue disease.
is_a: HP:0020359 ! Anti-nucleosome antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:10:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033559
name: Anti-myeloperoxidase antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the blood circulation that react against myeloperoxidase." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:30767872]
comment: MPO-ANCA are host-derived autoantibodies against shielded neutrophilic antigens. These antibodies react against primary granules present in neutrophils and monocytes. The formation of these antibodies has been hypothesized to be a two-step process. The first step involves exposure of neutrophils to inflammatory cytokines leading to surface exposure of cryptogenic antigens like myeloperoxidase or MPO. Next, predisposing genetic, environmental, and other factors result in the production of MPO-ANCA. In the second step, these MPO-ANCA cause damage to the host vasculature by reacting and crosslinking neutrophils to the endothelial receptors.
synonym: "Anti-MPO antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Anti-myeloperoxidase specific antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibody" EXACT []
synonym: "MPO-ANCA" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0032229 ! Perinuclear antineutrophil antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:16:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033560
name: Anti-PM-Scl antibody positivity
def: "Anti-PM-Scl antibodies target components of RNA-processing exosome complex in the nucleolus. There are ten proteins in this complex and antibodies to eight of them are found at varying frequencies; PM/Scl-100, PM/Scl-75, hRrp4, hRrp42, hRrp46, hCs14, hRrp41, and hRrp40." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:17643929]
comment: Anti-PM-Scl antibodies are found in up to 50% of polymyositis/systemic sclerosis (PM/SSc) overlap syndrome. Around 80% of individuals with antibodies present in their blood serum will have the disorder. The presence of the antibodies is linked to limited cutaneous involvement of PM/SSc overlap syndrome.
synonym: "Anti-PM/Scl antibody positivity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003493 ! Antinuclear antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:21:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033561
name: Anti-bactericidal/permeability-increasing protein antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the blood circulation that react against bactericidal/permeability-increasing protein (BPI). BPI is an endotoxin-binding host protein with important antibacterial effects against Gram-negative bacteria, such as Pseudomonas aeruginosa. BPI is a 55 kDalton protein that is most abundant in the azurophilic granules of neutrophils. BPI also acts as a target antigen for antineutrophil cytoplasmic autoantibodies." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:31508255]
synonym: "Anti-BPI antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0032230 ! Cytoplasmic antineutrophil antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:25:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033562
name: Anti-glycoprotein-210 antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the serum that react against glycoprotein-210." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:23814122]
comment: Anti-glycoprotein-210 antibody is an antibody directed against components of the nuclear membrane and is found in primary biliary cirrhosis.
synonym: "Anti-gp210 antibody positivity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:35:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033563
name: Anti-tissue transglutaminase antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the serum that react against tissue transglutaminase." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:33259121]
synonym: "Anti-tTG antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:45:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033564
name: Stasis dermatitis
def: "Stasis dermatitis commonly occurs in older age. It is caused by venous hypertension resulting from retrograde flow due to incompetent venous valves, valve destruction, or obstruction of the venous system. Further tissue changes arise from an inflammatory process mediated by metalloproteinases, which are up-regulated by ferric ion from extravasated red blood cells. Stasis dermatitis presents initially as poorly demarcated erythematous plaques of the lower legs bilaterally, classically involving the medial malleolus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:28063094]
synonym: "Varicose eczema" EXACT []
synonym: "Venous eczema" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000964 ! Eczematoid dermatitis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T12:54:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033565
name: Anti-epidermal transglutaminase antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that react against epidermal transglutaminase." [PMID:18503599]
synonym: "Anti-epidermal transglutaminase (anti-eTG) antibody" EXACT []
synonym: "Anti-eTG antibody positivity" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Anti-keratinocyte transglutaminase" EXACT []
synonym: "Anti-TG3 antibody" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033563 ! Anti-tissue transglutaminase antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-23T13:00:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033566
name: Abnormal ventricular axis
def: "Any deviation from the normal direction of the ventricular axis. The left ventricle makes up most of the heart muscle under normal circumstances and therefore generates the most electrical force visible on the EKG. The normal ventricular axis is directed downward and slightly towards the left. The ventricular axis can be determined by analyzing the QRS complex, which represents ventricular depolarization." [PMID:29262101]
comment: The normal adult QRS axis is between -30 degrees and +90 degrees, which is directed downward and to the left.
synonym: "Abnormal QRS axis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-24T13:37:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033567
name: Right axis deviation
def: "A kind of abnormal ventricular axis in the EKG whereby the QRS axis falls between +90 degrees and 180 degrees, or beyond +100 degrees if the adult range is used." [PMID:29262101]
synonym: "Electrical right axis deviation" EXACT []
synonym: "RAD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0033566 ! Abnormal ventricular axis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-24T13:39:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033568
name: Left axis deviation
def: "A kind of abnormal ventricular axis in the EKG whereby the QRS axis falls between -30 degrees and -90 degrees." [PMID:29262101]
synonym: "Electrical left axis deviation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033566 ! Abnormal ventricular axis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-24T13:42:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033569
name: Extreme axis deviation
def: "A kind of abnormal ventricular axis in the EKG whereby the QRS axis fall sbetween -90 degrees and 180 degrees. In this case, the ventricular vector is directed upward and to the right." [PMID:29262101]
is_a: HP:0033566 ! Abnormal ventricular axis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-24T13:43:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033570
name: Indeterminate ventricular axis
def: "A kind of abnormal ventricular axis in the EKG whereby the QRS complex is isoelectric or equiphasic in all leads with no dominant QRS deflection." [PMID:29262101]
is_a: HP:0033566 ! Abnormal ventricular axis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-24T13:44:44Z" xsd:dateTime

