[Term]
id: HP:0033597
name: Decreased mucosal sucrase-isomaltase activity
def: "Reduced activity of the linked disaccharidase, sucrase-isomaltase, which is a glycoprotein localized to the brush border membrane of small intestinal villi." [PMID:16329100]
comment: Sucrase-isomaltase has two subunits, sucrase and isomaltase. Isomaltase cleaves branched (1-6 linked) alpha-limit dextrins, while sucrase digests sucrose, maltose, short 1-4 linked glucose oligomers, and some branched starches into sugar monomers for intestinal absorption. Deficiency of this enzyme can lead to osmotic diarrhea, mild steatorrhea, chronic diarrhea, irritability, and vomiting after consuming sucrose.
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T13:48:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033598
name: Fibrillar glomerular subepithelial deposits
def: "Fibrillar deposits located between the outer (epithelial) aspect of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) and the visceral epithelial cell, with varying degrees of incorporation into the GBM. This feature is associated with a prominent GBM reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033603 ! Glomerular subepithelial deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:16:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033599
name: Glomerular amyloid subepithelial deposits
def: "A type of fibrillar glomerular subepithelial deposit characterized by extracellular aggregates composed of fine, randomly oriented, non-branching fibrils 8-12 nm in diameter, often forming a cottony mass. This feature is associated with a prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:25852856]
is_a: HP:0033598 ! Fibrillar glomerular subepithelial deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:44:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033600
name: Fibrillary glomerular subepithelial deposits
def: "A type of fibrillar glomerular subepithelial deposit characterized by extracellular aggregates of randomly arranged, straight, non-branching fibrils that are thicker than amyloid fibrils (average diameter about 20 nm) and are often admixed with smudgy, electron-dense material. This feature is associated with a prominent glomerular basement membrane (GBM) reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033598 ! Fibrillar glomerular subepithelial deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:47:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033601
name: Glomerular subepithelial immune-complex deposits
def: "A type of glomerular subepithelial deposit characterized by finely granular material deposited between the outer (epithelial) aspect of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) and the visceral epithelial cell, with varying degrees of incorporation into the GBM and corresponding to immunoglobulin and/or complement by immunofluorescence/immunohistochemistry. This feature is associated with a prominent GBM reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X, PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0033603 ! Glomerular subepithelial deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:51:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033602
name: Glomerular hyaline subepithelial deposits
def: "A type of glomerular subepithelial deposit characterized by a moderately electron-dense, generally homogenous, amorphous-appearing extracellular material located between the outer (epithelial) aspect of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) and the visceral epithelial cell, with varying degrees of incorporation into the GBM. This feature is associated with a prominent GBM reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
is_a: HP:0033603 ! Glomerular subepithelial deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:54:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033603
name: Glomerular subepithelial deposits
def: "Deposits located between the outer (epithelial) aspect of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) and the visceral epithelial cell, with varying degrees of incorporation into the GBM. This feature may be associated with a prominent GBM reflecting an diffuse and relatively uniform increase in thickness (subjective estimate)." [PMID:30085237]
is_a: HP:0030949 ! Glomerular deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T14:55:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033604
name: Glomerular capillary wire loop deposits
def: "Glomerulus showing markedly and irregularly thickened capillary walls with massive fuchsinophilic subendothelial deposits, resulting in narrowing of capillary lumina. This feature is said to resemble a wire loop." [PMID:32866505]
is_a: HP:0030949 ! Glomerular deposits
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T16:24:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033605
name: Pustular rash
def: "A rash composed of pustular lesions. A pustule is defined as a vesicle or bulla containing purulent material. It varies in size and may occur at different levels within the epidermis: subcorneal, intraepidermal, or basement membrane zones. The pustules may or may not be sterile and are normally filled with neutrophils." [PMID:25805031]
synonym: "Pustulosis" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0000988 ! Skin rash
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T16:59:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033606
name: Bone marrow maturation arrest
def: "Interruption of the procecss of diffferentiation of hematopoietic cells in the bone marrow, manifested by an increased proportion of immature cells in the bone marrow." []
synonym: "Haematopoietic maturation arrest" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Hematopoietic maturation arrest" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0005561 ! Abnormal bone marrow cell morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T21:26:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033607
name: Bone marrow arrest at the promyelocytic stage
def: "A type of bone marrow maturation arrest characterized by accumulation of neutrophil precursor cells in the bone marrow." [PMID:26456767]
is_a: HP:0033606 ! Bone marrow maturation arrest
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T21:32:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033608
name: Pulmonary nodule
def: "Focal rounded or ovoid opacity, not more than 3 cm in diameter. Pulmonary nodules are typically observed by chest radiography or computer tomography imaging." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:26977460]
synonym: "Spot on the lung" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0031983 ! Abnormal pulmonary thoracic imaging finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:05:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033609
name: Solid pulmonary nodule
def: "A type of pulmonary nodule whose density obscures the underlying parenchyma and thus has a \"solid\" appearance." [PMID:29143191]
is_a: HP:0033608 ! Pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:14:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033610
name: Subsolid pulmonary nodule
def: "Pulmonary subsolid nodules (SSNs) refer to pulmonary nodules with pure ground-glass nodules and part-solid ground-glass nodules. A ground-glass nodule (GGN) is the morphologic description of a pulmonary nodule category on thin-section chest computed tomography (CT). During the past decade, the natural history, management strategy and long-term prognosis in the case of GGNs have attracted attention." [PMID:24100062]
is_a: HP:0033608 ! Pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:17:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033611
name: Part-solid pulmonary nodule
def: "Part-solid pulmonary nodules are nodules that present with both ground-glass and solid components in which the underlying lung architecture cannot be visualized." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:24100062]
is_a: HP:0033610 ! Subsolid pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:22:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033612
name: Pure ground-glass pulmonary nodule
def: "Pure ground-glass pulmonary nodules (GGNs) are defined as focal nodular areas of increased lung attenuation through which lung parenchymal structures, such as the pulmonary vessels or bronchial structures, can be observed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:24100062]
is_a: HP:0033610 ! Subsolid pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:26:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033613
name: Perifissural pulmonary nodule
def: "Solid, homogenous nodules characterized by a smooth margin and oval, rounded, lentiform or triangular shape. They are typically located within 15 mm from the issue or the pleura. Perifissural nodules may be further differentiated into typical (have contact with interlobar septum) and atypical (do not have contact with interlobar septum). They likely represent intrapulmonary lymphnodes." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:20177105]
is_a: HP:0033608 ! Pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:28:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033614
name: Tracheal bronchus
def: "Aberrant or accessory bronchus supplying the upper lobe originating from the lateral wall of the trachea. The tracheal bronchus is more commonly right-sided, has a variable length and may be blind-ended. Two common types of tracheal bronchus are: supernumerary and displaced." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:11158647, PMID:19332762]
is_a: HP:0025426 ! Abnormal bronchus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:30:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033615
name: Displaced tracheal bronchus
def: "Accessory bronchus originating from trachea replacing one of the segmental branches of the anatomically normal upper lobe bronchus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:11158647, PMID:19332762]
is_a: HP:0033614 ! Tracheal bronchus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:31:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033616
name: Accessory cardiac bronchus
def: "Accessory bronchus originating from the medial wall of the right or left ban bronchus or bronchus intermedius. A cardiac bronchus is usually blind-ended." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:11158647]
is_a: HP:0025426 ! Abnormal bronchus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:33:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033617
name: Supernumerary tracheal bronchus
def: "Accessory bronchus which exits the trachea in addition to an anatomically normal branching upper lobe bronchus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:11158647, PMID:19332762]
is_a: HP:0033614 ! Tracheal bronchus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:34:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033618
name: Displaced lobar tracheal bronchus
def: "Accessory entire right upper lobe bronchial system originating from the trachea with absent anatomically normal upper lobe bronchus." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:11158647, PMID:19332762]
synonym: "Bronchus suis" EXACT []
synonym: "Pig bronchus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033614 ! Tracheal bronchus
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:35:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033619
name: Typical perifissural nodule
def: "A perifissural nodule that has contact with the interlobar septum (and is therefore considered typical)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489]
is_a: HP:0033613 ! Perifissural pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:37:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033620
name: Atypical perifissural nodule
def: "A perifissural nodule that does not have contact with the interlobar septum (and is therefore considered atypical)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489]
is_a: HP:0033613 ! Perifissural pulmonary nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:39:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033621
name: Bronchial diverticula
def: "Bronchial diverticula are blind-ended outpouchings arising from the bronchial tree. They are commonly pulsion diverticula acquired related to chronic cough. Subcarinal air cyst is thought to represent a small main bronchial diverticulum." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:18544671, PMID:27867581]
is_a: HP:0025426 ! Abnormal bronchus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T22:43:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033622
name: Migratory erythematous plaque
def: "A migratory, centrifugal, erythematous, tender, non-purpuric, and well-demarcated plaque. This feature may be observed in TNF receptor-associated periodic syndrome, in which it often occurs together with migratory myalgia in muscles located underneath the affected areas of skin." [PMID:31736939]
is_a: HP:0010783 ! Erythema
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:00:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033623
name: Birth history
def: "Information about the delivery and health status at birth typically elicited as a part of the past medical history." []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:06:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033624
name: History of congenital CMV infection
def: "A congenital cytomegalovirus (CMV) infection of the newborn can follow either a primary or recurrent maternal infection. Jaundice, petechiae, and hepatosplenomegaly are the most frequently noted clinical triad in symptomatic infants. Affected infants may develop permanent disabilities such as hearing loss, vision loss, motor and cognitive deficits." [PMID:29503048]
synonym: "History of congenital cytomegalovirus infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033623 ! Birth history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:08:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033625
name: Emotional insecurity
def: "A feeling of general unease or nervousness that may be triggered by a sense of vulnerability or instability, which is perceived as threatening." []
comment: It is difficult to give a precise definition of emotional insecurity, but it has been defined as deficits in emotional reactivity (inability to develop an attitude of resistance or vigilance in the presence of potentially threatening situations), behavior regulation (inappropriate behavioral response to threatening situations characterized by either overinvolvement in the situation or by the avoidance of it), and inappropriate internal representations (exaggerated conscious or unconscious schemas of potential danger).
is_a: HP:0020007 ! Abnormal affect regulation
is_a: HP:0031466 ! Impairment in personality functioning
is_a: HP:5200230 ! Maladaptive fear-related cognitions
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1111-7357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7954-5235
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2897-0458
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4298-5074
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4618-6544
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:12:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033626
name: Increased non-HDL cholesterol concentration
def: "Increase above normal levels of non-HDL cholesterol in the blood. Non-HDL cholesterol is total cholesterol minus high-density lipoprotein HDL-cholesterol (high-density lipoprotein-cholesterol)." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:RGD_gthayman, PMID:1596847]
synonym: "Elevated non-HDL cholesterol concentration" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003107 ! Abnormal circulating cholesterol concentration
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:17:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033627
name: Increased urine harderoporphyrin level
def: "Concentration of harderoporphyrin in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:31085196]
is_a: HP:0010473 ! Porphyrinuria
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:27:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033628
name: Bowel irritability
def: "Intermittent abdominal pain with diarrhea and/or constipation." [OMIM:ahamosh]
is_a: HP:0011458 ! Abdominal symptom
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-30T23:29:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033629
name: IgG4 autoimmune antibody positivity
def: "The presence of an antibody of subclass IgG4 in the blood circulation that is directed against the organism's own cells or tissues." [PMID:29483905]
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-31T18:32:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033630
name: Brain fog
def: "Brain fog is a type of transient cognitive dysfunction that comprises a constellation of symptoms that impair intellectual functioning to a level that interferes with daily activities, commonly including forgetfulness, mental slowness, difficulty thinking or focusing, a perceived slowing of mental processing speed, inability to find the right words, a sensation that the mind went blank or is \"cloudy\". Brain fog tends to recur and may be triggered by factors such as physical fatigue, lack of sleep, and prolonged standing or may appear to occur spontaneously." [PMID:23999934, PMID:30452327, PMID:32857796, PMID:32984564, PMID:33199820]
comment: Brain fog has been reported in a range of diseases including myalgic encephalomyelitis/chronic fatigue syndrome, non-celiac gluten disease, postural tachycardia syndrome, lupus, and COVID-19.
synonym: "Mental clouding" EXACT []
synonym: "Mental fatigue" EXACT []
synonym: "Mental fog" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100543 ! Cognitive impairment
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-01-31T18:36:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033631
name: Spondylitis
def: "Inflammation of the vertebrae (vertebral bodies) or spine." [PMID:22859929]
is_a: HP:0000925 ! Abnormality of the vertebral column
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T13:12:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033632
name: Abnormal alveolar volume
def: "Alveolar volume (VA) is a volume accessible during 10-second breath-hold, measured during a single breath maneuver. VA is calculated by knowing the fractional concentration of the tracer gas (eg helium) and the volume of the gas inhaled. VA = Vi*(Fi tracer/Fa tracer). In this equation, Vi = inspired volume of tracer gas, Fi tracer= inspired fraction of tracer gas, Fa tracer = alveolar (exhaled) fraction of tracer gas." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:25706496, PMID:28049168]
comment: Only a portion of each tidal volume (Vt) reaches the alveoli and participates in gas exchange. This is referred to as the alveolar volume (Va). The remainder, the so-called dead space volume (Vd), consists of gas that fills the upper and lower airways (anatomic dead space) or reaches nonperfused or relatively poorly perfused alveoli (alveolar dead space).
is_a: HP:0030878 ! Abnormality on pulmonary function testing
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T13:14:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033633
name: Decreased alveolar volume
def: "An abnormal reduction in alveolar volume." []
is_a: HP:0033632 ! Abnormal alveolar volume
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T13:16:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033634
name: Increased alveolar volume
def: "An abnormal elevation in alveolar volume." []
is_a: HP:0033632 ! Abnormal alveolar volume
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T13:19:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033635
name: Post-capillary pulmonary hypertension
def: "Post-capillary pulmonary hypertension is a hemodynamic condition characterized by elevated mean pulmonary artery pressure (mPAP greater than 20 mmHg) and pulmonary artery wedge pressure (PAWP greater than 15 mmHg) and pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR less than 3 Wood units)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:30545968]
comment: Post-capillary hypertension resulting from left heart disease causes backpressure and increases the hydrostatic pressure in the pulmonary veins which eventually results in increased pressure in pulmonary arteries.
synonym: "Postcapillary pulmonary hypertension" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004890 ! Elevated pulmonary artery pressure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T13:21:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033636
name: Combined pre- and post-capillary pulmonary hypertension
def: "Combined pre- and post-capillary pulmonary hypertension is a haemodynamic condition characterized by elevated mean pulmonary artery pressure (mPAP over 20 mmHg) and pulmonary artery wedge pressure (PAWP over 15 mmHg) and pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR at least 3 Wodd units)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:30545968]
is_a: HP:0004890 ! Elevated pulmonary artery pressure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-01T14:58:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033637
name: Anti-endomysial antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that react against endomysial tissue transglutaminase 2 (tTG2)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:9518950]
synonym: "Anti-transglutaminase 2 antibody positivity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033563 ! Anti-tissue transglutaminase antibody positivity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-03T13:26:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033638
name: Intralobular septal thickening
def: "Intralobular septal thickening is a computed tomography finding of increased width of the walls (septa) within a pulmonary lobule. Secondary pulmonary lobules represent a cluster of up to 30 acini 9 supplied by a common distal pulmonary artery and bronchiole. These clustered acini are bounded by interstitial fibrous septa (interlobular septa) which outline an irregular polyhedron of varying size between 1 and 2.5 cm. Interlobular septal thickening is seen on chest radiographs as thin linear opacities at right angles to and in contact with the lateral pleural surfaces near the lung bases. In contrast, intralobular septal thickening are visible as fine linear opacities in a lobule when the intralobular interstitial tissue is abnormally thickened. When numerous, they may appear as a fine reticular pattern." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:18195376, PMID:27852954]
comment: Intralobular lines may be seen in various conditions, including interstitial fibrosis and alveolar proteinosis.
synonym: "Intralobular lines" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033711 ! Pulmonary interstitial thickening
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-03T13:28:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033639
name: Septic pulmonary embolism
def: "Embolization of intravascular thrombus containing microorganisms into the pulmonary parenchyma via arterial system. Septic pulmonary embolism (PE) can be associated with multiple additional clinical manifestations such as fever, tachypnea, and hemoptysis. This HPO term refers to the finding of the septic embolus in the lung, which can be inferred from radiological findings. Typical radiographic features of septic PE include patchy air space lesions simulating non-specific bronchopneumonia; multiple ill defined round or wedge shaped densities of varying sizes from approximately 0.5 to 3.5 cm located peripherally; lesions abutting the pleura and located at the end of vessels (feeding vessel sign) seen on chest CT scans. Other pulmonary features suggesting septic PE include bilateral, occasional unilateral, rapid progression of cavities or abscess formations." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489, PMID:12244005]
synonym: "Septic pulmonary emboli" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033553 ! Septic embolism
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-03T13:30:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033640
name: Acetabular erosions
def: "Erosion (loss of substance) of the acetabular subchondral cortical bone. The acetabulum is the concave surface that meets with the head of the femur, forming the hip joint." [PMID:8793927]
is_a: HP:0003170 ! Abnormal acetabulum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-02-24T12:37:00Z" xsd:dateTime

