[Term]
id: HP:0033712
name: Repeated implantation failure
def: "Repeated implantation failure refers to a situation in which embryos of good quality fail to implant following several in vitro fertilization (IVF) treatment cycles." [PMID:22976427, PMID:25473625]
comment: Successful embryo implantation is a process which requires both a synchronous development and interaction between hatched blastocyst and endometrium. From the clinical point of view, implantation is considered to be successful when gestational sac is diagnosed by ultrasound.
synonym: "Recurrent implantation failure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033335 ! Abnormal preimplantation embryonic development
