[Term]
id: HP:0033766
name: Polymelia
def: "Polymelia is a congenital anomaly, which is defined as the presence of accessory limbs attached to various body regions and could be classified as cephalomelia (extra-limb attached to the head), notomelia (extra-limb attached to the back bone), thoracomelia (extra-limb attached to the thorax), and pyromelia (extra-limb attached to the pelvis)." [PMID:23814690]
is_a: HP:0040064 ! Abnormality of limbs
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-04-30T11:21:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033767
name: Abnormal single motor unit action potential
def: "Abnormally high or low single motor unit action potential reading (-Pk Amps)." [PMID:15961866]
is_a: HP:0003457 ! EMG abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-04-30T11:50:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033768
name: Penile thrush
def: "Overgrowth of candida albicans in the penis." [PMID:27659805]
synonym: "Penile candidiasis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000036 ! Abnormal penis morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-04-30T11:53:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033769
name: Fundic gland polyposis
def: "Multiple polyps in the acid-secreting mucosa of the gastric body and fundus. Fundic gland polyps (FGP) are usually 1 to 5 mm in size, though larger polyps have been found. FGPs are typically sessile, shiny, translucent, pale to pinkish in color (resembling the surrounding mucosa), and often exhibit tiny surface blood vessels. These polyps have characteristically been observed to chunk off or detach entirely at the base when removed with cold forceps, in contrast to other types of gastric polyps." [PMID:20567540]
synonym: "Fundic gland polyps" EXACT []
synonym: "Gastric polyposis" EXACT []
synonym: "Proximal polyposis of the stomach" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0006753 ! Neoplasm of the stomach
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-04-30T13:21:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033770
name: Gastric adenocarcinoma
def: "An adenocarcinoma arising from the stomach glandular epithelium. Gastric carcinoma often produces no specific symptoms when it is superficial and potentially surgically curable, although up to 50% of patients may have nonspecific gastrointestinal complaints such as dyspepsia." [NCIT:C4004, PMID:15621988, PMID:28569272]
comment: Ninety percent of all tumors of the stomach are malignant, and gastric adenocarcinoma comprises 95% of the total number of malignancies.
is_a: HP:0006753 ! Neoplasm of the stomach
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-04-30T14:02:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033771
name: Pleuritic chest pain
def: "Pleuritic chest pain is characterized by sudden and intense sharp, stabbing, or burning pain in the chest when inhaling and exhaling." [PMID:28925655]
is_a: HP:0100749 ! Chest pain
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-01T15:26:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033772
name: Abnormal RV/TLC ratio
def: "Any deviation from the normal ratio of residual volume (RV) to total lung capacity (TLC) on pulmonary function testing. RV is the amount of air remaining aftermaximal expiration and TLC is the total amount of air in theungs at full inspiration. These volumes cannot be determined by spirometry, but can be measured by inert gas dilution, nitrogen washout, and body plethysmography." [PMID:12934788]
is_a: HP:0030878 ! Abnormality on pulmonary function testing
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-01T15:42:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033773
name: Decreased RV/TLC ratio
def: "An abnormally low ratio of residual volume (RV) to total lung capacity (TLC) on pulmonary function testing. RV is the amount of air remaining after maximal expiration and TLC is the total amount of air in the lungs at full inspiration. These volumes cannot be determined by spirometry, but can be measured by inert gas dilution, nitrogen washout, and body plethysmography." [PMID:12934788]
is_a: HP:0033772 ! Abnormal RV/TLC ratio
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-01T15:44:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033774
name: Impaired renal tubular reabsorption of uric acid
def: "Decreased renal tubular reabsorption of uric acid." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2234-4248, PMID:27105641, PMID:31474092]
comment: Uric acid excretion rate is the product of the filtered load (which can be approximated as plasma ultrafilterable urate multiplied by the glomerular filtration rate) and fractional excretion of urate (FEUA), which represents the percentage of filtered urate that is excreted in the final urine.
is_a: HP:0011038 ! Abnormal renal tubular resorption
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-04T14:21:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033775
name: Pulmonary imaging sign
def: "An abnormal pulmonary imaging finding defined by eponym or reference to signs, symbols, or naturalistic images." [PMID:31802270]
is_a: HP:0031983 ! Abnormal pulmonary thoracic imaging finding
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-04T14:47:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033776
name: Enamel pearls
def: "Small nodules of enamel on the root of a tooth." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel pearls can typically not be seen on X-rays but need direct visualization. The pearls can be present on the surface of the dentine or cement of deciduous teeth, with a frequency of 33% or on the roots of maxillary molars, with a frequency of 1.2%.
is_a: HP:0000682 ! Abnormal dental enamel morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T09:49:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033777
name: Supernumerary cusp
def: "Additional cusps of a dental crown." [PMID:31468724]
comment: The crown is the part of the tooth that is visible in the oral cavity. Supernumerary cusps can occur on any tooth with cusps. Canines possess a single cusp, premolars two (bicuspid), and molars three to five cusps. Supernumerary cusps are frequently seen in patients with other dental anomalies. Prevalence varies by geographical region. A tubercle on the lingual surface of the maxillary first permanent molar is sometimes referred to as a Carabelli cusp. A supernumerary cusp on the lingual or palatal side of anterior teeth is called Talon cusp, and an additional cusp on the occlusal surface of a premolar is called Leung cusp.
synonym: "Additional cusp" EXACT []
synonym: "Extra cusp" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011063 ! Abnormal incisor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T09:52:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033778
name: Leung cusp
def: "An additional cusp located in the middle of the occlusal surface." [PMID:31468724]
comment: A Leung cusp is present on premolars only. In radiographs, a pulp extension may be seen inside the cusp.
is_a: HP:0033777 ! Supernumerary cusp
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T09:59:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033779
name: Barrel-shaped tooth
def: "A tooth crown with convex mesial and distal surfaces." [PMID:31468724]
comment: A barrel shape of a tooth occurs in incisors and canines only. The incisal edge is not pointed. Barrel-shaped teeth are frequently observed in association with hypodontia and oligodontia.
is_a: HP:0006482 ! Abnormal dental morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:08:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033780
name: Bulbous tooth
def: "A tooth crown with a marked cervical area constriction." [PMID:31468724]
is_a: HP:0006482 ! Abnormal dental morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:09:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033781
name: Tapered tooth
def: "A tooth with a crown that narrows from proximal toward the incisal edge. Tapering of teeth typically involves incisors." [PMID:31468724]
is_a: HP:0011063 ! Abnormal incisor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:14:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033782
name: Semilunar tooth
def: "An incisor with a half-moon shape incisal edge." []
comment: If a notch occupies most of incisal edge, it has been indicated as semilunar teeth or crescent-shaped.
synonym: "Crescent-shape tooth" EXACT []
synonym: "Hutchinson incisor" EXACT []
synonym: "Semicircular tooth" EXACT []
synonym: "Tooth, semilunar" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011063 ! Abnormal incisor morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:21:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033783
name: Molar incisor malformation
def: "Molar incisor malfomation (MIM) is composed of normal crown with marked cervical constriction, thin, narrow short roots which is a combination of signs that occurs in deciduous and permanent molars." [PMID:31468724]
comment: MIM affects one or more roots of deciduous second molars and permanent first molars. Permanent maxillary central incisors may also be affected. The diagnosis requires clinical and radiographic examinations.
is_a: HP:0011070 ! Abnormal molar morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:32:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033784
name: Dentin dysplasia
def: "This is a bundled term as dentin dysplasia is composed of short roots with pointed ends and taurodontism and intrapulpal calcifications." [PMID:31468724]
comment: This term designates a genetic condition, and an Element of Morphology rending its utilization sometimes confusing. The condition is characterized by multiple dental anomalies that affect both deciduous and permanent dentitions. It can exist in isolation or be associated with other signs and symptoms of various syndromes.
is_a: HP:0010299 ! Abnormal dentin morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:38:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033785
name: Enamel agenesis
def: "Complete or almost complete absence of enamel." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel agenesis can indicate a total absence of enamel or the presence of a very thin enamel layer that is difficult to visualize during clinical examination. It may need microscopic studies to determine whether any enamel is still present. It can be present isolated and as part of rare syndromic entities.
is_a: HP:0000682 ! Abnormal dental enamel morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T10:59:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033786
name: Hypomature enamel
def: "Enamel with a white or brown discoloration without hypoplasia." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Enamel maturation is a process through which enamel matrix proteins are removed to allow full growth of the enamel hydroxyapatite crystals. Hypomature enamel can be caused by genetic or environmental factors. It may occur in both deciduous and permanent dentitions, although more often in the permanent dentition. Hypomature enamel may concern a single tooth, several teeth, or the complete dentition and may affect part or the complete surface of the tooth. The enamel is usually hard, colored but not translucid. It is a qualitative defect of enamel.
synonym: "Enamel opacity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000682 ! Abnormal dental enamel morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:02:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033787
name: Cementum hypoplasia
def: "The decrease or absence of cementum. The cementum anchors the periodontal ligament attachment fiber between the tooth root and the alveolar bone. Its absence leads to early loss of teeth." [PMID:31468724]
synonym: "Cementum aplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100717 ! Abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:07:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033788
name: Cementum overgrowth
def: "Excess of cementum on the tooth root surface." [PMID:31468724]
comment: The excessive buildup of normal cementum (calcified tissue) on the roots of one or more teeth is an idiopathic, non-neoplastic condition. Cementum overgrowth may be either hyperplasia or hypertrophy of the cement; these terms can only be used if histological evidence of hypertrophy or hyperplasia have been established.
synonym: "Cementation hyperplasia" EXACT []
synonym: "Cementum hypertrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Cementum overdeveloped" EXACT []
synonym: "Drumstick-shaped root" EXACT []
synonym: "Hypercementosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100717 ! Abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:08:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033789
name: Triggered by cheese ingestion
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by eating cheese." [PMID:9398858]
comment: Cheese contains tyramine, which is thought to be responsible for tachycardia and hypertension that can be tirggered by eating cheese in persons with Trimethylaminuria.
is_a: HP:0033793 ! Triggered by food ingestion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:11:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033790
name: Thistle tube shaped pulp
def: "A thistle tube shape of the pulp chamber, meaning an enlarged coronal pulp chamber with narrow pulp canals giving a radiographic appearance of the shape of a thistle tube or a flame. It may occur isolated or associated with other dental anomalies and rare diseases such as dentinogenesis imperfecta, which should be assessed and coded separately. The diagnosis thistle tube shape pulp requires clinical and radiographic examinations." [PMID:31468724]
synonym: "Flame-shaped pulp" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0006479 ! Abnormal dental pulp morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:14:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033791
name: Tooth ankylosis
def: "Fusion of a tooth with alveolar bone." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Ankylosis is uncommon in the deciduous dentition and very rare in the permanent dentition. It may be observed after trauma. Ankylosis may occur at the crown or root level.
is_a: HP:0006482 ! Abnormal dental morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:24:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033792
name: Cross bite
def: "Lingual occlusion of buccal cusps and/or incisal edge of maxillary teeth to the buccal cusps and/or incisal edge of mandibular teeth." [PMID:31468724]
comment: Cross bite may occur unilaterally, bilaterally, or frontally. A total cross bite with buccal displacement of the maxillary posterior teeth, with or without contact between the lingual surface of the maxillary lingual cusp and the buccal surface of the buccal cusp of its mandibular antagonist, has been called scissor bite. If only a single tooth is affected, the term single cross bite can be used.
is_a: HP:0000692 ! Tooth malposition
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T11:30:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033793
name: Triggered by food ingestion
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by eating a certain food." []
is_a: HP:0025204 ! Triggered by
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-07T17:28:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033794
name: Acral overgrowth
def: "Excessive growth of hands and feet (predominantly due to soft tissue swelling). Typical manifestations include shoe size increase, foot enlargement, glove tightness, and hand enlargement." [PMID:27477558, PMID:27812777, PMID:30853479]
comment: This term should be used to encode the overgrowth of hands and feet that can be seen in acromegaly, a rare disorder caused by excessive growth hormone production, most commonly from an adenoma of the anterior pituitary gland. The resulting production of insulin-like growth factor 1 causes the characteristic overgrowth of certain tissues resulting in coarsening of facial features, enlarging hands and feet, as well as effects on multiple systems throughout the body. The Figure in PMID:30853479 illustrates large hands with stubby fingers characteristic of acromegaly.
synonym: "Acral enlargement" EXACT []
synonym: "Acral hypertrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Acromegalic growth" EXACT []
synonym: "Acromegaly" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0001507 ! Growth abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-08T12:21:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033795
name: Growth without growth hormone
comment: Growth hormone (GH) is essential for normal growth. However, cases of normal growth without GH may occur. The mechanism of growth without GH remains still unclear. However, regarding normal growth without GH arising after brain surgery, hypothalamic damage caused by the brain surgery is thought to induce obesity, and the resulting hyperinsulinemia and/or hyperprolactinemia are assumed to be important mechanisms of normal growth without GH in postsurgery patients. It is assumed that elevated insulin and/or prolactin concentration normalize IGF-1 levels even in GHD patients, restricts the increase in serum levels of IGFBP-3, and changes the distribution of circulating IGF-1. Thus, normal growth without GH continues because of the effects of IFG-I, which are independent of GH. {xref="PMID:28443260"}
is_a: HP:0001507 ! Growth abnormality
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-05-09T11:28:27Z" xsd:dateTime

