[Term]
id: HP:0033838
name: Dysphoria
def: "A pervasive state of negatively valenced emotional unease and dissatisfaction along with an inner discomfort that is disproportionate to external circumstances and may include heightened emotional reactivity. It is associated with a mixture of overlapping negative emotions that are difficult to disentangle." [PMID:10867572, PMID:30439852]
comment: Dysphoria has a mixed and unstable nonspecific quality and is a complex negative emotional state with multiple vague symptoms. Recent literature uses include gender dysphoria, but prior use was interchangeable with depression. The central features are dissatisfaction and resentment with a pronounced negative emotional experience.
synonym: "Emotional discomfort" BROAD layperson []
synonym: "Emotional discontent" BROAD []
synonym: "Emotional discord" BROAD []
synonym: "Emotional unrest" RELATED []
synonym: "Emotionally unsettled" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Feeling off inside" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Ill at ease" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Psychological unease" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0031467 ! Dysregulated negative emotional state
