[Term]
id: HP:0033958
name: Cortical radial artery foam cell hypercellularity
def: "A type of cortical radial artery endoarterial leukocyte hypercellularity due to the presence of lipid-filled cells, often macrophages, with a vacuolated appearance in the lumen of cortical radial artery (also known as the interlobular artery) of the kidney." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
synonym: "Endocapillary hypercellularity within interlobular arterial endothelium consisting of foam cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033955 ! Cortical radial artery leukocyte hypercellularity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-06-24T12:31:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033959
name: Cortical radial artery intima/media arteriosclerosis
def: "Thickening of the intima of the cortical radial artery (also known as the interlobular artery) of the kidney characterized by fibrosis and/or duplication of the elastic lamina." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
