[Term]
id: HP:0033960
name: Cortical radial artery intimal mucoid edema
def: "Accumulation of edematous extracellular matrix in the intima of the cortical radial artery (also known as the interlobular artery) of the kidney. This material resembles mucus and stains pale blue on hematoxylin and eosin staining." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2356-950X]
synonym: "Intimal mucoid edema within interlobular arterial intima/media" EXACT []
