[Term]
id: HP:0033987
name: Phosphaturic mesenchymal tumor
def: "A rare, endocrine active tumor that causes severe renal phosphate wasting, which in turn can lead to critical osteomalacia. Phosphaturic mesenchymal tumors (PMTs) are typically small and mostly benign tumors producing fibroblast growth factor 23 (FGF-23). FGF-23 lowers the expression of sodium/phosphate cotransporters, which are the primary transport proteins responsible for phosphate reabsorption in the kidneys. The paraneoplastic overproduction of FGF-23 lowers reabsorption of phosphate and causes severe paraneoplastic renal phosphate wasting and hypophosphatemia. FGF-23 also affects vitamin D levels by lowering 25-hydroxyvitamin D 1-alpha-hydroxylase in the proximal renal tubules and by increasing the expression of vitamin D 24-hydroxylase, a mitochondrial enzyme responsible for inactivating vitamin D metabolites." [PMID:33442358]
is_a: HP:0031459 ! Soft tissue neoplasm
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-07-15T12:04:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033988
name: Amygdala microinfarct
def: "An infarct located in the almond-shaped body of basal nuclei anterior to the inferior horn of the lateral ventricle of the brain, within the temporal lobe that can only be observed microscopically." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2307-1226, PMID:10867785]
is_a: HP:0033668 ! Abnormal amygdala morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-18T12:10:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033989
name: Hippocampal microinfarct
def: "An infarct located in the structure of the cerebrum involved with memory storage and spatial navigation that can only be observed microscopically." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2307-1226, PMID:10867785]
is_a: HP:0025100 ! Abnormal hippocampus morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-18T12:19:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033990
name: Cartilaginous tracheobronchomalacia
def: "Softening of the tracheal and/or bronchial cartilage resulting in segmental tracheal and/or bronchial weakness." []
comment: This term is to be distinguihsed from its sibling Excessive dynamic airway collapse, which refers to excessive anterior displacement of the membranous wall of the trachea.
synonym: "Cartilaginous malacia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002786 ! Tracheobronchomalacia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-18T12:24:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033991
name: Vasa previa
def: "Vasa previa occurs when the membranes that contain the umbilical cord traverse the membranes overlying the internal os of the cervix. There is a high risk of fetal mortality if not identified perinatally." [PMID:32028503, PMID:33880195]
comment: This abnormality is problematic because of the location of the unprotected vessels. If the fetal head compresses these vessels, it can result in fetal hypoperfusion and acidemia. If the vessels rupture it can lead to fetal hemorrhage.
is_a: HP:0011418 ! Abnormal insertion of umbilical cord
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-18T12:29:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033992
name: Chronotropic incompetence
def: "Inability of the heart to increase its rate commensurate with increased activity or demand." [PMID:21382903]
comment: Chronotropic incompetence is common in patients with cardiovascular disease, produces exercise intolerance that impairs quality of life, and is an independent predictor of major adverse cardiovascular events and overall mortality.
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-20T13:16:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033993
name: Viral encephalitis
def: "An inflammation of brain parenchyma due to infection with a virus. Viral encephalitis can occur as a rare complication of common infections (eg, herpes virus infections) or can occur as a characteristic presentation of rare viruses (eg, rabies virus infection). Encephalitis may be the only neurologic manifestation of infection, or may occur in association with meningitis, myelitis, radiculitis, or neuritis. Viral encephalitis is associated with neurological dysfunction." [PMID:21960712, PMID:30366550]
comment: Severe viral infections including viral encephalitis may occur in individuals with underlying mmunodeficiencies.
is_a: HP:0002383 ! Infectious encephalitis
is_a: HP:0032169 ! Severe infection
is_a: HP:0034317 ! Unusual viral infection
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2021-08-21T11:43:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0033994
