[Term]
id: HP:0034159
name: Pagetic bone lesion
def: "Paget's disease of bone (PDB) is a chronic progressive metabolic bone disease characterized by abnormal activation of osteoclasts that results in abnormal bone resorption and compensatory osteogenic sclerosis. DB can affect one (monostotic form) or more (polyostotic form) regions of the skeleton, with multiple constitutive symptoms, including bone pain, bone deformity, pathological fracture, tinnitus, hearing loss, vision loss, and osteoarthritis." [PMID:33599011]
comment: Paget disease is a feature of several Mendelian diseases including Paget disease of bone 3 (OMIM:167250).
synonym: "Osteitis deformans" EXACT []
synonym: "Paget bone lesion" EXACT []
synonym: "Paget disease of bone" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003330 ! Abnormal bone structure
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-02-19T11:36:51Z" xsd:dateTime

