[Term]
id: HP:0034190
name: Abnormal fetal cardiovascular physiology
def: "Abnormal functionality of the fetal cardiovascular system." []
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology
is_a: HP:0034059 ! Abnormal fetal physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-03-12T23:26:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034191
name: Elevated fetal middle cerebral artery peak systolic velocity
def: "Increased peak systolic velocity of the fetal middle cerebral artery (MCA) as evaluated by Doppler ultrasound." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8593-2186, PMID:28191060]
comment: The technique for MCA peak systolic velocity measurement involves an axial section through the fetal head that includes the thalami and cavum septum pellucidum is obtained and the circle of Willis visualized with color or power Doppler. The MCA is examined close to its origin from the internal carotid artery. The sample volume should be placed in the center of the vessel and the angle between the ultrasound beam and the direction of blood flow kept as close to 0 degrees as possible. Angle correction can be used if required. The highest peak systolic waveform is measured, in the absence of fetal breathing movements. An elevated MCA Doppler measurement indicates that the fetus is likely to be anemic, but this measurement is not perfectly sensitive or specific.
is_a: HP:0034190 ! Abnormal fetal cardiovascular physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-03-12T23:26:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034192
name: Pulmonary thromboembolism
def: "Pulmonary embolism is caused by emboli, which have originated from venous thrombi, traveling to and occluding the arteries of the lung." [PMID:29770793]
comment: Pulmonary embolism (PE) is the most dangerous form of venous thromboembolism, and undiagnosed or untreated PE can be fatal. Acute PE is associated with right ventricular dysfunction, which can lead to arrhythmia, haemodynamic collapse and shock. Furthermore, individuals who survive PE can develop post-PE syndrome, which is characterized by chronic thrombotic remains in the pulmonary arteries, persistent right ventricular dysfunction, decreased quality of life and/or chronic functional limitations.
is_a: HP:0001907 ! Thromboembolism
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-03-16T14:05:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034193
name: Stratum basale cleavage
def: "Cleavage within the epidermal keratinocytes, which is the innermost layer of the epidermis and consists of proliferating cells that give rise to the outer layers of the epidermis." []
comment: Cleavage in epidermolysis bullosa simplex occurs within the basal keratinocytes.
synonym: "Blistering with cleavage within basal keratinocytes" EXACT []
synonym: "Cleavage within the basal keratinocyte layer" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033802 ! Intra-epidermal blistering
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-03-16T14:18:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034194
name: Suprabasal cleavage
def: "Cleavage within the suprabasal cell layer of the epidermis, which lies directly above the basal layer and is composed of five to ten layers of cells." []
synonym: "Blistering with suprabasal clefting" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033802 ! Intra-epidermal blistering
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-03-16T14:20:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034195
name: Triggered by muscle relaxant
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by exposure to a muscle relaxant such as suxamethonium and mivacurium." []
is_a: HP:4000101 ! Triggered by exposure to medication
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-07T13:21:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034196
name: Ductus venosus agenesis
def: "A developmental defect characterized by lack of formation of the ductus venosus (a shunt that allows oxygenated blood in the umbilical vein to bypass the liver in the fetal circulation)." [PMID:10765517, PMID:21335936, PMID:24871613, PMID:24931552]
comment: The ductus venosus (DV) plays an essential role in the fetal circulation because it allows the oxygenated placental blood to bypass the liver and enables preferential flow via the right atrium and foramen ovale to the left atrium. Furthermore, normal umbilical flow via DV is involved in the normal development of the intrahepatic portal venous system. The lack of critical anastomoses between the portal and umbilical venous system and hepatic-systemic venous system results in agenesis of ductus venosus and shunting of umbilical blood through an aberrant vessel. Between 1 in 2532 to 1 in 556 fetuses are affected.
synonym: "Agenesis of the ductus venosus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010948 ! Abnormal fetal cardiovascular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-07T14:12:24Z" xsd:dateTime

