[Term]
id: HP:0034204
name: Decreased circulating C1-esterase inhibitor concentration
def: "Decreased concentration of C1-esterase inhibitor (C1INH) in the blood circulation." [PMID:30844193]
comment: C1-esterase inhibitor (C1INH) is an acute phase reactant and a serine protease inhibitor (serpin). Serpins inhibit the steps in the lectin complement pathway as well as kinin-producing pathways. While C1 inhibitor has many functions, its function in the kinin pathway leads to angioedema ctivated factor XII of the coagulation cascade and kallikrein catalyze the cleavage of kininogen, which produces bradykinin. C1 inhibitor usually limits this bradykinin production by inhibiting kallikrein and factor XIIa. Bradykinin is a potent vasodilator due to multifactorial downstream effects on the smooth muscle in blood vessels.
is_a: HP:0005339 ! Abnormality of complement system
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T10:49:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034205
name: Iniencephaly
def: "Iniencephaly is a rare neural tube defect involving dysmorphic spine and abnormal fusion of the portion of the occipital skull with the back. It results in extreme fixed head retroflexion." [PMID:33294089]
is_a: HP:0034237 ! Open neural tube defect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T10:56:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034206
name: Abnormal fetal central nervous system morphology
def: "An anomalous structural finding of the fetal central nervous system. Terms in this subhierarchy are restricted to findings that can only be observed in the prenatal period. Other HPO terms can also be used to describe fetal phenotypes." []
synonym: "Abnormal fetal CNS morphology" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Abnormal foetal CNS morphology" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T11:09:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034207
name: Abnormal fetal gastrointestinal system morphology
def: "An anomalous structural finding of the fetal gastrointestinal system. Terms in this subhierarchy are restricted to findings that can only be observed in the prenatal period. Other HPO terms can also be used to describe fetal phenotypes." []
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T11:11:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034208
name: Fetal intracranial hemorrhage
def: "Abnormal bleeding inside the skull (cranium) of a fetus." []
comment: Fetal intracranial hemorrhage occurs when a blood vessel within or adjacent to the brain ruptures or leaks, resulting in bleeding into the brain or surrounding area. Fetal intracranial hemorrhage can result in disruption of blood flow to the developing brain (ischemia). Addditionally, accumulation of blood can compress brain tissue.
is_a: HP:0002170 ! Intracranial hemorrhage
is_a: HP:0034206 ! Abnormal fetal central nervous system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T11:12:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034209
name: Fetal subependymal hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage located in the subependymal germinal matrix below the frontal horns of the lateral ventricles in the caudothalamic notch." []
comment: Subependymal hemorrhage originates from the germinal matrix and appears on sonography as echogenic material located below the frontal horns in the floor of the lateral ventricle within the caudothalamic notch. Acute hemorrhage appears sonographically as echogenic and homogeneous; the hemorrhage changes over time to a more complex appearance with an echogenic external lining and internal sonolucent center and then eventually becomes cystic in nature.
synonym: "Grade I fetal intracranial hemorrhage" EXACT []
synonym: "Grade I foetal intracranial haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034210 ! Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T11:31:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034210
name: Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage with bleeding into the ventricular system of the brain." [PMID:16082722, PMID:27734711]
comment: The evolution of the ultrasonographic pattern of intraventricular hemorrhage (IVH) is that fresh blood clots appear as homogeneously echogenic areas, separate from the choroid plexus. Over the course of several weeks some blood clots develop a complex appearance, with an external echogenic lining and an internal sonolucent core.
is_a: HP:0034208 ! Fetal intracranial hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T11:39:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034211
name: Fetal cerebral parenchymal hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage with bleeding into the parenchyma (tissue) of the brain." [PMID:16082722]
is_a: HP:0034208 ! Fetal intracranial hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:03:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034212
name: Fetal extra-axial hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage with bleeding that occurs within the skull but outside of the brain tissue itself (into the epidural, subdural, or arachnoid space)." []
is_a: HP:0034208 ! Fetal intracranial hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:07:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034213
name: Fetal posterior fossa hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage that occurs in the posterior cranial fossa, which is the part of the cranial cavity that is located between the foramen magnum and tentorium cerebelli and contains the brainstem and cerebellum." []
is_a: HP:0034208 ! Fetal intracranial hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:12:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034214
name: Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage without ventriculomegaly
def: "A type of fetal intraventricular hemorrhage characterized by clear hemorrhage spillover to the ventricles filling less than 50% of the lateral ventricle and without ventriculomegaly of greater than 15 mm in the transverse diameter of the lateral ventricular atrium." [PMID:16082722]
synonym: "Grade II fetal intracranial hemorrhage" EXACT []
synonym: "Grade II foetal intracranial haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034210 ! Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:15:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034215
name: Fetal cerebellar hemisphere hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage that occurs in the hemisphere of the cerebellum." [PMID:12795563, PMID:26426778]
is_a: HP:0034213 ! Fetal posterior fossa hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034216
name: Fetal cerebellar vermis hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intracranial hemorrhage that occurs in the vermis of the cerebellum." [PMID:26426778]
is_a: HP:0034213 ! Fetal posterior fossa hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:20:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034217
name: Sonographic non-visualized fetal bladder
def: "Inability to visualize the fetal bladder on targeted prenatal sonography examination. The fetal bladder can be visualized with sonography as a midline, fluid-filled structure in the pelvis as early as 10-12 weeks of gestation. The normal fetus voids at least once an hour but never completely empties the urinary bladder. The fetal bladdder should be consistently imaged after 13 weeks of gestation." [PMID:8915088]
is_a: HP:0034242 ! Abnormal fetal genitourinary system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:22:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034218
name: Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage with ventriculomegaly
def: "A type of fetal intraventricular hemorrhage (IVH) characterized by spillover to ventricles with flooding of 50% or more of one or both lateral ventricles accrued accompanying ventriculomegaly, but with no apparent brain parenchymal injury. This type of IVH may be defined as a diameter exceeding 15 mm in the transverse diameter of the lateral ventricular atrium as visualiuzed by prenatal sonography." []
synonym: "Grade III fetal intracranial hemorrhage" EXACT []
synonym: "Grade III foetal intracranial haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034210 ! Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:23:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034219
name: Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage with periventricular hemorrhage
def: "A type of fetal intraventricular hemorrhage that additionally includes hemorrhage in a large part of the periventricular parenchyma." [PMID:12905503]
synonym: "Grade IV fetal intracranial hemorrhage" EXACT []
synonym: "Grade IV foetal intracranial haemorrhage" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0034210 ! Fetal intraventricular hemorrhage
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T12:32:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034220
name: Temporal lobe megalencephaly
def: "Expansion of the temporal lobes of the brain along all axes, including rostrocaudal, superoinferior, and mediolateral, resulting in a globular appearance of the brain." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062, PMID:19098178]
is_a: HP:0001355 ! Megalencephaly
is_a: HP:0034221 ! Abnormal temporal lobe morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:08:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034221
name: Abnormal temporal lobe morphology
def: "An abnormal structural of the zone (lobe) of the cerebral cortex that is located inferior to the lateral fissure on other cerebral hemispheres." []
is_a: HP:0002538 ! Abnormal cerebral cortex morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:13:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034222
name: Temporal lobe dysplasia
def: "A developmental defect of the temporal lobe of the cerebral cortex that is characterized by prominent sulcations and radially directed gyrations." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062, PMID:24585534]
is_a: HP:0034221 ! Abnormal temporal lobe morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:16:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034223
name: Elevated umbilical artery pulsatility
def: "Human umbilical artery (UA) blood flow pulsatility measured by Doppler ultrasound is a widely used biomarker for the detection of elevated placental vascular resistance. Elevated UA pulsatility, which in the most extreme cases manifests as absent or even reversed end-diastolic velocity, is associated with intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR) and still-birth." [PMID:32746120]
synonym: "Elevated umbilical artery Dopplers" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased umbilical artery pulsatility index" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025715 ! Abnormal umbilical artery doppler waveform during pregnancy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:39:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034224
name: Absent end-diastolic umbilical artery flow
def: "An anomaly that is visualized by umbilical artery Doppler velocimetry. Flow in the umbilical artery should be in the forward direction in normal circumstances. This anomaly is characterized by an absence of flow in the umbilical artery at the end of diastole." []
comment: Abnormal umbilical artery Doppler velocimetry is correlated with a pathologic lesion of the placenta characterized by obliteration of arterioles in the tertiary stem villi; the umbilical artery flow velocity waveform is primarily determined by placental villous vascular architecture. The increased placental vascular resistance is reflected as a decreased diastolic phase of the umbilical artery waveform {xref="PMID:19797010"}
is_a: HP:0025715 ! Abnormal umbilical artery doppler waveform during pregnancy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:42:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034225
name: Reversed end-diastolic umbilical artery flow
def: "An anomaly that is visualized by umbilical artery Doppler velocimetry. Flow in the umbilical artery should be in the forward direction in normal circumstances. This anomaly is characterized by an reversal of flow in the umbilical artery at the end of diastole (i.e., backwards flow)." [PMID:19797010]
is_a: HP:0025715 ! Abnormal umbilical artery doppler waveform during pregnancy
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:46:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034226
name: Champagne cork sign
def: "Characteristic appearance of the chest and abdomen in the sagittal view on prenatal ultrasound when the chest is small and the abdomen protruding." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062, PMID:23408600, PMID:31173381]
comment: See Figure 4E of PMID:31173381 and Figure 1B of PMID:23408600.
is_a: HP:0025662 ! Abnormal fetal skeletal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T13:51:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034227
name: Aortic isthmus hypoplasia
def: "A type of aortic arch hypoplasia whereby the isthmus (arch between the left subclavian and insertion of the patent ductus arteriosus/ligamentum arteriosum) has a diameter of less than 40% of the diameter of the ascending aorta." [PMID:27860551]
is_a: HP:0012304 ! Hypoplastic aortic arch
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:00:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034228
name: Proximal aortic arch hypoplasia
def: "A type of aortic arch hypoplasia whereby the proximal aortic arch (arch proximal to the origin of the left subclavian artery) has a diameter of less than 60% of the diameter of the ascending aorta." [PMID:27860551]
is_a: HP:0012304 ! Hypoplastic aortic arch
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:03:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034229
name: Distal aortic arch hypoplasia
def: "A type of aortic arch hypoplasia whereby the distal aortic arch (arch distal to the ductus arteriosus) has a diameter of less than 60% of the diameter of the ascending aorta." []
is_a: HP:0012304 ! Hypoplastic aortic arch
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:04:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034230
name: Inferior crossed fused renal ectopia
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia characterized by fusion between the upper pole of the cross-fused ectopic kidney (located more inferiorly relative to the other kidney) and the lower pole of the other orthotopic kidney (located in a more superior position)." [PMID:29446682]
synonym: "Type A cross fused renal ectopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:14:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034231
name: Sigmoid kidney
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia where the normal side kidney is present superiorly and the direction of pelvic is medial, the kidney which crosses positioned inferiorly with direction of pelvic toward the lateral side. As kidneys fuse after complete rotation on the vertical axis, both renal pelves lie in correct orientation." [PMID:23599575, PMID:29446682]
comment: See Figure 2b of PMID:23599575.
synonym: "S-shaped kidney" EXACT []
synonym: "Type B cross fused renal ectopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:17:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034232
name: Unilateral lump kidney
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia where fusion occurs over a wide margin, both renal pelves anteriorly directed and placed more inferiorly." [PMID:29446682]
synonym: "Type C cross fused renal ectopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:23:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034233
name: Disc kidney
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia in which kidneys fuse along their medial borders." []
synonym: "Type D cross fused renal ectopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:26:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034234
name: L-shaped kidney
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia in which the crossed kidney lies inferiorly and transversely, fused with the lower pole of the normal kidney." [PMID:29446682]
synonym: "Tandem kidney" EXACT []
synonym: "Type E cross fused renal ectopia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:28:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034235
name: Superior crossed-fused renal ectopia
def: "A type of cross fused renal ectopia in which the ectopic kidney lies superiorly and its lower pole fuses with the upper pole of the normal kidney. The renal pelvis of both kidneys lies anteriorly." [PMID:29446682]
is_a: HP:0004736 ! Crossed fused renal ectopia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:29:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034236
name: Apnea of prematurity
def: "Recurrent episodes of apnea occurring in infants born less than 37 weeks of gestation, defined specifically as a pause of breathing for more than 15-20 s, or accompanied by oxygen desaturation (SpO2 not more than 80% for at least 4 s) and bradycardia (heart rate less than 2/3 of baseline for at least 4 s), in infants born less than 37 weeks of gestation." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157, PMID:21301866]
synonym: "AOP" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0002104 ! Apnea
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T14:32:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034237
name: Open neural tube defect
def: "A type of neural tube defect that is not covered by skin." [PMID:23456749]
is_a: HP:0045005 ! Neural tube defect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T17:29:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034238
name: Closed neural tube defect
def: "A type of neural tube defect that is covered by skin." [PMID:23456749]
is_a: HP:0045005 ! Neural tube defect
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T17:33:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034239
name: Renal vein thrombosis
def: "The presence of a thrombus (blood clot) in the major renal veins or its tributaries, generally leading to passive congestion that develops causes the affected kidney to swell and become engorged, leading to degeneration of nephrons and causing symptoms of flank pain, hematuria, and decreased urine output." [PMID:30725656]
comment: Diagnosis can be made by magnetic resonance angiography, Doppler ultrasonography, or computed tomography angiography.
is_a: HP:0033835 ! Abnormal renal vascular morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T17:38:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034240
name: Fetal neck mass
def: "An abnormal growth (lump) of tissue in the neck region of a fetus. Masses may be simple cystic,, cystic with a few simple septations (fewer than three septations and less than 3-mm thick), cystic with multiple or thick septations (greater than three septations or septations 3-mm-thick or more), a mass that is than is less than 50% solid, and a mass that is 50% solid or more." [PMID:30422714]
is_a: HP:0025667 ! Fetal neck anomaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T17:41:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034241
name: Prenatal death
def: "Death of a fetus in the uterus." []
synonym: "Death before birth" EXACT layperson []
synonym: "Intrauterine death" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011420 ! Age of death
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T17:51:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034242
name: Abnormal fetal genitourinary system morphology
def: "An anomalous structural finding of the fetal genitourinary system. Terms in this subhierarchy are restricted to findings that can only be observed in the prenatal period. Other HPO terms can also be used to describe fetal phenotypes." []
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T18:07:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034243
name: Abnormal fetal pulmonary morphology
def: "An anomalous structural finding of the fetal lungs. Terms in this subhierarchy are restricted to findings that can only be observed in the prenatal period. Other HPO terms can also be used to describe fetal phenotypes." []
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T18:08:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034244
name: Gastric pseudomass
def: "At US examination from the second trimester onward, the fetal stomach appears as a uniformly anechoic, sharply circumscribed round structure in the left upper quadrant. However, debris is commonly visualized in the stomach, forming a pseudomass." [PMID:15888614]
comment: The origin of echogenic masses within the gastric lumen is incompletely understood. As they are seen in multiple planes, technical issues are unlikely. They may be due to swallowed cells that aggregate because of the relatively poor peristaltic activity in the stomach early in the second trimester. When intraamniotic bleeding has occurred, these pseudomasses are commonly visualized. They inevitably disappear during follow-up examinations and are not associated with an adverse neonatal outcome.
is_a: HP:0034207 ! Abnormal fetal gastrointestinal system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T18:56:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034245
name: Fetal head anomaly
comment: A structural anomaly in the fetal head region. Terms in this subhierarchy are restricted to findings that can only be observed in the prenatal period. Other HPO terms can also be used to describe fetal phenotypes.
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T18:58:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034246
name: Fetal scalp mass
def: "An abnormal growth (lump) of tissue that projects from the fetal scalp." [PMID:24767653]
is_a: HP:0034245 ! Fetal head anomaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T18:59:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034247
name: Fetal lower urinary tract obstruction
def: "An obstruction in the ureter leading to bladder outlet obstruction. Special criteria are used for lower urinary tract obstruction (LUTO) in the fetus. Prenatal LUTO has classically been suspected on the basis of three ultrasonographic findings: megacystis, dilated posterior urethra (known as the keyhole sign) and hydronephrosis." [PMID:35136187]
is_a: HP:0034242 ! Abnormal fetal genitourinary system morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T19:18:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034248
name: Increased fetal lens echogenicity
def: "Increased echogenicity (increased brightness in the gray-scale sonography image) of the lens of a fetus." [PMID:27433255]
comment: Both the normal fetal lens and vitreous appear hypoechoic by ultrasound. On endovaginal ultrasound, the fetal lens may be visualized as early as 14 weeks of gestational age. The outline of the lens may be visible as a thin, echogenic line in the anterior aspect of the globe; however, the lens may be difficult to see depending on the angle of the insonation beam relative to the lens position. Increased echogenicity of the fetal lens can be observed with some forms of developmental cataract.
is_a: HP:0034058 ! Abnormal fetal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-10T19:22:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034249
name: Severe influenza infection
def: "An unusually severe infection by an influenza virus." [PMID:25814066]
synonym: "Severe influenza" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031691 ! Severe viral infection
is_a: HP:5210320 ! Unusual influenza infection
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5535-2845
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8124-8864
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-12T22:52:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034250
name: Fetal nuchal edema
def: "Nuchal edema is considered present in a fetus at gestational week 14 or more if in the midsagittal plane of the neck, there is subcutaneous edema that produces a characteristic tremor on ballotment of the fetal head. This constitutes the severe end of the spectrum of increased nuchal fold thickness, which is defined as soft-tissue thickening of 6 mm or more, seen in the suboccipitobregmatic view of the fetal head. Nuchal edema may be confined to the neck or it may be generalized, as part of hydrops fetalis." [PMID:16507941, PMID:9880279]
comment: In the fetus fluid collects behind the neck, much like it does in dependent ankle edema in later life. This occurs partly because of the tendency for the fetus to lie on its back and partly because of the laxity of the skin of the neck. As with ankle edema this accumulation of fluid can represent the end point of several pathological processes, including heart failure. Fluid collecting behind the neck can be detected as nuchal translucency by ultrasound scanning, and it can be measured. The more fluid that has accumulated, the greater the risk of an abnormality being present.
is_a: HP:0025667 ! Fetal neck anomaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-12T22:57:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034251
name: Abnormal corneal reflex
def: "An anomaly of the corneal reflex that normally induces involuntary blinking of the eyelids following contact of the cornea." [PMID:30480980]
comment: The corneal reflex can be tested by touching the cornea lightly with a cotton tip. The normal response to to blink (shut the eyelids) immediately. To evaluate the corneal reflex, the examiner uses a cotton-tipped applicator, the tip of which has been pulled into a thin strand. The examiner stabilizes the patient's head by placing a hand on the patient's eyebrow and head. The patient is asked to look to the left side as the cotton tip is brought in from the right side to touch the right cornea gently.
is_a: HP:0012373 ! Abnormal eye physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-23T11:42:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034252
name: Absent corneal reflex
def: "Absence of the corneal blinking reflex, which normally induces involuntary blinking of the eyelids following contact of the cornea. The corneal blink reflex is caused by a loop between the trigeminal sensory nerves and the facial motor (VII) nerve innervation of the orbicularis oculi muscles." [PMID:30480980]
is_a: HP:0034251 ! Abnormal corneal reflex
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-23T11:43:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034253
name: Eosinophil nuclear hypersegmentation
def: "An excessive division of the lobes of the nucleus of eosinophils. Eosinophils with more than two nuclear lobes are commonly regarded as hypersegmented, because seventy to ninety percent of peripheral blood eosinophils have two nuclear lobes." [PMID:10732836, PMID:25313414]
is_a: HP:0001879 ! Abnormal eosinophil morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-04-23T11:47:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034254
name: Face of the giant panda sign
def: "The face of the giant panda sign on T2-weighted MRI is characterized by preservation of normal signal intensity in the red nuclei and lateral portion of the pars reticulata of the substantia nigra, high signal in the tegmentum, and hypointensity of the superior colliculus. The findings are said to resemble the face of a giant panda." [PMID:14557570]
comment: See Figure b of PMID:14557570.
synonym: "Midbrain panda sign" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002418 ! Abnormal midbrain morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-05-07T14:24:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034255
name: Colovesical fistula
def: "An aberrant, pathological communication between the colon and the bladder." [PMID:30085532]
comment: The most common cause of colovesicular fistulas is the sequelae of complicated diverticulitis and accounts for over two-thirds of cases. The second most common cause is a malignancy in 10% to 20% of cases and is usually adenocarcinoma of the colon. Crohn's colitis is the third most common cause (5% to 7% of cases) and usually is a result of long-standing disease.
synonym: "Colovesicular fistula" EXACT []
synonym: "Vesicocolic fistula" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004321 ! Bladder fistula
is_a: HP:0100819 ! Intestinal fistula
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-05-07T14:27:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034256
name: Absent dermoepidermal hemidesmosomes
def: "Lack of demonstrable hemidesmosomes at the dermoepidermal junction. Hemidesmosomes are the specialized junctional complexes, that contribute to the attachment of epithelial cells to the underlying basement membrane in stratified and other complex epithelia, such as the skin." [PMID:19945618]
