[Term]
id: HP:0034356
name: Impaired renal tubular reabsorption of low molecular weight protein
def: "Increased loss of low-molecular weight proteins by the kidneys, measured in terms of the fractional excretion (FE). The FE of low-molecular-weight proteins such as beta2-microglobulin can be measured in terms of plasma and urine concentrations, since urinary low-molecular-weight protein concentrations can vary with water reabsorption." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2234-4248]
comment: Urinary proteins are reabsorbed by the renal tubule cells, and increased low molecular weight protein fractional excretion can be a sign of tubular proteinuria.
synonym: "Increased low molecular weight protein excretion" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011038 ! Abnormal renal tubular resorption
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-09-04T19:41:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034357
name: Impaired renal tubular reabsorption of glucose
def: "Increased fractional excretion (FE) of glucose in the urine. The FE of glucose is the percentage of the glucose filtered by the kidney which is excreted in the urine. It is measured in terms of plasma and urine glucose, rather than by the interpretation of urinary glucose concentration alone, as urinary glucose concentrations can vary with water reabsorption." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2234-4248]
is_a: HP:0011038 ! Abnormal renal tubular resorption
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-09-04T19:42:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034358
name: Impaired renal tubular reabsorption of sodium
def: "Increased fractional excretion (FE) of sodium in the urine. The FE of sodium is the percentage of the sodium filtered by the kidney which is excreted in the urine. It is measured in terms of plasma and urine sodium, rather than by the interpretation of urinary glucose concentration alone, as urinary glucose concentrations can vary with water reabsorption." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2234-4248]
is_a: HP:0011038 ! Abnormal renal tubular resorption
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-09-04T19:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034359
name: Impaired renal tubular reabsorption of phosphate
def: "Increased fractional excretion (FE) of glucose in the phosphate. The FE of glucose is the percentage of the phosphate filtered by the kidney which is excreted in the urine. It is measured in terms of plasma and urine phosphate, rather than by the interpretation of urinary phosphate concentration alone, as urinary glucose concentrations can vary with water reabsorption." [PMID:25287933, PMID:31474092]
is_a: HP:0011038 ! Abnormal renal tubular resorption
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-09-04T19:48:58Z" xsd:dateTime

