[Term]
id: HP:0034418
name: Erythematous oral mucosa
def: "An erythematous lesion of the oral mucosa may result from a variety of tissue alterations, including inflammation, erythrocyte extravasation, and atrophy or reduced keratinization of the surface epithelium." [PMID:30693460]
synonym: "Oral mucosa erythema" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011830 ! Abnormal oral mucosa morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-11-10T13:27:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034419
name: Mitral chordae tendinae rupture
def: "Breakage of the chordae tendinae of the mitral valve. This can lead to loss of tension of one of the mitral valve leaflets and mitral regurgitation." [PMID:30470812]
comment: The chordae provide the critical function of anchoring the mitral leaflets during systole, allowing for symmetric coaptation and preventing prolapse of the leaflets into the left atrium. The chordae are attached to the left ventricle via the papillary muscles.
synonym: "Flail mitral valve leaflet" EXACT []
synonym: "Mitral chordae tendineae rupture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025523 ! Abnormal morphology of the chordae tendinae of the mitral valve
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-11-12T11:59:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034420
name: History of cardiovascular procedure
def: "Indicates that a cardiovascular procedure such as stenting, bypass, catherization was performed on a patient." []
is_a: HP:0430103 ! Past surgical history
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-11-12T12:05:01Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034421
name: Ejection click
def: "A high-pitched sound that occurs at the moment of maximal opening of the aortic or pulmonary valves. They are heard just after the first heart sound. The sounds occur in the presence of a dilated aorta or pulmonary artery or in the presence of a bicuspid or flexible stenotic aortic or pulmonary valve. Ejection clicks may also be called ejection sounds." []
synonym: "Cardiac click sound on auscultation" EXACT []
xref: PMID:21250045
is_a: HP:0031657 ! Abnormal heart sound
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-11-12T12:09:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034422
name: Cryofibrinogenemia
def: "Cryofibrinogen is an abnormal protein that forms precipitate only in plasma. consisting of fibrinogen, fibronectin, alpha1-antitrypsin and alpha2-macroglobulin." [PMID:27789759]
comment: Cryofibrinogenemia (CF) can be detected in both healthy persons and patients with different disorders, including autoimmune diseases, cancer, infections, etc. Cryofibrinogen should be distinguished from cryoglobulin since, unlike the latter, it precipitates only in plasma and not in serum.
is_a: HP:0011898 ! Abnormality of circulating fibrinogen
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2022-11-12T12:21:29Z" xsd:dateTime

