[Term]
id: HP:0034508
name: Fingerprint bodies
def: "Fingerprint bodies are inclusion bodies located at the periphery of the muscle fibers underneath the sarcolemma (subsarcolemmal), consisting of non-membrane-bound packed lamellae arranged in concentric patterns resembling fingerprints." [PMID:32008911]
comment: See Figure 2 of PMID:32008911.
synonym: "Muscle biopsy: fingerprint bodies at periphery of muscle fibers" EXACT []
synonym: "Muscle biopsy: fingerprint bodies at periphery of muscle fibres" EXACT uk_spelling []
