[Term]
id: HP:0034636
name: Bone marrow myeloid vacuolization
def: "Formation of vacuoles (a space within a cell that is empty of cytoplasm, lined with a membrane, and filled with fluid) in the cytoplasm of myeloid precursors in the bone marrow." [PMID:33690844]
comment: See Figure 1 of PMID:33690844.
synonym: "Bone marrow: myeloid vacuolization" EXACT []
synonym: "Vacuolization of bone marrow myeloid precursors" EXACT []
