id: HP:0034689
name: Reduced sterol 27-hydroxylase activity
def: "Diminished activity of the enzyme sterol 27-hydroxylase, which participates in the degradation of cholesterol to bile acid. Sterol 27-hydroxylase catalyzes the first step in the normal oxidation of the steroid side chain, converting cholesterol, as well as different 7a-hydroxylated cholesterol metabolites, to 27-oxygenated steroids." [PMID:10856919]
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-03-26T18:22:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034690
name: Reduced short-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase activity
def: "Diminished activity of the enzyme Short-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase (SCAD), a key enzyme of fatty acid beta-oxidation that catalyzes the first step in mitochondrial beta-oxidation of fatty acids." [PMID:26989860]
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-03-26T18:24:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034691
name: Reduced 3-phosphoglycerate dehydrogenase activity
def: "Diminished activity of the enzyme 3-phosphoglycerate dehydrogenase (PGDH), which catalyzes the first step in the pathway by converting D-3-phosphoglycerate (PGA), an intermediate in glycolysis, to phosphohydroxypyruvate concomitant with the reduction of NAD+." [PMID:30619878]
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-03-26T18:26:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034692
name: Elongated mitochondria
def: "Increase in length of mitochondria." [PMID:33262702]
comment: Mitochondrial elongation can be initiated by a gradual merge of the outer mitochondrial membranes of two individual mitochondria.
