is_a: HP:0034268 ! Abnormal vaginal physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:06:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034807
name: Paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea
def: "Attacks of breathlessness that occur at night and may awaken the sleeping patient." [PMID:26933707]
is_a: HP:0002094 ! Dyspnea
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:11:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034808
name: Eyelid pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the eyelid." []
is_a: HP:0012531 ! Pain
is_a: HP:0031879 ! Abnormal eyelid physiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:16:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034809
name: Abnormal sperm physiology
def: "Abnormality of a sperm function including protection of paternal DNA, traversing the female reproductive tract, oocyte localisation, penetration of the zona pellucida, oocyte activation and centriole deposition." []
is_a: HP:0000025 ! Functional abnormality of male internal genitalia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:30:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034810
name: Small acrosomal area
def: "Reduction in size of the acrosome below the lower limit of normal. The acrosome is a unique membranous organelle located over the anterior part of the sperm nucleus. According to the World Health Organization criteria, the acrosome must be clearly visible, comprising approximately 40-70 percent of the sperm head." [PMID:31939391]
is_a: HP:0012865 ! Abnormal sperm head morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:43:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034811
name: Bent sperm flagella
def: "The proportion of sperm cells whose flagella is sharply curved or has a sharp angle is above normal limits." [PMID:20111080]
is_a: HP:0012868 ! Abnormal sperm tail morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T11:53:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034812
name: Spermiation failure
def: "Spermiation failure is indicated by apparently normal spermiogenesis, but the presence of retained Sd2 spermatids in stages III-V of human spermatogenesis, whereas maturation arrest is indicated by a lack of late Sd1 and Sd2 spermatids in the epithelium." [PMID:21866274]
comment: It is important to note that multiple spermatogenic abnormalities often occur simultaneously in infertile men, and the helical nature of human spermatogenesis can make it difficult to readily discriminate multiple abnormalities of spermatid development and release.
is_a: HP:0011961 ! Non-obstructive azoospermia
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7651-2403
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T12:16:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034813
name: Hypospermatogenesis
def: "A morphological abnormality visible upon biopsy of the germinal epithelium of the testis in which the cellularity of the germinal epithelium is reduced in general, so that all stages of germ cells (spermatogonia, spermatocytes, and spermatids) are present but reduced in number. This term applies to biopsies with some tubules showing diminished amounts of qualitatively complete spermatogenesis in combination with a vast majority of tubules that lack germ cells." [PMID:21346828]
is_a: HP:0008669 ! Abnormal spermatogenesis
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7651-2403
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T12:26:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034814
name: Conjunctival membrane
def: "Formation of a sheet of tissue by coagulum of exudate over the conjunctiva of the eye that if removed leaves behind a denuded bleeding surface." []
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:01:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034815
name: Extreme oligozoospermia
def: "A type of oligozoospermia characterized by a total number of more than zero but less than 2 million sperm in the ejaculate or a concentration of more than zero but less than one million sperm per milliliter." []
is_a: HP:0000798 ! Oligozoospermia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:05:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034816
name: Mild oligozoospermia
def: "A type of oligozoospermia characterized by a total number of more than 30 but less than 39 million sperm in the ejaculate or a concentration of more than 10 but less than 15 million sperm per milliliter." []
is_a: HP:0000798 ! Oligozoospermia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:06:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034817
name: Moderate oligozoospermia
def: "A type of oligozoospermia characterized by a total number of more than 10 but less than 29 million sperm in the ejaculate or a concentration of more than 5 but less than 10 million sperm per milliliter." []
is_a: HP:0000798 ! Oligozoospermia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:07:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034818
name: Severe oligozoospermia
def: "A type of oligozoospermia characterized by a total number of more than 2 but less than 10 million sperm in the ejaculate or a concentration of more than 1 but less than 5 million sperm per milliliter." []
is_a: HP:0000798 ! Oligozoospermia
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:08:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034819
name: Iris nodule
def: "The presence of a nodule (small rounded lump of tissue) in the iris." [PMID:12185117]
is_a: HP:0000525 ! Abnormality iris morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:30:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034820
name: Koeppe nodules
def: "A type of iris nodule consisting of inflammatory cell precipitates which lie at the pupillary margin." [PMID:8441952]
comment: Koeppe nodules can be observed in non-granulomaous and granulomatous uveitis.
synonym: "Koeppe iris nodules" EXACT []
synonym: "Koeppe's nodules" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034819 ! Iris nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:30:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0034821
name: Bussaca nodules
def: "A type of iris nodule consisting of inflammatory cell precipitates which lie on the iris surface." [PMID:8441952]
comment: Bussace nodules are considered pathognomonic for granulomatous uveitis.
is_a: HP:0034819 ! Iris nodule
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-07-01T13:49:42Z" xsd:dateTime

