[Term]
id: HP:0040103
name: Acquired stenosis of the external ear canal
def: "Stenosis or narrowing of the external ear canal (EAC) occurs lateral to the tympanic membrane resulting in a skin lined blind canal." []
comment: Acquired stenosis of the external ear canal typically presents as recurrent otorrhea, conductive hearing loss, often with significant cerumen impaction and ear canal cholesteatoma. Different etiologies such as chronic otitis externa, dermatologic diseases, iatrogenic (previous ear surgery or radiotherapy) or accidental rauma, tumor and inflammation lead to scarring/fibrosis and subsequent stenosis of the ear canal.
synonym: "Acquired medial canal fibrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Cutaneous stenosis of the external auditory canal" EXACT []
synonym: "Medial meatal fibrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Obliterative otitis externa" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000402 ! Stenosis of the external auditory canal
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399

[Term]
id: HP:0040104
name: Osseous stenosis of the external auditory canal
def: "A narrowing of the bony part of the ear canal, which can be congenital or acquired through causes like chronic infections, trauma, or radiation therapy." []
is_a: HP:0000402 ! Stenosis of the external auditory canal
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399

