[Term]
id: HP:0041090
name: Pelvic avulsion fracture
def: "An avulsion fracture (i.e., a type of fracture in which a piece of bone tears away from the site where the muscle attaches to the bone) of a bone of the pelvis." [PMID:32106326]
comment: Pelvic avulsion injuries can occur in both adolescents and adults when either the apophysis is not yet completely fused or the enthesis, i. e. the site of attachment of a tendon or ligament, cannot withstand the tractional force encountered. Anatomically, the enthesis refers to the site of insertion of a tendon or ligament and the adjacent tissues which are functionally related.
synonym: "Avulsion fractured pelvic region of trunk" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0041161 ! Pelvis fracture
is_a: HP:4000052 ! Avulsion fracture
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432
property_value: terms:date "2020-07-28T16:21:41Z" xsd:dateTime

