[Term]
id: HP:0041161
name: Pelvis fracture
def: "A break in one or more bones of the pelvis." [PMID:28613485]
comment: Pelvic fractures may be caused by damage to the pelvic ring's components, including the hip bones, sacrum, and coccyx. Pelvic fractures often result from high-impact trauma and are frequently accompanied by additional injuries elsewhere in the body.
