[Term]
id: HP:0045005
name: Neural tube defect
def: "A neural tube defect arises when the neural tube, the embryonic precursor of the brain and spinal cord, fails to close during neurulation. The cranial region (anencephaly) or the low spine (open spina bifida; myelomeningocele) are most commonly affected although, in the severe NTD craniorachischisis, almost the entire neural tube remains open, from midbrain to low spine." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:19808787]
synonym: "Abnormality of neural tube closure" EXACT []
synonym: "NTD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0410043 ! Abnormal neural tube morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399

