[Term]
id: HP:0045028
name: Microlissencephaly
def: "Severe microcephaly and lissencephaly with granular surfaces with immature cortical plate, reduced in thickness, with focal polymicrogyria and immature small neurons with rare processes, intermingled with a considerable number of glial elements." [PMID:8779318]
comment: This is a severe phenotype that can be diagnosed at the fetopathological level, by which a diagnosis of lissencephaly can be made by the examination of the 6 layers of the cortex. Examination may show 3 layers or an extremely thin cortical plate consistent with the diagnosis of lissencephaly.
synonym: "Lissencephaly type III" EXACT []
synonym: "Type 3 lissencephaly" EXACT []
synonym: "Type III lissencephaly" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001339 ! Lissencephaly
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399

