[Term]
id: HP:0045047
name: HbS hemoglobin
def: "Presence of an abnormal type of hemoglobin characterized by the substitution of a glutamic acid residue at position 7 following the initial methionine residue by a valine (the mutation causative of sickle cell disease). The mutation promotes the polymerization of the HbS under conditions of low oxygen concentration. HbS can be identified by multiple methodologies including hemoglobin electrophoresis and high-performance liquid chromatography." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:34406727, PMID:3953566]
synonym: "HbS haemoglobin" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0011902 ! Abnormal hemoglobin
property_value: terms:date "2015-09-24T18:31:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0045048
name: Increased HbA2 hemoglobin
def: "An elevated concentration in the blood of hemoglobin A2 (HbA2), which is a normal variant of hemoglobin A that consists of two alpha and two delta chains and is normally present at low levels in adults but may be increased in beta thalassemia." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:26372049]
synonym: "Increased haemoglobin A2" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Increased HbA2 haemoglobin" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Increased hemoglobin A2" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011902 ! Abnormal hemoglobin
property_value: terms:date "2015-09-24T18:44:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0045049
name: Abnormal DLCO
def: "An abnormal amount of oxygen passes into the blood from the lungs and/or an abnormal amount of carbon dioxide passes from the blood into the lungs." [PMID:32310609]
comment: Inhaled CO is used for this test due to its high affinity for hemoglobin (200-250 times that of oxygen). During a ten-second breath-hold, DLCO measures uptake of CO per unit time per mm of driving pressure of CO (cc of CO/sec/mm of Hg).
synonym: "Abnormal diffusing capacity" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal TLCO" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal transfer factor of the lung for carbon monoxide" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030878 ! Abnormality on pulmonary function testing
property_value: terms:date "2015-09-24T19:00:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0045050
name: Increased DLCO
def: "Increased ability of the lungs to transfer gas from inspired air to the bloodstream as measured by the diffusing capacity of the lungs for carbon monoxide (DLCO) test." [PMID:32310609]
comment: Factors that can increase the DLCO include polycythaemia, asthma (can also have normal DLCO) and increased pulmonary blood volume as occurs in exercise. Other factors are left to right intracardiac shunting, and alveolar hemorrhage.
synonym: "Increased diffusing capacity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0045049 ! Abnormal DLCO
property_value: terms:date "2015-09-24T19:00:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0045051
name: Decreased DLCO
def: "Reduced ability of the lungs to transfer gas from inspired air to the bloodstream as measured by the diffusing capacity of the lungs for carbon monoxide (DLCO) test." [PMID:32310609]
comment: DLCO is decreased in any condition which affects the effective alveolar surface area
synonym: "Decreased diffusing capacity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0045049 ! Abnormal DLCO
property_value: terms:date "2015-09-24T19:00:25Z" xsd:dateTime

