[Term]
id: HP:0100611
name: Multiple glomerular cysts
def: "The presence of many cysts in the glomerulus of the kidney related to dilatation of the Bowman's capsule." [HPO_CONTRIBUTOR:Eurenomics_fschaefer, PMID:20091054, PMID:20367310]
comment: Glomerular cysts, defined as Bowman space dilatation greater than 2 to 3 times normal size, are found in disorders of diverse etiology and with a spectrum of clinical manifestations. The term glomerulocystic kidney refers to a kidney with greater than 5% cystic glomeruli.
