[Term]
id: HP:0100651
name: Type I diabetes mellitus
def: "A chronic condition in which the pancreas produces little or no insulin. Type I diabetes mellitus is manifested by the sudden onset of severe hyperglycemia with rapid progression to diabetic ketoacidosis unless treated with insulin." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The onset of type 1 diabetes is typically during adolescence, but it can develop at any age.
