[Term]
id: HP:0100837
name: Atrophodermia vermiculata
def: "Symmetrical vermiform facial atrophy that affects mainly the forehead, the chin, the ear lobes and helices. Atrophodermia vermiculata is characterized by erythema and follicular plugs on the cheeks, developing into painless reticular impressions." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: The onset of atrophodermia vermiculata is usually between the ages of 5 and 12 years.
