[Term]
id: HP:0100880
name: Nephrogenic rest
def: "Abnormally persistent clusters of embryonal cells, representing microscopic malformations (dysplasias) of the developing kidney." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
comment: Though NR are best known as precursors of Wilms tumor (WT), many alternative fates are observed, and most rests are destined for eventual atresia. Nephroblastomatosis refers to the presence of multifocal or diffuse nephrogenic rests.
is_a: HP:0012210 ! Abnormal renal morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T02:41:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0100881
name: Congenital mesoblastic nephroma
def: "Congenital mesoblastic nephroma is a type of kidney tumor that is usually found before birth by ultrasound or within the first 3 months of life. It contains fibroblastic cells (connective tissue cells), and may spread to the other kidney or to nearby tissue." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
comment: Congenital mesoblastic nephroma is more common in males.
is_a: HP:0003549 ! Abnormality of connective tissue
is_a: HP:0011794 ! Embryonal renal neoplasm
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T02:44:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0100882
name: Fibrous hamartoma
def: "A rare, benign soft tissue tumor that typically occurs within the first two years of life." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
synonym: "Fibrous hamartoma of infancy" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010566 ! Hamartoma
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T02:48:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0100883
name: Chorangioma
def: "Hamartoma-like growth in the placenta consisting of blood vessels." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154, PMID:20594143, PMID:24251055]
comment: Chorioangiomas (also known as placental hemangiomas) are benign hamartomatous growth of the placenta comprising vascular tissue. The classification is controversial due to its pathologic features and clinical implications. Some authors call placental hemangiomas as true nontrophoblastic neoplastic tissues. As this abnormal vascular growth seems like the native placental tissue and it does not metastasize, some authors call it just as placental hamartoma. The general incidence is approximately 0.6 percent. Giant chorioangiomas with a diameter over 5 cm are very rare, with an incidence of one in 16-50 thousand pregnancies. Small tumors do not cause any adverse outcomes and they are asymptomatic. In contrast, tumors larger than 5 cm may lead to several complications.
synonym: "Placental hamartoma" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010566 ! Hamartoma
is_a: HP:0100767 ! Abnormal placenta morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T02:50:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0100884
name: Compensatory scoliosis
def: "A scoliosis which is the results of a difference in leg length (which might be due to hemihypertrophy or hemihypotrophy of a leg) and the resulting tilting of the pelvis. If untreated this will lead to the development of scoliosis over time." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
is_a: HP:0002650 ! Scoliosis
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T02:56:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0100885
name: Lateral venous anomaly
def: "Persistence of the embryonic dorsal or sciatic vein system that normally should have involuted around the tenth to twelfth week of intrauterine life." [https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154]
comment: Embryonic leg veins usually regress before birth, but in Klippel-Trenaunay syndrome (KTS) a persistent embryonic vein (PEV) may be located on the lateral aspect of the affected leg. Known PEVs of the leg are the lateral marginal vein (LMV) and the persistent sciatic vein (PSV). The nomenclature can be confusing because various terms are used to indicate the same aberrant leg vein in KTS (e.g. vein of Servelle, Klippel-Trenaunay vein, lateral marginal vein).
synonym: "Klippel-Trenaunay vein" EXACT []
synonym: "Lateral marginal vein of Servelle" EXACT []
synonym: "Vein of Servelle" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001015 ! Prominent superficial veins
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4530-3154
property_value: terms:date "2011-12-01T03:16:02Z" xsd:dateTime

