[Term]
id: HP:0410379
name: Abnormal memory CD4+ T cell proportion
alt_id: HP:0025623
alt_id: HP:0410381
alt_id: HP:0410382
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of the memory CD4+ T cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD45RA-, CD45RO+, or CD27-, measured as percentage of total CD4+ T cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [CL:0000897]
comment: Unlike in CD8+ T cells, in CD4+ T cells the populations of central memory, effector memory and TEMRA cells are not easily measurable and or are of limited clinical utility. Therefore, generally, only the distinction between naive and memory CD4 T cells is made.
synonym: "Abnormal CD4+ memory T cell proportion" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD4+ memory T cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD4-positive memory T cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031392 ! Abnormal CD4+ T cell subset proportion
is_a: HP:0032182 ! Abnormal memory T cell proportion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-05T15:04:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0410380
name: Abnormal memory CD8+ T cell proportion
def: "Abnormal increase or decrease of the memory CD8+ T cell subpopulation, commonly characterized as CD45RA-, CD45RO+, or CD27-, measured as percentage of total CD8+ T cells in the blood, compared to a reference range for a given sex and age-group." [PMID:20146720, PMID:28481945]
comment: Human CD8+T cells are commonly classified into four subsets based on the surface expression of the leukocyte common antigen isoform CD45RA and the lymph node addressin CCR7. Thereby, naive TN cells (CD45RA+/CCR7+) are separated from central memory TCM (CD45RA-/CCR7+), effector memory TEM (CD45RA-/CCR7-) and TEMRA (CD45RA+/CCR7-) T cells.
synonym: "Abnormal CD8+ memory T cell proportion" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of CD8-positive memory T cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020115 ! Abnormal CD8+ T cell subset proportion
is_a: HP:0032182 ! Abnormal memory T cell proportion
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432
property_value: terms:date "2019-04-05T15:04:39Z" xsd:dateTime

