[Term]
id: HP:0430104
name: Abnormal superficial temporal artery morphology
def: "Any structural abnormality of a superficial temporal artery, originating from the external carotid artery and passing over the zygomatic process. The superficial temporal artery is located on the superficial parts of the forehead and sides of the head and face." []
is_a: HP:0011004 ! Abnormal systemic arterial morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T08:08:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430105
name: Skip lesions on temporal artery biopsy
def: "Patchy inflammation of the superficial temporal artery, forming isolated foci of arteritis." [PMID:10767830, PMID:950804]
comment: This feature may be observed in temporal arteritis. The foci are characterized by mononuclear cell infiltrates or a granulomatous process with multinucleated giant cells.
is_a: HP:0430104 ! Abnormal superficial temporal artery morphology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T08:13:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:0430106
name: Abnormal brain-evoked potentials
def: "Any anomaly of brain-evoked potentials, defined as potentials generated by exteroceptive stimuli reflect synchronized activity by neuronal and axonal groups in the central nervous system (CNS) resulting from the arrival of nerve impulses after stimulation of a peripheral nerve or its receptors. Depending on the type of stimulus, evoked potentials are categorized as visual (VEP), auditory (AEP), or somatosensory (SSEP). Motor evoked potentials (MEP) occur when the brain's motor area is stimulated. They result from the activation of a sufficient number of motor units." [PMID:22995526]
is_a: HP:0030178 ! Abnormality of central nervous system electrophysiology
property_value: terms:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T17:19:38Z" xsd:dateTime

