[Term]
id: HP:5200023
name: Abnormal HLA-DR+ T cell proportion
def: "The proportion of peripheral blood T lymphocytes expressing HLA-DR (CD3+HLA-DR+) is outside of the reference limit for age." [PMID:9000587]
comment: HLA-DR expression on T cells is an activation marker; elevated proportions reflect in vivo T cell activation status even when measured ex vivo without prior stimulation. This feature can be measured by flow cytometry.
synonym: "Abnormal HLA-DR expression on T cells" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal proportion of DR+ T cells" EXACT []
