[Term]
id: HP:5200029
name: Social disinhibition
def: "A tendency to violate social norms because of a failure to resist temptations or urges in social settings." [PMID:27696753]
comment: A tendency to social disinhibition can be acquired after traumatic brain injury and may be described as insensitivity to others. Manifestions of social disinhibition may include (1) insertion of poorly considered utterances including insensitive remarks,overly intimate information, sexual references, and swear words, (2) failure to adhereto the rules of discourse leading to poor turn-taking, excessive side tracks, off topics,and talking too much, and (3) speaking from an egocentric perspective, that is,lacking concern, selfishness, childishness, arguing, not getting along with others.
is_a: HP:0000734 ! Disinhibition
is_a: HP:5200123 ! Abnormal response to social norms
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9112-5148
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9593-5508
property_value: terms:date "2023-03-23T14:48:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:5200030
name: Diminished integration of verbal and non-verbal communicative behavior
def: "A communicative abnormality where one's nonverbal and verbal communication are poorly integrated. This may occur when verbal and nonverbal communication are intact alone but are abnormal when used together, or an abnormality in the use of typically integrated communication such as the use of beat gestures during speech." []
is_a: HP:0034434 ! Abnormal communication
