[Term]
id: HP:5200290
name: Exploding head syndrome
def: "Sleep disorder in which one hears a loud noise or explosive crashing sound in one's head. The sound is not real or heard by anyone else. The episode typically happens suddenly, either when beginning to fall asleep or when waking up during the night." [PMID:32757464]
