[Term]
id: HP:5210111
name: Tuberculosis infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Mycobacterium tuberculosis infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with Mycobacterium tuberculosis, or by Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location." []
comment: In the context of inborn errors of immunity, disseminated tuberculosis is characteristic of Mendelian Susceptibility to Mycobacterial Disease (MSMD) and Severe Combined Immunodeficiency (SCID). A critical clinical distinction is the onset of severe or disseminated disease following BCG vaccination shortly after birth, which serves as a typical clue for underlying IEI (including SCID, MSMD, and CGD) compared to the later acquisition of environmental tuberculosis.
synonym: "TB infection" EXACT []
synonym: "TB Tuberculosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual susceptibility to tuberculosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual tuberculosis infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:5210110 ! Unusual mycobacterial infection
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-9822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9382-150X
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2029-0733
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3577-9021
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4315-9105
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8124-8864

[Term]
id: HP:5210112
name: Disseminated tuberculosis infection
def: "Disseminated infection with Mycobacterium tuberculosis, involving multiple organ systems. Organ-specific manifestations of disseminated tuberculosis include renal tuberculosis (tuberculous pyelonephritis, presenting with sterile pyuria and hematuria), hepatic tuberculosis, adrenal tuberculosis, and tuberculous osteomyelitis." []
comment: In the context of inborn errors of immunity, disseminated or severe mycobacterial infections (including both M. tuberculosis and non-tuberculous mycobacteria) are characteristically associated with three primary groups: Severe Combined Immunodeficiency (SCID), Chronic Granulomatous Disease (CGD), and Mendelian Susceptibility to Mycobacterial Disease (MSMD). This clinical presentation across these three groups applies to all mycobacterial subcategories.
synonym: "Disseminated tuberculosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Miliary tuberculosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Severe tuberculosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:5210111 ! Tuberculosis infection
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-9822
