[Term]
id: HP:5210114
name: Tuberculous osteomyelitis
def: "Osteomyelitis caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection that occurs in the context of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
comment: Tuberculous osteomyelitis classically affects the spine (Pott's disease), hip, or knee, and may occur as part of disseminated tuberculosis in patients with Mendelian susceptibility to mycobacterial disease (MSMD), T-cell deficiencies, or HIV co-infection.
synonym: "Pott's disease" EXACT []
synonym: "TB osteomyelitis" EXACT []
