[Term]
id: HP:5210122
name: Sclerosing cholangitis due to Cryptosporidium infection
def: "Sclerosing cholangitis caused by Cryptosporidium infection that occurs in the context of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
comment: Cryptosporidial sclerosing cholangitis and associated biliary complications are characteristic of three primary groups: Hyper-IgM syndromes (both X-linked and autosomal recessive forms), MHC class II deficiency, and DOCK8 deficiency. These conditions typically present with biliary stricturing, jaundice, and progressive hepatic dysfunction due to impaired T-cell mediated clearance of the parasite.
is_a: HP:0030991 {xref="PMID:12713884"} ! Sclerosing cholangitis
is_a: HP:5210119 {xref="PMID:12713884"} ! Unusual Cryptosporidium infection
is_a: HP:5210134 {xref="PMID:12713884"} ! Unusual cholangitis
