[Term]
id: HP:5210125
name: Persistent Giardia lamblia infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Giardia lamblia infections as manifested by a chronic or persistent Giardia lamblia infection." []
comment: Persistent or chronic Giardia lamblia infections are characteristic of primary immunodeficiencies that impair mucosal antibody production. This phenotype is most frequently associated with X-linked agammaglobulinemia (XLA), Common Variable Immunodeficiency (CVID), and Hyper-IgM syndromes.
synonym: "Chronic giardiasis" EXACT []
synonym: "Persistent giardiasis" EXACT []
