[Term]
id: HP:5210127
name: Unusual Toxoplasma infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Toxoplasma gondii infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with Toxoplasma gondii, or by Toxoplasma gondii infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location." []
comment: Severe or unusual Toxoplasma gondii infections, including CNS toxoplasmosis, are primarily associated with severe T-cell deficiencies (both primary and secondary). This phenotype has also been specifically described in X-linked Hyper-IgM syndrome, where impaired T-cell signaling increases susceptibility to central nervous system involvement.
synonym: "Unusual toxoplasmosis" EXACT []
