[Term]
id: HP:5210140
name: Bacterial sepsis
def: "Sepsis caused by bacterial infection, characterized by a dysregulated host response to a bacterial pathogen with systemic inflammation, organ dysfunction, and potential progression to septic shock." []
comment: Causative organisms range from gram-positive cocci such as Staphylococcus aureus and Streptococcus species to gram-negative bacilli such as Escherichia coli and Klebsiella pneumoniae, and may include anaerobic and atypical bacterial organisms.
synonym: "Bacterial bloodstream infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100806 ! Sepsis
is_a: HP:5210000 ! Unusual bacterial infection
