[Term]
id: HP:5210141
name: Fungal sepsis
def: "Sepsis caused by fungal infection, characterized by a dysregulated host response to a fungal pathogen with systemic inflammation, organ dysfunction, and potential progression to septic shock." []
comment: Common causative organisms include Candida species (candidaemia), Aspergillus species, Cryptococcus, and the Mucorales, as well as endemic dimorphic fungi.
synonym: "Fungal sepsis bloodstream infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020100 ! Unusual fungal infection
is_a: HP:0100806 ! Sepsis
