[Term]
id: HP:5210142
name: Viral sepsis
def: "Sepsis or sepsis-like syndrome caused by viral infection, characterized by a dysregulated host response to a viral pathogen with systemic inflammation, multi-organ involvement, and potential progression to circulatory and respiratory failure." []
comment: Causative organisms include, among others, influenza virus, SARS-CoV-2, dengue virus, enteroviruses, and various herpesviruses such as cytomegalovirus (CMV), Epstein-Barr virus (EBV), and varicella-zoster virus (VZV).
synonym: "Viral bloodstream infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034317 ! Unusual viral infection
is_a: HP:0100806 ! Sepsis
