[Term]
id: HP:5210143
name: Mycobacterial sepsis
def: "Sepsis or sepsis-like systemic illness caused by mycobacterial infection, characterized by a dysregulated host response with systemic inflammation, multi-organ involvement, and disseminated mycobacterial disease." []
comment: Causative organisms include Mycobacterium tuberculosis (notably as part of disseminated or miliary tuberculosis) and non-tuberculous mycobacteria.
synonym: "Mycobacterial bloodstream infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0100806 ! Sepsis
is_a: HP:5210110 ! Unusual mycobacterial infection
