[Term]
id: HP:5210144
name: Pneumonia with consolidation
def: "Pneumonia characterized by lobar or segmental consolidation on radiographic imaging, reflecting alveolar filling with inflammatory exudate that occurs in the context of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
comment: Recurrent pneumonia with consolidation is a characteristic of antibody deficiencies (CVID, X-linked agammaglobulinaemia) and may progress to bronchiectasis if untreated.
