comment: A characteristic feature of severe T-cell deficiency and neutrophil defects including chronic granulomatous disease.
synonym: "Candidal liver abscess" EXACT []
synonym: "Hepatic candidal infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:5210102 ! Unusual Candida infection
is_a: HP:5210166 ! Fungal liver abscess

[Term]
id: HP:5210168
name: Parasitic liver abscess
def: "A liver abscess or cystic hepatic lesion caused by parasitic infection, with principal causative organisms being Entamoeba histolytica (amoebic liver abscess) and Echinococcus species (hepatic hydatid disease)." []
comment: Susceptibility to parasitic liver abscesses (e.g., amebic or hydatid) is primarily determined by environmental exposure and geographic endemicity rather than an underlying immune defect. While severe or atypical cases can occur in immunocompromised states, they are not standard diagnostic markers for primary immunodeficiency.
is_a: HP:0100523 ! Liver abscess
