[Term]
id: HP:5210201
name: Unusual bacterial vaginal infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to bacterial vaginal infection, as manifested by recurrent or severe bacterial vaginosis or vaginal bacterial infection that is unusual in frequency or severity for a healthy individual of the same age." []
comment: Common causative agents include Gardnerella vaginalis and vaginal anaerobes including Prevotella species and Mobiluncus species.
