[Term]
id: HP:5210202
name: Unusual viral vaginal infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to viral vaginal infection, as manifested by recurrent or severe herpes simplex virus (HSV) infection of the vaginal or vulvovaginal area that can occur in the context of immune deficiency." []
comment: Severe or disseminated genital HSV infection can be observed in T-cell deficiencies.
