[Term]
id: HP:5210230
name: Recurrent boils
def: "A recurrent infection of hair follicles producing furuncles (boils), with common causative organisms being Staphylococcus aureus and Streptococcus species. A recurrent boil can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, particularly in chronic granulomatous disease, hyper-IgE syndrome (STAT3 deficiency), leukocyte adhesion deficiency, and atopic dermatitis-related immune defects." []
synonym: "Recurrent folliculitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Recurrent furuncles" EXACT []
