[Term]
id: HP:5210231
name: Bacterial cellulitis
def: "A cellulitis caused by bacterial infection of the dermis and subcutaneous tissue, with common causative organisms including Streptococcus pyogenes and Staphylococcus aureus." []
comment: A recurrent or severe bacterial cellulitis can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, including phagocyte defects, lymphoedema-associated immune defects, and complement deficiencies.
synonym: "Recurrent cellulitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual bacterial cellulitis" EXACT []
