id: HP:5210233
name: Unusual HSV skin infection
def: "A herpes simplex virus (HSV) infection of the skin, which may present as localised vesicular lesions in any host. A severe, persistent, or disseminated cutaneous HSV infection (including eczema herpeticum and chronic ulcerative herpes) can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
