[Term]
id: HP:5210234
name: Unusual parasitic skin infection
def: "An increased susceptibility to parasitic infection of the skin or subcutaneous tissue, as manifested by a recurrent, severe, or atypically distributed parasitic skin lesion, or by a cutaneous parasitic infection occurring in an unusual clinical context. Causative organisms include Leishmania species, Onchocerca volvulus, and Ancylostoma species. An atypical or disseminated cutaneous leishmaniasis can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
