[Term]
id: HP:5210239
name: Unusual bacterial nail bed infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to bacterial infection of the nail bed and proximal nail fold (paronychia), as manifested by recurrent or severe episodes that are unusual in frequency or severity for a healthy individual of the same age. Principal causative agents include Staphylococcus aureus and Streptococcus species." []
comment: Recurrent bacterial paronychia is a characteristic feature of phagocyte defects including leukocyte adhesion deficiency and chronic granulomatous disease.
synonym: "Recurrent paronychia" EXACT []
