[Term]
id: HP:5210243
name: Unusual fascia infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to infection of the fascia and surrounding soft tissue, as manifested by necrotizing fasciitis or other invasive fascial infection occurring in an unusual clinical context. Necrotizing fasciitis is a rapidly progressive, life-threatening infection of the superficial fascia and subcutaneous tissue." []
comment: Principal causative agents include Streptococcus pyogenes (type I, monomicrobial) and polymicrobial infections involving anaerobes, Gram-negative organisms, and Staphylococcus aureus (type II). Immunocompromise is present in approximately 50% of cases.
synonym: "Invasive fascial infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual necrotising fasciitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual necrotizing fasciitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual soft tissue necrotizing infection" EXACT []
