id: HP:5210254
name: Severe pharyngitis
def: "Increased susceptibility to pharyngitis, as manifested by a severe episode of pharyngeal infection requiring hospitalisation or intravenous antimicrobial therapy, or complicated by peritonsillar abscess, retropharyngeal abscess, or invasive spread." []
comment: Principal causative agents include Streptococcus pyogenes (Group A Streptococcus) and Fusobacterium necrophorum.
synonym: "Invasive pharyngitis" EXACT []
