[Term]
id: HP:5210261
name: Unusual keratitis
def: "Increased susceptibility to infectious keratitis, as manifested by recurrent or severe infection of the cornea, or by keratitis caused by an atypical or opportunistic organism." []
comment: Principal causative agents in the context of immune deficiency include herpes simplex virus (HSV stromal keratitis, with a recurrence rate of 50% in immunodeficient patients) and varicella-zoster virus (herpes zoster ophthalmicus with corneal involvement). Immunodeficiency is a significant independent risk factor for recurrent HSV keratitis.
synonym: "Unusual corneal infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual herpetic keratitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual infectious keratitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual susceptibility to keratitis" EXACT []
