[Term]
id: HP:5210264
name: Unusual retinitis
def: "Increased susceptibility to infectious retinitis, as manifested by recurrent or severe infection of the retina, or by retinitis caused by an atypical or opportunistic organism." []
comment: The principal causative agent in the context of immune deficiency is cytomegalovirus (CMV retinitis), which is a hallmark of severe T-cell deficiency and combined immunodeficiency. Other agents include VZV (acute retinal necrosis) and HSV.
synonym: "Unusual infectious retinitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual susceptibility to retinitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual viral retinitis" EXACT []
