[Term]
id: HP:5210271
name: Family history of lymphoma
def: "A family history (in a first- or second-degree relative) of a lymphoma." []
comment: A family history of lymphoma may indicate inherited cancer predisposition syndromes, including DNA repair defects, and inborn errors of immunity predisposing to lymphoproliferative disease such as X-linked lymphoproliferative syndrome and ITK deficiency.
