[Term]
id: HP:5210275
name: Consanguinity
def: "A reproductive relationship between two individuals who are related by blood as second cousins or closer. In a medical and genetic context, consanguinity increases the coefficient of inbreeding, raising the probability that an offspring will inherit identical alleles from a common ancestor (homozygosity by descent). This significantly increases the risk for autosomal recessive disorders, such as inborn errors of immunity, metabolic diseases, and rare neurodevelopmental syndromes. A history of consanguinity serves as a vital clinical marker for directing diagnostic investigations toward recessive genetic etiologies, especially in the presence of rare phenotypes or unexplained family medical history." []
is_a: HP:0032316 ! Family history
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-9822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9382-150X
