[Term]
id: HP:5210278
name: Unusual infectious osteomyelitis
def: "Increased susceptibility to osteomyelitis of infectious aetiology, as manifested by recurrent or severe bone infection, multifocal osteomyelitis, or osteomyelitis caused by an atypical or opportunistic organism." []
comment: Recurrent or multifocal osteomyelitis is a characteristic manifestation of various diseases, such as chronic granulomatous disease, phagocyte defects, innate signaling defects (such as MyD88 or IRAK4 deficiency), IFN-gamma pathway defects, and humoral immunodeficiencies (such as XLA).
