[Term]
id: HP:5210326
name: Chronic SARS-CoV-2 infection
def: "A persistent SARS-CoV-2 infection with prolonged active viral replication and continuous detection of virus beyond the typical duration of acute COVID-19, typically lasting several weeks or longer, often with culturable virus and intra-host viral evolution. A chronic COVID-19 infection is distinct from post-acute sequelae of SARS-CoV-2 infection (long COVID), which represents a post-infectious syndrome after viral clearance, and from recurrent COVID-19 reinfections, which are common in the general population." []
comment: A chronic COVID-19 infection can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, particularly in B-cell-depleted patients (following rituximab, anti-CD20 therapy, CAR-T cell therapy, or hematopoietic stem cell transplantation), antibody deficiencies, and combined immunodeficiencies.
synonym: "Chronic COVID-19" EXACT []
synonym: "Persistent COVID-19" EXACT []
synonym: "Persistent SARS-CoV-2 infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Protracted COVID-19" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034317 {xref="PMID:34796242", xref="PMID:36407883", xref="PMID:39039440"} ! Unusual viral infection
