[Term]
id: HP:5210331
name: Unusual HHV8 infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to human herpesvirus 8 (HHV-8) infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with HHV-8, or occurring in an unusual anatomical location." []
comment: Unusual or severe HHV-8 infections, including Kaposi sarcoma, are primarily associated with severe T-cell deficiencies (both primary and secondary) and CD4 T-cell lymphopenia. This phenotype has also been specifically described in cases of Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome.
synonym: "Unusual Kaposi's sarcoma-associated herpesvirus infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033432 ! Opportunistic viral infection
