[Term]
id: HP:5210332
name: BK virus nephropathy
def: "Nephropathy caused by BK polyomavirus infection that occurs in the context of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
comment: BK virus nephropathy is an opportunistic manifestation characteristic of solid organ transplant recipients (particularly renal transplant) and hematopoietic stem cell transplant patients, presenting with progressive renal dysfunction and tubulointerstitial nephritis.
synonym: "BK nephropathy" EXACT []
