[Term]
id: HP:5210333
name: BK virus encephalitis
def: "Encephalitis caused by BK polyomavirus infection that occurs in the context of unusual susceptibility to infection." []
comment: BK virus encephalitis is a rare opportunistic CNS manifestation typically seen in severe T-cell deficiencies and post-transplant patients. It may also present as Progressive Multifocal Leukoencephalopathy (PML), involving either BK or JC polyomavirus, and has been specifically described in cases of Hyper-IgM syndrome and DOCK8 deficiency. Clinical presentations often include altered consciousness, seizures, or focal neurological deficits.
synonym: "BK encephalitis" EXACT []
synonym: "Encephalitis caused by a Human polyomavirus 1 infection" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0033993 ! Viral encephalitis
is_a: HP:5210104 ! Unusual BK virus infection
