[Term]
id: HP:5210371
name: Pulmonary cryptococcosis
def: "An infection of the lungs caused by Cryptococcus species, which is the most common entry portal for cryptococcal disease and may present as nodules, consolidation, or interstitial infiltrates." []
comment: A pulmonary cryptococcosis can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, particularly in severe T-cell deficiencies, idiopathic CD4 lymphopenia, and anti-GM-CSF autoantibody syndromes.
synonym: "Cryptococcus lung infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Lung cryptococcosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Pulmonary cryptococcal infection" EXACT []
