[Term]
id: HP:5210377
name: Increased CD4+ TEMRA T cell proportion
def: "An abnormally increased proportion of CD4-positive TEMRA T cells (terminally differentiated effector memory T cells re-expressing CD45RA), relative to total CD4-positive T cells in the blood. These cells have a CD45RA-positive, CD45RO-negative, CCR7-negative phenotype." []
xref: PMID:34860194
is_a: HP:0410379 ! Abnormal memory CD4+ T cell proportion
