[Term]
id: HP:5210378
name: Unusual mold infection
def: "An increased susceptibility to mould infection, as manifested by a recurrent or severe invasive infection with filamentous fungi other than Aspergillus, or by a mould infection caused by an atypical or opportunistic organism. Common causative organisms include Fusarium species, Scedosporium species, and Lomentospora prolificans." []
comment: An invasive mould infection most often occurs in the context of severe immunocompromise, particularly in prolonged neutropenia and post-hematopoietic-stem-cell-transplant patients.
synonym: "Unusual filamentous fungal infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual Fusarium infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual invasive mould infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual Lomentospora prolificans infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual mould infection" EXACT uk_spelling []
synonym: "Unusual non-Aspergillus mould infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual Scedosporium infection" EXACT []
synonym: "Unusual susceptibility to moulds" EXACT []
