id: HP:5210400
name: Chronic poliovirus excretion
def: "A chronic shedding of poliovirus in stool over an extended period, typically following vaccination with live attenuated oral poliovirus vaccine, with viral excretion persisting for months or years. A chronic poliovirus excretion is characteristic of antibody deficiencies including X-linked agammaglobulinaemia and common variable immunodeficiency, in which patients may shed vaccine-derived poliovirus indefinitely." []
