[Term]
id: HP:5210408
name: BCG-associated disease
def: "An adverse disease following vaccination with the Bacillus Calmette-Guérin (BCG) live attenuated Mycobacterium bovis vaccine, ranging from local BCGitis (regional lymphadenitis or injection-site abscess) to disseminated BCGosis. BCG associated disease can be a manifestation of unusual susceptibility to infection, particularly in severe combined immunodeficiency, Mendelian susceptibility to mycobacterial disease (MSMD), and chronic granulomatous disease." []
synonym: "Adverse reaction to BCG vaccination" EXACT []
synonym: "BCG vaccine adverse event" EXACT []
synonym: "BCG-itis" EXACT []
synonym: "BCG-osis" EXACT []
