property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-14T12:47:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000024
name: Synesthesia
def: "A phenomenon whereby stimulation of one sensory or cognitive pathway leads to automatic, involuntary experiences in a second sensory or cognitive pathway. For instance, people with synaesthesia may experience unusual colors, tastes, and other sensations when engaged in everyday activities like reading or listening to music." [PMID:32114456]
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Abnormality of mental function
