property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T12:37:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000031
name: Phaeohyphomycosis
def: "Phaeohyphomycosis refers to infections due to a large group of heterogenous organisms called dematiaceous or melanized fungi. These fungi are distinguished by the predominance of melanin in their cell walls, which likely acts as a virulence factor. Virtually, everyone is exposed to dematiaceous fungi through inhalation, as they are ubiquitous in the environment, although the development of infection is extremely uncommon." [PMID:28217468, PMID:36377664]
comment: Invasive disease is rare but remains important due to the ability to cause serious disease in immunocompetent and immunocompromised hosts, unlike other fungal infections such as aspergillosis.
is_a: HP:0032255 ! Opportunistic fungal infection
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10251
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6310-0434
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T12:37:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000032
name: Autophony
def: "Hearing one's own voice resonating loudly in the ear." [PMID:31750425, PMID:34993986]
is_a: HP:0000364 ! Hearing abnormality
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10143
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T12:37:45Z" xsd:dateTime

