[Term]
id: HP:6000039
name: Pulsatile liver
def: "Cardiac synchronous pulsation on palpation." [PMID:8427187]
comment: A pulsating liver is characteristic of significant tricuspid regurgitation. Systolic pulsations of the liver in patients with primary severe tricuspid regurgitation are due to transmission of a prominent right atrial v wave.
is_a: HP:0031865 ! Abnormal liver physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10266
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T12:37:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000040
name: Neuropathic pain
def: "Neuropathic pain is triggered by lesions to the somatosensory nervous system that alter its structure and function so that pain occurs spontaneously and responses to noxious and innocuous stimuli are pathologically amplified." [PMID:19400724]
comment: Neuropathic pain can be characterized by pain that is triggered when clothes touch the skin, spontaneous burning that feels like boiling water, bursts of pins and needles(paresthesias) in the feet upon walking , a continuous crushing pain after an amputation as if your phantom foot is being squeezed, or a band of searing pain around the body at the level at whichsensation was lost after a spinal cord injury.
is_a: HP:0025280 ! Pain characteristic
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10141
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T15:12:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000041
name: Repeated cold water exposure
def: "A history of repeated exposure to cold water, as may result, for instance, from surfing, diving, kayaking, or swimming." []
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10142
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T15:12:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000042
name: Tinnitus exacerbated by swallowing
def: "Tinnitus (sound heard by a subjhect when no corresponding external sound is present) that is made worse by swallowing." [PMID:30085597]
comment: During swallowing, the tensor veli palatini (TVP) muscle is activated to assist in elevating the palate. Due to this dual innervation by CNV, the tensor tympani (TT) muscle can be activated and possibly cause tinnitus in some patients.
is_a: HP:0025285 ! Aggravated by
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10145
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T15:12:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000043
name: Rhythmic movements of the tympanic membrane
def: "Regularly occurring motion of the tympanic membrane (eardrum), which is located between the inner and middle ear. This can be a manifestation of tensor tympani myoclonus, which can also be ascertained as sawtooth patterns on long-term tympanometry." [PMID:30085597]
is_a: HP:0031704 ! Abnormal ear physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10146
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T15:12:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000044
name: Elongated temporal styloid process
def: "The length of the temporal styloid process is above the upper limit of normal. The styloid process is a cylindrical, slender, needle-like projection of varying lengths averaging 2 to 3 cm. The styloid process projects from the inferior part of the petrous temporal bone and offers attachment to the stylohyoid ligament and the stylohyoid, stylopharyngeus, and styloglossus muscles." [PMID:31082019]
synonym: "Temporal styloid process elongated" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0009911 ! Abnormal temporal bone morphology
