[Term]
id: HP:6000053
name: Snowstorm pattern of uterus on ultrasound
def: "A sonographic snowstorm pattern of the uterus that results from the presence of a complex vesicular intrauterine mass containing many grape-like cysts." [PMID:23599844]
comment: The snowstorm sign is the classic appearance of a complete hydatiform mole. The sign results from multiple hydropic villi and has the ultrasonographic appearance of a central heterogeneous mass with a solid, hyperechoic area together with numerous cystic areas and filling the entire uterine cavity.
is_a: HP:0031105 ! Abnormal uterus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10120
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-28T15:12:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000054
name: Multiparity
def: "History of multiple previous births." []
is_a: HP:0032467 ! Past obstetric history
