[Term]
id: HP:6000061
name: Vaginal passage of hydatidiform mole tissue
def: "Passage from the vagina of hyatidiform tissue, appearing as clusters of vesicles (similar to small grapes) developed from the transformation of chorionic villi. This is a manifestation of a molar pregnancy (hyatidiform mole)." [PMID:29083593]
