[Term]
id: HP:6000095
name: Draining sinus tract in skin
def: "A sinus tract is an abnormal channel that originates from the skin or a mucous surface to a deep-seated focus of suppuration." [PMID:34145466]
comment: A soft tissue ulcer can show a sinus tract leading to a deeper soft tissue abscess and may occasionally extend to a joint. Chronic osteomyelitis can be associated with a sinus tract and cloaca (opening or rupture of bony cortex overlying an area of osteomyelitis) draining granulation tissue, pus, or necrotic debris from the bone to the skin.
synonym: "Discharging sinus" EXACT []
synonym: "Draining tract in skin" EXACT []
synonym: "Tract under skin draining associated abscess" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9996
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2023-12-31T08:27:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000096
name: Corneal transplant history
def: "Past medical history of surgical replacement of the cornea with corneal tissue from a donor." []
synonym: "History of corneal transplantation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430103 ! Past surgical history
