[Term]
id: HP:6000149
name: Reduced in vitro contracture test threshold
def: "The in vitro contracture test determines the sensitivity of freshly obtained skeletal muscle specimens to caffeine or halothane applied to a bathing solution. Muscles from persons susceptible to malignant hyperthermia have lower contracture thresholds for these agents than do normal muscle." [PMID:1833602]
synonym: "Caffeine in vitro contracture test positive" EXACT []
synonym: "Halothane in vitro contracture test positive" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011804 ! Abnormal muscle physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9050
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-07T13:13:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000150
name: Reduced F-wave amplitude
def: "Reduced strength (amplitude) of the F-wave, which is an electrophysiological artifact produced by antidromic activation of motoneurons following distal electrical stimulation of motor nerve fibers." [PMID:17334607]
comment: Because F-waves traverse the entire length of a peripheral nerve between the spinal cord and muscle, F-waves provide a means of examining transmission between stimulation sites in the arm and the leg and the related motoneurons in the cervical and lumbosacral cord. The F-wave is so named because it was originally studied in the small muscles of the foot. It is one of several responses that may follow the direct motor (M) response evoked by electrical stimulation of mixed or motor nerves.
is_a: HP:0030179 ! Abnormal peripheral action potential amplitude
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9052
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-07T13:13:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000151
name: Enlarged peroxisomes
def: "Abnormal increase in size of peroxisomes." [PMID:2894756]
comment: See figure 2 of PMID:2894756.
synonym: "Peroxisomal enlargement" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034552 ! Abnormal peroxisomal morphology
