property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-07T13:13:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000152
name: Adrenocortical hyperplasia
def: "A non-malignant growth, or enlargement, of the adrenal glands, specifically the cortex, although the cortex cannot be definitively identified by conventional imaging. Adrenal cortical hyperplasia is defined radiologically as a non-malignant growth, or enlargement, of the adrenal glands." [PMID:28707538]
comment: Controlled by the pituitary gland, the adrenal cortex drives critical processes, such as the production of cortisol, mineralocorticoid and sex hormones. Any disruption in the multiple enzymes and hormones involved in these pathways may cause serious or life-threatening symptoms, often associated with anatomical changes in the adrenal glands.
is_a: HP:0000849 ! Adrenocortical abnormality
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9200
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-08T08:51:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000153
name: Lymphocytic infiltration of the parotid gland
def: "Accumulation of lymphocytes in the parotid gland. This feature is generally defined as a count of lymphocytes per area that is above normal limits on histopathological examination." []
