id: HP:6000184
name: Filum terminale lipoma
def: "Filum terminale lipomas (FTLs) are a type of lumbosacral lipoma in which the fat is entirely within the filum terminale and separate from the conus medullaris." [PMID:24628511]
comment: Filum terminale lipomas (FTL) are occasionally associated with tethered cord syndrome, and some authors have advocated for prophylactic sectioning of the filum terminale when an FTL is identified. With the increasing use of MRI, FTLs have been identified more frequently in asymptomatic individuals.
synonym: "Fatty filum terminale" EXACT []
synonym: "LFT" EXACT abbreviation []
synonym: "Lipoma of filum terminale" EXACT []
synonym: "Lipoma of the filum terminale" EXACT []
is_a: HP:6000590 ! Spinal lipoma
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7713
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-22T05:48:12Z" xsd:dateTime

