[Term]
id: HP:6000190
name: Abnormal seminal vesicle morphology
def: "A structural abnormality of the seminal vesicle. The seminal vesicles are a pair of glands that also include the prostate gland and the bulbourethral glands and are located in the pelvis superior to the rectum, inferior to the fundus of the bladder and posterior to the prostate. The seminal vesicles contribute around 70% of the fluid that will eventually become semen." [PMID:29763029]
is_a: HP:0000022 ! Abnormal male internal genitalia morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10270
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-25T09:04:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000191
name: Seminal vesicle cyst
def: "A cyst (sac-like mass that may contain serous liquid or semisolid material) caused by distention of the seminal vesicle due to atresia of the ejaculatory duct." [PMID:31024871, PMID:9829485]
comment: Congenital seminal vesical cysts are caused by altered development of the mesonephric (Wolffian) duct. They are often associated with abnormal development of other ipsilateral mesonephric derivatives, such as vas deferens, kidney, and ureter.
is_a: HP:6000190 ! Abnormal seminal vesicle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10270
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-01-25T09:04:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000192
name: Silica dust exposure
def: "History of exposure to respirable crystalline silica (SiO2)." [PMID:22529751]
comment: Silicosis is a well known consequence of silica dust exposure, and exposure has also been associated with the risk of lung cancer, pulmonary tuberculosis, and other airway diseases.
