id: HP:6000292
name: Elevated tissue sphingomyelin concentration
def: "Concentration of sphoingomyelin in tissues above the upper limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0034370 ! Abnormal muscle tissue metabolite concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9061
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-10T18:56:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000293
name: History of recent iodated contrast medium administration
def: "Medical history of recent iodinated or radioiodine contrast use." [PMID:23148056, PMID:33948409]
comment: Iodinated contrast media commonly used in various radiologic examinations and interventional procedures results in massive iodide exposure to the thyroid gland. Whereas people with normal thyroids usually experience no ill effects, those with pre-existing thyroid disease may experience thyrotoxicosis (often referred to as thyroid storm in this context), which, if unrecognized, could lead to serious, potentially life-threatening consequences, including atrial arrhythmias, heart failure, pulmonary arterial hypertension, cerebrovascular and pulmonary embolism, and cardiomyopathy.
is_a: HP:4000144 ! Recent past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9815
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T09:36:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000294
name: Difficulty passing nasogastric tube
def: "Difficulty inserting a nasogastric tube (NGT), a flexible plastic tube that is placed through the nose and esophagus into the stomach and used to administer drugs or for feeding. There are certain circumstances that may make NGT insertion difficult. They are esophageal narrowing, comatose or intubated patients, and patients who have sustained severe facial or skull injuries." [PMID:2917506]
is_a: HP:0430103 ! Past surgical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9817
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T09:36:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000295
name: Persistent falcine venous sinus
def: "A falcine sinus that does not involute but persists beyond birth is defined as a persistent falcine sinus. In the 20-mm embryo stage, the primitive falx cerebri contains the sagittal plexus, a meshwork of anastomotic venous channels from which the superior sagittal sinus and straight sinus are thought to develop. A persistent falcine sinus represents a persistent channel of the caudal anastomotic loops of the sagittal plexus." [PMID:19779000]
is_a: HP:0033723 ! Abnormal cerebral venous sinus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9866
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T09:36:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000296
name: Penis uncircumcised
def: "A medical history in a male of not having been circumcized." [PMID:25011345]
comment: Neonatal male circumcision is a common surgical procedure.
synonym: "Foreskin present" EXACT []
synonym: "Prepuce present" EXACT []
