property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T09:36:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000305
name: Proximal to distal progression
def: "Refers to symptomatology that begins in the proximal limbs and subsequently affects the distal limbs." []
is_a: HP:0011008 ! Temporal pattern
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9922
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T09:36:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000306
name: Autonomic-voluntary dissociation of facial movements
def: "The selective paralysis of voluntary fascio-pharyngo-glosso-masticatory movements with preservation of reflexive and automatic functions is referred to as autonomic-voluntary dissociation, which is a distinctive feature of Anterior opercular syndrome (also known as Foix-Chavany-Marie syndrome)." [PMID:23809752]
comment: The patient cannot open or close the mouth, protrude the tongue or close the eyes to orders, but can smile, cry, yell or yawn automatically. Ischemia is the most frequent cause and it is generally due to bilateral opercular lesions, but bilateral subcortical lesions have also been reported. In the anterior opercular syndrome the connections be-tween the motor cortex and the V, VII, IX, XII cranial nuclei and brainstem are interrupted bilaterally. Emotional and spontaneous movements, dependent on extrapyramidal connections, thalamus and hypothalamus, are preserved (automatic-voluntary dissociation).
is_a: HP:0012638 ! Abnormal nervous system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7803
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000307
name: Jaw mass
def: "A swelling or enlargement localized to the jaw. The word mass is usually used at an early stage of the diagnostic workup before the precise nature of the swelling has been determined." []
is_a: HP:0030791 ! Abnormal jaw morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7821
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000308
name: Excessive nocturnal light exposure
def: "Exposure to continuous light at night, including night-shift work or a nocturnal lifestyle." [PMID:34903129]
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7839
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000309
name: Menstruating female between menarche and menopause
def: "Past medical history of a woman who is menstruating, i.e., not premenstrual or post-menopause." []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7855
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000310
name: Preterm premature rupture of membranes
def: "PPROM (preterm premature rupture of membranes) occurs at less than 37 weeks of gestation. PPROM can happen spontaneously, during preterm labor, or following a procedure such as amniocentesis." [PMID:15167875]
synonym: "PPROM" EXACT [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp#abbreviation]
is_a: HP:0001788 ! Premature rupture of membranes
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7862
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000311
name: History of abdominal surgery
def: "A past medical history that indicates that the patient had a surgical procedure involving the abdomen." []
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7882
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000312
name: Thickened Descemet membrane
def: "The thickness of the Descement membrane is above the upper limit of normal." []
synonym: "Thick Descemet membrane" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011490 ! Abnormal Descemet membrane morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7582
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000313
name: Incomplete right bundle branch block
def: "Right bundle branch block (RBBB) represents an abnormality in the intraventricular electrical conduction system of the human heart, generating enlarged QRS and modified vectors on the electrocardiogram (ECG). Incomplete RBBB (IRBBB) is defined by (i) QRS duration between 110 and 120 ms in adults; (ii) rsr, rsR, or rSR in leads V1 or V2. The R or r deflection is usually wider than the initial R wave. In a minority of patients, a wide and often notched R wave pattern may be seen in leads V1 and/or V2; (iii) S wave of greater duration than R wave or greater than 40 ms in leads I and V6 in adults; and (iv) Normal R peak time in leads V5 and V6 but greater than 50 ms in lead V1. The first 3 criteria should be present to make the diagnosis. When a pure dominant R wave with or without a notch is present in V1, criterion 4 should be satisfied." [PMID:34100724]
comment: Right bundle branch block appears with a prevalence of 3% to 7% in the general population, more frequently in men than in women.
is_a: HP:0011710 ! Bundle branch block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7585
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000314
name: Perimenopausal onset
def: "Onset of signs or symptoms of disease during the period of a woman's life shortly before the occurrence of the menopause." []
is_a: HP:0003674 ! Onset
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7603
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000315
name: Postmenopausal onset
def: "Onset of signs or symptoms of disease during the period of a woman's life after the occurrence of the menopause." []
is_a: HP:0003674 ! Onset
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7603
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000316
name: Spastic monoplegia
def: "Spastic weakness found in only one upper or lower extremity." [PMID:24111874]
is_a: HP:0034353 ! Appendicular spasticity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7653
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000317
name: Mosaic attenuation pattern in lung
def: "Mosaic attenuation pattern in the lung is a term used to describe regions of differing pulmonary attenuation on CT imaging. It is a non-specific finding, although is associated with several conditions such as obstructive small airway disease, occlusive vascular disease (in which case is called mosaic perfusion pattern), pulmonary edema, and parenchymal diseases." []
is_a: HP:0031983 ! Abnormal pulmonary thoracic imaging finding
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7702
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4095-8489
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000318
name: Elevated aldosterone:renin ratio
def: "The ratio of aldosterone concentration to renin concentration is above the upper limit of normal. If aldosterone is expressed in ng/dl and plasma renin activity is expressed as ng/ml/hr, then values above 20 with aldosterone level above 15 are considered indicative of primary aldosteronism." [PMID:25907736]
is_a: HP:0000847 ! Abnormality of renin-angiotensin system
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7772
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000319
name: Meteorism
def: "An increase in the gas content inside the bowel associated with distension of the abdomen and hydroaeric noises. The most common symptom of meteorism is a bloated sensation. It may be associated with abdominal discomfort. Some individuals may also complain of a distended stomach and excessive belching and/or passage of flatus." [PMID:28613601]
is_a: HP:0011458 ! Abdominal symptom
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7773
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000320
name: Failure to elevate ammonia on ischemic exercise
def: "Normal subjects display an increase in the concentration of ammonia in the blood following an ischemic exercise test. This term refers to an increase in ammonia that is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:3476851]
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7775
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000321
name: Labile Hypertension
def: "Frequent fluctuations of blood pressure between normal and high levels, changing more dramatically than normal." []
comment: It is normal for BP to fluctuate from moment to moment and from day to day. BP fluctuation is related to many factors such as physical activity, emotion, position, respiratory cycle, diet, salt intake, alcohol ingestion, sleep deprivation, and others. Even in otherwise normotensive individuals, BP fluctuation can be substantial during moments of physical or emotional stress or even without overt provocation.
is_a: HP:0000822 ! Hypertension
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7777
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000322
name: Absent axon flare response after intradermal histamine injection
def: "The axon reflex (also known as the flare response) is a response that is stimulated by peripheral nerves of the body that travels away from the nerve cell body and branches to stimulate target organs. In the human skin, there are three different phenomena mediated by axon reflex mechanism; flare, sweating and pilomotion. Stroking or intradermal injection of histamine or substance P into the human skin pro- duces widespread vasodilatation (flare) and plasma extravasation (wheal). This term refers to the failure of intradermal hista injection to elicit flare." [PMID:2456128]
is_a: HP:0032120 ! Abnormal peripheral nervous system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7778
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000323
name: Reduced sympathoneural responses to the cold pressor test
def: "Response to the cold pressor test below the lower limit of normal. The cold pressor test is a simple and validated test in which the subject immerses one hand or foot into ice water for 1 to 3 minutes while blood pressure (BP) and heart rate are monitored. The cold stimulus activates afferent sensory pathways that, in turn, trigger a sympathetic response resulting in an increase in BP." [PMID:33712946]
is_a: HP:0012332 ! Abnormal autonomic nervous system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7779
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T10:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000324
name: Positive stool Giardia antigen test
def: "Fecal analysis for Giardia antigen is abnormal. Tests include direct fluorescent-antibody (DFA), which detects intact organisms, and enzyme immunoassays (EIAs), which detect soluble stool antigens." [PMID:12574257]
is_a: HP:0034866 ! Positive stool infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7921
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000325
name: Excessive blood loss during delivery
def: "Loss of a substantial amount of blood during delivery (some definitions stipulate 1000 ml or more), typically associated with manifestations such as low blood pressure, a rapid heart rate, dizziness, light-headedness, fatigue, and weakness." [PMID:33913640]
is_a: HP:0032467 ! Past obstetric history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7788
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000326
name: Cardiac valve vegetations
def: "Endocarditis infection occurs along the edges of the heart valves. Damage to the cardiac endothelium followed by platelet and fibrin deposition results in a sterile lesion known as nonbacterial thrombotic endocarditis (NBTE) or vegetation. Microbes entering the bloodstream via routine or invasive procedures adhere to the vegetation and are engulfed in an outer meshwork of fibrin and platelets. Subsequent rapid microbial multiplication in a protected area of impaired host defense leads to vegetation growth and continuous bacteremia." [PMID:17678415]
is_a: HP:0001654 ! Abnormal heart valve morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7790
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000327
name: Thoracic cage flatness
def: "The anteroposterior dimension of the chest on the lateral radiograph is often relatively narrow compared with the chest width on the frontal radiograph." [PMID:3500611]
synonym: "Flat chest" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001547 ! Abnormal rib cage morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7791
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000328
name: Absent zona pellucida
def: "Lack of the oocyte extracellular matrix region (zona pellucida). This feature can be observed following follicular aspiration (retrieval of eggs for fertility treatments)." [PMID:24670168]
comment: During in vitro fertilization treatment, oocyte retrieval is performed after ovarian stimulation via vaginal puncture. Cumulus-oocyte complexes, which consist of cumulus cells surrounding the centrally located oocyte, are isolated from the individual's follicular fluid. This term refers to the finding of oocytes lacking zonae pellucidae.
is_a: HP:0020156 ! Abnormal zona pellucida morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7394
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000329
name: Umbilical cord prolapse
def: "The presence of the umbilical cord (UC) between the fetal presenting part and the cervix, regardless of the membrane status (intact or ruptured). Descent of the UC through the cervix is essential for diagnosing cord prolapse. It can be either overt (past the presenting part) or occult (alongside the presenting part)." [PMID:31194398]
is_a: HP:0010881 ! Abnormality of the umbilical cord
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7462
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-9157
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000330
name: Increased ratio of deoxypyridinoline to pyridinoline cross-links in urine
def: "The relative concentration of deoxypyridinoline (Dpyr) to that of pyridinoline (Pyr) cross-links in urine is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:20301635]
comment: Detection of an increased ratio of deoxypyridinoline (Dpyr) to pyridinoline (Pyr) cross-links in urine quantitated by high-performance liquid chromatography is a highly sensitive and specific test for PLOD1-related kyphoscoliotic Ehlers-Danlos syndrome. The normal ratio of Dpyr:Pyr cross-links is approximately 0.2, whereas in kyphoscoliotic EDS the ratio is approximately 6.0.
is_a: HP:0033384 ! Elevated urinary collagen degradation products
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8800
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000331
name: Elevated urinary thymine level
def: "The amount of thymine in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." []
is_a: HP:0033162 ! Abnormal urinary pyrimidine level
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8801
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000332
name: Elevated urinary indoleacetic acid level
def: "The amount of indoleacetic acid in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:4228120]
is_a: HP:0040156 ! Elevated urinary carboxylic acid
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8824
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-11T16:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000333
name: Reduced hepatic phosphorylase kinase activity
def: "Activity of phosphorylase kinase in liver tissue below the lower limit of normal. Phosphorylase kinase (PhK) has a major regulatory role in the breakdown of glycogen. The enzyme PhK comprises four copies each of four subunits, encoded by PHKA1, PHKA2, PHKB, and PHKG." [PMID:21634085]
comment: Phosphorylase kinase (PhK) deficiency causing glycogen storage disease type IX (GSD IX) results from deficiency of the enzyme phosphorylase b kinase, which has a major regulatory role in the breakdown of glycogen. While liver biopsy or muscle biopsy was done routinely in previous years to measure PhK activity, the availability of molecular genetic testing has reduced the need for such invasive procedures.
synonym: "Decreased hepatic phosphorylase kinase activity" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034685 ! Abnormal liver enzyme activity or concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9194
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-12T08:07:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000334
name: Reduced hepatic ornithine transcarbamylase activity
def: "Activity or concentration of ornithine transcarbamylase in the liver below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:6733950]
is_a: HP:0034685 ! Abnormal liver enzyme activity or concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9216
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-12T08:07:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000335
name: Elevated urinary quinolinic acid level
def: "The amount of quinolinic acid in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal. Quinolinic acids is a pyridinedicarboxylic acid that is pyridine substituted by carboxy groups at positions 2 and 3. It is a metabolite of tryptophan." [PMID:29517768]
is_a: HP:0033162 ! Abnormal urinary pyrimidine level
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8652
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000336
name: Rectal duplication
def: "A developmental anomaly characterized by an additional rectum that is typically lined with intestinal mucosa with one or more cell types of the gastrointestinal tract overlying submucosa and smooth muscle layer." [PMID:26691370]
is_a: HP:0002034 ! Abnormal rectum morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8654
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000337
name: Thinned small intestinal mucosa
def: "Abrnormal reduction in the height of the mucosa of the small intestine. The mucosa is arranged in regular circular folds (the circular valves of Kerckrin), the mucosal surface is covered with small projections called villi, which are slender, about 1.5-2 mm long projections of the mucosa into the lumen. In between the villi are the crypts. This term refers to a pathological thinning of these structures." []
is_a: HP:0025129 ! Abnormal small intestinal mucosa morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8664
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000338
name: Seminal vesicle hypoplasia
def: "A congenital anomaly characterized by underdevelopment of one or both seminal vesicles, which are the two small glands that store and produce the majority of the fluid that makes up semen." []
is_a: HP:6000190 ! Abnormal seminal vesicle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8682
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000339
name: Decreased fetal abdominal circumference
def: "The distance around the abdomen of a fetus, generally as measured by prenatal sonography, is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:30646865]
comment: This finding may be associated with fetal growth restriction.
synonym: "Small fetal abdominal circumference" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020303 ! Abnormal fetal abdominal circumference
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8684
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000340
name: Prenatal flattened diaphragm
def: "The diaphragm normally projects up into the thoracic cavity. In the presence of malformations such as enlarged lungs, the diaphragm may appear abnormally flat or even everted (with the middle of the diaphragm projecting downwards into the abdominal cavity)." [PMID:30319217]
comment: Serr Figures 1 and 2 of PMID:30319217.
is_a: HP:0034243 ! Abnormal fetal pulmonary morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8686
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000341
name: Snowflake effect in amniotic cavity
def: "Dense floating particles in amniotic fluid, said to resemble snowflakes. This finding can result from shedding of the epidermis in conditions such as Harlequin ichthyosis." [PMID:33569485]
comment: See Figure 1A of PMID:33569485.
synonym: "Snowflake sign" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001560 ! Abnormality of the amniotic fluid
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8693
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000342
name: Thickened mitral valve cusp
def: "An abnormally increased thickness of a leaflet of the mitral valve." []
is_a: HP:0031480 ! Abnormal mitral valve leaflet morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8702
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000343
name: Antiparietal cell antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the serum that react against parietal cell antigens." [PMID:34913949]
comment: This finding may be observed in autoimmune gastritis.
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8704
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000344
name: Anti-intrinsic factor antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that react against intrinsic factor." [PMID:34913949]
comment: This finding may be observed in autoimmune gastritis.
