[Term]
id: HP:6000348
name: Antistreptolysin O antibody positivity
def: "The presence of antibodies in the blood circulation that react against streptolysin O." []
comment: Antistreptolysin O (ASO) is an antibody against streptolysin O that is generally produced by Group A Streptococcus (GAS). GAS causes a diverse range of human infections, like pharyngitis, cellulitis, scarlet fever, and others. Moreover, a GAS infection can trigger postinfectious immune-mediated disorders, including acute poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis, acute rheumatic fever, and rheumatic heart disease.
is_a: HP:0430061 ! Bloodstream antibacterial antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8712
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-20T09:54:55Z" xsd:dateTime

