id: HP:6000361
name: Reduced succinyl-CoA:3-oxoacid-CoA transferase activity in cultured fibroblasts
def: "Activity of succinyl-CoA:3-oxoacid-CoA transferase (SCOT, or OXCT1; EC 2.8.3.5) below the lower limit of normal in cultured fibroblasts." [PMID:11757586]
is_a: HP:4000195 ! Abnormal enzyme activity in cultured fibroblasts
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7935
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T10:53:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000362
name: Blunted aldosterone response to aldosterone suppression test
def: "A non-suppressible aldosterone excess, defined as an abnormal result of one of any four suppression tests. These tests use oral sodium loading, oral fludrocortisone, oral captopril, or saline infusion to suppress aldosterone secretion." [PMID:20482833]
comment: For instance, the sral sodium loading test involves increasing sodium intake to over 200 mmol/d for 3 days and determining urinary aldosterone from the morning of day 3 to the morning of day 4. The test is abnormal if the amount of urinary aldosterone is above the upper limit of normal. An abnormal test result generally indicates primary aldosteronism.
is_a: HP:0031073 ! Abnormal response to endocrine stimulation test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7954
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T10:53:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000363
name: Flank mass
def: "An abnormal enlargement or swelling in the flank, which is the fleshy part of the side of the body between the ribs and the hip." []
is_a: HP:0001438 ! Abnormal abdomen morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7956
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
