[Term]
id: HP:6000376
name: Jugular foramen stenosis
def: "Reduction in diameter of the jugular foramen, an opening in the base of the skull that is located behind the carotid canal and is formed by the temporal bone and the occipital bone. The inferior petrosal sinus, three cranial nerves, the sigmoid sinus, and meningeal arteries pass through the jugular foramen." [PMID:17236138]
is_a: HP:0002693 ! Abnormal skull base morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8966
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000377
name: Intramural intestinal gas
def: "The presence of extraluminal gas within the bowel wall." [PMID:25400871]
comment: In a symptomatic postoperative patient such a finding on plain radiology or computerized tomography (CT) is often viewed as a signal of impending or actual acute mesenteric ischaemia especially when associated with portal venous gas.
synonym: "Pneumatosis intestinalis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002242 ! Abnormal intestine morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8968
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000378
name: Delayed scintigraphic gallbladder filling
def: "Hepatobiliary scintigraphy is a nuclear imaging technique that permits evaluation of the liver and biliary system for acute and chronic cholecystitis, biliary atresia, biliary obstruction, and post-surgical biliary leak. With this investigation, a radiotracer is administered intravenously, bound to albumin, transported to the liver, and excreted into the biliary system. This term refers to a longer than normal time for the radiotracer to be visualized in the gallbladder. This finding may be a sign of chronic gallbladder disease or partial obstruction of the common bile duct." [PMID:30855831]
is_a: HP:0012438 ! Abnormal gallbladder physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8969
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000379
name: Pancreatic arteriovenous malformation
def: "Pancreatic arteriovenous malformation is defined as an abnormal vascular net, developed from one or more feeding arteries and enlarged early draining veins, creating an arteriovenous shunting." [PMID:29904461]
is_a: HP:0012090 ! Abnormal pancreas morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8970
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000380
name: Anti-perilipin-1 antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the serum that react against perilipin-1 (PLIN1)." [PMID:30283460, PMID:35709010, PMID:35771980, PMID:36538601]
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8972
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3387-1836
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

