property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000382
name: Short esophagus
def: "Abnormal reduction in the length of the esophagus." [PMID:29262377]
comment: The short esophagus was defined by surgeons as the inability to reduce the gastroesophageal (GE) junction below the diaphragm during surgery, due to inadequate esophageal mobilization. Short esophagus was also defined by endoscopists when the GE junction is positioned in adults at a distance less than 40 cm from the mouth (normal value is approximately 45 cm).
is_a: HP:0002031 ! Abnormal esophagus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8988
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000383
name: Gastric perforation
def: "A full-thickness injury of the wall of the stomach." [PMID:30137838]
synonym: "Gastric rupture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002577 ! Abnormal stomach morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8989
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-02-24T19:28:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000384
name: Gastric volvulus
def: "A gastric volvulus occurs when the stomach rotates on itself at least 180 degrees along its transverse or longitudinal axis." [PMID:29939663]
comment: Gastric strangulation is a complication that can occur after the development of acute gastric volvulus.
is_a: HP:0002577 ! Abnormal stomach morphology
