[Term]
id: HP:6000422
name: Tympanic membrane bulla
def: "Presence of blisters (bullae) on the tympanic membrane, often accompanied by fever, thickening, and erythematous appearance of the tympanic membrane, decreased or absent light reflex, and decreased mobility." [PMID:31971705]
