[Term]
id: HP:6000507
name: Non-pitting edema
def: "Non-pitting edema occurs when excess fluid builds up in the body causing swelling that does not indent when pressure is applied. It usually occurs in the limbs, and often results from underlying medical conditions affecting lymphatic system function." [PMID:32119339]
is_a: HP:0000969 ! Edema
