[Term]
id: HP:6000553
name: Bloodstream Malaria parasite
def: "Presence of malaria parasites in the peripheral blood." [PMID:35255896]
comment: The analysis of thick blood smears (TBS) is the reference method chosen as a first option for the malaria diagnosis worldwide. In this method, after a blood sample is taken and dried, the TBS is stained. After the staining process, the smear is visually analysed by microscopy, where parasites and leukocytes are identified and counted.
is_a: HP:0034523 ! Blood parasite
