property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-03-18T20:19:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000603
name: Elevated urinary 2-methyl-3-hydroxybutyric acid level
def: "The amount of 2-methyl-3-hydroxybutyric acid in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:9700610]
comment: 2-methyl-3-hydroxybutyric acid is a normal urinary metabolite involved in the isoleucine catabolism and is excreted in abnormally high amounts in alpha-methylacetoacetic aciduria.
is_a: HP:0033097 ! Increased urine proteinogenic amino acid derivative level
