[Term]
id: HP:6000630
name: Hypoechoic breast mass
def: "A breast mass visualized by sonography that displays a lower than normal echo signal (and this that appears dark gray in the typical ultrasound image)." [PMID:26576116]
comment: Ultrasonography (US) is an essential tool for evaluating breast masses. Irregular hypoechoic masses on breast ultrasound are usually considered suspicious lesions.
synonym: "Hypoechoic breast nodule" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032408 ! Breast mass
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10113
