[Term]
id: HP:6000671
name: Breast myxoma
def: "A rare, benign mesenchymal tumor of the breast characterized histologically by stellate, round, and spindle-shaped cells with vesicular nuclei and scant cytoplasm that are scattered in the myxoid stroma." [PMID:17214801]
