id: HP:6000709
name: Absent Bell phenomenon
def: "The Bell phenomenon is the reflex upward movement of the front of the eyeball when the eyelids close (or blink). It protects the eye by helping to keep the cornea moist. This term refers to a lack of this phenomenon, which can be observed with certain conditions such as congenital fibrosis of the extraocular muscles." [PMID:16815872, PMID:36780505]
synonym: "Absent palpebral-oculogyric reflex" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012547 ! Abnormal involuntary eye movements
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9644
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T15:03:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000710
name: Dalen-Fuchs nodules
def: "Nodules (yellow-white subretinal pigment epithelium lesions) that form between Bruch membrane and the retinal pigment epithelium." [PMID:35145783]
comment: Dalen-Fuchs nodules may be observed with sympathetic ophthalmia, a rare, severe condition that typically presents as bilateral diffuse granulomatous uveitis secondary to trauma in one eye. Dalen-Fuchs nodules could be also observed in Harada disease.
synonym: "Dalen Fuchs nodules" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030506 ! Yellow/white retinal lesion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9657
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T15:03:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000711
name: Triggering by ocular trauma
def: "Applies to a sign or symptom that is provoked or brought about by trauma to the eye." [PMID:30081702, PMID:35647958]
is_a: HP:0031135 ! Triggered by physical trauma
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9658
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T15:03:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000712
name: Gelatinous drop-like dystrophic cornea
def: "Deposition of amyloid material in the subepithelial space of the cornea." [PMID:23038033]
comment: See Figure 2 in PMID:23038033.
is_a: HP:0001131 ! Corneal dystrophy
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9661
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T15:03:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000713
name: Hepatic reticuloendothelial system cell iron deposition
def: "Abnormal accumulation of iron in reticuloendothelial cells of the liver. This feature can be appreciated on liver biopsy by Perls iron stain for granular iron deposition, based on agreement that only discernible hemosiderin granules represent significant iron deposition." [PMID:21274866]
is_a: HP:0040134 ! Abnormal hepatic iron concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9154
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T18:55:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000714
name: Reduced epidermal kindlin-1 expression
def: "Lower than normal amount of kindlin-1 in the epidermis." [PMID:14962093]
comment: In control skin, immunofluorescence labeling with antikindlin-1 antibody shows bright, pan-epidermal staining. In individuals with Kindler syndrome (OMIM 173650), staining is markedly reduced and in some cases absent.
is_a: HP:0034573 ! Abnormal epidermal protein expression
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9173
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T18:55:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000715
name: Central giant cell lesion of the jaw
def: "A benign proliferative and asymptomatic intraosseous lesion of the jaw formed by fibrous tissue that contains multiple focus of hemorrhage and an aggregation of multinucleated giant cells." [PMID:20301316, PMID:28316283, PMID:29988246]
comment: These lesions occur more frequently in the mandible than in the maxilla, and occur more frequently on the right side than on the left side. In the maxilla, the lesion may invade the maxillary sinus floor, the orbit and/or nasal passages, which can lead to facial asymmetry, nasal deviation, and mobility of associated dental elements. CGCLs can be classified as aggressive or non-aggressive.
is_a: HP:0030791 ! Abnormal jaw morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9184
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-08T18:55:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000716
name: Terminal hepatic lobular vascular occlusion
def: "A type of Hepatic venous outflow obstruction characterized by fibrous concentric narrowing of zone 3 terminal hepatic venules, centrilobular hepatocyte necrosis, and sinusoidal congestion, accomapnied by necrosis of pericentral hepatocytes, and narrowing and eventual fibrosis of central veins." [PMID:17461490, PMID:20301448]
comment: Hepatic veno-occlusive disease (VOD) may present with fragmented red blood cells, fibrinogen, and Factor VIII/von Willebrand factor can be demonstrated in the subendothelial space of central veins and perivenular zones of hepatic acini. In the later stages, sinusoidal and venous lumen become obliterated by typeI, III, and IV collagen accompanied by an increase in the stellate cells that line the sinusoids. In some cases, fibrous bridges between central venules are observed.
synonym: "Hepatic sinusoidal obstruction syndrome" EXACT []
synonym: "Hepatic veno-occlusive disease" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0006707 ! Abnormality of the hepatic vasculature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9158
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-09T07:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000717
name: Axonal spheroids
def: "During neurodegeneration, bubble-like swellings form along the length of the axon, a primary and early effect of dynamic axonal deformation. These varicosities, spheroids, or swellings have been described as beads on a string and branches bearing fruit, and they frequently appear on degenerating axons." [PMID:20301718, PMID:34678457]
comment: Axonal spheroids have been found in developmental degeneration and the aging brain, as well as in injury, neuropathy, neuroaxonal dystrophy, and many neurodegenerative diseases. Axonal spheroids can be observed in neurons in a conjunctival biopsy.
is_a: HP:0012757 ! Abnormal neuron morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9239
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-09T07:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000718
name: Decreased liver bile salt export pump expression
def: "Amount of bile salt export pump (BSEP, coded by the ABCB11 gene) in liver tissue below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:20800306, PMID:22795478]
is_a: HP:0034644 ! Abnormal liver metabolite concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9261
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-09T07:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000719
name: Reduced tissue type II iodothyronine deiodinase activity
def: "Concentration or activity of type II iodothyronine deiodinase below the lower limit of normal. The activity can be measured in tissues such as cultured fibroblasts." []
comment: Type II iodothyronine deiodinase is a selenoprotein that catalyzes the 5-prime deiodination of thyroxine (T4) to generate an active thyroid hormone, 3,3-prime,5-triiodothyronine (T3).
is_a: HP:6000231 ! Abnormal tissue enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9306
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-09T07:03:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000720
name: Reduced tissue fatty aldehyde dehydrogenase activity
def: "Activity of fatty aldehyde dehydrogenase (EC 1.2.1.3) in tissues below the lower limit of normal. The activity can be measured in multiple tissues including culutured fibroblasts and leukocytes." [PMID:1939650]
is_a: HP:6000231 ! Abnormal tissue enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8204
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-21T09:58:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000721
name: Decreased circulating pancreatic isoamylase activity
def: "The activity of alpha-Amylase (1,4-alpha-D-glucan-4-glucanohydrolase E. C. 3.2.1.1, pancreatic isoamylase) in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:30675141]
comment: Alpha-Amylase (1,4-alpha-D-glucan-4-glucanohydrolase E. C. 3.2.1.1.) catalyses the hydrolysis of starch, glycogen and related poly- and oligosaccharides. In acute pancreatitis the hyperamylasemia is characterised by an increased activity in plasma of pancreatic isoamylase.
is_a: HP:0012379 ! Abnormal circulating enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8206
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-05-21T09:58:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000722
name: Reduced tissue guanidinoacetate methyltransferase activity
def: "Activity of the mitochondrial enzyme guanidinoacetate methyltransferase in tissues below the lower limit of normal. The activity can be measured in multiple tissues including culutured fibroblasts." [PMID:15651030]
is_a: HP:6000231 ! Abnormal tissue enzyme concentration or activity
