[Term]
id: HP:6000839
name: Horizontal position of testicle
def: "The Bell Clapper deformity is one of the causes for the testicular torsion. In this condition, testis lacks a normal attachment to tunica vaginalis and hangs freely, causing it to sit horizontally rather than vertically in the scrotum." [PMID:22606621]
synonym: "Bell-clapper deformity" EXACT []
