property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000840
name: Localized soft-tissue swelling on extremity
def: "Abnormal enlargement (swelling) that is restricted to a specific part of a limb." []
comment: This term is meant to describe new-onset swelling. For instance, patients with Ewing sarcoma often present with local symptoms such as pain, stiffness, or swelling for a few weeks or months.
is_a: HP:0040064 ! Abnormality of limbs
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7971
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000841
name: Abnormal scleral thickness
def: "Any deviation from the normal height of the sclera, the white part of the eye that forms the tough, fibrous outer layer of the exterior of the eyeball." []
comment: The sclera forms the outer layer of the ocular globe and serves to stabilize size and shape to the eye. Stability of the globe shape is of utmost importance for the optical system which heavily depends on constant distances between cornea, lens and retina. The thickness of the sclera is a major factor in providing a firm structure to the globe.
is_a: HP:0000591 ! Abnormal sclera morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7984
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000842
name: Multiple eyelid beaded papules
def: "Multiple beaded papules along the eyelid margins and inner canthus." [PMID:26655007]
comment: See Figure 2 of PMID:26655007.
synonym: "Moniliform blepharosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000492 ! Abnormal eyelid morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7991
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000843
name: Nonexudative conjunctivitis
def: "A type of conjunctivitis that is not characterized by appreciable exudate, i.e., fluid, cells, or other substances that have escaped from blood vessels and have been deposited around the eyelids." []
is_a: HP:0000509 ! Conjunctivitis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7994
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000844
name: Nematode in retina
def: "Demonstration of a nematode (roundworm) in the retina, generally by an imaging procedure such as fundoscopy." [PMID:2086470]
is_a: HP:0430030 ! Positive infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/7995
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T13:45:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000845
name: Vascular compression of the eighth cranial nerve
def: "A condition in which blood vessels adjacent to the eighth cranial nerve (vestibulocochlear nerve) such as the anterior inferior cerebellar artery abnormally contact or compress the vestibulocochlear nerve as it exits the brainstem or travels within the cerebellopontine angle." [PMID:9452229]
comment: CN VIII consists of 3 components: the cochlear nerve, the superior vestibular nerve, and the inferior vestibular nerve. If the NVC syndrome of CN VIII exists, symptoms specifically reflecting the nerve component affected should be manifested. If compression by a vascular loop is limited to the cochlear nerve alone, tinnitus or a hearing disturbance (or both) should occur, whereas if the compression is limited to the vestibular nerve, vertigo should occur, and if the cochlear nerve and the vestibular nerve are compressed, the patient should experience tinnitus and vertigo at the same time.
synonym: "Neurovascular compression syndrome of the vestibulocochlear nerve" EXACT []
synonym: "Vestibulocochlear nerve compression syndrome" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0009591 ! Abnormal vestibulocochlear nerve morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8896
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T16:38:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000846
name: Beaded bile ducts
def: "Multifocal intra- and extra-hepatic bile duct strictures alternating with normal caliber or slightly dilated segments, resembling beads on a string." [PMID:30600377]
comment: This abnormality can be observed in primary sclerosing cholangitis and can be ascertained by ndoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography (ERCP) or MRCP (magnetic resonance cholangiopancreatography).
is_a: HP:0012440 ! Abnormal biliary tract morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8899
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T16:38:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000847
name: Cardiac mass
def: "An abnormal enlargement or swelling localized in the heart. The word mass is usually used at an early stage of the diagnostic workup before the precise nature of the swelling has been determined." []
is_a: HP:0001627 ! Abnormal heart morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8901
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T16:38:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000848
name: Superior olive hypertrophy
def: "Abnormal increase in size of the superior olive, also known as the superior olivary complex. The superior olive is a collection of brainstem nuclei that is located in pons, functions in multiple aspects of hearing and is an important component of the ascending and descending auditory pathways of the auditory system." []
is_a: HP:0007361 ! Abnormal pons morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8909
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T16:38:56Z" xsd:dateTime

