property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T18:24:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000861
name: Diminished tissue glycogen branching enzyme activity
def: "Activity of glycogen branching enzyme in tissues below the lower limit of normal. The activity can be measured in multiple tissues including culutured fibroblasts." [PMID:26199317]
is_a: HP:6000231 ! Abnormal tissue enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9113
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T18:24:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000862
name: Parotid adenoma
def: "A benign tumor of the parotid salivary gland." [PMID:26124628]
comment: Pleomorphic adenoma (PA), also known as benign mixed tumor, is the most common salivary tumor, constituting up to two-thirds of all salivary gland neoplasms.
is_a: HP:0100684 ! Salivary gland neoplasm
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9117
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-30T18:24:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000863
name: Elevated serum-ascites albumin gradient (SAAG)
def: "An elevation of the serum ascites albumin gradient (SAAG), which is based on the difference between the albumin level of serum and of ascitic fluid, may be used to assess the extent of ascites. The SAAG is thought to reflect the colloid osmotic pressure gradient and the degree of portal hypertension. It has been shown that SAAG is a better discriminator of portal hypertension than ascites. A SAAG of 1.1 gm/dL or higher is considered as high, indicating the presence of portal hypertension, while SAAG less than 1.1 gm/dL is low, indicating the absence of portal hypertension." [PMID:29201716]
synonym: "Abnormally high serum-ascites albumin gradient (SAAG)" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025032 ! Abnormality of digestive system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10563
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000864
name: Transverse smile
def: "Inability to raise the corners of the mouth during the act of smiling due to facial muscle weakness. The act of smiling is accompanied by a horizontal movement of the mouth." [PMID:25037087]
is_a: HP:0030319 ! Weakness of facial musculature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10567
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9942-3886
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000865
name: Hyperphalangy of the 4th finger
def: "An accessory phalanx of the fourth (ring) finger that is arranged linearly with the other phalanges. Hyperphalangy results from an accessory ossification center at the metacarpophalangeal joint." []
synonym: "Hyperphalangy of fourth finger" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030367 ! Finger hyperphalangy
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10521
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000866
name: Delayed distal femoral epiphyseal ossification
def: "Developmental delay of ossification of the distal epiphysis of the femur." []
comment: The distal femoral epiphysis (DFE), is the first of the long bone epiphyses to ossify and appears before the proximal tibial epiphysis (PTE). Around birth, the DFE consists of a rounded or oval nucleus with pitting and osseous circumvolutions. These epiphyses are maturation indicators marking the different stages of progression of bone maturation. They appear in a constant and defined order, which makes the infracranial sequence of maturation useful for age estimation of immature individuals.
is_a: HP:0010590 ! Abnormality of the distal femoral epiphysis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10524
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000867
name: Delayed tibial epiphyseal ossification
def: "Developmental delay of ossification of an epiphysis of the tibia." [PMID:24144387, PMID:9559711]
is_a: HP:0006508 ! Abnormality of tibial epiphyses
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10525
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1020-5412
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000868
name: Toe hyperphalangy
def: "Hyperphalangy is a digit morphology in which increased numbers of phalanges are arranged linearly within a toe. That is, there is an accessory phalanx that is arranged linearly with the other phalanges." [PMID:15032905]
is_a: HP:0010161 ! Abnormal toe phalanx morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10526
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

