[Term]
id: HP:6000876
name: Anti-Glutamate Receptor delta2 antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies in the serum that react against glutamate receptor delta2." [PMID:17049194, PMID:36696031]
comment: Glutamate receptor delta2, a member of the glutamate receptor family, is predominantly expressed in cerebellar Purkinje cells and plays a crucial role in cerebellar functions. Anti-GluRdelta2 autoantibody has been detected in a patient with chronic cerebellitis.
is_a: HP:0030057 ! Autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10543
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-01T09:06:35Z" xsd:dateTime

