id: HP:6000919
name: Trousseau sign
def: "After inflating a blood pressure cuff from 10 mm Hg to 20 mm Hg over the patient's systolic blood pressure, the Trousseau sign is considered positive if carpal spasm develops, with flexion of the thumb and adduction of the finger within 3 minutes. However, this can be painful, so the time should be noted, and the cuff should be deflated once the test is positive." [PMID:28722928]
synonym: "Carpal spasm" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003394 ! Muscle spasm
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10328
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000920
name: Craniocervical junction constriction
def: "Congenital or acquired abnormalities of the occipital bone, foramen magnum, or first two cervical vertebrae that decrease the space for the lower brain stem and cervical cord. These malformations can lead to cranial nerve compression, vertebral artery compression, and obstructive hydrocephalus." [PMID:1566672]
synonym: "Tight craniocervical junction" EXACT []
synonym: "Tight craniovertebral junction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0046508 ! Abnormal cervical spine morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10437
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000921
name: Fibular torsion
def: "Excessively rotated (also called torsion) position of the fibula (calf bone). An increased external rotation of the fibula in the incisura tibiofibularis of more than 5 degrees may lead to an increased pressure and will negatively affect the cartilage." [PMID:24796832, PMID:9409794]
synonym: "Fibular rotation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002991 ! Abnormal fibula morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10438
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000922
name: Abnormal finger phalanx ossification
def: "Any abnormal process of ossification of the phalangeal bones, which normally are ossified from the body and proximal extremity. Ossification of the body commences during the eighth week of fetal development. Ossification of the proximal extremity commences in the bones between the third and fourth years." []
is_a: HP:0005918 ! Abnormal finger phalanx morphology
is_a: HP:0010660 ! Abnormal hand bone ossification
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10439
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000923
name: Positive bloodstream EBV monospot test
def: "The monospot test is a latex agglutination test which utilizes equine erythrocytes as the primary substrate and tests for specific heterophile antibodies produced by the human immune system in response to EBV infection. When these specific antibodies are present in the patient's blood specimen, exposure to equine erythrocytes will lead to clumping of the sample, thus signaling a positive agglutination reaction." [PMID:30969561]
is_a: HP:0430051 ! Bloodstream pathogen-specific antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8714
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000924
name: Positive CSF Toxoplasma gondii antibody positivity
def: "The presence of antibodies in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) that react against a component of Toxoplasma gondii." []
is_a: HP:0430139 ! CSF pathogen-specific antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8732
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000925
name: Positive tuberculin skin test
def: "A positive result of the tuberculin skin test suggesting previous expouse or infection with mycobacterium teberculosis. A standard dose of five tuberculin units (TU) (0.1ml) is injected intradermally (into the skin) and read 48 to 72 h later. A person who has been exposed to the bacteria is expected to mount an immune response in the skin containing the bacterial proteins. The volar aspect of the forearm is the preferred site of test. The basis of reading is the presence or absence of induration, which may be determined by inspection (from a side view against the light as well as by direct light) and by palpation. For standardization, the diameter of induration should be measured transversely to the long axis of the forearm and recorded in millimeters." []
comment: The tuberculin most widely used is purified protein derivative (PPD), which is derived from cultures of M. tuberculosis.
synonym: "Positive Mantoux tuberculosis test" EXACT []
synonym: "Tuberculosis skin test positive" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430030 ! Positive infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8733
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000926
name: Anti-Treponema pallidum antibody positivity
def: "The presence of antibodies in the blood circulation that react against a component of Treponema pallidum." []
synonym: "Positive Fluorescent treponemal antibody absorption test" EXACT []
synonym: "Positive Treponema pallidum hemoagglutination assay" EXACT []
synonym: "Treponemal antibody titer high in blood" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430061 ! Bloodstream antibacterial antibody positivity
