[Term]
id: HP:6000929
name: Neutralizing anti-rabies virus antibody positivity
def: "The presence of antibodies in the blood circulation that act against the rabies virus function by blocking the binding of the glycoprotein to a receptor or preventing the membrane fusion process." [PMID:38075404]
is_a: HP:0430051 ! Bloodstream pathogen-specific antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8744
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-05T10:44:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000930
name: Impaired hepatobiliary scintigraphy tracer uptake
def: "An abnormal reduction in the amount of radioactive tracer uptake upon hepatobiliary scintigraphy." [PMID:15347715]
comment: A normal HBS shows rapid clearance of the radio-tracer from the blood pool. Prompt and uniform hepatic uptake is reached within 5 min, functional visualization of the gall bladder is seen as early as 10 min and bowel activity by 30 to 40 minutes. The presence of tracer in the bowel confirm patency of biliary channels and excludes biliary atresia.
is_a: HP:0025155 ! Abnormal hepatobiliary system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8917
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000931
name: Calcified pulmonary nodule
def: "A pulmonary nodule with calcium deposits. On radiography, these nodules appear dense." [PMID:20582171]
comment: Calcification in a pulmonary nodule (PN) on imaging indicates a high probability that the lesion is benign. But not all calcified PN are benign and the differential considerations include a primary central lung carcinoid, metastasis and a primary bronchogenic carcinoma.
is_a: HP:0033608 ! Pulmonary nodule
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8918
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000932
name: Postprandial exacerbation
def: "Applied to a sign or symptom that is more severe following a meal." []
is_a: HP:0025285 ! Aggravated by
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10573
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000933
name: Koebner Phenomenon
def: "The appearance of new skin lesions on previously unaffected skin secondary to trauma. This phenomenon is also termed the isomorphic (from Greek, equal shape) response, given the fact that the new lesions that appear are clinically and histologically identical to the patient's underlying cutaneous disease." [PMID:31971748]
comment: The Koebner phenomenon is typically associated with preexisting skin disease. Clinical entities that commonly display the Koebner phenomenon include psoriasis, vitiligo, lichen planus. The incidence of Koebnerization ranges broadly within these entities; estimates of the prevalence of the Koebner phenomenon are approximately 11 to 75% in psoriasis and 21 to 62% in vitiligo.
is_a: HP:0011122 ! Abnormal skin physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10577
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000934
name: Glenoid dysplasia
def: "Glenoid dysplasia is a developmental anomaly of the scapula that is characterized by a bony deficiency of the posteroinferior glenoid and the adjacent scapular neck." [PMID:27055054]
comment: Glenoid dysplasia may occur as a primary isolated condition or in association with various syndromes. It is thought to be related to defective ossification of the inferior glenoid precartilage. Radiographs typically demonstrate bilateral, symmetric dysplasia of the scapular neck with a range of associated bony changes. Glenoid dysplasia has been associated with instability and premature glenohumeral arthritis, although the clinical presentation is highly variable. Symptoms are delayed or mitigated as a result of compensatory glenoid labral hyperplasia.
synonym: "Glenohumeral dysplasia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011912 ! Abnormality of the glenoid fossa
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10008
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000935
name: Prolonged retraction of penile foreskin
def: "A past medical history of recently having retracted the penile foreskin for a prolonged period of time. Paraphimosis commonly occurs iatrogenically, when the foreskin is retracted for cleaning, placement of a urinary catheter, a procedure such as a cystoscopy, or for penile examination. Failure to return the retracted foreskin over the glans promptly after the initial retraction can lead to paraphimosis." [PMID:29083645]
comment: This can be a risk factor for paraphimosis, a urologic emergency that occurs in uncircumcised males when the foreskin becomes trapped behind the corona of the glans penis.
is_a: HP:4000144 ! Recent past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10016
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-06T11:45:23Z" xsd:dateTime

