[Term]
id: HP:6000941
name: Thumb hypoplasia grade 3B
def: "A type of developmental undergrowth of the thumb, whereby there are musculotendinous and osseous deficiencies characterized by basal metacarpal aplasia with deficient carpometacarpal (CMC) joint, and absence of metacarpophalangeal (MCP) or interphalangeal (IP) joint." [PMID:24362256]
synonym: "Hypoplasia of the thumb grade IIIB" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0009778 ! Short thumb
