[Term]
id: HP:6000946
name: Transverse terminal lower limb defect
def: "A congenital anomaly that appears as an amputation at different levels of the leg, e.g. femur, foreleg, ankle or toe. The limb is missing the terminal (distal) segment(s), with preservation of all the segment(s) proximal to the missing segment." [PMID:34263545]
