[Term]
id: HP:6000984
name: Coved type ST segment elevation
def: "An ST-segment elevation of at least 2 mm in at least one right precordial lead (V1 to V3), followed by an r'-wave and a concave or straight ST segment. The descending ST segment crosses the isoelectric line and is followed by a negative and symmetric T-wave." [PMID:30139433]
comment: This finding is highly suggestive of Brugada syndrome.
is_a: HP:0012251 ! ST segment elevation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10032
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-07T17:11:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6000985
name: Saddle-back type ST segment elevation
def: "An ST-segment elevation of at least 0.5 mm (generally at least 2 mm in V2) in at least one right precordial lead (V1 to V3), followed by a convex ST. The r'-wave may or may not overlap the J point, but it has a slow downward slope. The ST segment is followed by a positive T-wave in V2 and is of variable morphology in V1." [PMID:30139433]
comment: ECG anomaly is only suggestive of Brugada syndrome.
is_a: HP:0012251 ! ST segment elevation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10032
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-07T17:11:14Z" xsd:dateTime

