[Term]
id: HP:6001010
name: Inability to protrude lips
def: "Lack of ability to purse or pucker the lips." [PMID:30804066]
comment: The anomaly can be related to abnormalities of the muscles, nerves, or structure of the face.
is_a: HP:0030319 ! Weakness of facial musculature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10570
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9942-3886
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001011
name: Wet voice
def: "Wet voice is a perceptual vocal quality that is gurgly or liquid sounding and is due to the voice being produced through moisture. It is commonly used as an indicator of penetration and/or aspiration in clinical swallowing assessments and bedside screening tests." [PMID:25001523]
is_a: HP:0001608 ! Abnormality of the voice
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10572
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001012
name: Erythema marginatum
def: "An erythematous (pink-red, depending on the skin color of the affected individual) macule that spreads peripherally and coalesces to form polycyclic or serpentine patches or plaques. Lesions occur in crops over days to weeks and are evanescent. The rate of migration is 2 to 12 mm over a period of a few hours. Erythema marginatum tends to affect the trunk more than the extremities and to not be accompanied by pruritus." [PMID:32491767]
is_a: HP:0010783 ! Erythema
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10579
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001013
name: Mechanic's hands
def: "Mechanic's hands are fissured, erythematous, hyperkeratotic eruptions on the hands, resembling the type of occupational dermatosis said to resemble the hands of a manual laborer. The lesions are classically on the lateral edges of the fingers and thumbs, largely sparing the palmar, and dorsal aspects of the digits." [PMID:32284267, PMID:36186825]
comment: This feature can be observed in antisynthetase syndrome (ASyS), an autoimmune disease clinically manifested most often by interstitial lung disease, myositis, and arthritis.
is_a: HP:0010765 ! Palmar hyperkeratosis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10598
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001014
name: Hiker's feet
def: "Hyperkeratotic scaly fissured plaques on the fingers/palms or soles, generally more evident on the lateral aspect of index fingers." [PMID:32284267, PMID:35382516]
comment: Hiker's feet is a finding that is analogous to mechanic's hands with similar hyperkeratotic eruptions on the toes and feet, and is a manifestation of antisynthetase syndrome.
is_a: HP:0007556 ! Plantar hyperkeratosis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10599
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001015
name: Anti-HLA-DQ antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the blood circulation that react against a human leukocyte antigen (HLA-DQ). DQ is one of several antigens involved in antibody-mediated rejection of organ transplants." [PMID:23260706]
is_a: HP:0034018 ! Anti-class II HLA antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10615
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001016
name: Inappropriate normal or low erythropoietin
def: "Erythropoietin is produced and released into the blood by the kidneys in response to hypoxemia, and would normally be expected to increase with decreasing hemoglobin levels. This term applies if the increase fails to occur, as may be seen in conditions including chronic kidney disease." [PMID:32311841]
is_a: HP:0034442 ! Abnormal circulating erythropoietin concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10616
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001017
name: Rapid gastric emptying
def: "A condition in which food moves through the stomach into the small intestine at an abnormally fast rate." [PMID:16207692]
comment: Dumping is the effect of alteration in the motor functions of the stomach, including disturbances in the gastric reservoir and transporting function. Anatomic and physiologic changes introduced by gastric surgery result in clinically significant dumping syndrome in approximately 10% of patients. Gastrointestinal hormones play an important role in dumping by mediating responses to surgical resection. Treatment options of dumping syndrome include diet, medications, and surgical revision.
synonym: "Dumping syndrome" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030896 ! Abnormal gastrointestinal transit time
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10617
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001018
name: Mediastinal lymph node calcification
def: "Abnormal deposition of calcium in mediastinal lymph nodes." [PMID:29791561]
comment: Lymph node calcifications most often result from prior granulomatous infections, especially tuberculosis and histoplasmosis. Other, less common, causes are sarcoidosis, silicosis, amyloidosis, and calcifications secondary to the treatment of lymphomas (radiation therapy or chemotherapy).
synonym: "Calcified mediastinal lymph nodes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002733 ! Abnormal lymph node morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10619
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001019
name: Eggshell calcification of lymph nodes
def: "Eggshell calcification refers to fine calcification seen at the periphery of a mass and usually relates to lamellar lymph node calcification." [PMID:29791561, PMID:6779537]
comment: Eggshell calcification, commonly occurs in patients with silicosis and coal-worker's pneumoconiosis. Sarcoidosis, postirradiation Hodgkin disease, blastomycosis, and scleroderma are other reported causes. Eggshell calcification has more rarely been observed in amyloidosis and histoplasmosis.
synonym: "Peripheral calcification of lymph nodes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002733 ! Abnormal lymph node morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10620
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001020
name: Knee joint effusion
def: "Abnormal accumulation of fluid within the knee joint or around the knee. Symptoms maye include, pain, swelling, and stiffness." [PMID:31575400]
comment: Increased intra-articular amount of (synovial) fluid is not specific for a particular disorder, as can occur in a variety of settings but draws attention to the presence of a joint disorder, such as knee osteoarthritis, or rheumatoid arthritis.
is_a: HP:0034669 ! Abnormal knee morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10622
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001021
name: Subcutaneous emphysema
def: "Skin emphysema/Subcutaneous emphysema occurs when gas or air accumulates and seeps under the skin, where normally no gas should be present. While the presence of air in subcutaneous or mediastinal tissue is not dangerous in itself, prompt recognition of the underlying cause is essential." [PMID:31194349]
comment: Subcutaneous emphysema can be caused by medical procedures and medical conditions that cause the pressure in the alveoli of the lung to be higher than that in the tissues outside of them. Its most common causes are pneumothorax or a chest tube that has become occluded by a blood clot or fibrinous material. It can also occur spontaneously due to rupture of the alveoli, with dramatic presentation. When the condition is caused by surgery it is called surgical emphysema. The term spontaneous subcutaneous emphysema is used when the cause is not clear.
synonym: "Skin emphysema" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011124 ! Abnormal epidermal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10623
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-12T10:19:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001022
name: Elevated bone scintigraphy uptake
def: "Bone scintigraph is performed with technetium 99m-labeled diphosphonates. The uptake of these radiopharmaceuticals depicts osteoblastic activity and regional blood flow to bone." [PMID:21889871]
comment: Bone scintigraphy is frequently performed as part of the routine staging of patients with a wide variety of primary malignancies. Although it is a sensitive imaging modality, it is relatively nonspecific, and there are many potential causes of increased isotope uptake that can mimic metastatic disease.
synonym: "Bone scan (scintigraphy): abnormally increased uptake" EXACT []
synonym: "Increase bone scan uptake" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011842 ! Abnormal skeletal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9014
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001023
name: Diminished long-chain-enoyl-CoA hydratase activity in cultured fibroblasts
def: "Concentration or activity of long-chain-enoyl-CoA hydratase (EC 4.2.1.74) as measured in cultured fibroblasts is below the limits of normal." []
is_a: HP:4000195 ! Abnormal enzyme activity in cultured fibroblasts
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9102
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001024
name: Diminished acetyl-CoA C-acyltransferase activity in cultured fibroblasts
def: "Concentration or activity of acetyl-CoA C-acyltransferase (EC 2.3.1.16) as measured in cultured fibroblasts is below the limits of normal. This enzyme catalyzes the reaction acetyl-CoA + an acyl-CoA = a 3-oxoacyl-CoA + CoA. It is also known as 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase and beta-ketothiolase." []
synonym: "Reduced 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase activity in cultured fibroblasts" EXACT []
is_a: HP:4000195 ! Abnormal enzyme activity in cultured fibroblasts
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9103
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001025
name: Pathological inclusion body
def: "Pathological inclusion bodies are are composed of glycogen, proteins, nucleic acids, lipids, hemosiderin, and calcium, that accumulate as metabolic by-products, catabolic products of macromolecular complexes, or in the context of cell injury." []
is_a: HP:0025461 ! Abnormal cell morphology
