[Term]
id: HP:6001031
name: Cystine nephrolithiasis
def: "A cystine stone is a type of kidney stone that is yellowish brown with a granular surface. They are observed in individuals with Cystinuria and tend to be of early onset, to occur repeatedly, and to be associated with urinary tract infections." [PMID:25383320, PMID:32494553]
synonym: "Yellowish brown character to kidney stone suggestive of cystine" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0000787 ! Kidney stone
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9133
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001032
name: Hepatic cystine accumulation
def: "Accumulation of cystine in the liver." [PMID:32727395]
comment: Cystine crystal accumulation activates Kupffer cells and secreted vasoactive substances cause vasoconstriction in microcirculation resulting in portal hypertension
is_a: HP:0030146 ! Abnormal liver parenchyma morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9134
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001033
name: Bone marrow cystine accumulation
def: "The presence of cystine crystals in bone marrow cells as demonstrated in a fresh bone marrow aspiration sample." [PMID:28871612]
is_a: HP:0005561 ! Abnormal bone marrow cell morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9136
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001034
name: Desmoid tumor
def: "Desmoid tumors are rare, locally aggressive, fibroblastic soft-tissue tumors that are characterized by infiltrative growth and tendency to recur. Desmoid tumors do not metastasize but can arise in any part of the body: extra-abdominal (appear in the head and neck, chest, extremities), and abdominal wall or intra-abdominal (originating in tissue that connects abdominal organs)." [PMID:32004793, PMID:37436594]
synonym: "Aggressive fibromatosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Desmoid-type fibromatosis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0031459 ! Soft tissue neoplasm
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9138
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-18T14:41:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001035
name: Tubular jejunal duplication
def: "A segment of the jejunum that runs parallel to the normal jejunum and communicates with the jejunal lumen at one or both ends." [PMID:1773546]
is_a: HP:0005265 ! Abnormal jejunum morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8992
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-20T13:25:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001036
name: Left ventricular rupture
def: "A full thickness tear or breakage of the myocardium of the left ventricle." [PMID:20301667, PMID:32644697]
is_a: HP:0001637 ! Abnormal myocardium morphology
is_a: HP:0001711 ! Abnormal left ventricle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8993
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-20T13:25:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001037
name: Punctate pontine perivascular enhancement
def: "Multiple punctate (speckled, patchy spot-like) and/or curvilinear areas of gadolinium enhancement distributed around blood vessels in the pons." [PMID:24028073]
comment: The lesions may extend into adjacent CNS structures, caudally to the medulla oblongata or the cervicothoracal spinal cord, rostrally to the midbrain, and even involve supratentorial regions such as the thalami, capsula interna, basal ganglia, corpus callosum and cerebral white matter. See Figure 1 of PMID:24028073.
is_a: HP:0007361 ! Abnormal pons morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9004
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-20T13:25:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001038
name: Intestinal worm
def: "Presence of one or more adult worms in the intestine as demonstrated by sonography or passage of a worm in the stool. On sonography, worms may appear as linear, echogenic structures within the intestines." [PMID:27551336]
is_a: HP:0430030 ! Positive infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9030
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-20T13:25:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001039
name: Scrotal worm
def: "Demonstration of one or more worms in the scrotum. This finding can be appreciated by sonography, where echogenic, linear structures could be seen moving within the scrotum." [PMID:12636874]
