[Term]
id: HP:6001082
name: Abnormal urine D-xylose test
def: "An abnormal result of the xylose absorption test that is used to assess the ability of the intestines to absorb D-xylose. D-xylose is a five-carbon monosaccharide found in some plants. The patient drinks a solution containing a specific amount of D-xylose and the concentration of xylose is measured in the blood circulation and then in the urine. A low amount of D-xylose indicates reduced small intestinal absorbtion." [PMID:11418788]
comment: The standard 25-g D-xylose test in adults, based on analysis of a 5-h urine collection and a 1-h serum sample, discriminates between normal subjects and patients with proximal small intestinal malabsorption with X5% specificity and sensitivity.
is_a: HP:0012719 ! Functional abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8876
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001083
name: Cerebral hemisphere mass lesion
def: "An abnormal growth or accumulation of tissue in a hemisphere of the cerebrum. Typically a mass is an initial finding that will lead to additional workup." []
is_a: HP:0002060 ! Abnormal cerebral morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8892
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001084
name: T2-hyperintense putaminal rim
def: "Increased signal on T2 magnetic resonance imaging characterized by a linear region of high signal surrounding the lateral aspect of the putamen at 1.5 Tesla." [PMID:19147717]
is_a: HP:0031982 ! Abnormal putamen morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8893
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001085
name: Posterior fossa mass lesion
def: "An abnormal growth or accumulation of tissue in the posterior fossa, affecting the cerebellum or fourth ventricle. Typically a mass is an initial finding that will lead to additional workup." []
is_a: HP:0000932 ! Abnormal posterior cranial fossa morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8897
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001086
name: Irregular RR interval
def: "Abnormal increased variability in the timing between consecutive R-waves on an electrocardiogram." [PMID:30725696, PMID:35813391]
comment: Sinus arrhythmia is a variation of normal sinus rhythm that characteristically presents with an irregular rate in which the change in the R-R interval is greater than 0.12 seconds.
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9605
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001087
name: Irregular P-P interval
def: "Abnormally increased variability in the timing between consecutive P-waves on an electrocardiogram." [PMID:35813391]
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9951
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001088
name: Fungal hair infection
def: "Demonstration of fungi growing on hair by a method such as microscopy of hairs mounted on slides with 10% potassium hydroxide." [PMID:29494084, PMID:31424762, PMID:32644450]
synonym: "Fungal infection of hair" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430030 ! Positive infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9968
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001089
name: Long hairstyle
def: "A past medical history of having long, full hair." [PMID:31424762]
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9969
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001090
name: Conjunctival subepithelial fibrosis
def: "fine white linear scars under intact conjunctival epithelium. This scarring appears in areas of previous conjunctival ulceration or pseudomembrane formation, weeks to months after the insult is healed." [PMID:28789979]
comment: Subepithelial fibrosis can be a manifestation of ocular graft-versus-host disease (oGVHD), but can also be found after epidemic keratoconjunctivitis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, and chemical burns.
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9974
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001091
name: Conjunctival fornix foreshortening
def: "Abnormal reduction in depth of the fornix of the conjunctiva. The fornix is the area where the conjunctiva folds back upon itself, thereby creating a recessed space." [PMID:24314841]
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9975
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001092
name: Strong ultraviolet light exposure
def: "History of exposure to ultraviolet light, such as may be encountered with outdoor activities, living near equator, radiation." []
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9976
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001093
name: Exposure to vaginal douching
def: "A history of intravaginal cleansing with a liquid solution for personal hygiene or aesthetic reasons." [PMID:12762087]
comment: Douching represents a risk factor for bacterial vaginosis.
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9981
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001094
name: Exposure to oily lotions or creams
def: "A history of applying oily lotions or creams to the skin." [PMID:29494106]
comment: This may be a risk factor for tinea versicolor.
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9982
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001095
name: Elevated circulating pristanic acid concentration following branched-chain fatty acid ingestion
def: "Concentration of pristanic acid in the blood circulation above the upper limit of normal. This finding can be observed in Zellweger syndrome. Note that branched-chain fatty acid accumulation depends on dietary intake of phytanic acid, which is minimal in formula- and breast-fed infants. Thus, phytanic and pristanic acid levels are normal in a neonate with Zellweger spectrum disorder." [PMID:20301621]
is_a: HP:0010964 ! Abnormal circulating long-chain fatty-acid concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8269
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001096
name: Decreased CD4+ T cell ZAP-70 protein expression
def: "Reduction in the level of ZAP-70 protein CD4-positive T cells." [PMID:20301777]
comment: Testing of CD4+ T cells reveals absence or near absence of ZAP-70 protein in most individuals affected by ZAP70-related combined immunodeficiency.
synonym: "Decreased T-cell ZAP-70 protein expression in CD4-positive T cells" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002843 ! Abnormal T cell morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8725
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-07-21T13:51:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001097
name: Dorsal flexion contracture of the ankle
def: "A type of contracture in which the dorsal flexion muscles of the ankle are contracted." []
comment: Dorsiflexion of the ankle is the movement of the top of the foot towards the leg in an upward motion. With dorsal flexion contracture, the ability to passively or actively move the tip of the toe away from the leg is limited.
synonym: "Dorsiflexion contracture of the ankle" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034677 ! Ankle contracture
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10353
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001098
name: Metaphyseal undermodelling
def: "Lack of the normal diaphyseal constriction (thinning of long bones toward the midshaft area) giving the submetaphyseal areas an abnormally wide appearance." [PMID:34484289]
synonym: "Metaphyseal modeling defect" EXACT []
synonym: "Undermodelled metaphyses" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000944 ! Abnormal metaphysis morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10442
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8612-1062
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001099
name: Iliac vein compression
def: "Compression of the common iliac vein against the spine by the contralateral common iliac artery." [PMID:32119264]
comment: Pulsations of the overriding artery cause shear stress and endothelial changes in the vein, resulting in the formation of fibrous bands or spurs. Over time, the affected area forms a stricture, causing impaired venous return and, in some circumstances, deep venous thrombosis. Common iliac vein compression can be ascertained by Doppler sonography.
is_a: HP:0002624 ! Abnormal venous morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10515
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001100
name: Positive serum amyloid P scintigraphy
def: "Detection of abnormal amyloid deposits in the body by 123I-labeled serum amyloid P component (SAP) scintigraphy." [PMID:16564782]
synonym: "Positive SAP scan" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011034 ! Amyloid deposition
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10536
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001101
name: Crossed brainstem sign
def: "Motor and/or sensory cranial nerve findings ipsilateral to the lesion, and at the same time motor and/or sensory findings on the contralateral side of the body." [PMID:19252797, PMID:32809731]
is_a: HP:0011442 ! Abnormal central motor function
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10550
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001102
name: Inability to puff cheeks
def: "Reduced ability to inflate the cheeks by blowing air into them while keeping the lips closed." []
comment: This feature may be related to facial muscle weakness as well as to cranial nerve VII lesions.
is_a: HP:0030319 ! Weakness of facial musculature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10568
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9942-3886
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001103
name: Entoptic phenomenon
def: "Visual sensations caused by changes within the eye itself, rather than by the normal light stimulation process. Entoptic phenomena are classified in the syndrome as floaters, blue field entoptic phenomenon, photopsia and self-light of the eye." [PMID:36788360]
synonym: "Entoptic phenomenona" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000504 ! Abnormality of vision
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10588
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-05T13:00:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001104
name: Abnormal vestibulo-spinal reflex
def: "An abnormality of the vestibulospinal (VS) reflexes, which contribute to the control of postural orientation. In this task, they continuously collaborate with reflexes elicited by stimulation of visual and somatosensory receptors. Labyrinthine receptors are sensitive to modifications (i) of the head position with respect to the earth vertical or (ii) of the angular/linear velocity of head motion in space. This information can be used to monitor deviations from the maintained body position." [PMID:29081426, PMID:38178884]
is_a: HP:0001751 ! Abnormal vestibular function
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10638
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001105
name: Positive probe-to-bone test
def: "An abnormal result of the probe-to-bone (PTB) test. The PTB test is performed by inserting a sterile, metal surgical probe into the ulcer and is positive if a hard, gritty surface is felt inside. For large wounds, this may require gentle exploration of the wound with the probe." [PMID:27369321]
comment: The basis behind the PTB test is that if a probe can reach bone, so can bacteria.
synonym: "Abnormal probe-to-bone test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0032674 ! Cutaneous wound
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10656
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001106
name: Exposure to repetitive hand impact
def: "A history of exposure to repetitive impact on palm or hand, such as working with a jackhammer." []
comment: This history can be a risk factor for carpal tunnel syndrome.
synonym: "Use of vibratory tools" EXACT []
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10670
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001107
name: Fractured scaphoid bone
def: "A partial or complete breakage of the scaphoid bone." [PMID:24298746]
synonym: "Scaphoid bone fracture" EXACT []
synonym: "Scaphoid fracture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0041248 ! Fractured carpal bone
