property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001108
name: Local anesthetic ineffectiveness
def: "Resistance to the effects of local anaesthesia, with delayed onset or failure of local anesthetics to incude numbness or relieve pain." [PMID:31723666]
comment: This feature has been reported in individuals with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome.
is_a: HP:0001311 ! Abnormal nervous system electrophysiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9469
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001109
name: Palmoplantar location
def: "Applied to lesions whose distribution is confined or restricted to the palms of the hands and soles of the feet." []
is_a: HP:0012838 ! Localized
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9912
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001110
name: Oral mucosa plaque
def: "A raised, flat-topped lesion with a diameter of one centimeter or more that is located in the mucosa of the mouth." []
is_a: HP:0011830 ! Abnormal oral mucosa morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8006
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001111
name: Positive saliva rabies nucleic acid test
def: "Detection of rabies nucleic acid in saliva by a method such as polymerase chain reaction." []
is_a: HP:6000579 ! Positive oropharangeal infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8074
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001112
name: Elevated tissue arylsulfatase A activity
def: "Activity of arylsulfatase A (EC 3.1.6.8) above the upper limit of normal. The activity can be measured in multiple tissues including culutured fibroblasts and leukocytes or in the blood circulation." []
is_a: HP:6000231 ! Abnormal tissue enzyme concentration or activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8202
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001113
name: Elevated circulating methysterol concentration
def: "The concentration of a methysterol in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." []
comment: This group of compounds includes thje 4-alpha-monomethyl sterols and 4,4-prime-dimethyl sterols.
is_a: HP:0003119 ! Abnormal circulating lipid concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8278
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001114
name: Elevated urinary adipic acid
def: "The amount of adipic acid in the urine, normalized for urine concentration, is above the upper limit of normal. Adipic acid is an alpha,omega-dicarboxylic acid that is the 1,4-dicarboxy derivative of butane." []
is_a: HP:0003215 ! Elevated urinary dicarboxylic acid level
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/8599
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-08-06T16:34:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001115
name: EEG with temporal slowing
def: "Slow-wave activity observed in the temporal area of the scalp electro-encephalogram (EEG)." [PMID:31085562]
synonym: "EEG with slow activity in temporal lobes" EXACT []
synonym: "EEG with slow-wave activity involving the temporal lobes" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0010843 ! EEG with focal slow activity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10829
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-13T22:02:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001116
name: History of high-pressure injection injury of the hand
def: "Medical history of the hand having come into contact with the nozzle of a high-pressure injecting system such as a paint gun or air compressor." [PMID:31194367]
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10833
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-13T22:02:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001117
name: Hypertrophic ulnar styloid process
def: "Excessively long styloid process of the ulna." [PMID:31192047]
comment: Ulnar styloid impaction syndrome involves impaction between the tip of the ulnar styloid process and the triquetrum bone. This syndrome is most commonly seen in patients with excessively long or hypertrophic ulnar styloid processes and is not necessarily associated with positive ulnar variance. The ulnar styloid process index (USPI), calculated as the difference between the ulnar styloid length and the ulnar variance divided by the transverse diameter of the ulnar head, is commonly used to assess the size of the ulnar styloid. An excessively long ulnar styloid has a length greater than 6 mm or a USPI more than 0.21. Repetitive friction of the proximal pole of the triquetrum and the ulnar styloid tip leads to chondromalacia, synovitis, and ulnar-sided wrist pain.
synonym: "Ulnar styloid large" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0040071 ! Abnormal morphology of ulna
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10834
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-13T22:02:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001118
name: History of recent peripheral venous catheter
def: "A history of placement of a peripehral venous catheter in the hours, days, or weeks before the current presenting complaint." []
is_a: HP:4000144 ! Recent past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10690
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001119
name: Purulent drainage from skin
def: "Exudation of a thick, opaque fluid from a wound or skin lesion, typically as a result of infection and draining pus, i.e., dead white blood cells, bacteria, and tissue debris." []
is_a: HP:0011123 ! Inflammatory abnormality of the skin
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10692
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001120
name: Occupational history of putting fingers in other people's mouths
def: "A history of exposure of fingers by putting them in other peoples' mouths occupationally, e.g., as a dentist or physician." []
comment: This is a risk factor for Herpetic whitlow.
is_a: HP:0035010 ! Occupational exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10693
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001121
name: Single-finger involvement
def: "Applies to an abnormality whose distribution and appearance are limited to or predominantly affect a single finger." []
synonym: "Single finger involvement" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10694
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001122
name: Multiple-finger involvement
def: "Applies to an abnormality whose distribution and appearance affect more than one finger." []
synonym: "Multiple finger involvement" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10694
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001123
name: Pain disproportionate to abnormality on physical exam
def: "Exquisite tenderness in a specific region, beyond what one would surmise from examination." []
comment: This finding may be observed with several diseases including necrotizing fasciitis and gas gangrene.
is_a: HP:0025280 ! Pain characteristic
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10695
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001124
name: Sphenoid wing dysplasia
def: "Hypoplasia or aplasia of the greater or lesser wing of the sphenoid bone, typically resulting in widening of the superior orbital fissure, elevation of the [lesser sphenoid wing, and ipsilateral orbital enlargement." [PMID:28409229, PMID:33758729, PMID:4980937]
comment: All reported cases of congenital sphenoid wing dysplasia have been attributed to neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1). Sphenoid bone dysplasia occurs in 3-11 percent of the subjects with neurofibromatosis type 1 NF1 patients. This malformation, a distinctive diagnostic feature for NF1, is characterized by progressive proptosis and facial disfiguration secondary to herniation of meningeal and cerebral structures. Unilateral in most of the cases, sphenoid bone dysplasia associated with plexiform neurofibroma in the territory of the trigeminal nerve in several cases and pooling of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) in all cases often described in the past as an arachnoid cyst.
is_a: HP:0011821 ! Abnormal facial skeleton morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10696
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001125
name: Skin laceration
def: "An injury in which skin and underlying tissues are cut or torn." [PMID:31424750]
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10701
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001126
name: Metacarpal fracture
def: "A partial or complete breakage of a metacarpal bone." []
synonym: "Fractured metacarpal bone" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004277 ! Fractured hand bones
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10702
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001127
name: Pain at the base of the thumb
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort localized to the base of the thumb, over thenar eminence or thumb metacarpal." []
comment: The base of the thumb is the fleshy area on the palm side of the hand near where the thumb attaches to the hand.
is_a: HP:0046505 ! Hand pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10704
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001128
name: History of recent participation in athletics
def: "Medical history of participation in sports (football, basketball, soccer, skiing) in the hours, days, or weeks prior to the current presenting complaint." []
is_a: HP:4000144 ! Recent past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10706
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-11-16T16:11:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001129
name: Remote trauma history
def: "History of trauma months to years ago, including but not limited to fracture or other orthopedic injury at the symptomatic area." []
comment: This feature may suggest scaphoid nonunion advanced collapse, scapholunate advanced collapse, or distal radioulnar joint arthritis.
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10718
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001130
name: Distal radioulnar joint arthritis
def: "An inflammatory condition of the joint that connects the far ends of the radius and the ulna, known as the distal radioulnar joint (DRUJ). DRUJ arthritis may be characterized by widening of the DRUJ interval, volar/dorsal displacement of the distal ulna, radiographic evidence of osteoarthritis at the DRUJ joint including osteophytes, subchondral cysts, subchrondal sclerosis, and joint space narrowing." [PMID:23027692]
comment: Arthritis of the distal radioulnar joint (DRUJ) between the sigmoid notch of the distal radius and the ulnar head can be caused by traumatic, inflammatory, congenital, and degenerative processes.
synonym: "Arthritis of the distal radioulnar joint" EXACT []
synonym: "DRUJ arthritis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003059 ! Abnormality of the radioulnar joints
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10719
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001131
name: Radial head fracture
def: "Fracture of the proximal end of the radius involving the radial head." []
is_a: HP:0003978 ! Fractured radius
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10796
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001132
name: Elbow lateral collateral ligament tear
def: "An injury to the lateral collateral ligament (LCL) of the elbow. The LCL is a complex capsuloligamentous structure critical in stabilizing the ulnohumeral and radiocapitellar articulations. LCL injury can result in elbow instability, allowing the proximal radius and ulna to externally rotate away from the humerus as a supination stress is applied to the forearm." [PMID:23261198]
synonym: "Lateral ulnar collateral ligament tear" EXACT []
synonym: "Ligamentous tear on the lateral aspect of the elbow" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020300 ! Abnormal elbow morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10797
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001133
name: Elbow medial collateral ligament tear
def: "An injury to the medial collateral ligament (MCL) of the elbow." [PMID:19468906]
comment: Elbow medial collateral ligament sprain occurs when the elbow is subjected to a valgus force exceeding the tensile properties of the medial collateral ligament (MCL). This is an injury seen more often in throwing athletes.
synonym: "Ligamentous tear on the medial aspect of the elbow" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0020300 ! Abnormal elbow morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10798
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001134
name: Coronoid fracture
def: "Fracture of the coronoid process on the proximal ulna." [PMID:39381286]
comment: The coronoid process acts to buttress against the posterior translation of the ulna on the humerus. It is also the attachment site for the anterior elbow capsule, brachialis, and the medial collateral ligament of the elbow. Coronoid fractures are critical injuries and are suggestive of elbow instability.
is_a: HP:0003987 ! Fractured ulna
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10799
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001135
name: History of spinal cord injury
def: "A medical history of hving had a spinal cord injury prior to the presenting complaint." [PMID:32809556]
comment: Spinal cord injury (SCI) results from direct or indirect spinal cord damage. The most common SCI cause is acute trauma from motor vehicular crashes (MVCs), although the condition may also arise from insidious etiologies such as malignancies and chronic tuberculous infection. Spinal cord lesions may lead to permanent disability, significant morbidity, and even mortality. High spinal injuries often impair cardiorespiratory function, requiring emergent interventions.
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10804
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001136
name: Femoral nerve distribution
def: "Paresthesias in anterior/medial aspect of the thigh (anterior and medial cutaneous nerves of the thigh) and/or medial aspect of the lower leg and foot (saphenous distribution). May be accompanied by weakness in the quadriceps." []
is_a: HP:0025849 ! Localized along nerve distribution
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10805
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001137
name: Triceps tendon rupture
def: "Breakage (tear) of the triceps tendon." [PMID:28832209]
is_a: HP:0100550 ! Tendon rupture
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10807
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-03T17:26:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001138
name: Digoxin exposure
def: "History of having been treateed with digoxin." [PMID:29262029]
comment: Digoxin is a cardiac glycoside derived from the foxglove plant (digitalis species). It has inotropic effects and is utilized in the management of systolic dysfunction in patients with congestive heart failure (CHF) and as an atrioventricular nodal blocking agent for managing atrial tachydysrhythmias. Gastrointestinal upset is the most common symptom of digoxin toxicity. Patients also may report visual symptoms, which classically present as a yellow-green discoloration, and cardiovascular symptoms, such as palpitations, dyspnea, and syncope.
synonym: "Digitalis exposure" EXACT []
synonym: "Lanoxin exposure" EXACT []
is_a: HP:4000112 ! Medication history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10675
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001139
name: Upper arm pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the upper arm." []
comment: Pain anywhere between the shoulder and elbow. Upper arm pain may be observed with conditions such as ulnar shaft fracture, intersection syndrome of hand tendons, Galeazzi fracture, radial tunnel syndrome, and wrist dislocation.
synonym: "Proximal arm pain" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012513 ! Upper limb pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10793
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001140
name: Capitellum fracture
def: "A partial or complete breakage of the capitulum of the humerus, which is a smooth, rounded eminence on the lateral portion of the distal articular surface of the humerus." []
synonym: "Capitellar fracture" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0041055 ! Fractured humerus
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10794
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001141
name: Anterior shoulder pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the anterior (front) part of the shoulder." []
comment: Pain localized to the anterior aspect of the shoulder. Anterior shoulder pain may be observed in conditions such as proximal biceps tendon tear.
is_a: HP:0030834 ! Shoulder pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10811
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001142
name: Pain at the anterior aspect of the elbow
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the front part of the elbow front part of the elbow, that is, on the ventral side of the arm where the arm bends." []
is_a: HP:0030835 ! Elbow pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10817
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001143
name: Posterior fat pad sign of the elbow
def: "Lateral elbow x-ray showing lucent crescent of fat that indicates a joint effusion in the elbow ." [PMID:22735922]
is_a: HP:0020300 ! Abnormal elbow morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10821
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001144
name: Pain at the anterior aspect of the knee
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the front part of the knee, that is, the side of the knee where the patella is located." []
is_a: HP:0030839 ! Knee pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001145
name: Pain at the posterior aspect of the knee
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the back part of the knee, that is, opposite to the side of the knee where the patella is located." []
comment: Pain at the posterior aspect of the knee may be observed with Baker cyst.
is_a: HP:0030839 ! Knee pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10822
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001146
name: Biceps tendonitis
def: "Biceps tendinitis is inflammation of the tendon around the long head of the biceps muscle." [PMID:19725488]
comment: MRI may show increased T2 signal around the biceps tendon or ultrasound showing thickening of the biceps tendon.
synonym: "Biceps tendinitis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025230 ! Tendonitis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10826
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-06T08:59:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001147
name: Increased peripheral nerve cross sectional area
def: "Ultrasonography showing increased cross sectional area (CSA) of a peripheral nerve as it travels through a potential site of compression." []
comment: This feature may be observed in conditions such as carpal tunnel syndrome, ulnar tunnel syndrome, cubital tunnel syndrome, and radial tunnel syndrome.
synonym: "Peripheral nerve enlargement" EXACT []
synonym: "Peripheral nerve swelling" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000759 ! Abnormal peripheral nervous system morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10783
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001148
name: Pain exacerbated by passive flexion at joint
def: "Pain in extremity that worsens with joint is passively flexed." [PMID:25878982]
comment: This feature may be observed in acute compartment syndrome.
is_a: HP:0025280 ! Pain characteristic
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10786
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001149
name: Positive hook test at the elbow
def: "With forearm fully supinated and elbow flexed to 90 degrees, examiner hooks a finger a bit around the distal biceps tendon at the anterior aspect of the elbow. Test is positive when there is lack of appreciable cord like structure to hook around." [PMID:32788933]
comment: This sign can indicate a distal biceps tendon tear.
synonym: "Positive distal biceps hook test" EXACT []
synonym: "Positive O'Driscoll hook test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034430 ! Abnormal joint physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10814
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001150
name: Positive Speed's test
def: "Manual downward pressure on the arm with the shoulders flexed forward to 90 degrees, elbows fully extended, and palm facing up recreates pain in the anterior shoulder region; named after Dr. Speed." [PMID:9848587]
comment: The Speed's test was recorded as positive if the patient experienced pain in the proximal portion of the shoulder during the application of a downward force applied to the arm. The patient's arm was placed with the forearm in full supination at 90 degrees of shoulder elevation. See Figure 1 of PMID:9848587.
is_a: HP:0025823 ! Positive provocative functional shoulder test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10825
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001151
name: Triangular lunate bone
def: "A disruption of the greater and lesser arcs of the lunate bone, with the lunate having a triangular silhouette, know as the piece of pie sign. Often caused by falling on an outstretched hand, patients will have tenderness to palpation over the dorsum of the wrist and may have sensory deficits in the median nerve distribution." [PMID:22529764, PMID:23616330]
comment: See Figure 3 of PMID:23616330.
synonym: "Piece of pie sign of lunate bone" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004248 ! Abnormal lunate bone morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10733
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001152
name: Pain exacerbated by wrist deviation
def: "Pain worsens with wrist ulnar or radial deviation." []
comment: Ulnar: Triangular fibrocartilage complex tear; Ulnocarpal abutment syndrome Radial: Triangular fibrocartilage complex tear.
is_a: HP:0025280 ! Pain characteristic
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10742
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001153
name: Pain on the lateral aspect of the foot
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the side of the foot nearest to the little (fifth) toe." []
synonym: "Lateral foot pain" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025238 ! Foot pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10743
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001154
name: Pain at the medial aspect of the knee
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the inner side of knee, that is, the region of the knee that faces the other knee." []
comment: This feature may be observed with medial collateral ligament knee injury.
is_a: HP:0030839 ! Knee pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10744
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001155
name: Pain at the lateral aspect of the knee
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the outer side of knee, that is, the region of the knee that faces away from the other knee." []
comment: This feature may be observed with lateral collateral ligament injury.
is_a: HP:0030839 ! Knee pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10745
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2024-12-08T19:44:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001156
name: obsolete Synovial crystals
