[Term]
id: HP:6001157
name: Occupational exposure to frequent kneeling
def: "A history of exposure to frequent squatting/kneeling and/or heavy lifting." [PMID:18597397]
comment: Occupations that require frequent kneeling such as roofing, construction workers, plumbers, electricians, landscapers, gardeners, carpenters, and housekeepers may increase risk of prepatellar bursitis and knee osteoarthritis.
synonym: "History of frequent kneeling" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0035010 ! Occupational exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10823
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001158
name: Trochanteric pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the structures around the greater trochanter (the bony prominence on the outer part of the femur)." []
synonym: "Lateral hip pain" EXACT []
synonym: "Pain at the lateral aspect of the hip" EXACT []
synonym: "Pain on the outside of the hip" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030838 ! Hip pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10824
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001159
name: Pulsatile mass in extremity
def: "A noticeable lump or swelling in the arm or leg that you can feel with you fingers and this lump is beating or pulsating, similar to the feeling of a heartbeat." []
comment: This finding may be observed with conditions such as arteriovenous malformation located in the arm or leg or withulnar artery thrombosis.
is_a: HP:0040064 ! Abnormality of limbs
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10832
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001160
name: Abnormal R wave
def: "Any anomaly of the R wave of the EKG, which is the first upward deflection after the P wave. The R wave reflects early ventricular depolarisation." []
is_a: HP:0003115 ! Abnormal EKG
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10839
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001161
name: Poor R-wave progression
def: "Absence of the normal increase in size of the R wave in the precordial leads when advancing from lead V1 to V6 of the electrocardiogram." [PMID:35181482]
comment: With normal R wave progression, the amplitude of the R wave gradually increased from V1 to V5 and decreases from V5 to V6. Abnormal R wave progression may be observed with myocardial infarction, cardiomyopathy, right or left ventricular hypertrophy, and other conditions.
is_a: HP:6001160 ! Abnormal R wave
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10839
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001162
name: Prominent V1-V2 R wave
def: "The R wave in leads V1-V2 is normally considerably smaller in amplitude than the S wave in the same leads. Prominent R wave in these leads implies the R wave is larger than the S-wave, which may indicate cardiovascular pathology. This term includes Tall R wave in lead V1, which is defined by a R/S ratio greater than 1." [PMID:11593472]
comment: This electrocardiographic finding exists as a normal variant in only 1% of patients. Physicians should therefore be familiar with the differential diagnosis for this important QRS configuration. The electrocardiographic entities which can present with this finding include right bundle branch block, left ventricular ectopy, right ventricular hypertrophy, acute right ventricular dilation (acute right heart strain), type a Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome, posterior myocardial infarction, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, progressive muscular dystrophy, dextrocardia, misplaced precordial leads, and normal variant.
synonym: "High voltage R wave in V1/V2" EXACT []
synonym: "Prominent R wave in lead V1" EXACT []
is_a: HP:6001160 ! Abnormal R wave
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10839
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-07T09:05:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001163
name: Finger mass
def: "An abnormal enlargement or swelling localized to a finger." []
comment: The word mass is usually used at an early stage of the diagnostic workup before the precise nature of the swelling has been determined.
synonym: "Bump on finger" EXACT []
synonym: "Finger growth" EXACT []
synonym: "Lump on finger" EXACT []
