[Term]
id: HP:6001165
name: Abnormal retinal vein morphology
def: "A condition characterized by structural abnormalities of the retinal veins, including tortuosity, dilation, narrowing, or irregularities in branching patterns. These changes may be associated with systemic or ocular diseases such as retinal vein occlusion, diabetic retinopathy, or hypertensive retinopathy." []
is_a: HP:0008046 ! Abnormal retinal vascular morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10933
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-31T09:45:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001166
name: Spongiosis
def: "Spongiosis refers to the increased intercellular edema in the epidermis resulting in the pulling away of the keratinocytes from their surrounding desmosomes. Histologically, the spongiotic tissue reaction pattern involves the accumulation of fluid in the intercellular spaces of the epidermis, making the desmosomes junctions more easy to appreciate. Parakeratosis forms above the areas of spongiosis. The foci of spongiosis can be microscopic to grossly identifiable clinically with vesicles or bullae." [PMID:28237387, PMID:37445645]
comment: Comment: Spongiosis is present in all diseases manifesting clinically as eczema; however, there are diseases with spongiosis that do not belong to the eczema spectrum, e.g., pityriasis rosea, erysipelas or tinea. . Spongiotic dermatoses include a very large list of disorders which are best grouped under neutrophilic, eosinophilic, miliarial, follicular and pityriasiform forms of spongiosis.
is_a: HP:0011124 ! Abnormal epidermal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10935
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-31T09:45:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001167
name: Discoid adrenal gland
def: "A congenital finding where the adrenal gland does not form it's typical triangular, Y or V shape and is instead discoid, straight or elongated in shape. It is often found incidentally on renal ultrasound and is associated with renal agenesis and other renal congenital anomalies." [PMID:33552228]
synonym: "Elongated adrenal gland" EXACT []
synonym: "Lying down adrenal gland" EXACT []
synonym: "Lying down adrenal sign" EXACT []
synonym: "Pancake adrenal gland" EXACT []
synonym: "Straight adrenal gland" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011732 ! Abnormal adrenal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10938
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-31T09:45:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001168
name: Abnormal optic disc vasculature morphology
def: "A structural abnormality in the blood vessels of the optic disc, including bleeding, tortuosity, dilation, shunting, or other unusual branching patterns." []
comment: May be associated with conditions such as glaucoma, papilledema, leber optic neuropathy, or optic disc drusen, and can contribute to visual field defects or other optic neuropathies.
is_a: HP:0012795 ! Abnormal optic disc morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10941
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-31T09:45:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001169
name: Supraclavicular nerve distribution
def: "Localization of symptoms such as numbness or paresthesias on the skin over the upper chest, specifically above the clavicle and over the lateral aspect of the neck, corresponding to the distribution of the supraclavicular nerve." []
comment: May be observed with clavicle shaft fracture.
is_a: HP:0025849 ! Localized along nerve distribution
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10942
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-01-31T09:45:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001170
name: Limited shoulder internal rotation
def: "Difficulty rotating the lower part of the arm towards the body (tested with the elbow flexed and the elbow held next to the side of the body or shoulder 90 degrees abducted to the side) secondary to pain, weakness, or mechanical block." []
comment: Conditions characterized by this finding include shoulder internal impingement syndrome, pectoralis major rupture, proximal humeral epiphysiolysis, and rotator cuff tear arthropathy.
synonym: "Shoulder internal rotation limited" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0006467 ! Limited shoulder movement
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10998
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-02-22T15:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001171
name: Superior displacement of the humeral head
def: "An anterior posterior (AP) shoulder radiograph shows distance between the the proximal aspect of the humeral head and inferior aspect of the acromion of less than 7 mm." [PMID:8816337]
comment: Conditions characterized by this finding include rotator cuff tear arthropathy, rotator cuff tear, and shoulder external impingement syndrome.
synonym: "Decreased acromiohumeral distance" EXACT []
synonym: "High-riding shoulder" EXACT []
synonym: "Proximal subluxation of the humeral head" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003887 ! Abnormal humeral head morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11002
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-02-22T15:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001172
name: Increased compartment pressure
def: "intracompartmental pressure (ICP) over 30 mmHg. Acute compartment syndrome occurs when there is increased pressure within a closed osteofascial compartment, resulting in impaired local circulation. Acute compartment syndrome is considered a surgical emergency since, without proper treatment, it can lead to ischemia and eventually necrosis. Generally, acute compartment syndrome is considered a clinical diagnosis. However, ICP over 30 mmHg can be used as a threshold to aid in diagnosis." [PMID:28846257]
comment: Fascia is a thin, inelastic sheet of connective tissue that surrounds muscle compartments and limits the capacity for rapid expansion. The earliest objective physical finding is the tense, or wood-like feeling of the involved compartment. Pain is typically severe, out of proportion to the injury. Measurement of intracompartmental pressure is not required but can aid in diagnosis if uncertainty exists. Compartment pressures are often measured with a manometer, a device that detects intracompartmental pressure by measuring the resistance that is present when a saline solution is injected into the compartment. The normal pressure within the compartment is between 0 mmHg to 8 mmHg. An intra-compartmental pressure greater than 30 mmHg indicates compartment syndrome and a need for fasciotomy.
is_a: HP:0011804 ! Abnormal muscle physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10787
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-02-22T15:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001173
name: Pain at the lateral aspect of the elbow
def: "Pain localized to the radial aspect of the elbow." []
synonym: "Lateral elbow pain" EXACT []
synonym: "Radial elbow pain" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030835 ! Elbow pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10788
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-02-22T15:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001174
name: Pain at the posterior aspect of the elbow
def: "Pain localized to the posterior aspect of the elbow." []
comment: The posterior aspect of the elbow refers to the back side of the elbow, which forms the prominent bony tip of the elbow.
is_a: HP:0030835 ! Elbow pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10788
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-02-22T15:17:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001175
name: Pain at the medial aspect of the elbow
def: "Pain localized to the medial aspect of the elbow." []
comment: The medial aspect of the elbow refers to the inner side of the elbow. Conditions characterized by this finding include medial epicondylitis.
is_a: HP:0030835 ! Elbow pain
