[Term]
id: HP:6001197
name: Wrist arthritis
def: "Inflammation of the wrist joint." [PMID:30285392]
comment: Symptoms of arthritis include pain, swelling, redness, stiffness, and loss of motion of the involved joint. Three primary types of arthritis affect the human wrist: osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and post-traumatic arthritis.
is_a: HP:0001369 ! Arthritis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10714
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001198
name: Scapholunate interval widening
def: "Widening of the space between the scaphoid and lunate on x-ray; scapholunate dissociation." [PMID:608295]
synonym: "Terry-Thomas sign" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10716
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001199
name: FInger pulp localization
def: "Applies to an abnormality whose distribution is limited to or predominantly affects the fleshy mass on the volar (palmar) aspect of the digit, distal to the distal interphalangeal (DIP) joint (known as the pulp of the finger)." []
synonym: "Symptoms localized to pulp of the finger" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0012838 ! Localized
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10717
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001200
name: Ulnar wrist pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the ulnar side of the wrist." []
comment: The ulnar side of the wrist is the side of the wrist closest to the little finger (fifth finger, pinky). Conditions characterized by this term include triangular fibrocartilage complex, distal radioulnar joint (DRUJ) arthritis, and pisotriquetral (PT) osteoarthritis.
is_a: HP:0030836 ! Wrist pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10722
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001201
name: Lunotriquetral interval widening
def: "Radiographic widening of the space between the lunate and triquetrum bones." []
comment: This finding may be observed with lunotriquetral ligament injury.
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10729
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001202
name: Ulnar translocation of the carpus
def: "Anteroposterior wrist radiograph showing ulnar translocation of the carpus from the distal radius with widening of the radial styloid-scaphoid space." [PMID:35415594]
comment: This finding may be observed with Carpal instability nondissociative (CIND).
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10731
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-01T12:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001203
name: Snapping sensation at time of injury
def: "A popping or snapping sensation (noise or feeling) at the time of an injury." []
comment: Sudden snapping or popping at the time of an injury can be a sign of significant damage to muscles, tendons, ligaments, or bones.
is_a: HP:0025280 ! Pain characteristic
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9914
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-08T14:14:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001204
name: Pagetoid spread
def: "Pagetoid spread connotes the spread of single neoplastic cells, and small nests of them above the basal layer in a variety of melanocytic and nonmelanocytic neoplasms similar to the pattern seen in Paget's and in extramammary Paget disease." [PMID:20431478]
comment: Pagetoid proliferation of single melanocytic cells or small nests of melanocytes may be seen in a variety of melanocytic neoplasms including pagetoid spitz nevi, de novo epithelioid melanocytic dysplasia, and melanoma. Pagetoid melanocytosis may also be a common feature of acral nevi, traumatized nevi, or in nevi after acute sun exposure.
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9951
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-08T14:14:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001205
name: Central scarring
def: "Central scarring of skin lesions." [PMID:29261968, PMID:36911588]
is_a: HP:0012836 ! Spatial pattern
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/9962
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-08T14:14:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001206
name: Scapholunate ligament tear
def: "A breakage (partial or complete tear) of the scapholunate ligament. The most common cause is physical trauma to the wrist such as a fall onto an outstretched hand. Tear of the scapholunate ligament may lead to carpal instability." [PMID:32684689, PMID:38817761]
comment: Together with the lunotriquetral interosseous ligament, the scapholunate ligament is one of the two proximal interosseous carpal ligaments of the wrist. It is a C-shaped ligament that binds the scaphoid bone to the lunate bone of the wrist. A scapholunate tear can be partial or complete. Since it is C-shaped, it often is only one limb of the C that is torn.
synonym: "Scapholunate ligament injury" EXACT []
synonym: "Scapholunate ligament rupture" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10725
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T08:44:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001207
name: Lunotriquetral ligament tear
def: "A breakage (partial or complete tear) of the lunotriquetral ligament. The most common cause is physical trauma to the wrist such as a fall onto an outstretched hand. Rupture or tear of the the lunotriquetral ligament may lead to carpal instability." [PMID:36689137]
comment: The scapholunate and lunotriquetral interosseous ligaments form the interconnections between the bones of the proximal carpal row and share several anatomic features. Each forms a barrier between the radiocarpal and midcarpal joints, connecting the dorsal, proximal, and palmar edges of the respective joint surfaces.
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10726
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T08:44:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001208
name: Pisotriquetral arthritis
def: "Arthritis at the pisotriquetral joint. Radiographic evidence of arthritis at the pisotriquetral joint includes joint space narrowing, osteophytes, subchondral cysts, and/or subchondral sclerosis." [PMID:27777815]
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10724
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T08:44:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001209
name: Volar intercalated segment instability
def: "A type of carpal instability characterized by volar tilt of the lunate bone." [PMID:32491661]
comment: Lateral wrist radiograph showing volar flexion of the lunate with a scapholunate angle less than 30 degrees. This finding may be observed with conditions such as lunotriquetral ligament injury and carpal instability nondissociative.
is_a: HP:0001191 ! Abnormal carpal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10727
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T08:44:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001210
name: Inaccurate finger pulse oximetry oxygen saturation measurement
def: "Any substantial discrepancy between the measurement of oxygen saturation with finger probe pulse oximetry as compared to an arterial blood gas, which is considered the gold standard." [PMID:34652479]
comment: Pulse oximetry is an useful, readily available and non-invasive tool of measuring oxygen saturation. It uses light sensors containing two light sources of different wavelengths, that are absorbed by haemoglobin (both oxy and deoxy forms) and transmitted through tissues to a photodetector. Any discrepancy in the light transmission caused either by vascular abnormality of the fingers or anatomical change may lead to inaccurate or absence of reading in the pulse oximeter.
is_a: HP:0025323 ! Abnormal arterial physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10671
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001211
name: Finger pulse oximetry lower than arterial blood gas analysis measurement of oxygen saturation
def: "Inaccurately reduced oxygen saturation as measured by finger or toe pulse oximetry compared to oxygen saturation as measured by venous or arterial blood gas analysis." [PMID:38340159]
comment: This feature may be observed with conditions such as Raynaud phenomenon and scleroderma, in which peripheral microvasculopathy leads to poor perfusion of the fingers.
is_a: HP:6001210 ! Inaccurate finger pulse oximetry oxygen saturation measurement
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10671
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001212
name: Finger pulse oximetry higher than arterial blood gas analysis measurement of oxygen saturation
def: "Inaccurately elevated oxygen saturation as measured by finger or toe pulse oximetry compared to oxygen saturation as measured by venous or arterial blood gas analysis." [PMID:9792574]
comment: This feature may be observed with Carbon monoxide poisoning. Presently available pulse oximeters overestimate arterial oxygenation in patients with severe CO poisoning. An elevated COHb level falsely elevates the SaO2 measurements from pulse oximetry.
is_a: HP:6001210 ! Inaccurate finger pulse oximetry oxygen saturation measurement
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10671
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001213
name: History of thumb sucking past the age of four years
def: "Thumb sucking is a behavior that ceases spontaneously in most children between 2 and 4 years of age. If thumb sucking continues, negative consequences can occur, such as a deformity of the nail or paronychia. This term refers to a history of habitual thumb sucking past the age of 4 years of life." [PMID:32310572]
is_a: HP:0032443 ! Past medical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10673
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001214
name: Cutaneous granulomatosis
def: "Skin inflammatory reaction triggered by a wide variety of stimuli, including infections, foreign bodies, malignancy, metabolites, and chemicals. From a pathogenic point of view, they are divided into non-infectious and infectious granulomas. From a clinical point of view, it is useful to divide cutaneous granulomatosis into localized and more disseminated forms, although this distinction can be sometimes artificial." [PMID:29352388]
is_a: HP:0002955 ! Granulomatosis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10682
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7371-8158
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001215
name: Ureteric stricture
def: "Obstruction of urine flow through one or both ureters caused by issues such as injury, infection, tumours and surgery." [PMID:25100183]
is_a: HP:0025633 ! Abnormal ureter morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10958
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-03-09T11:22:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001216
name: Arteriovenous crossing sign
def: "A retinal vascular abnormality characterized by indentation or compression of a retinal vein at an arteriovenous crossing, leading to changes in venous caliber. AV crossing signs are commonly associated with hypertensive retinopathy and may contribute to retinal vein occlusion. They are indicative of vascular remodeling due to chronic hypertension or other systemic vascular diseases." []
comment: This feature may be present in diseases such as hypertensive retinopathy and retinal vein occlusion.
synonym: "Arteriovenous nicking" EXACT []
synonym: "AV crossing changes" EXACT []
synonym: "AV nicking" EXACT []
synonym: "Gunn sign" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0008046 ! Abnormal retinal vascular morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10985
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001217
name: Haab striae
def: "Curvilinear or circumferential breaks in Descemet membrane, typically associated with congenital glaucoma. Haab striae result from elevated intraocular pressure during corneal development, leading to the formation of horizontal or arcuate lines that may be visible on slit-lamp examination. They can contribute to corneal astigmatism and visual impairment." [PMID:27993263, PMID:30554872]
synonym: "Haab's striae" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011490 ! Abnormal Descemet membrane morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10986
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001218
name: Positive Legionella sputum culture
def: "Growth of Legionella bacteria in a sputum culture." [PMID:38501659]
is_a: HP:0430107 ! Sputum infectious agent
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10988
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001219
name: Positive Streptococcus pneumoniae sputum culture
def: "Streptococcus pneumoniae growth in sputum culture." [PMID:24475349]
is_a: HP:0430107 ! Sputum infectious agent
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10989
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001220
name: Positive Blastomyces dermatitidis sputum fungal stain
def: "Demonstration of Blastomyces dermatitidis by microscopic examination of a stained sputum specimen." [PMID:28723016]
comment: Blastomycosis is a fungal infection caused by Blastomyces dermatitidis. It presents as a pulmonary infection after the inhalation of spores, and it may be either asymptomatic or have severe life-threatening complications like acute respiratory distress syndrome.
synonym: "Blastomyces dermatitidis on sputum fungal stain" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430107 ! Sputum infectious agent
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10990
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001221
name: Posterior shoulder pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the posterior (back) part of the shoulder." []
comment: Posterior shoulder pain may be observed in conditions such as shoulder internal impingement syndrome, suprascapular neuropathy, labrum tear, and shoulder dislocation.
is_a: HP:0030834 ! Shoulder pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10991
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001222
name: Superior shoulder pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the superior or proximal aspect of the shoulder over the acromion, distal clavicle, and/or acromioclavicular (AC) joint." []
comment: Superior shoulder pain may be observed in conditions such as acromioclavicular joint injury, acromioclavicular joint osteoarthritis, and distal clavicle osteolysis.
is_a: HP:0030834 ! Shoulder pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10991
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001223
name: Lateral shoulder pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the localized aspect (on the side) of the shoulder." []
comment: Lateral shoulder pain may be observed in conditions such as proximal humerus fracture, proximal humeral epiphysiolysis, adhesive capsulitis, and suprascapular neuropathy.
is_a: HP:0030834 ! Shoulder pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10991
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001224
name: Shoulder instability
def: "Subjective or objective feeling of clunking/clicking in the shoulder with movement, shoulder 'giving way', or sensation of shoulder dislocating." []
comment: Shoulder instability may be observed in conditions such as shoulder dislocation, labrum tear, and suprascapular neuropathy.
is_a: HP:0033129 ! Abnormal shoulder physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10993
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001225
name: Shoulder labrum tear
def: "A injury with a team (rip, split, or disruption) to the labrum, which is the ring of cartilage that surrounds the socket of the shoulder joint (the glenoid)." []
comment: Shoulder labral tears can be classified as superior Labral Anterior Posterior tear (SLAP); bankart lesion; anterior labral periosteal sleeve avulsion (ALPSA); and glenoid labral articular defect (GLAD) and may be observed in conditions such as shoulder dislocation, shoulder internal impingement syndrome, and acromioclavicular joint injury.
synonym: "Glenoid labral tear" EXACT []
synonym: "Labral tear in the shoulder" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003043 ! Abnormal shoulder morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10994
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001226
name: Positive modified dynamic labral shear test
def: "Sensation of a pain with or without clicking or clunking sensation with the following test. Flex patients elbow to 90 degrees and abduct the arm 120 degrees while maximally externally rotating the arm, then examiner lowers the arm to 60 degrees of abduction. A positive test occurs with pain and/or a painful click along the posterior joint line between 120 degrees and 90 degrees of abduction." [PMID:19509414]
comment: This test is frequently positive with labrum tear of the shoulder.
is_a: HP:0033129 ! Abnormal shoulder physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10995
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001227
name: Positive O'Brien active compression test
def: "Pain in shoulder reproduced when examiner applies downward pressure on the arm while patient resists pressure in the following position: elbow extended, shoulder forward flexed to 90 degrees and 10-15 degrees adducted with palm facing down. This can be compared to the same position but with the palm facing up which should be less painful." [PMID:17936025]
comment: A positive test may be observed in conditions such as acromioclavicular joint injury, shoulder labrum tear, adhesive capsulitis, and biceps subluxation.
is_a: HP:0025823 ! Positive provocative functional shoulder test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10996
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001228
name: Positive shoulder apprehension test
def: "The individual being investigated displays noticeable apprehension (unease) during a test for shoulder instability in which the individual is laying supine with shoulder abducted to 90 degrees, elbow flexed to 90 degrees, and an external rotation pressure with combined downward pressure is applied on the upper arm." [PMID:14977651]
is_a: HP:0025823 ! Positive provocative functional shoulder test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10997
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T13:13:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001229
name: Foamy tear film
def: "A condition characterized by the presence of foam or bubbles within the tear film, often associated with meibomian gland dysfunction or ocular surface diseases." [PMID:35508212]
comment: This feature may be observed in conditions such as Meibomian gland dysfunction and blepharitis.
synonym: "Frothy tear film" EXACT []
synonym: "Tear bubbles" EXACT []
synonym: "Tear foam" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000632 ! Lacrimation abnormality
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10870
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001230
name: Salzmann corneal nodules
def: "The formation of large, bluish, nodular lesions in the superficial corneal stroma, often associated with chronic keratitis or aging. These nodules may lead to visual impairment." [PMID:22228492]
synonym: "Salzmann nodular corneal degeneration" EXACT []
synonym: "Salzmann nodular corneal dystrophy" EXACT []
synonym: "Salzmann's nodules" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0007705 ! Corneal degeneration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10871
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001231
name: Corneal stromal vascularisation
def: "The abnormal growth of blood vessels into the corneal stroma, often associated with ocular herpes, chronic inflammation, infection, or hypoxia. This condition can lead to corneal scarring and vision impairment." []
comment: This feature may be observed in herpetic eye disease.
synonym: "Corneal stromal neovascularization" EXACT []
synonym: "Stromal vascularization of the cornea" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011496 ! Corneal neovascularization
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10874
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001232
name: Corneal iron line
def: "Linear or arcuate deposition of iron within the corneal epithelium or stroma, typically associated with conditions such as keratoconus, corneal degeneration, or postsurgical corneal changes." [PMID:21599747]
is_a: HP:0011495 ! Abnormal corneal epithelium morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10875
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001233
name: Conjunctivochalasis
def: "A condition characterized by redundant, loose conjunctival tissue, typically located between the globe and the lower eyelid, which may cause ocular discomfort, tear film instability, or epiphora." []
comment: Conjunctivochalasis can be observed with conditions such as dry eye and floppy eyelid syndrome.
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10876
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001234
name: Conjunctival hyperpigmentation
def: "Increased pigmentation of the conjunctiva, characterized by brown or black discoloration due to melanocytic proliferation or pigment deposition. It may be associated with benign conditions such as primary acquired melanosis or malignant transformation into conjunctival melanoma." [PMID:34424954]
synonym: "Conjunctival melanosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Hyperpigmentation of the conjunctiva" EXACT []
synonym: "Pigmented conjunctiva" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0000502 ! Abnormal conjunctiva morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10880
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001235
name: Anti-Saccharomyces cerevisiae antibodies
def: "Antibodies against antigens presented by the cell wall of the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae." [PMID:3143445]
comment: Anti-Saccharomyces cerevisiae antibodies (ASCAs) have been used as a marker for Crohn disease, Behcet disease, celiac disease, and other conditions.
synonym: "ASCA" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0430076 ! Bloodstream antifungal antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10890
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001236
name: Elevated fraction exhaled nitric oxide
def: "The fractional exhaled nitric oxide (FeNO) is elevated above the upper limit of normal. FeNO is an endogenous gaseous molecule which can be measured in the human breath test because of airway inflammation. It has been studied extensively as a marker of inflammation and has been incorporated into an algorithm for asthma management." [PMID:31417809]
comment: Fractional exhaled nitric oxide (FeNO) is a simple, reproducible, and a noninvasive marker of inflammation that may be elevated in diseases such as ssthma, eosinophilic pneumonia, COPD, pulmonary fibrosis, and interstitial lung disease.
synonym: "Fraction exhaled nitric oxide elevated" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002795 ! Abnormal respiratory system physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10894
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-26T14:44:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001237
name: Iris hyperemia
def: "A condition characterized by increased blood flow and congestion of the iris vasculature, leading to a reddish discoloration of the iris. Iris hyperemia is commonly associated with anterior uveitis, angle-closure glaucoma, or ocular inflammation." []
synonym: "Congested iris vessels" EXACT []
synonym: "Increased iris vascularity" EXACT []
synonym: "Iris hyperaemia" EXACT uk_spelling []
is_a: HP:0007905 ! Abnormal iris vasculature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10983
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-04-28T10:05:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001238
name: Elevated circulating reticulated platelet count
def: "The number of reticulated platelets per volume of blood in the peripheral circulation is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:24807169]
comment: Reticulated platelets (RPs) are young, hyper-reactive platelets that are newly released from the bone marrow. RPs are thus immature platelets circulating in blood; they reflect the activity of megakaryopoiesis in the bone marrow.They are larger and contain more RNA compared to older platelets. In comparison to more mature platelets, they exhibit a significantly higher thrombogenicity and are known to be elevated in patients with an increased platelet turnover such as, diabetics and after acute myocardial infarction.
is_a: HP:0011873 ! Abnormal platelet count
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10683
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-05-03T09:32:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001239
name: Reduced circulating reticulated platelet count
def: "The number of reticulated platelets per volume of blood in the peripheral circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:24807169]
comment: Reticulated platelets (RPs) are young, hyper-reactive platelets that are newly released from the bone marrow. RPs are thus immature platelets circulating in blood; they reflect the activity of megakaryopoiesis in the bone marrow.They are larger and contain more RNA compared to older platelets. In comparison to more mature platelets, they exhibit a significantly higher thrombogenicity and are known to be elevated in patients with an increased platelet turnover such as, diabetics and after acute myocardial infarction.
synonym: "Decreased immature platelet fraction" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011873 ! Abnormal platelet count
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10683
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-05-03T09:32:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001240
name: Abnormal circulating reticulated platelet count
def: "The number of reticulated platelets per volume of blood in the peripheral circulation is outside the limits of normal." [PMID:24807169]
comment: Reticulated platelets (RPs) are young, hyper-reactive platelets that are newly released from the bone marrow. RPs are thus immature platelets circulating in blood; they reflect the activity of megakaryopoiesis in the bone marrow.They are larger and contain more RNA compared to older platelets. In comparison to more mature platelets, they exhibit a significantly higher thrombogenicity and are known to be elevated in patients with an increased platelet turnover such as, diabetics and after acute myocardial infarction.
is_a: HP:0011873 ! Abnormal platelet count
