[Term]
id: HP:6001265
name: Localized to lower eyelid
def: "A descriptor indicating that a condition, lesion, or abnormality is confined to the lower eyelid. This localization may be relevant for various ocular conditions, including infections, structural abnormalities, or dermatological diseases affecting the lower eyelid region." [PMID:30616908, PMID:37777491]
comment: An anatomical spatial pattern or localization referring to the lower eyelid, the smaller, less mobile fold of skin and tissue positioned below the eye.
synonym: "Inferior palpebral location" EXACT []
synonym: "Lower lid location" EXACT []
