[Term]
id: HP:6001376
name: Forefoot pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized about the metatarsal heads in the front part of the foot." [PMID:28109624]
synonym: "Metatarsalgia" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025238 ! Foot pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11183
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-27T09:02:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001377
name: Spur at inferior pole of patella
def: "A bone spur (osteophyte), i.e., de novo bone formation at the lower edge of the patella (knee cap). Radiographically, it is visible as calcification at inferior pole of the patella." [PMID:39346060]
comment: This finding is characteristic of Sinding-Larsen-Johansson disease.
is_a: HP:0003045 ! Abnormal patella morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11195
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-27T09:02:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001378
name: Urinary ascites
def: "The presence of urine in the peritoneal cavity, an entity that typically results from bladder rupture or damage to the ureters." [PMID:23190938, PMID:37580961]
comment: Urinary ascites is commonly due to an obstructive uropathy or a neurogenic bladder.
is_a: HP:0001541 ! Ascites
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-27T09:02:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001379
name: Abnormal mixed venous oxygen saturation
def: "Abnormal oxygen saturation in mixed venous blood (SvO2). SvO2 can be measured in a sample of mixed venous blood drawn from the distal lumen of a catheter placed in the pulmonary artery. The SvO2 is dependent on arterial oxygen saturation, hemoglobin concentration, cardiac output, and tissue oxygen demands." [PMID:6870412]
comment: A fall in SvO2 usually implies anemia, arterial oxygen desaturation, and/or decreased cardiac output; however, a normal or high value does not exclude such disturbances. When employed in conjunction with the other indicators of tissue oxygenation available in an intensive care unit, SvO2 can be useful as a guide for both prognosis and urgency of therapy.
is_a: HP:0500165 ! Abnormal blood oxygen level
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11232
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-27T09:02:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001380
name: Elevated circulating lysosphingomyelin concentration
def: "The concentration of lysosphingomyelin in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal. Acid sphingomyelinase deficiency (ASMD) or Niemann-Pick type A/B is a lysosomal disorder caused by the deficiency of acid sphingomyelinase (ASM) due to pathogenic variants in the SMPD1 gene. Sphingomyelin (SM) is the substrate for ASM that cleaves the phosphorylcholine linkage of SM producing ceramide. SM is a major compound of most cell membranes and coupled with cholesterol constitutes most of the membrane rafts. In the deficiency of ASM, there is primary storage of SM, and the concentration of lysosphingomyelin in dried blood spots and in the blood circulation is typically elevated." [PMID:36348386]
is_a: HP:0003119 ! Abnormal circulating lipid concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11240
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-27T09:02:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001381
name: Abnormal lens capsule morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the lens capsule, the smooth, transparent, acellular basement membrane that envelops the lens of the eye and serves as the attachment site for the lens zonules and the lens epithelium." []
is_a: HP:0004328 ! Abnormal anterior eye segment morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10845
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001382
name: Posterior capsule opacification
def: "Posterior capsule opacification, also known as secondary cataract, is the most frequent complication following manual extracapsular cataract extraction. Secondary cataract results from the proliferation and migration of residual epithelial cells in the posterior region of the lens capsule into the visual axis, leading to thickening and reduction in transparency (opacification), which in turn can cause a decrease in visual acuity." [PMID:21750620]
synonym: "Secondary cataract" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004328 ! Abnormal anterior eye segment morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10845
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001383
name: Bronchial stenosis
def: "A narrowing (constriction) of the lumen of a bronchus, which may involve one or more of the major airways branching from the trachea." []
comment: Bronchial stenosis may affect the main bronchi, lobar bronchi, or segmental bronchi. Clinical manifestations depend on the location and severity of narrowing and can include wheezing, dyspnea, recurrent pneumonia, or asymmetric lung ventilation on imaging.
synonym: "Bronchial narrowing" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025426 ! Abnormal bronchus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10861
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001384
name: Skin tenting due to fracture
def: "Skin tenting may occur in the setting of a fracture when a displaced bone fragment pushes on the skin, causing it to bulge outward in a tent-like shape." [PMID:34423090]
is_a: HP:0011355 ! Localized skin lesion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10861
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001385
name: Follicular conjunctivitis
def: "A type of conjunctivitis characterized by the formation of conjunctival follicles, which appear as raised domes on the are round collections of lymphocytes, and are often most prominent in the inferior fornix (interior part of the lower eyelid)." []
is_a: HP:0000509 ! Conjunctivitis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10919
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001386
name: Granulomatous conjunctivitis
def: "A type of conjunctivitis characterized by the formation of conjunctival granulomata, i.e., localized nodular inflammatory lesions of the conjunctiva, characterized histologically by aggregates of epithelioid histiocytes, often with multinucleated giant cells, surrounded by lymphocytes and fibroblasts." [PMID:37318529]
is_a: HP:0000509 ! Conjunctivitis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10919
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001387
name: Areas of hypopigmentation and hyperpigmentation that follow Blaschko lines
def: "Linear streaks of hypopigmentation or hyperpigmentation that are distributed according to Blaschko lines, which are V-shaped, S-shaped, or linear patterns on the skin that reflect the embryonic migration pathways of epidermal cells (keratinocytes, melanocytes, etc.) during early development." [PMID:9125765]
is_a: HP:0009123 ! Mixed hypo- and hyperpigmentation of the skin
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10921
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001388
name: Retinal drusen
def: "Small focal extracellular deposits underneath the retina, visible ophthalmoscopically as yellow dots." [PMID:19726434, PMID:30404862]
comment: Drusen are lipid-, mineral-, and protein-containing extracellular deposits that accumulate between the basal lamina of the retinal pigment epithelium and Bruch's membrane of the human eye. They are a defining feature of age-related macular degeneration, a common sight-threatening disease of older adults.
is_a: HP:0000479 ! Abnormal retinal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10955
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9042-0508
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001389
name: Intrauterine amputation
def: "A developmental anomaly characterized by partial or complete absence of a limb or digit at birth, resulting from interruption of normal limb development in utero." [PMID:25531236, PMID:31407870, PMID:40818398]
comment: The two main mechanisms involve amniotic band disruption (constriction of a developing limb or digit by fibrous amniotic bands) and vascular disruption (e.g., thrombosis, hemorrhage, or ischemia).
synonym: "Congenital amputation" EXACT []
synonym: "Intra-uterine amputation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025662 ! Abnormal fetal skeletal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10960
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001390
name: Intrauterine digital amputation
def: "A developmental anomaly characterized by partial or complete absence of a finger or toe at birth, resulting from interruption of normal development in utero." []
is_a: HP:6001389 ! Intrauterine amputation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10961
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001391
name: Intrauterine limb amputation
def: "A developmental anomaly characterized by partial or complete absence of an arm or leg at birth, resulting from interruption of normal development in utero." [PMID:31407870, PMID:31424867, PMID:31787161]
is_a: HP:6001389 ! Intrauterine amputation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10962
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-28T08:50:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001392
name: Proximal interphalangeal joint arthritis
def: "Inflammation and deterioration of the proximal interphalangeal (PIP) joints. Radiographically, PIP arthritis can be characterized by PIP joint space narrowing, subchondral cysts, and osteophytes." [PMID:31312517]
comment: PIP arthritis manifests clinically with swollen, tender PIP joints, with a more diffuse, swollen appearance and a fusiform joint contour. Joint stiffness is almost always present and often correlates with the degree of swelling.
is_a: HP:0001369 ! Arthritis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10712
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T08:04:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001393
name: Dorsal intercalated segment instability
def: "A nondissociative form of carpal instability, in which the lunate bone angulates to the dorsal side of the hand." [PMID:23790423]
comment: Carpal instability can be defined as the lack of ligamentous and bony support to maintain a wrist stable to external forces.
is_a: HP:0025799 ! Abnormal wrist physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10728
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T08:04:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001394
name: Disruption of carpal arcs
def: "The arcs of the Gilula are used on PA wrist radiographs as part of assessing the normal alignment of the carpus. The 1st arc (red) outlines the proximal surfaces and the 2nd arc (yellow) the distal surfaces of the scaphoid, lunate and triquetrum. The 3rd arc (white) outlines the proximal surfaces of the capitate and hamate. Disruption of carpal arcs (i.e., the arcs appear broken or discontinuous on radiographs) indicates a fracture or ligamentous injury in the wrist." [PMID:37511801]
synonym: "Disruption of Gilula carpal arcs" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025798 ! Abnormal wrist morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10730
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T08:04:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001395
name: Spilled teacup sign of the wrist
def: "Dislocation of the lunate bone, generally as a result of trauma. Volar displacement of the lunate is said to result a tipped teacup." [PMID:23616330, PMID:37511801]
comment: Lateral wrist x-ray showing proximal dorsal displacement of the capitate and volar displacement of the dislocated lunate in a flexed position.
is_a: HP:0004248 ! Abnormal lunate bone morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10732
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T08:04:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001396
name: Positive Finkelstein sign
def: "Finkelstein's test produces severe tenderness and usually pain on the radial aspect of the wrist when the thumb is flexed into the palm and the wrist is ulnar deviated." [PMID:30969590]
comment: The Finkelstein test is a provocative test for diagnosis of De Quervain disease that can easily be performed in an office setting or at the bedside.
is_a: HP:0025799 ! Abnormal wrist physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10754
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T08:04:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001397
name: Forefoot abduction
def: "Outward deviation or turning of the front part of the foot away from the body's midline. An anteroposterior foot x-ray shows increased Simmon angle (angle between the talus and first metatarsal, normal is 7 degrees plus/minus 4 to 5 degrees) or increased talonavicular uncoverage of over 30 to 40 percent. A common clinical observation is the too many toes sign; when viewed from behind, more than two toes will flare out laterally due to the valgus alignment of the foot." [PMID:31194317]
is_a: HP:0001760 ! Abnormal foot morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11175
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001398
name: Posterior tibial tendon injury
def: "Damage to the posterior tibialis tendon, which runs along the inside of the ankle and foot, supporting the arch of the foot. MRI or ultrasound of the ankle/foot shows posterior tibial tendon degeneration such as tendinosis, tenosynovitis, edema around the tendon, or tendon tear." [PMID:28979585, PMID:31194317]
comment: The posterior tibialis muscle originates from the posterior proximal tibia, interosseous membrane and proximal fibula; it is in the deep posterior compartment of the leg and turns at the medial malleolus, changing its line of pull from the vertical one to the horizontal one. The myotendinous junction is situated at the distal third of the leg and only the tendinous portion turns at the medial malleolus; anterior subluxation is prevented by a flexor retinaculum which binds the tendon into the shallow groove at the medial malleolus.
is_a: HP:0001760 ! Abnormal foot morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11176
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001399
name: Plantar pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to palpation of plantar aspect of the foot (the sole)." []
is_a: HP:0025238 ! Foot pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11177
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001400
name: Flexor hallucis longus tendon injury
def: "Damage to the flexor hallucis longus (FHL) tendon. The FHL tendon is a long tendon that runs from the deep calf muscle down through the ankle to the big toe, enabling toe flexion and supporting foot mechanics.. MRI or ultrasound of the ankle/foot shows degenerative changes of the FHL tendon such as fluid around the tendon at the level of the ankle joint, intra-substance tendinous signal, tendon thickening, tendonitis, or tenosynovitis, or tendon rupture." []
is_a: HP:0001844 ! Abnormal hallux morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11178
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001401
name: Hallux pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the big toe (hallux)." []
synonym: "Big toe pain" EXACT []
synonym: "First toe pain" EXACT []
synonym: "Great toe pain" EXACT []
synonym: "Pain in hallux" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030841 ! Toe pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11179
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001402
name: Pain on the medial aspect of the foot
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the side of the foot nearest to the big toe (hallux)." []
is_a: HP:0025238 ! Foot pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11180
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001403
name: Hallux sesamoid injury
def: "Damage affecting one or both of the two small, pea-shaped bones (sesamoids) embedded in the tendons beneath the first metatarsophalangeal joint of the big toe. Foot x-ray shows fracture, subluxation, or dislocation of the sesamoid of the hallux." [PMID:19232995]
is_a: HP:0001844 ! Abnormal hallux morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11185
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-10-30T09:46:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001404
name: Radial wrist pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the radial side of the wrist." []
synonym: "Radial-sided wrist pain" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0030836 ! Wrist pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10755
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-02T23:10:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001405
name: Volar wrist pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the volar side of the wrist (i.e., to the palm side - front - of the wrist)." []
is_a: HP:0030836 ! Wrist pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10755
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-02T23:10:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001406
name: Dorsal wrist pain
def: "An unpleasant sensation characterized by physical discomfort (such as pricking, throbbing, or aching) localized to the dorsal side (back) of the wrist." []
is_a: HP:0030836 ! Wrist pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10755
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-02T23:10:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001407
name: Peroneal tendon tenderness
def: "Pain elicited with palpation along the course of the peroneal tendons, located posterior to the lateral malleolus and extending distally toward the base of the fifth metatarsal." [PMID:31335074]
is_a: HP:0025238 ! Foot pain
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11166
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001408
name: Peroneal tendon subluxation
def: "Dynamic ultrasound of the lateral ankle showing subluxation or dislocation of one or both of the peroneal tendons out of the peroneal groove." [PMID:31335074]
is_a: HP:0034673 ! Abnormal ankle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11167
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001409
name: Peroneal tendon injury
def: "Ankle MRI or ultrasound showing edema or thickening of peroneal tendon(s), fluid within peroneal tendon sheath, or a partial or complete tear in one or both of the peroneal tendons." [PMID:31335074]
is_a: HP:0034673 ! Abnormal ankle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11168
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001410
name: Elevated circulating succinylacetone concentration
def: "The concentration of succinylacetone in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:16448836, PMID:32832707]
comment: Succinylacetone can be created by the oxidation of glycine, and is a precursor of methylglyoxal. Succinylacetone is an abnormal tyrosine metabolite that arises from defects in the enzyme called fumarylacetoacetase.
synonym: "Succinylacetone high in blood" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0004354 ! Abnormal circulating carboxylic acid concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11241
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001411
name: Flat palate
def: "Reduced height of the palate. A flat palate is present with a palatal index angle below 30 degrees, a normal palate with an angle between 30 and 45 degrees, and a steep palate with an angle above 45 degrees." [PMID:18402092]
is_a: HP:0000174 ! Abnormal palate morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11246
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001412
name: Elevated circulating C-terminal telopeptide cross-link of type1 collagen concentration
def: "The concentration of C-terminal telopeptide cross-link of type1 collagen in the blood circulation is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:40638774]
comment: C-terminal telopeptide cross-link of type1 collagen is a biomarker of bone resorption.
is_a: HP:0033386 ! Abnormal circulating collagen degradation product concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11247
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001413
name: Exacerbated by pulmonary vasodilator exposure
def: "Applied to a sign or symptom that is worsened by treatment with a pulmonary vasodilator medication such as prostacyclin analogs, endothelin receptor antagonists, and phosphodiesterase-5 (PDE5) inhibitors." []
synonym: "Exacerbated by pulmonary vasodilators" EXACT []
is_a: HP:4000176 ! Aggravated by exposure to medication
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11268
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001414
name: Mercury exposure
def: "History of exposure to mercury." [PMID:40287162]
is_a: HP:4000110 ! Exposure history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11306
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001415
name: Urinoma
def: "Encapsulated collections of urine around the kidney in the retroperitoneum, most commonly in the perirenal space, as a consequence of renal tract leakage caused by urinary obstruction, trauma, or post-instrumentation." [PMID:34507797]
is_a: HP:6000285 ! Retroperitoneal mass
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11313
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001416
name: Umbilical discharge
def: "Abnormal fluid draining from the umbilicus (from wounds, surgical sites, or fistulas)." [PMID:34277280]
comment: The dischanrge may be serous, purulent, bloody, or foul-smelling.
is_a: HP:0004298 ! Abnormal abdominal wall morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001417
name: Abnormal biparietal diameter
def: "Abnormal biparietal diameter (BPD) refers to a fetal head width measurement, taken between the outer edge of the proximal parietal bone and the inner edge of the distal parietal bone on an ultrasound image, that lies outside the expected range for a given gestational age. The expected range typically falls between the 10th and 90th percentiles, with microcephaly defined as a BPD below the 3rd percentile (or more than 2 standard deviations below the mean) and macrocephaly defined as a BPD above the 97th percentile (or more than 2 standard deviations above the mean)." [PMID:6152941, PMID:6979175]
synonym: "Abnormal BPD" EXACT abbreviation []
is_a: HP:0034245 ! Fetal head anomaly
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11333
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5177-8109
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001418
name: Abnormal fetal femur length
def: "Femur length is measured between the outer border of one end of the the femoral diaphysis to the other outer border, excluding the epiphysis or other artifact. Abnormal femur length is defined as being more than two standard deviations away from the mean." []
is_a: HP:0025662 ! Abnormal fetal skeletal morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11335
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5177-8109
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-15T12:26:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001419
name: Pain exacerbated by wrist ulnar deviation
def: "Pain worsens with wrist ulnar deviation (i.e., the pain is exacerbated if the hand is moved towards the side with the fifth finger)." []
is_a: HP:6001152 ! Pain exacerbated by wrist deviation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10742
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001420
name: Pain exacerbated by wrist radial deviation
def: "Pain worsens with wrist radial deviation (i.e., the pain is exacerbated if the hand is moved towards the side with the thumb)." []
is_a: HP:6001152 ! Pain exacerbated by wrist deviation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10742
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001421
name: Ulnar positive variance
def: "A phenomenon whereby the distal ulna articular surface is more distal than the distal radius articular surface." [PMID:36752828]
comment: The triangular fibrocartilage complex (TFCC) is a well-defined anatomical entity of the wrist joint known as the primary stabilizing structure of the distal radioulnar joint (DRUJ). The TFCC provides considerable DRUJ stability. The instability of DRUJ caused by the foveal tear of the TFCC also results in an abnormal anatomic relationship between the radius and ulna. When the foveal attachment of the TFCC is disrupted, the ulnar head is free to sublux dorsally relative to the sigmoid notch of the radius, which is aggravated under the stress of pronation. This change in the anatomic relationship between the radius and ulna can be easily observed on plain radiographs.
is_a: HP:0002973 ! Abnormal forearm morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10750
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001422
name: Negative ulnar variance
def: "Negative ulnar variance is a condition in which the ulna is relatively shorter than the radius at the carpus. AP wrist X-ray shows the distal ulna articular surface more proximal than the distal radius articular surface." []
comment: Negative ulnar variance may be observed in Kienbock disease.
is_a: HP:0002973 ! Abnormal forearm morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10750
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001423
name: Flexor carpi radialis tendonitis
def: "Inflammation of the flexor carpi radialis (FCR) tendon, which traverses the carpus through a narrow fibro-osseous tunnel." [PMID:39166186]
comment: Flexor carpi radialis (FCR) tendinitis is an uncommon but important cause of volar radial wrist pain. The FCR tendon may become inflamed primarily or as a sequelae of carpometacarpal arthroplasty, arthritis, or trauma.
synonym: "FCR inflammation" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025230 ! Tendonitis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10757
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001424
name: Transillumination test shows high light transmission
def: "A transillumination test involves shining light through an area of the body or a mass. This term refers to a transillumination test that shows especially high (positive) transillumination, which may be observed when a mass or swelling contains clear fluid rather than solid tissue or blood." [PMID:20124823]
comment: Ganglion cysts may show high transillumination.
synonym: "Bright transillumination" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0025758 ! Characteristic of mass
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10767
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001425
name: Hyperleukocytosis
def: "Hyperleukocytosis is commonly defined as a white blood cell (WBC) count of greater than 100,000 luekocytes per microliter." [PMID:33080779]
comment: Hyperleukocytosis can be observed in conditions such as acute myeloid leukemia, which is characterized by the clonal proliferation of hematopoietic stem cells. Hyperleukocytosis is regarded as a hematological emergeny and can lead to complications such as leukostasis, disseminated intravascular coagulation, and tumor lysis syndrome.
is_a: HP:0001974 ! Increased total leukocyte count
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10782
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001426
name: Elbow instability
def: "Impairment of the ability of the elbow joint to maintain proper anatomical alignment and functional mechanics. Elbow instability is a spectrum from subluxation to dislocation, with corresponding clinical and pathologic features and therapeutic implications." [PMID:28160902, PMID:7962147]
is_a: HP:0020301 ! Abnormal elbow physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10795
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001427
name: Valgus instability of the elbow
def: "A type of elbow instability that arises through injuries to the medial collateral ligament (MCL), specifically the anterior bundle (AMCL). In the valgus stress test, the elbow is placed in 20 to 30 degrees of flexion with the forearm supinated and a valgus stress is applied. The test is positive when no firm end point is palpated, greater than 1 mm of medial joint opening is noted (fluoroscopically), or there is reproduction of the patient's pain." [PMID:28160902]
comment: Medial collateral ligament injuries may occur after trauma, such as an elbow dislocation, or as a repetitive overuse injury, commonly seen in overhead-throwing athletes. The typical history includes a pop and medial elbow pain following throwing activities, or patients may present with recurrent medial elbow pain, classically during the late cocking to early acceleration phase of throwing. Athletes typically complain of a progressive loss of velocity, accuracy, and endurance, which may be exacerbated by glenohumeral internal rotation deficits common to throwing athletes. The physical examination typically elicits tenderness over the MCL.
is_a: HP:6001426 ! Elbow instability
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10795
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001428
name: Varus instability of the elbow
def: "A type of elbow insttability characterized by abnormal widening or gapping of the lateral (radial) side of the elbow joint when a varus stress is applied, due to insufficiency of the lateral collateral ligament complex." [PMID:28160902]
is_a: HP:6001426 ! Elbow instability
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10795
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-19T09:34:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001429
name: Limited foot eversion
def: "Decreased foot eversion secondary to pain, weakness, or mechanical block." []
comment: This feature is assocaited with a reduced foot range of motion and may be experienced as a stiff foot.
synonym: "Foot eversion limited" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034430 ! Abnormal joint physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11156
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-20T11:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001430
name: Limited foot inversion
def: "Decreased foot inversion secondary to pain, weakness, or mechanical block." []
comment: This feature is assocaited with a reduced foot range of motion and may be experienced as a stiff foot.
synonym: "Foot inversion limited" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0034430 ! Abnormal joint physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11156
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-20T11:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001431
name: Positive synovial Tropheryma whipplei bacteria microscopy
def: "Demonstration of Tropheryma whipplei bacteria in the synovial (joint) fluid by microscopic analysis." []
is_a: HP:6000581 ! Positive synonvial fluid infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11157
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-20T11:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001432
name: Positive calf squeeze test
def: "An abnormal result of the calf-squeeze test (also known as the Thompson test), which is considered a sign of Achilles tendon rupture. The test is positive (abnormal) if no plantar flexion of the foot occurs at calf squeezing." [PMID:25409728]
comment: With the patient laying prone and feet hanging over the edge of a table, passive squeeze of the calf does not reproduce normal plantarflexion of the foot.
synonym: "Positive Simmonds-Thompson test" EXACT []
synonym: "Positive Thompson test" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0011843 ! Abnormal musculoskeletal physiology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11158
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-20T11:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001433
name: Achilles tendon tear
def: "A partial or complete break in the Achilles tendon (the tendon that connects the gastrocnemius and soleus to the calcaneus). This feature can be ascertained by magnetic resonance imaing (MRI) of the foot/ankle showing partial or complete tear of the achilles tendon." []
is_a: HP:0005109 ! Abnormal Achilles tendon morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11159
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-20T11:19:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001434
name: Positive bursa fluid gram stain
def: "Demonstration of the presence of bacteria by gram staining of bursa fluid. The sample is generally obtained by bursal fluid aspiration." []
is_a: HP:0430030 ! Positive infectious agent test
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10819
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-29T18:44:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001435
name: Abnormal medial epicondyle morphology
def: "A structural anomaly of the medial epicondyle, which is the site of the attachment of various muscles, including the radial and ulnar flexor of the wrist, the superficial flexor of the fingers, the palmaris longus and the pronator teres muscle." [PMID:37344531]
is_a: HP:0031095 ! Abnormal humerus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10828
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-29T18:44:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001436
name: Medial humerus epicondyle avulsion fracture
def: "An avulsion fracture of the medial epicondyle of the elbow. Radiological examination in the anteroposterior and lateral projection can be used to make the diagnosis and to determine the degree and direction of the fracture displacement." [PMID:37344531]
is_a: HP:6001435 ! Abnormal medial epicondyle morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10828
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-29T18:44:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001437
name: Hand mass
def: "A swelling or enlargement localized to the hand. The word mass is usually used at an early stage of the diagnostic workup before the precise nature of the swelling has been determined." []
synonym: "Bump on the hand" EXACT []
synonym: "Hand cyst" RELATED []
synonym: "Hand growth" EXACT []
synonym: "Hand nodule" EXACT []
synonym: "Hand tumor" EXACT []
synonym: "Lump on the hand" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0005922 ! Abnormal hand morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10843
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-11-29T18:44:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001438
name: Tenosynovitis
def: "Inflammation of the synovial sheath that surrounds a tendon." [PMID:16331793]
comment: Tenosynovitis can be ascertained as hypoechoic or anechoic thickened tissue with or without fluid within the tendon sheath, which is seen in 2 perpendicular planes and which may exhibit Doppler signal.
is_a: HP:0100261 ! Abnormal tendon morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11347
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7382-9958
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001439
name: Tigroid fundus
def: "Enhanced visibility of large choroidal vessels through the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE). This reticulated pattern is commonly observed on fundus examination and color fundus photography. Such hypopigmented areas alternate with hyperpigmented zones in a tigroid pattern. Fundus tessellation is often associated with myopia and choroidal thinning." [PMID:40914444]
comment: Tigroid fundus may be a normal variant or an early phenotypic indicator of various retinal or choroidal diseases. In pathological conditions such as high myopia, age-related choroidal atrophy, or inherited retinal dystrophies, FT may reflect underlying structural alterations in the choroid, RPE, or sclera, some of which may predispose to significant visual impairment
synonym: "Fundus tesselation" EXACT []
synonym: "Mosaic fundus" EXACT []
synonym: "Tessellated fundus" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001098 ! Abnormal fundus morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11354
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001440
name: Decreased myocardial glycogen content
def: "The amount of glycogen in the myocardial tissue of the heart is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:17928598, PMID:21958591, PMID:40536305]
synonym: "Glycogen depletion in cardiac muscle tissue" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001637 ! Abnormal myocardium morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11357
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001441
name: CSF anti-myelin oligodendrocyte glycoprotein antibody positivity
def: "The presence of autoantibodies (immunoglobulins) in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) that react against myelin oligodendrocyte glycoprotein." [PMID:39318613, PMID:40327177]
comment: CSF anti-myelin oligodendrocyte glycoprotein antibody positivity can be seen in MOG antibody-associated disease (MOGAD), multiple sclerosis, and other neuroimmunological diseases.
is_a: HP:0032265 ! CSF autoimmune antibody positivity
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11360
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001442
name: Spinal cord H sign
def: "The H sign can be ascertained by spinal magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and represents spinal cord myelitis isolated to the gray matter. A longitudinally extensive T2 hyperintense spinal cord lesion from C6 to T10, predominantly involving the gray matter. The appearance of the anomaly is said to resemble the letter H." [PMID:39318613, PMID:40327177]
comment: The H sign can be observed with Myelin oligodendrocyte glycoprotein antibody-associated disease (MOGAD), multiple sclerosis, and other neuroimmunological diseases.
synonym: "H sign in the spinal cord" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002143 ! Abnormal spinal cord morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11361
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001443
name: Abnormal testosterone: estradiol ratio
def: "Any deviation from the normal ratio of testosterone and estradiol (the primary sex steroids) to each other. The testosterone:estradiol ratio is derived from total testosterone in ng/dL and total estradiol in pg/mL, and expressed as T:E. Normal ranges are affected by sex, age, and other factors." [PMID:39344113]
comment: There is a natural balance between the major sex steroids, testosterone and estradiol, controlled by gonadal secretion and peripheral conversion by aromatase. This balance is impacted by a variety of inborn and acquired conditions.
is_a: HP:0033799 ! Abnormal circulating sex hormone concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11365
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001444
name: Abnormal circulating insulin-like growth factor 3 concentration
def: "The concentration of IGFBP-3 (Insulin-like Growth Factor-Binding Protein 3) in the blood circulation is outside the limits of normal." [PMID:37008935]
is_a: HP:0003117 ! Abnormal circulating hormone concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11371
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001445
name: Decreased circulating insulin-like growth factor 3 concentration
def: "The concentration of insulin-like growth factor 3 concentration (IGF3) in the blood circulation is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:1373347]
is_a: HP:6001444 ! Abnormal circulating insulin-like growth factor 3 concentration
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11371
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001446
name: Airway chondritis
def: "Inflammation of the cartilage of the airway, including especially the trachea and bronchi." [PMID:40271291]
synonym: "Respiratory tract chondritis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0002087 ! Abnormality of the upper respiratory tract
is_a: HP:0100662 ! Chondritis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11377
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001447
name: Costochondritis
def: "inflammation of the costal cartilage (the cartilage that connects the ribs to the sternum). The typical presentation of costochondritis is bilateral parasternal chest wall pain exacerbated by deep breaths, coughing, and stretching. The upper (predominantly second through fifth) costochondral and/or costosternal junctions are most commonly involved. The areas of tenderness are not generally accompanied by heat, erythema, or localized swelling." [PMID:34264599]
synonym: "Inflammation of he cartilage that connects the ribs to the sternum (breastbone)" EXACT layperson []
is_a: HP:0000772 ! Abnormal rib morphology
is_a: HP:0100662 ! Chondritis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11379
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-17T15:52:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001448
name: History of ocular surgery
def: "Past medical history of surgical procedure on the eye or its surroundings." []
is_a: HP:0430103 ! Past surgical history
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/10930
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001449
name: Increased plantar fascia thickness
def: "Increased thickness of the plantar fascia. This finding can be ascertained by ultrasound or magnetic resonance imaging." [PMID:27957702]
comment: The plantar fascia, also called the plantar aponeurosis, is a strong connective tissue structure that helps maintain the longitudinal arch of the foot. The diagnosis of plantar fasciitis generally relies on clinical history and physical examination. The main symptoms include pain and stiffness in the morning, or pain at the beginning of activity after rest. Physical examination reveals tenderness at the origin of the PF and impaired dorsiflexion of the ankle and extension of the toes. MRI or ultrasound of the foot show thickening of the plantar fascia (over 4.5mm) or increased signal within the plantar fascia.
synonym: "Plantar fasciitis" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001760 ! Abnormal foot morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11181
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001450
name: Increased mixed venous oxygen saturation
def: "Oxygen saturation in mixed venous blood (SvO2), as measured in a sample of mixed venous blood drawn from the distal lumen of a catheter placed in the pulmonary artery, is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:6870412]
is_a: HP:6001379 ! Abnormal mixed venous oxygen saturation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11232
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001451
name: Decreased mixed venous oxygen saturation
def: "Oxygen saturation in mixed venous blood (SvO2), as measured in a sample of mixed venous blood drawn from the distal lumen of a catheter placed in the pulmonary artery, is below the lower limit of normal." [PMID:6870412]
is_a: HP:6001379 ! Abnormal mixed venous oxygen saturation
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11232
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001452
name: Chocolate brown blood
def: "Characteristic chocolate-brown color of circulating blood with an elevated methemoglobin content." [PMID:30726002]
synonym: "Circulating blood brown or black" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0001871 ! Abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11163
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001453
name: Elevated pCO2 gap
def: "The difference between the venous-to-arterial carbon dioxide saturation (Pv-aCO2) is above the upper limit of normal." [PMID:32377433]
comment: Central venous-arterial carbon dioxide difference (PCO2 gap) can be a marker of cardiac output adequacy in global metabolic conditions that are less affected by the impairment of oxygen extraction capacity.
synonym: "Increased pCO2 gap" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0500164 ! Abnormal blood carbon dioxide level
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11232
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001454
name: Putaminal eye sign
def: "An imaging anomly of the putamen that is thought to be pathognomic for MEGDEL syndrome (3-MethylGlutaconic aciduria, Deafness, Encephalopathy, Leigh-like syndrome MIM #614739). In stage 1 of the disease, T2 signal changes of the pallidum are present. In stage 2, swelling of the putamen and caudate nucleus is seen. The dorsal putamen contains an eye that shows no signal alteration and (thus) seems to be spared during this stage of the disease. It later increases, reflecting progressive putaminal involvement. Sparing of the mid dorsal putamen (showing normal signal surrounded by T2 hyperintense signal) is referred to as the putaminal eye." [PMID:25642805, PMID:37996139]
is_a: HP:0031982 ! Abnormal putamen morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11391
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6714-5727
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001455
name: Decreased coracohumeral distance
def: "Axial view on shoulder X-ray or MRI showing decreased distance between posterior border of the coracoid process and anterior border of the humeral head of less than 6 mm; subcoracoid impingement; decreased coracohumeral interval." []
comment: Decreased coracohumeral distance can be observed in conditions such as rotator cuff tear and shoulder external impingement syndrome.
synonym: "Coracohumeral distance decreased" EXACT []
is_a: HP:0003043 ! Abnormal shoulder morphology
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11003
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199
property_value: terms:date "2025-12-18T15:49:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: HP:6001456
name: Abnormal deltoid muscle morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of the deltoid muscle, the large triangular intrinsic shoulder muscle, so named because its shape resembles the inverted Greek letter delta." [PMID:30725741]
