comment: Foregut duplication cysts (FDCs) are rare congenital anomalies of primitive foregut origin that arise during early embryonic development. FDCs comprise approximately 10% of all mediastinal tumors and can occur at any level of the alimentary track. Computed tomography (CT) is widely used as a modality for the evaluation and diagnosis of duplication cysts.
