[Term]
id: HP:6001516
name: Impaired first-phase insulin secretion
def: "An abnormal reduction in the ability to produce first-phase insulin secretion, which is defined as the initial burst of insulin released in the first 5 to 10 minutes after the beta cell is exposed to a rapid increase in glucose (or other secretagogues)." [PMID:11424229, PMID:15308473]
comment: In patients with impaired glucose tolerance or in the early stages of type 2 diabetes, first-phase insulin release is almost invariably lost despite the enhancement of second-phase secretion.
is_a: HP:0011014 ! Abnormal glucose homeostasis
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11674
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199

[Term]
id: HP:6001517
name: Impaired gastric accommodation
def: "Reduced capacity of the stomach, particularly the fundus, to relax and expand in response to a meal." [PMID:16042912, PMID:34337824]
comment: Gastric accommodation to a meal consists of relaxation of the proximal stomach without a concomitant increase in intragastric pressure. The gastric accommodation response consists of two primary and complementary motor functions during meal consumption: receptive relaxation and adaptive relaxation.
is_a: HP:0030895 ! Abnormal gastrointestinal motility
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11675
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4998-8617

[Term]
id: HP:6001518
name: Prominent plantar fat pad of forefoot
def: "An abnormally prominent soft tissue pad overlying the head of a metatarsal bone on the plantar surface of the foot." [PMID:24131727, PMID:32184933, PMID:41464288]
comment: The plantar fat pad of forefoot is a connective and adipose layer located between the reticular dermis and deeper structures such as the plantar fascia, muscles, and bones. In the forefoot, beneath the metatarsal heads, the plantar fat pad is organized into closed compartments with a honeycomb-like structure, where adipocytes are surrounded by fibrous septa rich in elastin. It encompasses the metatarsal and toe bd fat pad. This term refers to an unusually prominent fat pad.
synonym: "Prominent metatarsal fat pad" NARROW []
synonym: "Prominent toe base pad" NARROW []
is_a: HP:0100872 ! Abnormality of the plantar skin of foot
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/issues/11677
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4998-8617

