property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4429-6024

[Term]
id: HP:6001524
name: Poor oral mucosal wound healing
def: "An impairment of the normal tissue-repair process following injury to the oral mucosa, resulting in delayed or incomplete wound closure." [PMID:34439831]
comment: In general, wounds in the oral mucosa heal relatively fast and with little scarring, despite being continuously exposed to motion, tension, mechanical abrasion, and a great variety of microbes.
is_a: HP:0031815 ! Abnormal oral physiology
